{"path":"orchestrator/adapters/__init__.py","perm":"0644","sha":"d73c69aae70f2b157a1ce2e4e226a579fbe7262135d128a7609199d26cc846ad","data":"\"\"\"adapters \u2014\u2014 \u5c0d\u5916\u90e8\u7cfb\u7d71\u7684\u8584\u5c01\u88dd\uff0c\u5168\u90e8\u662f\u884c\u7a0b\u5167\u7684\u666e\u901a\u51fd\u5f0f\u3002\n\nS1 \u8d77 \u2460\uff08ado_pr_tools\uff09\u8207 \u2462\uff08review_result_tools\uff09\u4e0d\u518d\u662f\u7368\u7acb\u884c\u7a0b\uff1a\u552f\u4e00\u7684\u547c\u53eb\u8005\n\u5c31\u662f\u9019\u500b orchestrator\uff0c\u800c\u4e14\u5728\u540c\u4e00\u53f0\u6a5f\u5668\uff0cMCP \u90a3\u5c64\u53ea\u662f\u591a\u4e09\u500b port \u8207\u4e09\u4efd env\u3002\n\u9019\u88e1\u7684\u51fd\u5f0f\u662f\u540c\u6b65\u7684\uff08httpx.Client\uff09\uff0casync \u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u7d93 clients.py \u7528 asyncio.to_thread \u5305\u3002\n\"\"\"\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/adapters/ado.py","perm":"0644","sha":"7151c8916e94fef89df22f1e35cb6f5897e72a1ba7df6a1f61faed6e287af4f1","data":"\"\"\"Azure DevOps adapter \u2014\u2014 \u539f \u2460 ado_pr_tools\uff08\u8b80\uff09\u8207 \u2462 review_result_tools\uff08\u5beb\uff09\u5408\u4e00\u3002\n\n\u8b80\uff1aget_pr_metadata / list_pr_files / get_pr_diff\n\u5beb\uff1apost_review_comment / post_knowledge_draft / get_past_reviews\n\n\u5beb\u9019\u4e00\u5074\u4fdd\u7559\u539f\u672c\u7684\u96d9\u958b\u95dc\u8a9e\u610f\uff0c\u53ea\u662f\u4f4f\u5728\u540c\u4e00\u500b\u884c\u7a0b\u88e1\uff1a\n  review \u7559\u8a00   AUTO_POST\uff08orchestrator \u9ede\u4e0d\u9ede\u706b\uff09\u00d7 DRY_RUN\uff08\u9019\u88e1\u715e\u4e0d\u715e\u8eca\uff09\n  \u77e5\u8b58\u7a3f        KNOWLEDGE_POST\uff08\u7368\u7acb\u958b\u95dc\uff0c\u53ef\u5148\u884c\u8a66\u9ede\uff09\n\u51fa\u5ee0\u5168\u5b89\u5168\u5074\uff1b\u8aa4\u8a2d\u4efb\u4f55\u55ae\u9846\u90fd\u4e0d\u6703\u8aa4\u767c\u3002\u6bcf\u4e00\u6b21\u771f\u767c\u90fd\u7559\u4e00\u7b46\u7a3d\u6838\uff08audit_log\uff09\uff0c\nS3 \u7684\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u76f4\u63a5\u8b80\u5b83\u3002\n\n\u5168\u90e8\u662f\u540c\u6b65\u51fd\u5f0f\uff08httpx.Client\uff09\uff1basync \u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u898b clients.py\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport difflib\nimport time\nfrom collections import deque\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\n\nfrom shared.azdo import PrRef, client, get_json, get_text, parse_pr_url\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\nPAGE = 200          # ADO \u55ae\u9801\u4e0a\u9650\uff1b\u9760 $skip \u8ff4\u5708\u628a\u5168\u90e8\u6488\u5b8c\n\nMARKER = \"<!-- pr-review-bot -->\"                       # review \u7559\u8a00\u7684\u96b1\u5f62\u6d6e\u6c34\u5370\nKNOWLEDGE_MARKER = \"<!-- pr-review-knowledge-draft -->\"  # \u77e5\u8b58\u7a3f\u7684\u6d6e\u6c34\u5370\nREDISTILL_PREFIX = (\"_Draft updated after new commits; earlier author notes \"\n                    \"were kept._\")\n\n# \u6700\u8fd1 200 \u7b46\u5c0d ADO \u7684\u5beb\u5165\uff08\u542b dry-run\uff09\uff1a(\u6642\u9593, \u7a2e\u985e, pr_url, posted?, \u8aaa\u660e)\naudit_log: deque[dict] = deque(maxlen=200)\n\n\ndef _audit(kind: str, pr_url: str, posted: bool, note: str) -> None:\n    audit_log.append({\"ts\": time.time(), \"kind\": kind, \"pr_url\": pr_url,\n                      \"posted\": posted, \"note\": note})\n\n\n# ---------- \u8b80 ----------\n\ndef _latest_iteration(c, ref: PrRef) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"\u6700\u65b0\u4e00\u6b21 iteration \u7684\u5b8c\u6574\u7269\u4ef6\u3002\n\n    \u88e1\u9762\u6709\u4e09\u500b commit\uff0c\u9078\u5c0d\u54ea\u4e00\u500b\u6c7a\u5b9a\u4e86 diff \u5c0d\u4e0d\u5c0d\u5f97\u4e0a PR \u9801\u9762\uff1a\n      commonRefCommit  merge base \u2014\u2014 PR UI \u5de6\u6b04\u5c31\u662f\u5b83\uff08\u4e09\u9ede diff \u7684\u57fa\u6e96\uff09\n      sourceRefCommit  \u4f86\u6e90\u5206\u652f tip \u2014\u2014 PR UI \u53f3\u6b04\n      targetRefCommit  \u76ee\u6a19\u5206\u652f tip \u2014\u2014 **\u4e0d\u8981\u62ff\u4f86\u7576 base**\uff0cmaster \u4e00\u52d5\u5b83\u5c31\u8b8a\n    \"\"\"\n    iterations = get_json(c, f\"{ref.pr_api}/iterations\")[\"value\"]\n    return iterations[-1] if iterations else None\n\n\ndef _iteration_changes(c, ref: PrRef, iteration_id: int) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"\u8a72 iteration \u76f8\u5c0d merge base \u7684\u5b8c\u6574\u8b8a\u66f4\u6e05\u55ae\uff08$skip \u5206\u9801\uff0c\u4e0d\u622a\u65b7\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    entries: list[dict] = []\n    skip = 0\n    while True:\n        page = get_json(\n            c, f\"{ref.pr_api}/iterations/{iteration_id}/changes\",\n            **{\"$top\": PAGE, \"$skip\": skip},\n        ).get(\"changeEntries\", [])\n        entries += page\n        if len(page) < PAGE:\n            return entries\n        skip += PAGE\n\n\ndef _is_folder(entry: dict) -> bool:\n    item = entry.get(\"item\") or {}\n    return bool(item.get(\"isFolder\")) or item.get(\"gitObjectType\") == \"tree\"\n\n\ndef get_pr_metadata(pr_url: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"PR \u7684\u6a19\u984c\u3001\u63cf\u8ff0\u3001\u5206\u652f\u8207 head/base commit\u3002\"\"\"\n    ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n    with client() as c:\n        pr = get_json(c, ref.pr_api)\n        it = _latest_iteration(c, ref) or {}\n    # source_commit \u53d6\u81ea iteration \u800c\u975e lastMergeSourceCommit\uff1a\u5169\u8005\u5e73\u6642\u76f8\u540c\uff0c\n    # \u4f46\u524d\u8005\u624d\u662f\u9019\u4efd diff \u771f\u6b63\u7684\u53f3\u6b04\uff0c\u5feb\u53d6\u9375\u8981\u8ddf diff \u7d81\u5728\u4e00\u8d77\u624d\u4e0d\u6703\u5931\u6e96\u3002\n    source_commit = ((it.get(\"sourceRefCommit\") or {}).get(\"commitId\")\n                     or (pr.get(\"lastMergeSourceCommit\") or {}).get(\"commitId\"))\n    return {\n        \"repo\": ref.repo,  # \u8b93 orchestrator \u80fd\u8f09\u5165 per-repo \u898f\u5247\uff08rules/<repo\u5c0f\u5beb>/\uff09\n        \"title\": pr.get(\"title\", \"\"),\n        \"description\": pr.get(\"description\", \"\"),\n        \"source_branch\": pr.get(\"sourceRefName\", \"\"),\n        \"target_branch\": pr.get(\"targetRefName\", \"\"),\n        \"author\": (pr.get(\"createdBy\") or {}).get(\"displayName\", \"\"),\n        \"status\": pr.get(\"status\", \"\"),\n        \"source_commit\": source_commit,\n        \"merge_base\": (it.get(\"commonRefCommit\") or {}).get(\"commitId\"),\n        \"target_commit\": (pr.get(\"lastMergeTargetCommit\") or {}).get(\"commitId\"),\n    }\n\n\ndef list_pr_files(pr_url: str) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"\u9019\u689d PR \u8b8a\u66f4\u7684\u6a94\u6848\uff08\u8def\u5f91 + \u8b8a\u66f4\u578b\u614b\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n    with client() as c:\n        it = _latest_iteration(c, ref)\n        entries = ([e for e in _iteration_changes(c, ref, it[\"id\"]) if not _is_folder(e)]\n                   if it else [])\n    return [{\"path\": (e.get(\"item\") or {}).get(\"path\", \"\"),\n             \"change_type\": e.get(\"changeType\", \"\")}\n            for e in entries if (e.get(\"item\") or {}).get(\"path\")]\n\n\ndef get_pr_diff(pr_url: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u7d44\u51fa\u9019\u689d PR \u7684 unified diff\uff08\u7d14\u6587\u5b57\uff09\u3002\n\n    \u53d6\u6700\u65b0 iteration \u7684\u8b8a\u66f4\u6e05\u55ae\uff0c\u9010\u6a94\u6293 merge base / head \u5169\u4efd\u5167\u5bb9\uff0c\u7528 difflib\n    \u7522\u751f unified diff\u3002\u904e\u5927\u6216\u7591\u4f3c\u4e8c\u9032\u4f4d\u7684\u6a94\u6848\u6703\u6a19\u8a3b\u7565\u904e\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n    cfg = settings().ado\n    out: list[str] = []\n    with client() as c:\n        it = _latest_iteration(c, ref)\n        if it is None:\n            return \"# \u9019\u689d PR \u6c92\u6709 iteration\uff0c\u7121\u6cd5\u53d6\u5f97\u8b8a\u66f4\"\n\n        # \u4e09\u9ede diff\uff1amerge base \u2194 \u4f86\u6e90\u5206\u652f tip\uff0c\u8207 PR \u9801\u9762\u5de6\u53f3\u5169\u6b04\u4e00\u81f4\u3002\n        # \u7528 targetRefCommit \u7576 base \u6703\u628a\u76ee\u6a19\u5206\u652f\u4e0a\u5225\u4eba\u7684\u6539\u52d5\u53cd\u5411\u7b97\u9032\u4f86\uff0c\n        # \u800c\u4e14\u76ee\u6a19\u5206\u652f\u4e00\u5f80\u524d\u63a8\uff0c\u540c\u4e00\u689d\u6c92\u52d5\u904e\u7684 PR \u5c31\u6703\u8dd1\u51fa\u4e0d\u540c\u7684 diff\u3002\n        base = (it.get(\"commonRefCommit\") or {}).get(\"commitId\")\n        head = (it.get(\"sourceRefCommit\") or {}).get(\"commitId\")\n\n        entries = [e for e in _iteration_changes(c, ref, it[\"id\"])\n                   if not _is_folder(e)]\n\n        total = len(entries)\n        if total > cfg.diff_max_files:\n            out.append(f\"# \u6ce8\u610f\uff1a\u5171 {total} \u500b\u6a94\u6848\uff0c\u50c5\u5448\u73fe\u524d {cfg.diff_max_files} \u500b\\n\")\n            entries = entries[:cfg.diff_max_files]\n\n        item_url = f\"{ref.repo_api}/items\"\n\n        def _content(commit_id: str | None, p: str) -> str | None:\n            if not commit_id:\n                return None\n            return get_text(\n                c, item_url, path=p,\n                **{\"versionDescriptor.version\": commit_id,\n                   \"versionDescriptor.versionType\": \"commit\"},\n            )\n\n        # (\u65b0\u8def\u5f91, \u820a\u8def\u5f91)\uff1brename \u6642 base \u5074\u8981\u7528\u820a\u8def\u5f91\uff0c\u5426\u5247\u6574\u6a94\u6703\u88ab\u8aa4\u5224\u6210\u65b0\u589e\n        targets: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n        for e in entries:\n            path = (e.get(\"item\") or {}).get(\"path\")\n            if path:\n                targets.append((path, e.get(\"sourceServerItem\") or path))\n\n        def _pair(t: tuple[str, str]) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n            path, old_path = t\n            return _content(base, old_path), _content(head, path)\n\n        # \u6bcf\u6a94\u8981\u6293 base/head \u5169\u4efd\uff1b\u5e8f\u5217\u5316\u8dd1\u767e\u6a94\u6703\u62d6\u5230\u5206\u9418\u7d1a\uff0c\u7528\u57f7\u884c\u7dd2\u4f75\u767c\u3002\n        # httpx.Client \u662f thread-safe \u7684\uff1bexecutor.map \u4f9d\u8f38\u5165\u9806\u5e8f\u56de\u50b3\uff0c\u8f38\u51fa\u4ecd deterministic\u3002\n        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=cfg.diff_fetch_concurrency) as pool:\n            fetched = list(pool.map(_pair, targets))\n\n        for (path, old_path), (old, new) in zip(targets, fetched):\n            if old_path != path:\n                out.append(f\"# {old_path} \u2192 {path}: renamed\\n\")\n            if (old and len(old) > cfg.diff_max_file_bytes) \\\n                    or (new and len(new) > cfg.diff_max_file_bytes):\n                out.append(f\"# {path}: file too large \u2014 diff skipped\\n\")\n                continue\n            if (old and \"\\x00\" in old[:1024]) or (new and \"\\x00\" in new[:1024]):\n                out.append(f\"# {path}: binary file suspected \u2014 skipped\\n\")\n                continue\n            diff = difflib.unified_diff(\n                (old or \"\").splitlines(keepends=True),\n                (new or \"\").splitlines(keepends=True),\n                fromfile=f\"a{old_path}\", tofile=f\"b{path}\",\n            )\n            out.append(\"\".join(diff))\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(s for s in out if s.strip()) or \"# \u9019\u689d PR \u6c92\u6709\u53ef\u5448\u73fe\u7684\u6587\u5b57\u8b8a\u66f4\"\n\n\n# ---------- \u5beb ----------\n\ndef _new_thread(c, ref: PrRef, content: str) -> dict:\n    r = c.post(f\"{ref.pr_api}/threads\", params={\"api-version\": \"7.1\"},\n               json={\"comments\": [{\"parentCommentId\": 0, \"content\": content,\n                                   \"commentType\": 1}],\n                     \"status\": \"active\"})\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    return r.json()\n\n\ndef post_review_comment(pr_url: str, markdown: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\u628a review markdown \u767c\u6210 PR \u4e0a\u7684\u4e00\u689d comment thread\u3002\n\n    DRY_RUN=true\uff08\u9810\u8a2d\uff09\u6642\u4e0d\u6253 API\uff0c\u53ea\u56de\u50b3\u9810\u89bd \u2014\u2014 \u5167\u6e2c\u5b89\u5168\u6c23\u56ca\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n    content = f\"{MARKER}\\n{markdown}\"\n    if settings().posting.dry_run:\n        _audit(\"review\", pr_url, False, \"DRY_RUN=true\uff0c\u53ea\u9810\u89bd\")\n        return {\"posted\": False, \"dry_run\": True,\n                \"would_post_to\": ref.pr_api + \"/threads\", \"preview\": content[:500]}\n    with client() as c:\n        thread = _new_thread(c, ref, content)\n    _audit(\"review\", pr_url, True, f\"thread {thread.get('id')}\")\n    return {\"posted\": True, \"dry_run\": False, \"thread_id\": thread.get(\"id\")}\n\n\ndef post_knowledge_draft(pr_url: str, markdown: str,\n                         thread_id: int | None = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\u628a\u77e5\u8b58\u84b8\u993e\u7a3f\u767c\u6210 PR \u4e0a\u7684\u4e00\u689d thread\uff08KNOWLEDGE_POST=true \u624d\u771f\u8cbc\uff09\u3002\n\n    thread_id \u7d66\u5b9a\u6642\u6539\u6210\u300c\u56de\u8986\u9032\u90a3\u689d\u65e2\u6709 thread\u300d\u800c\u4e0d\u662f\u958b\u65b0\u7684\u2014\u2014\u91cd\u84b8\u7684\u66f4\u65b0\u7a3f\u8981\n    \u63a5\u5728\u4f5c\u8005\u56de\u904e\u8a71\u7684\u90a3\u4e32\u4e0b\u9762\uff0c\u4e0d\u7136\u540c\u4e00\u689d PR \u6703\u51fa\u73fe\u5169\u4efd\u4e92\u76f8\u77db\u76fe\u7684\u8349\u7a3f\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n    reply = thread_id is not None\n    body = f\"{REDISTILL_PREFIX}\\n\\n{markdown}\" if reply else markdown\n    content = f\"{KNOWLEDGE_MARKER}\\n{body}\"\n    target = (f\"{ref.pr_api}/threads/{thread_id}/comments\" if reply\n              else f\"{ref.pr_api}/threads\")\n    if not settings().posting.knowledge_post:\n        _audit(\"knowledge\", pr_url, False, \"KNOWLEDGE_POST=false\uff0c\u5f71\u5b50\u6a21\u5f0f\")\n        return {\"posted\": False, \"dry_run\": True, \"reply\": reply,\n                \"thread_id\": thread_id, \"would_post_to\": target,\n                \"preview\": content[:500]}\n    with client() as c:\n        if reply:\n            r = c.post(target, params={\"api-version\": \"7.1\"},\n                       json={\"content\": content, \"commentType\": 1})\n            r.raise_for_status()\n            _audit(\"knowledge\", pr_url, True, f\"reply in thread {thread_id}\")\n            return {\"posted\": True, \"dry_run\": False, \"reply\": True,\n                    \"thread_id\": thread_id}\n        thread = _new_thread(c, ref, content)\n    _audit(\"knowledge\", pr_url, True, f\"thread {thread.get('id')}\")\n    return {\"posted\": True, \"dry_run\": False, \"reply\": False,\n            \"thread_id\": thread.get(\"id\")}\n\n\ndef get_past_reviews(pr_url: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u9019\u689d PR \u4e0a\u300c\u672c bot \u767c\u904e\u300d\u7684\u6b77\u53f2\u8a55\u8ad6\uff08\u9760\u96b1\u5f62\u6d6e\u6c34\u5370\u904e\u6ffe\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n    with client() as c:\n        threads = get_json(c, f\"{ref.pr_api}/threads\")[\"value\"]\n    out: list[str] = []\n    for t in threads:\n        for cm in t.get(\"comments\", []):\n            body = cm.get(\"content\") or \"\"\n            if MARKER in body:\n                out.append(body.replace(MARKER, \"\").strip())\n    return out\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/anatomy.py","perm":"0644","sha":"2fc17b22bf1b7a2d8f045d238e2064d7c37a30bd4e3747b4c784703ea8feb8c0","data":"\"\"\"anatomy\uff08v2 \u7b2c 0 \u6bb5\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u7d14 code \u7684 diff \u89e3\u5256\uff0c\u96f6 LLM\u3002\n\n\u628a unified diff \u89e3\u6790\u6210\u7d50\u69cb\uff1a\u6bcf\u6a94\u7684 hunks\u3001\u65b0\u6a94\u884c\u865f\u5c0d\u7167\u8868\u3001\u7d71\u8a08\u3002\n\u5169\u500b\u4e0b\u6e38\u5403\u5b83\uff1astatic pass \u7528\u300c\u7a00\u758f\u91cd\u5efa\u300d\u8b93\u6383\u63cf\u5668\u62ff\u5230\u6b63\u78ba\u884c\u865f\uff1b\nreviewer \u7528\u300c\u884c\u865f\u6a19\u8a3b\u7684 diff \u5207\u7247\u300d\u8b93\u6a21\u578b\u5831\u884c\u865f\u5831\u5f97\u6e96\u3002\n\n\u5bb9\u932f\uff1a\u2460 \u7522\u7684 diff \u593e\u96dc `# xxx: \u6a94\u6848\u904e\u5927\uff0c\u7565\u904e` \u9019\u985e\u8a3b\u8a18\u884c\uff0c\u89e3\u6790\u5668\u4e00\u5f8b\u8df3\u904e\u3002\n\n\u53e6\u5916\u4f4f\u8457\u4e09\u500b\u300cdiff \u5e7e\u4f55 predicates\u300d\u2014\u2014match_path / line_in_view / line_near\u3002\n\u5b83\u5011\u662f\u7d14\u5e7e\u4f55\u3001\u96f6\u696d\u52d9\u8a9e\u610f\uff0c\u51e1\u662f\u8981\u9a57\u300c\u6a21\u578b\u5831\u7684 file:line \u662f\u4e0d\u662f\u771f\u7684\u5728\u9019\u4efd diff\n\u88e1\u300d\u7684\u5730\u65b9\uff08pipeline \u7684 adversary\u3001knowledge \u7684 evidence \u9a57\u8b49\u5668\uff09\u90fd\u5403\u9019\u4e00\u4efd\uff0c\n\u4ee5\u514d\u540c\u4e00\u500b\u5224\u65b7\u5728\u5169\u500b\u6a21\u7d44\u5404\u9577\u4e00\u7248\u7136\u5f8c\u6f02\u79fb\u3002\u653e\u5728\u6700\u5e95\u5c64\u4e5f\u8b93 knowledge \u4e0d\u5fc5\u53cd\u5411\nimport pipeline\uff08\u90a3\u6703\u6210\u74b0\uff09\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\n_FILE_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\+\\+\\+ b(?P<path>/.*)$\")\n_OLD_RE = re.compile(r\"^--- (?:a(?P<path>/.*)|/dev/null)$\")\n_HUNK_RE = re.compile(r\"^@@ -(\\d+)(?:,(\\d+))? \\+(\\d+)(?:,(\\d+))? @@\")\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Hunk:\n    old_start: int\n    old_count: int\n    new_start: int\n    new_count: int\n    # (tag, new_lineno|None, text)\uff1btag \u2208 {\"+\", \"-\", \" \"}\uff1b\"-\" \u884c\u6c92\u6709\u65b0\u884c\u865f\n    lines: list[tuple[str, int | None, str]] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass FileChange:\n    path: str                      # \u65b0\u6a94\u8def\u5f91\uff08\u7167 diff \u539f\u6a23\uff0c\u901a\u5e38\u4ee5 / \u958b\u982d\uff09\n    hunks: list[Hunk] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n    @property\n    def added(self) -> list[tuple[int, str]]:\n        \"\"\"\u6240\u6709\u65b0\u589e\u884c\uff1a(\u65b0\u6a94\u884c\u865f, \u5167\u5bb9)\u3002\"\"\"\n        return [(n, t) for h in self.hunks for tag, n, t in h.lines\n                if tag == \"+\" and n is not None]\n\n    @property\n    def added_linenos(self) -> set[int]:\n        return {n for n, _ in self.added}\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Anatomy:\n    files: list[FileChange] = field(default_factory=list)\n    skipped_notes: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)  # \u904e\u5927/\u4e8c\u9032\u4f4d\u7b49\u8a3b\u8a18\n\n    @property\n    def stats(self) -> dict:\n        return {\n            \"files\": len(self.files),\n            \"added_lines\": sum(len(f.added) for f in self.files),\n            \"hunks\": sum(len(f.hunks) for f in self.files),\n            \"skipped\": len(self.skipped_notes),\n        }\n\n\ndef parse_diff(diff: str) -> Anatomy:\n    ana = Anatomy()\n    cur: FileChange | None = None\n    hunk: Hunk | None = None\n    new_no = old_no = 0\n\n    for raw in diff.splitlines():\n        if raw.startswith((\"diff --git \", \"index \", \"new file mode\",\n                           \"deleted file mode\", \"similarity index\",\n                           \"rename from\", \"rename to\", \"old mode\",\n                           \"new mode\", \"Binary files \")):\n            hunk = None                              # git \u982d\u884c\uff1a\u6a94\u6848\u5206\u9694\uff0c\u975e\u5167\u5bb9\n            continue\n        if raw.startswith(\"# \"):                    # \u2460 \u7684\u8a3b\u8a18\u884c\n            ana.skipped_notes.append(raw[2:].strip())\n            hunk = None\n            continue\n        m = _FILE_RE.match(raw)\n        if m:\n            cur = FileChange(path=m.group(\"path\"))\n            ana.files.append(cur)\n            hunk = None\n            continue\n        if _OLD_RE.match(raw) or raw.startswith(\"\\\\ No newline\"):\n            continue\n        m = _HUNK_RE.match(raw)\n        if m and cur is not None:\n            old_no = int(m.group(1))\n            new_no = int(m.group(3))\n            hunk = Hunk(old_start=old_no, old_count=int(m.group(2) or 1),\n                        new_start=new_no, new_count=int(m.group(4) or 1))\n            cur.hunks.append(hunk)\n            continue\n        if hunk is None or cur is None:\n            continue\n        if raw.startswith(\"+\"):\n            hunk.lines.append((\"+\", new_no, raw[1:]))\n            new_no += 1\n        elif raw.startswith(\"-\"):\n            hunk.lines.append((\"-\", None, raw[1:]))\n            old_no += 1\n        else:                                        # context\uff08\u542b\u7a7a\u884c\uff09\n            text = raw[1:] if raw.startswith(\" \") else raw\n            hunk.lines.append((\" \", new_no, text))\n            new_no += 1\n            old_no += 1\n    return ana\n\n\ndef sparse_new_file(fc: FileChange) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u628a\u300c\u65b0\u6a94\u7684\u5df2\u77e5\u5167\u5bb9\u300d\u653e\u56de\u6b63\u78ba\u884c\u865f\u3001\u5176\u9918\u88dc\u7a7a\u884c \u2014\u2014 \u6383\u63cf\u5668\u56e0\u6b64\u56de\u5831\u771f\u884c\u865f\u3002\"\"\"\n    known: dict[int, str] = {n: t for h in fc.hunks\n                             for tag, n, t in h.lines\n                             if tag in (\"+\", \" \") and n is not None}\n    if not known:\n        return \"\"\n    top = max(known)\n    return \"\\n\".join(known.get(i, \"\") for i in range(1, top + 1)) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef numbered_slice(fc: FileChange, max_chars: int = 6000) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u884c\u865f\u6a19\u8a3b\u7684 diff \u5207\u7247\uff08\u9935 reviewer\uff09\uff1a+/context \u884c\u524d\u7db4\u65b0\u6a94\u884c\u865f\uff0c- \u884c\u4e0d\u6a19\u3002\"\"\"\n    out = [f\"### {fc.path}\"]\n    for h in fc.hunks:\n        out.append(f\"@@ -{h.old_start},{h.old_count} +{h.new_start},{h.new_count} @@\")\n        for tag, n, t in h.lines:\n            prefix = f\"{n:>5} {tag}\" if n is not None else \"      -\"\n            out.append(f\"{prefix} {t}\")\n    text = \"\\n\".join(out)\n    return text[:max_chars] + (\"\\n\u2026\uff08\u5207\u7247\u622a\u65b7\uff09\" if len(text) > max_chars else \"\")\n\n\n# ---------- diff \u5e7e\u4f55 predicates\uff08\u4e0b\u6e38\u5171\u7528\uff1apipeline / knowledge\uff09 ----------\n\ndef _norm(p: str) -> str:\n    p = (p or \"\").strip().lstrip(\"/\")\n    if p[:2] in (\"a/\", \"b/\"):\n        p = p[2:]\n    return p.lower()\n\n\ndef match_path(a: str, b: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\u8def\u5f91\u5f8c\u7db4\u76f8\u7b49\uff0c\u4f46\u53ea\u5728\u8def\u5f91\u6bb5\u908a\u754c\u6210\u7acb\uff08Cache.java \u4e0d\u7b97 SessionCache.java\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    na, nb = _norm(a), _norm(b)\n    if not na or not nb:\n        return False\n    return na == nb or na.endswith(\"/\" + nb) or nb.endswith(\"/\" + na)\n\n\ndef line_in_view(ana: Anatomy, file: str, line, tol: int = 2) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"line \u843d\u5728\u8a72\u6a94\u300e\u5207\u7247\u53ef\u898b\u884c\u300f\uff08added \u222a context\uff09\u00b1tol \u5167\u3002\n    challenge #1\uff08pre-existence\uff09\u7684\u8b49\u64da\u672c\u4f86\u5c31\u5728 context \u884c\uff0c\u53ea\u8a8d added \u6703\u8aa4\u50b7\u3002\"\"\"\n    try:\n        line = int(line)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return False\n    for fc in ana.files:\n        if match_path(fc.path, file):\n            visible = {n for h in fc.hunks for tag, n, _ in h.lines\n                       if n is not None}\n            return bool(visible) and any(abs(line - n) <= tol for n in visible)\n    return False\n\n\ndef line_near(ana: Anatomy, file: str, line, tol: int = 2) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\u884c\u865f\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u9a57\u8b49\uff1aline \u5fc5\u9808\u843d\u5728\u8a72\u6a94\u300e\u65b0\u589e\u884c\u300f\u96c6\u5408\u7684 \u00b1tol \u5167\u3002\"\"\"\n    try:\n        line = int(line)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return False\n    for fc in ana.files:\n        if match_path(fc.path, file):\n            added = fc.added_linenos\n            return bool(added) and any(abs(line - n) <= tol for n in added)\n    return False\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/app.py","perm":"0644","sha":"0ef4138ba870cc7b2faaa5ff25a18a8a5968a5b0dd02e130e3d63978485ff0c6","data":"\"\"\"review-orchestrator \u2014\u2014 \u552f\u4e00\u7684\u5927\u8166\u3001\u552f\u4e00\u63a5 Langfuse \u7684\u670d\u52d9\u3002\n\n\u6a94\u4f4d\u4e00\uff08\u72c0\u614b\u65c1\u767d\u4e32\u6d41\uff09\uff1a/v1/chat/completions \u5728 stream=true \u6642\uff0c\n\u4e00\u908a\u57f7\u884c pipeline \u4e00\u908a\u628a\u9032\u5ea6\u65c1\u767d\u5373\u6642\u5410\u7d66\u804a\u5929\u5ba4\uff08\ud83d\udd0d \u89e3\u6790 \u2192 \ud83d\udccb metadata \u2192\n\ud83d\udcc4 diff \u2192 \ud83e\udd16 review\uff09\uff0c\u6700\u5f8c\u4e32\u51fa markdown \u2014\u2014 \u4f7f\u7528\u8005\u770b\u76f4\u64ad\uff0c\u4e0d\u518d\u76ef\u9ed1\u7bb1\u3002\n\u8ffd\u8e64\u7d50\u69cb\u4e0d\u8b8a\uff1ahandle_review \u4ecd\u662f @observe \u7684\u6700\u5916\u5c64\uff0c\u65c1\u767d\u53ea\u662f\u65c1\u8def\u3002\n\n\u555f\u52d5\uff1auvicorn orchestrator.app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport time\nimport uuid\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom typing import AsyncIterator, Awaitable, Callable, Optional\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Header, HTTPException, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import StreamingResponse\nfrom langfuse import get_client, observe, propagate_attributes\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nfrom orchestrator import clients\nfrom orchestrator.core import run_review\nfrom orchestrator.models import ReviewResult\nfrom orchestrator import console, jobs, knowledge, progress, store\nfrom shared.azdo import find_pr_url\nfrom shared.settings import fail_fast, settings\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def _lifespan(_app: FastAPI):\n    fail_fast()          # \u8a2d\u5b9a\u58de\u503c\u5728\u555f\u52d5\u5c31\u5831\uff0c\u4e0d\u7b49\u7b2c\u4e00\u689d review\n    for st in jobs.start():\n        print(f\"[jobs] {st.name}: \" + (f\"\u6bcf {st.interval_min} \u5206\" if st.enabled else \"off\"))\n    try:\n        yield\n    finally:\n        jobs.stop()\n\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"review-orchestrator\", lifespan=_lifespan)\nconsole.mount(app)          # /console/*\uff1a\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\uff08S2 \u8d77\uff09\n\nMODEL_ID = \"pr-reviewer\"\nHELP_TEXT = (\n    \"\u628a Azure DevOps \u7684 PR \u9023\u7d50\u8cbc\u7d66\u6211\uff08\u5f62\u5982 https://.../_git/<repo>/pullrequest/<id>\uff09\uff0c\"\n    \"\u6211\u6703\u6293 diff \u505a code review\u3002\"\n)\n\n# ---- \u5143\u4efb\u52d9\u76fe + \u53bb\u91cd\u5feb\u53d6\uff08\u9632 Open WebUI \u7684 title/tags/follow-up \u5077\u8dd1 pipeline\uff09----\n\n_META_MARKERS = (\n    \"### task:\", \"generate a concise\", \"3-5 word title\", \"concise title\",\n    \"generate 1-3 broad tags\", \"categorizing the main themes\", \"broad tags\",\n    \"follow-up\", \"suggest 3\", \"emoji\",\n)\n\ndef _is_meta_task(body: dict, last_text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Open WebUI \u7684\u5143\u4efb\u52d9\uff08\u6a19\u984c/\u6a19\u7c64/\u8ffd\u554f\u751f\u6210\uff09\u8fa8\u8b58\uff1a\n    \u65b0\u7248\u6703\u5e36 metadata.task \u6b04\u4f4d\uff1b\u820a\u7248\u9760\u6a21\u677f\u5b57\u6a23\u3002\u547d\u4e2d\u5c31\u4e0d\u9032 review pipeline\u3002\"\"\"\n    task = ((body.get(\"metadata\") or {}).get(\"task\")\n            or body.get(\"task\") or \"\")\n    if task:\n        return True\n    low = last_text.lower()\n    return any(m in low for m in _META_MARKERS)\n\n\n_RECENT: dict[str, tuple[float, str]] = {}   # pr_url -> (\u6642\u9593\u6233, markdown)\n\n\ndef _ttl() -> float:\n    return settings().orchestrator.dedupe_ttl\n\n\ndef _cache_get(pr_url: str, source_commit: str = \"\") -> str | None:\n    hit = _RECENT.get(pr_url)\n    if hit and (time.time() - hit[0]) < _ttl():\n        cached_commit = hit[2] if len(hit) > 2 else \"\"\n        if source_commit and cached_commit and source_commit != cached_commit:\n            return None                    # push \u4e86\u65b0 commit \u2192 \u820a review \u4f5c\u5ee2\n        return hit[1]\n    return None\n\ndef _cache_put(pr_url: str, markdown: str, source_commit: str = \"\") -> None:\n    _RECENT[pr_url] = (time.time(), markdown, source_commit)\n    if len(_RECENT) > 200:   # \u7c97\u7cd9\u4f46\u5920\u7528\u7684\u6e05\u7406\n        cutoff = time.time() - _ttl()\n        for k in [k for k, (t, *_rest) in _RECENT.items() if t < cutoff]:\n            _RECENT.pop(k, None)\n\nStatusCb = Optional[Callable[[str], Awaitable[None]]]\n\n_BG_TASKS: set = set()          # F5\uff1aevent loop \u53ea\u6301\u5f31\u5f15\u7528\uff0c\u5f37\u5f15\u7528\u6536\u5728\u9019\n\n\ndef _bg(coro) -> None:\n    t = asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task(coro)\n    _BG_TASKS.add(t)\n    t.add_done_callback(_BG_TASKS.discard)\n\n\n_EVAL_BUSY = {\"flag\": False}    # eval-webhook \u4f75\u767c\u9396\uff08\u9632\u9023\u9ede\u758a\u8003\uff09\n\n\ndef _check_auth(authorization: str | None):\n    \"\"\"\u8a2d\u5b9a ORCH_API_KEY \u6642\u624d\u9a57\uff1b\u6c92\u8a2d\u5c31\u958b\u653e\uff08\u5167\u7db2 POC \u6a21\u5f0f\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    want = settings().orchestrator.api_key.get_secret_value()\n    if not want:\n        return\n    got = (authorization or \"\").removeprefix(\"Bearer \").strip()\n    if got != want:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=401, detail=\"invalid api key\")\n\n\n@observe(name=\"pr-review\")\nasync def handle_review(pr_url: str, user: str,\n                        on_status: StatusCb = None) -> ReviewResult:\n    \"\"\"\u4e00\u689d PR review \u7684\u5b8c\u6574\u904e\u7a0b \u2014\u2014 trace \u7684\u6700\u5916\u5c64\u3002\n\n    on_status\uff1a\u65c1\u767d\u56de\u547c\uff08SSE \u76f4\u64ad\u7528\uff09\uff1b\u4e0d\u7d66\u5c31\u662f\u539f\u672c\u7684\u5b89\u975c\u6a21\u5f0f\uff08/review \u7528\uff09\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    async def note(msg: str):\n        if on_status:\n            await on_status(msg)\n\n    token = progress.set_status_cb(on_status)  # v2 pipeline \u5404\u7ad9\u65c1\u767d\u7531\u6b64\u64ad\u51fa\n    rid = store.start_review(pr_url, user)       # \u6b77\u53f2\uff08SQLite\uff09\uff1bstore \u505c\u7528\u6642\u662f None\n    try:\n        result = await _handle_review_inner(pr_url, user, note, rid)\n    except Exception as e:\n        store.fail_review(rid, f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\")\n        raise\n    finally:\n        progress.reset_status_cb(token)\n    try:\n        trace_id = get_client().get_current_trace_id()\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        trace_id = None\n    store.finish_review(rid, result, trace_id)\n    return result\n\n\nasync def _handle_review_inner(pr_url: str, user: str, note,\n                               rid: int | None = None) -> ReviewResult:\n    with propagate_attributes(session_id=pr_url, user_id=user, tags=[\"live\"]):\n        await note(\"Resolving pull request URL\")\n        metadata = await clients.fetch_pr_metadata(pr_url)\n        title = (metadata or {}).get(\"title\", \"\")[:50]\n        store.set_title(rid, (metadata or {}).get(\"title\", \"\"))\n        await note(f\"PR located \u2014 \\\"{title}\\\"; fetching diff\")\n\n        diff = await clients.fetch_pr_diff(pr_url)\n        n_files = len(re.findall(r\"^\\+\\+\\+ b\", diff, re.M))\n        await note(f\"Diff retrieved \u2014 {n_files} file(s), {len(diff)} characters; running review pipeline\")\n\n        result = await run_review(diff, metadata)\n\n        if settings().orchestrator.auto_post:\n            await clients.post_review_comment(pr_url, result.markdown)\n            await note(\"Review comment posted to the PR (subject to the results service DRY_RUN setting)\")\n\n        # K \u6bb5\uff1a\u975e\u540c\u6b65\u84b8\u993e + \u8cbc\u7a3f + _pending \u2014\u2014 \u4e0d\u64cb\u4f7f\u7528\u8005\u3001\u5931\u6557\u53ea\u9032 journal\n        try:\n            files = [r[\"path\"] for r in (result.stats.get(\"file_table\") or [])]\n            # reviewer \u770b\u7684\u662f\u9019\u4efd diff\u3001\u5831\u544a\u88e1\u7684\u7de8\u865f\u662f F1..Fn\uff08render \u7684\u9806\u5e8f\uff09\u2014\u2014\n            # \u84b8\u993e\u5403\u540c\u4e00\u4efd\uff0c\u8b49\u64da\u624d\u9a57\u5f97\u52d5\uff1b\u4e0d\u53e6\u9020 diff \u8868\u793a\u3001\u4e0d\u91cd parse markdown\n            finding_ids = {f\"F{i}\" for i in range(1, len(result.findings) + 1)}\n            finding_files = [f.file for f in result.findings if f.file]\n            # \u77db\u76fe\u5075\u6e2c\uff08\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\uff09\uff1a\u5831\u544a\u88e1\u300c\u8e29\u5230\u65e2\u6709\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u300d\u7684 finding \u5f15\u4e86\u54ea\u4e9b id\u3002\n            # \u9019\u6279 id \u4e4b\u5f8c\u6703\u8ddf\u8457\u7a3f\u8d70\uff1aPR \u82e5\u5e36\u8457\u77db\u76fe\u5b8c\u6210\uff0c\u4ee3\u8868\u5be6\u4f5c\u63a8\u7ffb\u4e86\u898f\u5247\uff0c\n            # \u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u8981\u70ba\u5b83\u505a\u4e00\u6b21\u88c1\u6c7a\uff08\u898b knowledge_harvest \u7684 contradiction \u6bb5\uff09\u3002\n            contradicted = {ref for f in result.findings\n                            if f.severity in (\"error\", \"warning\")\n                            for ref in (f.knowledge_ref or [])}\n            _bg(knowledge.distill_and_stage(\n                pr_url, metadata, files, result.markdown,\n                list(result.stats.get(\"graph_impacted\") or []),\n                diff=diff, finding_ids=finding_ids,\n                finding_files=finding_files, contradicted=contradicted))\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"[knowledge] \u6392\u7a0b\u5931\u6557\uff1a{e}\")\n\n        return result\n\n\n# ---------- OpenAI \u76f8\u5bb9\u5c64\uff08Open WebUI \u7528\uff09 ----------\n\n@app.get(\"/v1/models\")\nasync def models(authorization: str | None = Header(default=None)):\n    _check_auth(authorization)\n    return {\"object\": \"list\",\n            \"data\": [{\"id\": MODEL_ID, \"object\": \"model\", \"owned_by\": \"pr-review-suite\"}]}\n\n\ndef _delta(rid: str, **delta) -> str:\n    payload = {\"id\": f\"chatcmpl-{rid}\", \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n               \"created\": int(time.time()), \"model\": MODEL_ID,\n               \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": delta, \"finish_reason\": None}]}\n    return f\"data: {json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False)}\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef _finish(rid: str) -> str:\n    payload = {\"id\": f\"chatcmpl-{rid}\", \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n               \"created\": int(time.time()), \"model\": MODEL_ID,\n               \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": {}, \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}]}\n    return f\"data: {json.dumps(payload)}\\n\\ndata: [DONE]\\n\\n\"\n\n\nasync def _stream_text(rid: str, text: str,\n                       chunk: int = 800) -> AsyncIterator[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u975c\u614b\u6587\u5b57\uff08help / \u932f\u8aa4\uff09\u4e5f\u8d70 SSE\u3002\"\"\"\n    yield _delta(rid, role=\"assistant\")\n    for i in range(0, len(text), chunk):\n        yield _delta(rid, content=text[i:i + chunk])\n    yield _finish(rid)\n\n\nasync def _stream_review(rid: str, pr_url: str, user: str,\n                         commit_hint: str = \"\") -> AsyncIterator[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u6a94\u4f4d\u4e00\u7684\u5fc3\u81df\uff1aqueue \u76f4\u64ad \u2014\u2014 pipeline \u6bcf\u904e\u4e00\u7ad9\u5c31\u5410\u4e00\u884c\u65c1\u767d\u3002\"\"\"\n    q: asyncio.Queue[tuple[str, str] | None] = asyncio.Queue()\n\n    async def on_status(msg: str):\n        await q.put((\"status\", msg))\n\n    async def runner():\n        try:\n            result = await handle_review(pr_url, user, on_status=on_status)\n            _cache_put(pr_url, result.markdown, commit_hint)\n            await q.put((\"result\", result.markdown))\n        except Exception as e:  # \u4e32\u6d41\u5df2\u958b\u5834\uff0c\u4e0d\u80fd\u518d\u56de 500 \u2014\u2014 \u628a\u932f\u8aa4\u6f14\u51fa\u4f86\n            await q.put((\"error\",\n                         f\"\u274c review \u5931\u6557\uff1a{type(e).__name__}: {e}\\n\"\n                         f\"\uff08\u7d30\u7bc0\u898b\u4f3a\u670d\u5668 journalctl -u review-orchestrator\uff09\"))\n            raise  # \u8b93 traceback \u7167\u5e38\u9032 journal\n        finally:\n            await q.put(None)\n\n    task = asyncio.create_task(runner())\n    yield _delta(rid, role=\"assistant\")\n    try:\n        while True:\n            item = await q.get()\n            if item is None:\n                break\n            kind, text = item\n            if kind == \"status\":\n                yield _delta(rid, content=text + \"\\n\\n\")\n            elif kind == \"result\":\n                yield _delta(rid, content=\"---\\n\\n\")\n                for i in range(0, len(text), 800):\n                    yield _delta(rid, content=text[i:i + 800])\n            else:  # error\n                yield _delta(rid, content=text)\n    finally:\n        task.cancel()  # client \u65b7\u7dda\u6642\u5225\u8b93 runner \u8b8a\u5b64\u5152\n    yield _finish(rid)\n\n\n@app.post(\"/v1/chat/completions\")\nasync def chat_completions(\n    request: Request,\n    authorization: str | None = Header(default=None),\n    x_openwebui_user_email: str | None = Header(default=None),\n    x_openwebui_user_name: str | None = Header(default=None),\n):\n    _check_auth(authorization)\n    body = await request.json()\n    user = x_openwebui_user_email or x_openwebui_user_name or \"anonymous\"\n\n    last_user_msg = \"\"\n    for m in reversed(body.get(\"messages\", [])):\n        if m.get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n            c = m.get(\"content\", \"\")\n            last_user_msg = c if isinstance(c, str) else json.dumps(c, ensure_ascii=False)\n            break\n\n    pr_url = find_pr_url(last_user_msg)\n    rid = uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]\n    stream = bool(body.get(\"stream\"))\n\n    def _reply(text: str):\n        \"\"\"\u975c\u614b\u6587\u5b57\u56de\u8986\uff08\u76fe\u724c\u8207 help \u5171\u7528\uff09\uff0c\u4e32\u6d41/\u975e\u4e32\u6d41\u90fd\u5403\u3002\"\"\"\n        if stream:\n            return StreamingResponse(_stream_text(rid, text),\n                                     media_type=\"text/event-stream\")\n        return {\n            \"id\": f\"chatcmpl-{rid}\", \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n            \"created\": int(time.time()), \"model\": MODEL_ID,\n            \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n                         \"message\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": text}}],\n            \"usage\": {\"prompt_tokens\": 0, \"completion_tokens\": 0,\n                      \"total_tokens\": 0},\n        }\n\n    # \u76fe\u4e00\uff1a\u5143\u4efb\u52d9\uff08title/tags/follow-up\uff09\u7d66\u975c\u614b\u77ed\u7b54\uff0c\u7d55\u4e0d\u9032 pipeline\n    if _is_meta_task(body, last_user_msg):\n        return _reply(f\"PR Review {pr_url.rsplit('/', 1)[-1]}\" if pr_url else \"PR Review\")\n\n    # \u76fe\u4e8c\uff1a\u540c\u4e00\u689d PR \u5728 TTL \u5167\u91cd\u8907\u89f8\u767c \u2192 \u91cd\u64ad\u5feb\u53d6\uff0c\u4e0d\u518d\u71d2\u4e00\u8f2a\n    commit_hint = \"\"\n    if pr_url:\n        try:\n            commit_hint = (await clients.fetch_pr_metadata(pr_url)) \\\n                .get(\"source_commit\") or \"\"\n        except Exception:\n            pass                            # metadata \u5931\u6557 \u2192 \u7167\u820a TTL \u8a9e\u610f\n    if pr_url and (cached := _cache_get(pr_url, commit_hint)) is not None:\n        return _reply(cached)\n\n    if not pr_url:\n        return _reply(HELP_TEXT)\n\n    if stream:\n        return StreamingResponse(_stream_review(rid, pr_url, user,\n                                                commit_hint),\n                                 media_type=\"text/event-stream\")\n\n    result = await handle_review(pr_url, user)\n    _cache_put(pr_url, result.markdown, commit_hint)\n    return _reply(result.markdown)\n\n\n# ---------- \u8173\u672c / CI \u7528\u7684\u4e7e\u6de8\u4ecb\u9762 ----------\n\nclass ReviewRequest(BaseModel):\n    pr_url: str\n    user: str = \"api\"\n\n\n@app.post(\"/review\")\nasync def review(req: ReviewRequest,\n                 authorization: str | None = Header(default=None)):\n    _check_auth(authorization)\n    result = await handle_review(req.pr_url, req.user)\n    return {\"pr_url\": req.pr_url,\n            \"markdown\": result.markdown,\n            \"findings\": result.findings_summary()}\n\n\nclass RedistillRequest(BaseModel):\n    pr_url: str\n\n\n@app.post(\"/knowledge/redistill\", status_code=202)\nasync def knowledge_redistill(req: RedistillRequest,\n                              authorization: str | None = Header(default=None)):\n    \"\"\"stale \u88dc\u6551\uff1aharvester \u5075\u6e2c\u5230\u300cdraft \u4e4b\u5f8c\u53c8\u6709 push\u300d\u6642\u6253\u9019\u88e1\u3002\n\n    harvester \u53ea\u5075\u6e2c\uff0c\u84b8\u993e\u9019\u4ef6\u4e8b\u6574\u500b\u7559\u5728 orchestrator\uff08`_land` \u4ecd\u7136\u96f6 LLM\uff0c\n    \u4e0d\u628a\u534a\u500b orchestrator \u642c\u9032\u6536\u5272\u5668\uff09\u3002\u9019\u689d\u7aef\u9ede\u6709 LLM \u82b1\u8cbb\u8207\u5beb\u6a94\u8a9e\u610f\uff0c\n    \u4e0d\u662f\u7d14\u8b80\u2014\u2014\u6240\u4ee5\u7167 `_check_auth` \u8d70\uff1b\u90e8\u7f72\u6642\u52d9\u5fc5\u628a ORCH_API_KEY \u8a2d\u8d77\u4f86\u3002\n    \u6536\u5230\u5373\u56de 202\u3001\u80cc\u666f\u57f7\u884c\uff1b\u91cd\u8a66\u4e0a\u9650\u7531 harvester \u7684\u8acb\u6c42\u6233\u5b88\uff08\u2264 2 \u6b21\uff09\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    _check_auth(authorization)\n    if not knowledge.redistill_enabled():\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"pr_url\": req.pr_url,\n                \"note\": \"KNOWLEDGE_REDISTILL=false \u2014\u2014 \u91cd\u84b8\u95dc\u9589\"}\n    _bg(knowledge.redistill(req.pr_url))\n    return {\"ok\": True, \"pr_url\": req.pr_url,\n            \"note\": \"\u91cd\u84b8\u5df2\u5728\u80cc\u666f\u958b\u8dd1\uff1b\u7d50\u679c\u8986\u5beb _pending\uff0c\u770b journal\"}\n\n\n# ---------- Langfuse UI\u300cCustom Experiment\u300d\u6309\u9215\u7684\u843d\u9ede ----------\n\n@app.post(\"/eval-webhook\")\nasync def eval_webhook(request: Request):\n    \"\"\"Langfuse Remote Experiment webhook\uff1a\u6536\u5230\u5373\u56de\u3001\u80cc\u666f\u958b\u8003\u3002\n\n    Langfuse \u53ea\u7b49 10 \u79d2\uff0c\u6240\u4ee5\u9019\u88e1\u7528 subprocess \u4e1f\u80cc\u666f\u8dd1 run_eval\uff0c\n    \u5206\u6578\u7531 run_eval \u81ea\u5df1\u56de\u5beb\u6210\u65b0\u7684 dataset run\u3002\u6ce8\u610f\uff1a\u6b64\u7aef\u9ede\u523b\u610f\u4e0d\u8d70\n    ORCH_API_KEY\uff08Langfuse \u89f8\u767c\u6642\u7121\u6cd5\u5e36\u81ea\u8a02 Authorization\uff09\uff0c\u5167\u7db2\u74b0\u5883\n    \u53ef\u63a5\u53d7\uff1b\u8981\u66f4\u56b4\u5c31\u5728 Langfuse \u8a2d\u5b9a\u88e1\u958b HMAC \u7c3d\u7ae0\u518d\u65bc\u6b64\u9a57\u8b49\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    import sys\n    from pathlib import Path\n\n    try:\n        body = await request.json()\n    except Exception:\n        body = {}\n    cfg = {}\n    for key in (\"config\", \"payload\"):\n        if isinstance(body.get(key), dict):\n            cfg.update(body[key])\n    q = request.query_params\n    # pipeline \u53ef\u7531 query\uff08?pipeline=v2\uff09\u6216 body \u6307\u5b9a\uff1b\u9810\u8a2d\u8ddf\u670d\u52d9 env \u8d70\u3002\n    # \u5728 Langfuse \u5b58\u5169\u500b Remote Experiment \u8a2d\u5b9a\uff08v1 / v2 \u5404\u4e00\uff09= UI \u4e00\u9375 A/B\u3002\n    pipeline = (q.get(\"pipeline\") or cfg.get(\"pipeline\")\n                or settings().orchestrator.pipeline).strip().lower()\n    if pipeline not in (\"v1\", \"v2\"):\n        pipeline = \"v1\"\n    run_name = (q.get(\"run_name\") or cfg.get(\"run_name\")\n                or f\"ui-{pipeline}-{time.strftime('%m%d-%H%M%S')}\")\n\n    if _EVAL_BUSY[\"flag\"]:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=409,\n                            detail=\"\u4e0a\u4e00\u8f2a eval \u9084\u5728\u8dd1\uff08\u4f75\u767c\u9396\uff09\uff1b\u7b49\u5b83\u6536\u5c3e\u518d\u89f8\u767c\")\n    _EVAL_BUSY[\"flag\"] = True\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    env[\"REVIEW_PIPELINE\"] = pipeline\n    proc = await asyncio.create_subprocess_exec(\n        sys.executable, \"-m\", \"eval.run_eval\", run_name,\n        cwd=str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]),\n        env=env,\n    )\n    async def _reap():\n        try:\n            await proc.wait()\n        finally:\n            _EVAL_BUSY[\"flag\"] = False\n    _bg(_reap())                       # \u6536\u5c4d + \u91cb\u653e\u4f75\u767c\u9396\uff08\u5f37\u5f15\u7528\u9632 GC\uff09\n    return {\"ok\": True, \"run_name\": run_name, \"pipeline\": pipeline,\n            \"note\": \"eval \u5df2\u5728\u80cc\u666f\u958b\u8dd1\uff0c\u7a0d\u5f8c\u5230 Datasets \u2192 Runs \u770b\u5206\u6578\"}\n\n\n@app.get(\"/healthz\")\nasync def healthz():\n    return {\"ok\": True, \"pipeline\": settings().orchestrator.pipeline,\n            \"jobs\": jobs.snapshot()}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/clients.py","perm":"0644","sha":"0a2009962139a71e18e1d58084a35f08b227ec153b1e0924d1cc356c9e5cc988","data":"\"\"\"Orchestrator \u5c0d\u5916\u90e8\u7cfb\u7d71\u7684\u547c\u53eb\u5c64\u3002\n\nS1 \u8d77 Azure DevOps \u7684\u8b80\u5beb\u662f\u884c\u7a0b\u5167\u7684\u51fd\u5f0f\uff08orchestrator/adapters/ado.py\uff09\uff0c\n\u9019\u88e1\u53ea\u8ca0\u8cac\u5169\u4ef6\u4e8b\uff1a(1) \u7528 asyncio.to_thread \u628a\u540c\u6b65\u7684 httpx \u547c\u53eb\u79fb\u51fa event loop\n\uff08\u6293\u767e\u6a94 diff \u662f\u79d2\u5230\u5206\u9418\u7d1a\uff0c\u4e0d\u80fd\u5361\u4f4f SSE \u65c1\u767d\uff09\uff1b(2) \u758a @observe\uff0c\u7011\u5e03\u5716\u88e1\n\u300c\u6293 diff \u82b1\u591a\u4e45\u3001\u767c\u8a55\u8ad6\u6210\u4e0d\u6210\u529f\u300d\u5404\u81ea\u6210\u5c64\u3002\n\n\u51fd\u5f0f\u540d\u8207\u7c3d\u540d\u8ddf \u2460\u2461\u2462 \u6642\u4ee3\u4e00\u6a21\u4e00\u6a23\uff1apipeline / knowledge / app \u4e00\u884c\u6c92\u6539\uff0c\ntests \u7684 monkeypatch \u4e5f\u7167\u820a\u3002\n\n\u2463 code graph \u4ecd\u662f\u5916\u90e8\u884c\u7a0b\uff08code-review-graph serve --http\uff09\uff0c\u8d70 fastmcp Client\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\n\nfrom langfuse import observe\n\nfrom orchestrator.adapters import ado\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\n\n# ---------- Azure DevOps\uff08\u884c\u7a0b\u5167\uff09 ----------\n\n@observe()\nasync def fetch_pr_metadata(pr_url: str) -> dict:\n    return await asyncio.to_thread(ado.get_pr_metadata, pr_url)\n\n\n@observe()\nasync def fetch_pr_diff(pr_url: str) -> str:\n    return await asyncio.to_thread(ado.get_pr_diff, pr_url)\n\n\n@observe()\nasync def post_review_comment(pr_url: str, markdown: str) -> dict:\n    return await asyncio.to_thread(ado.post_review_comment, pr_url, markdown)\n\n\n@observe()\nasync def post_knowledge_draft(pr_url: str, markdown: str,\n                               thread_id: int | None = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"thread_id \u7d66\u5b9a = \u56de\u8986\u9032\u65e2\u6709 thread\uff08\u91cd\u84b8\u7684\u66f4\u65b0\u7a3f\uff09\uff0c\u4e0d\u958b\u65b0 thread\u3002\"\"\"\n    return await asyncio.to_thread(ado.post_knowledge_draft, pr_url, markdown, thread_id)\n\n\n# ---------- \u2463 code graph\uff08\u9078\u914d\uff1b\u5916\u90e8 MCP server\uff09 ----------\n# \u88dd\u597d\u5f8c\u5148 list tools \u78ba\u8a8d\u540d\u7a31\u8207\u53c3\u6578\uff0c\u518d\u8a2d GRAPH_TOOL_BLAST /\n# GRAPH_TOOL_BLAST_ARGS\uff08JSON \u6a23\u677f\uff0c$files / $repo \u6703\u88ab\u4ee3\u5165\uff09\u3002\n# GRAPH_TOOLS_URL \u672a\u8a2d = \u6574\u500b graph \u529f\u80fd\u505c\u7528\uff0c\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u5168\u90e8\u512a\u96c5\u964d\u7d1a\u3002\n\n\nasync def _mcp_call(server_url: str, tool: str, args: dict):\n    \"\"\"\u547c\u53eb\u9060\u7aef MCP tool \u4e26\u628a\u7d50\u679c\u6524\u5e73\u6210 Python \u7269\u4ef6\u3002\"\"\"\n    from fastmcp import Client\n    async with Client(server_url) as c:\n        res = await c.call_tool(tool, args)\n    data = getattr(res, \"data\", None)          # fastmcp 2.x\uff1a\u512a\u5148\u7528\u7d50\u69cb\u5316 data\n    if data is not None:\n        return data\n    for block in getattr(res, \"content\", None) or []:\n        text = getattr(block, \"text\", None)\n        if text is not None:\n            try:\n                return json.loads(text)\n            except (json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError):\n                return text\n    return None\n\n\n@observe()\nasync def graph_call(tool: str, args: dict):\n    url = settings().graph.tools_url\n    if not url:\n        return None\n    return await _mcp_call(url, tool, args)\n\n\nasync def graph_blast(files: list[str], repo: str | None = None):\n    \"\"\"\u53d7\u5f71\u97ff\u7bc4\u570d\u6458\u8981\u3002\u5de5\u5177\u540d/\u53c3\u6578\u6a23\u677f\u7531 env \u6c7a\u5b9a\uff08\u4e0d\u540c graph \u5de5\u5177\u53ef\u63db\u76ae\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    g = settings().graph\n    tool = g.tool_blast\n    if not tool:\n        return None\n    template = g.tool_blast_args\n    if \"$repo_dir\" in template and not (repo or \"\").strip():\n        return None                      # \u6a23\u677f\u8981 repo\u3001\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u6c92\u7d66 \u2192 \u975c\u9ed8\u8df3\u904e\n    rendered = (template\n                .replace(\"$files\", json.dumps(files))\n                .replace(\"$repo_dir\", (repo or \"\").strip().lower())\n                .replace(\"$repo\", json.dumps((repo or \"\").strip().lower())))\n    try:\n        args = json.loads(rendered)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return None\n    return await graph_call(tool, args)\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/__init__.py","perm":"0644","sha":"12353556f8d4144241602761b582471c9d54d03845883593e7ca5762016686fb","data":"\"\"\"console \u2014\u2014 \u639b\u5728 orchestrator \u4e0a\u7684\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\uff08/console/*\uff09\u3002\n\n\u70ba\u4ec0\u9ebc\u4e0d\u662f\u7368\u7acb\u670d\u52d9\uff1aS1 \u628a\u7cfb\u7d71\u7e2e\u6210\u4e00\u500b\u884c\u7a0b\uff0c\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u8981\u770b\u7684\u6771\u897f\uff08\u8a2d\u5b9a\u3001jobs \u72c0\u614b\u3001\n\u5beb\u5165\u7a3d\u6838\u3001\u4e4b\u5f8c\u7684 review \u6b77\u53f2\uff09\u5168\u5728\u9019\u500b\u884c\u7a0b\u7684\u8a18\u61b6\u9ad4\u88e1\uff1b\u518d\u958b\u4e00\u500b\u670d\u52d9\u5c31\u8981\u518d\u958b\u4e00\u500b\nport\u3001\u4e00\u4efd\u8a2d\u5b9a\u3001\u4e00\u689d IPC\u3002\n\n\u6280\u8853\u9078\u64c7\u5168\u90e8\u70ba\u4e86\u300c\u5167\u7db2\u3001\u96f6 build\u3001\u4e00\u500b\u4eba\u7dad\u8b77\u300d\uff1aFastAPI + Jinja2 \u4f3a\u670d\u7aef\u6e32\u67d3\uff0c\n\u4e00\u652f 2 KB \u7684 console.js\uff08\u8868\u55ae\u975e\u540c\u6b65\u9001\u51fa\u3001\u5c40\u90e8\u63db\u9801\uff09\uff0c\u4e00\u652f\u81ea\u5beb CSS\uff0c\u7121 node\u3001\u7121 CDN\u3002\n\n\u8a8d\u8b49\uff1a\u6cbf\u7528 ORCH_API_KEY\u3002\u8a2d\u4e86 \u2192 \u767b\u5165\u9801\u63db\u4e00\u9846 HMAC cookie\uff1b\u6c92\u8a2d \u2192 \u958b\u653e\uff08\u5167\u7db2\nPOC \u6a21\u5f0f\uff0c\u9801\u9762\u9802\u7aef\u639b\u8b66\u793a\u689d\uff09\u3002\u4e0d\u53e6\u9020\u7b2c\u4e8c\u628a\u9470\u5319\u3002\n\nS2 \u6709\u5169\u9801\uff1aOverview\uff08doctor \u4e00\u5f35\u8868 + jobs\uff09\u3001Settings\uff08schema \u751f\u8868\u55ae\u3001Apply \u71b1\u91cd\u8f09\u3001\n\u6539\u52d5\u7d00\u9304\uff09\u3002Sources / Reviews / Knowledge \u662f S3 / S4\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.staticfiles import StaticFiles\n\nfrom orchestrator.console.router import router as console_router\n\n_HERE = Path(__file__).parent\n\n\ndef mount(app: FastAPI) -> None:\n    app.mount(\"/console/static\", StaticFiles(directory=str(_HERE / \"static\")), name=\"console-static\")\n    app.include_router(console_router)\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/auth.py","perm":"0644","sha":"21cd8cb506e19417892dde1f5fa005481119654bffd0e1b2d1b62d50616b48f1","data":"\"\"\"\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u8a8d\u8b49\uff1a\u4e00\u628a\u9470\u5319\uff08ORCH_API_KEY\uff09\u63db\u4e00\u9846 HMAC cookie\u3002\n\n- ORCH_API_KEY \u672a\u8a2d\uff1a\u958b\u653e\uff08\u5167\u7db2 POC \u6a21\u5f0f\uff09\uff1b\u9801\u9762\u9802\u7aef\u639b\u8b66\u793a\u3002\n- \u8a2d\u4e86\uff1aGET \u4efb\u4f55 /console \u9801\u6c92 cookie \u2192 302 \u5230 /console/login\uff1bPOST token \u5c0d\u4e86\u5c31\u767c cookie\u3002\n- cookie \u503c = HMAC-SHA256(key, \"pr-review-console\")\uff1bkey \u4e00\u63db\u6240\u6709 cookie \u7acb\u523b\u5931\u6548\uff0c\n  \u4e0d\u9700\u8981 session \u5132\u5b58\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport hmac\n\nfrom fastapi import Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import RedirectResponse\n\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\nCOOKIE = \"prc\"\n\n\ndef _key() -> str:\n    return settings().orchestrator.api_key.get_secret_value()\n\n\ndef expected_cookie(key: str | None = None) -> str:\n    k = key if key is not None else _key()\n    return hmac.new(k.encode(), b\"pr-review-console\", hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef is_open() -> bool:\n    return not _key()\n\n\ndef is_authed(request: Request) -> bool:\n    if is_open():\n        return True\n    got = request.cookies.get(COOKIE, \"\")\n    return bool(got) and hmac.compare_digest(got, expected_cookie())\n\n\ndef token_ok(token: str) -> bool:\n    k = _key()\n    return bool(k) and hmac.compare_digest(token.strip(), k)\n\n\ndef login_redirect(request: Request) -> RedirectResponse:\n    nxt = request.url.path\n    return RedirectResponse(f\"/console/login?next={nxt}\", status_code=302)\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/labels.py","perm":"0644","sha":"87321d1867396c879d683f02e06efa0ce871f9381805ab9d5e465001d83fc65a","data":"\"\"\"\u8a2d\u5b9a\u9801\u6bcf\u500b\u6b04\u4f4d\u7684\u4eba\u8a71\u6a19\u7c64\uff08\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\u540d \u2192 \u77ed\u6a19\u7c64\uff09\u3002\n\nschema \u7684 description \u662f\u300c\u89e3\u91cb\u300d\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u300c\u540d\u5b57\u300d\uff1b\u8868\u55ae\u5de6\u6b04\u8981\u7684\u662f\u540d\u5b57\u3002\u9019\u5f35\u8868\u662f\u624b\u5beb\u7684\uff0c\n\u65b0\u589e\u6b04\u4f4d\u6c92\u5beb\u5c31\u9000\u56de\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\u540d\u3002\n\"\"\"\nLABELS: dict[str, str] = {\n    # ado\n    \"ADO_PAT\": \"Personal Access Token\",\n    \"ADO_VERIFY_SSL\": \"\u6191\u8b49\u9a57\u8b49 / CA bundle\",\n    \"ADO_DIFF_MAX_FILES\": \"\u6bcf PR \u6700\u5927\u6a94\u6848\u6578\",\n    \"ADO_DIFF_MAX_FILE_BYTES\": \"\u55ae\u6a94\u5167\u5bb9\u4e0a\u9650\uff08bytes\uff09\",\n    \"ADO_DIFF_FETCH_CONCURRENCY\": \"\u6293\u53d6\u4f75\u767c\u6578\",\n    # posting\n    \"DRY_RUN\": \"Dry run\uff08\u4e0d\u767c\u5e03 review comment\uff09\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_POST\": \"\u767c\u5e03 knowledge draft \u81f3 PR\",\n    # llm\n    \"LLM_BASE_URL\": \"Gateway base URL\",\n    \"LLM_API_KEY\": \"API key\",\n    \"LLM_MODEL\": \"\u9810\u8a2d\u6a21\u578b\",\n    \"LLM_MODEL_ADVERSARY\": \"Adversary \u6a21\u578b\",\n    \"LLM_MODEL_DIGEST\": \"Digest \u5206\u6790\u6a21\u578b\",\n    \"LLM_TIMEOUT_S\": \"\u55ae\u6b21\u547c\u53eb\u903e\u6642\uff08\u79d2\uff09\",\n    # langfuse\n    \"LANGFUSE_HOST\": \"Langfuse \u4f4d\u5740\",\n    \"LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY\": \"Public key\",\n    \"LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY\": \"Secret key\",\n    # orchestrator\n    \"REVIEW_PIPELINE\": \"Pipeline \u7248\u672c\",\n    \"AUTO_POST\": \"\u81ea\u52d5\u767c\u5e03 review comment\",\n    \"REVIEW_DEDUPE_TTL\": \"\u53bb\u91cd TTL\uff08\u79d2\uff09\",\n    \"ORCH_API_KEY\": \"API key\uff08\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u8207 /review\uff09\",\n    \"ORCH_URL\": \"Orchestrator URL\uff08harvester \u56de\u547c\uff09\",\n    \"DATA_DIR\": \"\u8cc7\u6599\u76ee\u9304\uff08review \u8a18\u9304\uff09\",\n    # jobs\n    \"REPO_SYNC_INTERVAL_MIN\": \"repo-sync \u9593\u9694\uff08min\uff09\",\n    \"HARVEST_INTERVAL_MIN\": \"harvest \u9593\u9694\uff08min\uff09\",\n    \"REPO_SYNC_GRAPH_REBUILD\": \"\u540c\u6b65\u5f8c\u91cd\u5efa code graph\",\n    # review\n    \"REVIEW_MAX_DIMENSIONS\": \"\u6700\u5927\u5be9\u67e5\u9762\u5411\u6578\",\n    \"REVIEW_MAX_PARALLEL\": \"LLM \u4f75\u767c\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    \"REVIEW_LLM_BASE_CONF\": \"LLM finding \u521d\u59cb\u4fe1\u5fc3\u503c\",\n    \"REVIEW_MIN_CONFIDENCE\": \"\u4fe1\u5fc3\u9580\u6abb\",\n    \"REVIEW_MAX_FINDINGS\": \"finding \u6578\u91cf\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    \"REVIEW_ADVERSARY\": \"\u555f\u7528 adversary \u9a57\u8b49\",\n    \"ADVERSARY_CHUNK\": \"Adversary \u6279\u6b21\u5927\u5c0f\",\n    \"REVIEWER_RULES_MAX_CHARS\": \"\u6bcf\u9762\u5411\u898f\u5247\u5b57\u5143\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    \"REVIEWER_SLICES_MAX_CHARS\": \"\u6bcf\u9762\u5411 diff \u5207\u7247\u9810\u7b97\",\n    \"REVIEWER_FILE_SLICE_MAX_CHARS\": \"\u55ae\u6a94\u5207\u7247\u5b57\u5143\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    # static\n    \"STATIC_SEMGREP\": \"semgrep\",\n    \"STATIC_RUFF\": \"ruff\",\n    \"STATIC_TIMEOUT\": \"\u6383\u63cf\u903e\u6642\uff08\u79d2\uff09\",\n    \"STATIC_MISSING_TEST\": \"\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027 MISSING-TEST\",\n    # repos\n    \"REPOS_ROOT\": \"\u672c\u5730 clone \u6839\u76ee\u9304\",\n    \"CONTEXT_LINES\": \"base \u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\u884c\u6578\uff08\u00b1\uff09\",\n    \"CONTEXT_MAX_CHARS\": \"base \u8207 graph \u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\u9810\u7b97\",\n    # graph\n    \"GRAPH_TOOLS_URL\": \"code graph MCP \u4f4d\u5740\",\n    \"GRAPH_TOOL_BLAST\": \"Impact radius \u5de5\u5177\u540d\",\n    \"GRAPH_TOOL_BLAST_ARGS\": \"\u5de5\u5177\u53c3\u6578\u6a23\u677f\",\n    \"GRAPH_REPO\": \"graph \u7d81\u5b9a\u7684 repo\",\n    # rules\n    \"RULES_ROOT\": \"\u898f\u5247 repo \u6839\u76ee\u9304\",\n    \"RULES_SUBDIR\": \"\u898f\u5247\u5b50\u76ee\u9304\u540d\",\n    \"RULES_COMMON_DIR\": \"\u5171\u7528\u898f\u5247\u76ee\u9304\u540d\",\n    \"RULES_MAX_CHARS\": \"\u898f\u5247\u5b57\u5143\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    # knowledge\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT\": \"\u77e5\u8b58\u5e33\u672c\u6839\u76ee\u9304\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_BRANCHES\": \"\u7d0d\u5165\u5e33\u672c\u7684 target branch\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_MAX_CHARS\": \"\u6ce8\u5165\u5340\u584a\u5b57\u5143\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    \"DISTILL_DIFF_MAX_CHARS\": \"\u84b8\u993e diff \u5207\u7247\u9810\u7b97\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_REDISTILL\": \"Stale \u8349\u7a3f\u91cd\u65b0\u84b8\u993e\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_CYCLE_SOURCE\": \"\u9a57\u6536 PR \u7684 source \u5206\u652f\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_CYCLE_TARGET\": \"\u9a57\u6536 PR \u7684 target \u5206\u652f\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_DIGEST\": \"\u6536\u53e3\u6642\u767c\u5e03 digest\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_DIGEST_LLM\": \"digest \u7684 LLM \u9867\u554f\u6bb5\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_DIGEST_MAX_FLAGS\": \"\u9867\u554f\u65d7\u6a19\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    \"KNOWLEDGE_RETIRE_ON_CONTRADICTION\": \"\u77db\u76fe\u6642\u8a3b\u92b7\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\",\n    # eval\n    \"EVAL_KNOWLEDGE_ROOT\": \"\u77e5\u8b58\u984c\u7684\u7a2e\u5b50\u5e33\u672c\",\n    \"EVAL_KNOWLEDGE_AB\": \"\u57f7\u884c\u5c0d\u7167\u7d44\",\n    \"EVAL_MIN_RECALL\": \"recall \u4e0b\u9650\",\n    \"EVAL_MAX_NOISE\": \"\u566a\u97f3\u7387\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    \"EVAL_MAX_FORBIDDEN\": \"\u7981\u8a9e\u7387\u4e0a\u9650\",\n    \"EVAL_MIN_KNOWLEDGE_DELTA\": \"knowledge_delta \u4e0b\u9650\",\n    \"EVAL_MIN_DISTILL_SCORE\": \"\u84b8\u993e\u5206\u6578\u4e0b\u9650\",\n}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/router.py","perm":"0644","sha":"a7fab967ecda89b86cb6e279b6ea48c3352809290e18042ef82e1e3397c83418","data":"\"\"\"\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u8def\u7531\u3002\u9801\u9762\uff1a/console\uff08Overview\uff09\u3001/console/settings\u3001/console/login\u3002\n\nSettings \u9801\u7684 Apply \u8d70 POST /console/settings/{group}\uff1a\n  \u8868\u55ae\u503c \u2192 settings.validate_group_values\uff08\u7d14 schema \u9a57\u8b49\uff0c\u58de\u503c\u56de\u8868\u55ae\u539f\u5730\u7d05\u5b57\uff09\n  \u2192 \u5371\u96aa\u65cb\u9215\u7ffb\u5411\u5371\u96aa\u5074\u8981\u52fe\u78ba\u8a8d \u2192 settings.save_toml\uff08\u5099\u4efd\u3001\u539f\u5b50\u5beb\u3001change log\u3001reset\uff09\n  \u2192 \u56de\u8a72\u7d44\u7684\u5c40\u90e8 HTML\uff08console.js \u539f\u5730\u66ff\u63db\uff09\u3002\n\u88ab\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\u8986\u5beb\u7684\u6b04\u4f4d\u662f\u552f\u8b80\u7684\uff1aenv \u6c38\u9060\u8d0f\uff0c\u6539\u6a94\u7121\u6548\uff0c\u9801\u9762\u76f4\u8aaa\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Form, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\nfrom fastapi.templating import Jinja2Templates\nfrom pydantic import SecretStr, ValidationError\n\nfrom orchestrator import jobs, ledger, sources, store\nfrom orchestrator.adapters import ado\nfrom orchestrator.console import auth, status as stat\nfrom orchestrator.console.labels import LABELS\nfrom shared import doctor\nfrom shared import settings as S\n\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix=\"/console\", include_in_schema=False)\ntemplates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(Path(__file__).parent / \"templates\"))\ntemplates.env.filters[\"datetime\"] = lambda ts: time.strftime(\"%m-%d %H:%M\", time.localtime(ts))\n\n# \u4f9d\u7dad\u904b\u8005\u7684\u4efb\u52d9\u5206\u56db\u9801\uff1bsources / setup \u4ecd\u6709\u8def\u7531\uff0c\u5f9e \u8a2d\u5b9a \u8207 \u72c0\u614b \u9801\u9032\uff0c\u4e0d\u4f54\u5c0e\u89bd\u3002\nNAV = [(\"status\", \"\u72c0\u614b\", \"/console\"),\n       (\"reviews\", \"\u5be9\u67e5\", \"/console/reviews\"),\n       (\"knowledge\", \"\u77e5\u8b58\", \"/console/knowledge\"),\n       (\"settings\", \"\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings\")]\n\n# \u8a2d\u5b9a\u9801\u4f9d\u4efb\u52d9\u5206\u6bb5\uff08\u4e0d\u662f\u4f9d\u6a21\u7d44\uff09\uff1a\u7dad\u904b\u8005\u627e\u7684\u662f\u300c\u9023\u7dda\u300d\u300c\u767c\u6587\u958b\u95dc\u300d\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f ado / posting\nTASKS = [\n    {\"title\": \"\u9023\u7dda\", \"why\": \"LLM gateway\u3001Langfuse\u3001Azure DevOps \u8207 orchestrator \u672c\u9ad4\u3002Secrets\uff08PAT\u3001API key\uff09\u50c5\u7531 secrets.env \u8a2d\u5b9a\u3002\",\n     \"groups\": [\"llm\", \"langfuse\", \"ado\", \"orchestrator\"]},\n    {\"title\": \"\u767c\u5e03\u958b\u95dc\", \"why\": \"\u63a7\u5236\u5c0d Azure DevOps \u7684\u5beb\u5165\u3002\u9810\u8a2d\u5168\u70ba\u5b89\u5168\u5074\uff1b\u5207\u63db\u81f3\u767c\u5e03\u5074\u9700\u78ba\u8a8d\u3002\",\n     \"groups\": [\"posting\"]},\n    {\"title\": \"Review pipeline\", \"why\": \"v2 pipeline \u7684\u9762\u5411\u6578\u3001\u4f75\u767c\u3001\u4fe1\u5fc3\u9580\u6abb\u3001\u5207\u7247\u9810\u7b97\u8207\u975c\u614b\u6383\u63cf\u3002\u8abf\u6574\u524d\u5148\u901a\u904e eval\u3002\",\n     \"groups\": [\"review\", \"static\"]},\n    {\"title\": \"\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90\", \"why\": \"\u672c\u5730 clone\u3001\u5718\u968a\u898f\u5247\u3001\u77e5\u8b58\u5e33\u672c\u3001code graph \u7684\u8def\u5f91\u8207\u555f\u7528\u72c0\u614b\u3002\",\n     \"groups\": [\"repos\", \"rules\", \"knowledge\", \"graph\"], \"link\": \"/console/sources\", \"link_label\": \"\u4f86\u6e90\u72c0\u614b\u8207\u6ce8\u5165\u9810\u89bd\"},\n    {\"title\": \"\u6392\u7a0b\", \"why\": \"\u884c\u7a0b\u5167\u6392\u7a0b\u5de5\u4f5c\u7684\u57f7\u884c\u9593\u9694\uff1b0 \u70ba\u505c\u7528\u3002\", \"groups\": [\"jobs\"]},\n    {\"title\": \"Eval gate\", \"why\": \"CI gate \u9580\u6abb\u3002\u672a\u8a2d\u5b9a\u6642\u50c5\u56de\u5831\u3001\u4e0d\u64cb\u3002\", \"groups\": [\"eval\"]},\n]\n\n# \u7ffb\u5411\u9019\u4e00\u5074\u8981\u52fe\u300c\u6211\u78ba\u5b9a\u300d\uff1a\u6703\u5c0d\u5916\u771f\u767c\u3001\u6216\u95dc\u6389\u5b89\u5168\u6c23\u56ca\nDANGEROUS = {(\"orchestrator\", \"auto_post\"): True,\n             (\"posting\", \"dry_run\"): False,\n             (\"posting\", \"knowledge_post\"): True}\n\n\ndef _ctx(request: Request, page: str, **extra: Any) -> dict:\n    return {\"request\": request, \"page\": page, \"nav\": NAV,\n            \"open_mode\": auth.is_open(), \"warnings\": S.warnings_for(), **extra}\n\n\n# ---------- \u767b\u5165 ----------\n\n@router.get(\"/login\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def login_page(request: Request, next: str = \"/console\", error: str = \"\"):\n    if auth.is_open():\n        return RedirectResponse(next, status_code=302)\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"login.html\",\n                                      _ctx(request, \"login\", next=next, error=error))\n\n\n@router.post(\"/login\")\nasync def login(request: Request, token: str = Form(\"\"), next: str = Form(\"/console\")):\n    if not auth.token_ok(token):\n        return RedirectResponse(\"/console/login?error=1\", status_code=302)\n    resp = RedirectResponse(next if next.startswith(\"/console\") else \"/console\", status_code=302)\n    resp.set_cookie(auth.COOKIE, auth.expected_cookie(), httponly=True, samesite=\"lax\",\n                    max_age=30 * 24 * 3600)\n    return resp\n\n\n@router.post(\"/logout\")\nasync def logout():\n    resp = RedirectResponse(\"/console/login\", status_code=302)\n    resp.delete_cookie(auth.COOKIE)\n    return resp\n\n\n# ---------- Overview ----------\n\n_doctor_cache: dict[str, Any] = {\"ts\": 0.0, \"checks\": []}\nDOCTOR_TTL_S = 30.0\n\n\nasync def _doctor_checks(force: bool = False) -> list[doctor.Check]:\n    if force or time.time() - _doctor_cache[\"ts\"] > DOCTOR_TTL_S:\n        checks, _code = await asyncio.to_thread(doctor.run, network=True, pr_url=None)\n        _doctor_cache.update(ts=time.time(), checks=checks)\n    return _doctor_cache[\"checks\"]\n\n\n@router.get(\"\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\n@router.get(\"/\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def overview(request: Request, refresh: int = 0):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    checks = await _doctor_checks(force=bool(refresh))\n    groups: dict[str, list[doctor.Check]] = {}\n    for c in checks:\n        groups.setdefault(c.group, []).append(c)\n    counts = {k: sum(1 for c in checks if c.status == k)\n              for k in (doctor.OK, doctor.WARN, doctor.FAIL, doctor.SKIP)}\n    views = await asyncio.to_thread(sources.all_views)\n    js = jobs.snapshot()\n    reviews = store.list_reviews(15)\n    audit = list(ado.audit_log)[-15:]\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"status.html\", _ctx(\n        request, \"status\", groups=groups, counts=counts,\n        hl=stat.headline(checks), blockers=stat.blockers(checks), healthy=stat.healthy(checks),\n        feed=stat.feed(reviews, audit, js, S.recent_changes(10)), ago=stat.ago,\n        checked_at=_doctor_cache[\"ts\"], jobs=js, now=time.time(),\n        sources=views, reviews=reviews[:8], summary=store.summary(7),\n        config_exists=S.config_path().exists()))\n\n\n@router.post(\"/jobs/{name}/run\")\nasync def run_job(request: Request, name: str, back: str = \"/console?refresh=1\"):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    if name in jobs.JOBS:\n        asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task(jobs.run_once(name))\n    return RedirectResponse(back if back.startswith(\"/console\") else \"/console\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# ---------- Sources ----------\n\n@router.get(\"/sources\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def sources_page(request: Request, rules_repo: str = \"\", k_repo: str = \"\", k_paths: str = \"\"):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    views = await asyncio.to_thread(sources.all_views)\n    rp = await asyncio.to_thread(sources.rules_preview, rules_repo) \\\n        if (rules_repo or \"rules_repo\" in request.query_params) and views[\"rules\"].exists else None\n    paths = [p.strip() for p in k_paths.split(\",\") if p.strip()]\n    kp = await asyncio.to_thread(sources.knowledge_preview, k_repo, paths) \\\n        if k_repo and paths and views[\"knowledge\"].exists else None\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"sources.html\", _ctx(\n        request, \"sources\", v=views, jobs=jobs.snapshot(), now=time.time(),\n        rules_repo=rules_repo, rp=rp, k_repo=k_repo, k_paths=k_paths, kp=kp,\n        add_result=request.query_params.getlist(\"added\")))\n\n\n@router.post(\"/sources/repos/add\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def sources_add_repo(request: Request, name: str = Form(\"\"), url: str = Form(\"\"),\n                           branch: str = Form(\"\")):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    lines = await asyncio.to_thread(sources.add_repo, name, url, branch or \"main\")\n    from urllib.parse import urlencode\n    return RedirectResponse(\"/console/sources?\" + urlencode([(\"added\", ln) for ln in lines]) + \"#repos\",\n                            status_code=303)\n\n\n# ---------- Reviews ----------\n\n@router.get(\"/reviews\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def reviews_page(request: Request, error: str = \"\"):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    rows = store.list_reviews(50)\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"reviews.html\", _ctx(\n        request, \"reviews\", reviews=rows, summary=store.summary(7), now=time.time(),\n        store_ok=store.enabled(), store_reason=store.disabled_reason(),\n        auto_post=S.settings().orchestrator.auto_post, run_error=error))\n\n\n@router.post(\"/reviews/run\")\nasync def reviews_run(request: Request, pr_url: str = Form(\"\")):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    from shared.azdo import find_pr_url\n    url = find_pr_url(pr_url)\n    if not url:\n        return RedirectResponse(\"/console/reviews?error=\u4e0d\u662f PR URL\uff08\u8981\u542b /_git/<repo>/pullrequest/<id>\uff09\",\n                                status_code=303)\n    from orchestrator import app as A       # \u5ef6\u9072 import\uff1aapp \u5148 import console\n    asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task(_run_and_log(A.handle_review, url))\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.2)                # \u8b93 start_review \u5148\u843d\u5e33\uff0c\u5217\u8868\u7b2c\u4e00\u5217\u5c31\u662f\u5b83\n    return RedirectResponse(\"/console/reviews\", status_code=303)\n\n\nasync def _run_and_log(handle, url: str) -> None:\n    try:\n        await handle(url, \"console\")\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001  \u2014\u2014 \u5df2\u7531 handle_review \u843d\u5e33\u70ba error\n        print(f\"[console] review {url} \u5931\u6557\uff1a{type(e).__name__}: {e}\")\n\n\n# ---------- Knowledge ----------\n\n@router.get(\"/knowledge\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def knowledge_page(request: Request, digest_repo: str = \"\", msg: str = \"\"):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    pend, stg, cyc, verd = await asyncio.to_thread(\n        lambda: (ledger.pending(), ledger.staged(), ledger.cycle_state(), ledger.verdicts()))\n    dig = await asyncio.to_thread(ledger.digest_preview, digest_repo) if digest_repo else \"\"\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"knowledge.html\", _ctx(\n        request, \"knowledge\", root=ledger._root() is not None, pending=pend, staged=stg,\n        cycle=cyc, verdicts=verd, digest=dig, digest_repo=digest_repo, msg=msg,\n        job=jobs.snapshot().get(\"harvest\"), now=time.time()))\n\n\n@router.post(\"/knowledge/verdict\")\nasync def knowledge_verdict(request: Request, repo: str = Form(\"\"), kind: str = Form(\"\"),\n                            token: str = Form(\"\")):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    who = request.client.host if request.client else \"console\"\n    msg = ledger.add_verdict(repo, kind, token, by=who)\n    from urllib.parse import quote\n    return RedirectResponse(f\"/console/knowledge?msg={quote(msg)}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n@router.post(\"/knowledge/verdict/remove\")\nasync def knowledge_verdict_remove(request: Request, repo: str = Form(\"\"), kind: str = Form(\"\"),\n                                   token: str = Form(\"\")):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    msg = ledger.remove_verdict(repo, kind, token)\n    from urllib.parse import quote\n    return RedirectResponse(f\"/console/knowledge?msg={quote(msg)}\", status_code=303)\n\n\n# ---------- Setup \u7cbe\u9748 ----------\n\nSETUP_STEPS = [\n    {\"key\": \"llm\", \"title\": \"LLM gateway\", \"groups\": [\"llm\"], \"doctor\": [(\"llm\", None)],\n     \"why\": \"planner / reviewer / adversary \u7684\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u9ede\uff1bLLM_MODEL \u9808\u5b58\u5728\u65bc gateway \u7684\u6a21\u578b\u6e05\u55ae\u3002\",\n     \"secrets\": [\"LLM_API_KEY\"]},\n    {\"key\": \"langfuse\", \"title\": \"Langfuse\", \"groups\": [\"langfuse\"], \"doctor\": [(\"langfuse\", None)],\n     \"why\": \"Trace\u3001prompt \u7248\u63a7\u8207 eval \u7684\u5f8c\u7aef\uff1b\u6191\u8b49\u9808\u8207 host \u76f8\u7b26\u3002\",\n     \"secrets\": [\"LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY\", \"LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY\"]},\n    {\"key\": \"ado\", \"title\": \"Azure DevOps\", \"groups\": [\"ado\", \"posting\"], \"doctor\": [(\"ado\", None)],\n     \"why\": \"\u8b80\u53d6 PR \u8207\u767c\u5e03 comment \u7686\u4f7f\u7528 ADO_PAT\uff1bDRY_RUN / KNOWLEDGE_POST \u9810\u8a2d\u70ba\u5b89\u5168\u5074\u3002\",\n     \"secrets\": [\"ADO_PAT\"]},\n    {\"key\": \"service\", \"title\": \"Orchestrator \u670d\u52d9\", \"groups\": [\"orchestrator\", \"jobs\"],\n     \"doctor\": [(\"settings\", None), (\"python\", None), (\"services\", None), (\"jobs\", None), (\"systemd\", None)],\n     \"why\": \"\u884c\u7a0b\u72c0\u614b\u3001Python \u4f9d\u8cf4\u3001\u6392\u7a0b\u5de5\u4f5c\u3002\u8a2d\u5b9a ORCH_API_KEY \u5f8c\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u9700\u767b\u5165\u3002\",\n     \"secrets\": [\"ORCH_API_KEY\"]},\n    {\"key\": \"repos\", \"title\": \"\u672c\u5730 clone\uff08base \u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\uff09\", \"groups\": [\"repos\"], \"doctor\": [(\"paths\", \"REPOS_ROOT\")],\n     \"why\": \"\u9078\u914d\uff1a\u63d0\u4f9b\u8b8a\u66f4\u5468\u908a\u7684 base \u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\u3002\u53ef\u65bc\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90\u9801\u76f4\u63a5 clone\u3002\",\n     \"link\": \"/console/sources#repos\", \"link_label\": \"\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90 \u203a repos\"},\n    {\"key\": \"rules\", \"title\": \"\u5718\u968a\u898f\u5247\", \"groups\": [\"rules\", \"static\"], \"doctor\": [(\"paths\", \"RULES_ROOT\")],\n     \"why\": \"RULES_ROOT \u6307\u5411\u898f\u5247 repo \u7684\u672c\u5730 clone\uff1bsemgrep \u898f\u5247\u4ea6\u7531\u6b64\u8f09\u5165\u3002\", \"link\": \"/console/sources#rules\", \"link_label\": \"\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90 \u203a rules\"},\n    {\"key\": \"knowledge\", \"title\": \"\u77e5\u8b58\u8ff4\u5708\uff08\u9078\u914d\uff09\", \"groups\": [\"knowledge\"],\n     \"doctor\": [(\"paths\", \"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT\"), (\"paths\", \"DATA_DIR\")],\n     \"why\": \"\u8a2d\u5b9a KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u5f8c\u555f\u7528\u84b8\u993e\u3001\u6ce8\u5165\u8207\u6536\u5272\uff1bDATA_DIR \u70ba review \u8a18\u9304\u76ee\u9304\u3002\",\n     \"link\": \"/console/knowledge\", \"link_label\": \"\u77e5\u8b58\u5e33\u672c\"},\n]\n\n_RANK = {\"OK\": 0, \"SKIP\": 0, \"WARN\": 1, \"FAIL\": 2}\n\n\n@router.get(\"/setup\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def setup_page(request: Request, refresh: int = 0):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    checks = await _doctor_checks(force=bool(refresh))\n    steps = []\n    for st in SETUP_STEPS:\n        mine = [c for c in checks for (g, n) in st[\"doctor\"] if c.group == g and (n is None or c.name == n)]\n        worst = max((_RANK.get(c.status, 0) for c in mine), default=0)\n        status = {0: \"OK\", 1: \"WARN\", 2: \"FAIL\"}[worst]\n        if mine and all(c.status == \"SKIP\" for c in mine):\n            status = \"SKIP\"\n        steps.append({**st, \"checks\": mine, \"status\": status})\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"setup.html\", _ctx(\n        request, \"setup\", steps=steps, config_path=str(S.config_path()),\n        config_exists=S.config_path().exists()))\n\n\n@router.get(\"/reviews/{review_id}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def review_detail(request: Request, review_id: int):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    r = store.get_review(review_id)\n    if not r:\n        return HTMLResponse(\"not found\", status_code=404)\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"review_detail.html\", _ctx(\n        request, \"reviews\", r=r, now=time.time(),\n        langfuse_host=S.settings().langfuse.host.rstrip(\"/\")))\n\n\n# ---------- Settings ----------\n\ndef _control(info) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u578b\u5225 \u2192 \u63a7\u4ef6\u7a2e\u985e\uff08\u6a21\u677f\u7528\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    ann = info.annotation\n    if ann is SecretStr:\n        return \"secret\"\n    if ann is bool:\n        return \"bool\"\n    meta = getattr(ann, \"__metadata__\", None)\n    origin = getattr(ann, \"__origin__\", None)\n    base = getattr(ann, \"__args__\", (ann,))[0] if meta else ann\n    if base is bool:\n        return \"bool\"\n    if getattr(base, \"__origin__\", None) is not None and \"Literal\" in str(base):\n        return \"choice\"\n    if \"Literal\" in str(ann):\n        return \"choice\"\n    if base in (int, float) or ann in (int, float):\n        return \"number\"\n    if origin is list or base is list or \"list[\" in str(ann):\n        return \"csv\"\n    return \"text\"\n\n\ndef _choices(info) -> list[str]:\n    import typing\n    for t in (info.annotation, *getattr(info.annotation, \"__args__\", ())):\n        if typing.get_origin(t) is typing.Literal:\n            return [str(x) for x in typing.get_args(t)]\n    return []\n\n\ndef _group_view(gname: str, errors: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n                posted: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> dict:\n    s = S.settings()\n    gcls = S.Settings.model_fields[gname].annotation\n    grp = getattr(s, gname)\n    fields = []\n    for fname, info in gcls.model_fields.items():\n        v = getattr(grp, fname)\n        src = S.source_of(gname, fname, info)\n        kind = _control(info)\n        shown = (posted or {}).get(fname)\n        if shown is None:\n            shown = \"\" if v is None else (\",\".join(v) if isinstance(v, list)\n                                          else (\"true\" if v is True else \"false\" if v is False\n                                                else str(v)))\n        extra = info.json_schema_extra if isinstance(info.json_schema_extra, dict) else {}\n        desc = (info.description or \"\").strip()\n        env = S.env_names(info)[0]\n        default_native = S._native(info.get_default(call_default_factory=True))\n        fields.append({\n            \"label\": LABELS.get(env, env), \"more\": desc,\n            \"default_raw\": S._render_value(default_native),\n            \"name\": fname, \"env\": S.env_names(info)[0], \"kind\": kind,\n            \"choices\": _choices(info), \"value\": shown,\n            \"masked\": S._mask(v) if kind == \"secret\" else None,\n            \"source\": src, \"locked\": src.startswith(\"env:\") or kind == \"secret\",\n            \"description\": info.description or \"\",\n            \"default\": S._render_value(S._native(info.get_default(call_default_factory=True))) or \"(unset)\",\n            \"dangerous\": (gname, fname) in DANGEROUS,\n            \"min\": getattr(info, \"metadata\", None) and next((m.ge for m in info.metadata if hasattr(m, \"ge\")), None),\n            \"max\": getattr(info, \"metadata\", None) and next((m.le for m in info.metadata if hasattr(m, \"le\")), None),\n            \"error\": (errors or {}).get(fname, \"\"),\n            \"required\": bool(extra.get(\"required\")),\n        })\n    return {\"name\": gname, \"doc\": (gcls.__doc__ or \"\").strip(), \"fields\": fields,\n            \"saved\": False}\n\n\n@router.get(\"/settings\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def settings_page(request: Request):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    views = {g: _group_view(g) for g in S.GROUP_ORDER}\n    tasks = []\n    for t in TASKS:\n        gs = [views[g] for g in t[\"groups\"]]\n        tasks.append({**t, \"groups\": gs,\n                      \"modified\": sum(1 for g in gs for f in g[\"fields\"] if f[\"source\"] == \"file\")})\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"settings.html\", _ctx(\n        request, \"settings\", tasks=tasks, groups=list(views.values()),\n        config_path=str(S.config_path()),\n        config_exists=S.config_path().exists(), changes=S.recent_changes(20)))\n\n\n@router.post(\"/settings/{gname}\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def settings_apply(request: Request, gname: str):\n    if not auth.is_authed(request):\n        return auth.login_redirect(request)\n    if gname not in S.GROUP_ORDER:\n        return HTMLResponse(\"unknown group\", status_code=404)\n    form = await request.form()\n    gcls = S.Settings.model_fields[gname].annotation\n    posted: dict[str, str] = {}\n    changes: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    errors: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for fname, info in gcls.model_fields.items():\n        if info.annotation is SecretStr or S.source_of(gname, fname, info).startswith(\"env:\"):\n            continue                       # \u552f\u8b80\uff1asecret \u8d70 secrets.env\uff1benv \u8986\u5beb\u6539\u6a94\u7121\u6548\n        kind = _control(info)\n        if kind == \"bool\":\n            if f\"_b_{fname}\" not in form:\n                continue                   # checkbox \u6c92\u96a8\u8868\u55ae\u9001\u4f86 = \u9019\u6b04\u6c92\u5728\u9019\u6b21\u8868\u55ae\u88e1\uff0c\u4e0d\u52d5\n            raw = \"true\" if form.get(fname) in (\"on\", \"true\", \"1\") else \"false\"\n        else:\n            raw = str(form.get(fname, \"\")).strip()\n        posted[fname] = raw\n        default = S._native(info.get_default(call_default_factory=True))\n        if raw == \"\" or raw == \"(unset)\":\n            changes[fname] = None          # \u56de\u9810\u8a2d / \u522a\u9375\n            continue\n        if kind == \"bool\":\n            val: Any = raw == \"true\"\n        elif kind == \"csv\":\n            val = [x.strip() for x in raw.split(\",\") if x.strip()]\n        elif kind == \"number\":\n            try:\n                val = int(raw) if info.annotation is int or \"int\" in str(info.annotation) else float(raw)\n            except ValueError:\n                errors[fname] = \"\u9808\u70ba\u6578\u5b57\"\n                continue\n        else:\n            val = raw\n        try:                               # \u5148\u7d93 schema \u6b63\u898f\u5316\uff08\"true\" \u2192 True\u3001\u8def\u5f91\u3001\u6e05\u55ae\uff09\u518d\u6bd4\n            val = S.validate_group_values(gname, {fname: val})[fname]\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            errors[fname] = e.errors()[0][\"msg\"]\n            continue\n        if val == default and fname not in (S.load_toml().get(gname) or {}):\n            continue                       # \u7b49\u65bc\u9810\u8a2d\u4e14\u6a94\u88e1\u672c\u4f86\u6c92\u6709 \u2192 \u4e0d\u5beb\n        changes[fname] = val\n        if (gname, fname) in DANGEROUS and val == DANGEROUS[(gname, fname)] \\\n                and form.get(f\"confirm_{fname}\") != \"on\":\n            errors[fname] = \"\u6b64\u8b8a\u66f4\u6703\u5c0d\u5916\u5beb\u5165\u6216\u505c\u7528\u5b89\u5168\u9632\u8b77\uff0c\u9700\u52fe\u9078\u78ba\u8a8d\"\n    view: dict\n    if errors:\n        view = _group_view(gname, errors=errors, posted=posted)\n    else:\n        log = S.save_toml({gname: changes},\n                          actor=request.client.host if request.client else \"console\") \\\n            if changes else []\n        view = _group_view(gname)\n        view[\"saved\"] = True\n        view[\"applied\"] = log\n        view[\"restart_needed\"] = gname == \"orchestrator\" and any(\n            e[\"field\"] in (\"url\",) for e in log)\n    return templates.TemplateResponse(request, \"_group.html\", {\n        \"request\": request, \"g\": view, \"warnings\": S.warnings_for(),\n        \"changes\": S.recent_changes(20)})\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/static/console.css","perm":"0644","sha":"14a035cdaec5203261fc192e7eb21b756774cd4f9843ac5018e631f08183f9bd","data":"/* pr-review console \u2014\u2014 \u8a2d\u8a08\u7cfb\u7d71\u3002\n   \u7248\u578b\uff1a\u56fa\u5b9a\u5de6\u5074\u5c0e\u89bd 232px + \u5167\u5bb9\u5340\uff1b\u6bcf\u9801\u4e00\u689d\u6a19\u984c\u5217\uff08\u6a19\u984c / \u526f\u6a19 / \u4e3b\u8981\u52d5\u4f5c\uff09\u3002\n   \u8272\u5f69\uff1a\u5e36\u85cd\u7070\u504f\u5411\u7684\u4e2d\u6027\u8272 + \u4e00\u500b\u6df1\u9752\u8272 accent\uff1b\u72c0\u614b\u8272\uff08ok / warn / fail / skip\uff09\u7368\u7acb\u65bc accent\u3002\n   \u578b\u5225\uff1a\u7cfb\u7d71\u5b57\u9ad4 + Noto Sans TC\uff1b\u7b49\u5bec\u7d66 ID\u3001sha\u3001\u8def\u5f91\uff1b\u6578\u5b57\u4e00\u5f8b tabular\u3002\n   \u96f6\u5916\u90e8\u8cc7\u6e90\uff08\u5167\u7db2\uff09\u3002\u4eae\u6697\u5169\u5957\u8ddf\u7cfb\u7d71\u3002 */\n\n:root {\n  --bg: #f3f5f8;            /* \u9801\u9762\u5e95 */\n  --surface: #ffffff;       /* \u5361\u7247 / \u5074\u6b04 */\n  --surface-2: #f8fafc;     /* \u8868\u982d\u3001\u8f38\u5165\u5e95 */\n  --line: #e3e8ef;\n  --line-strong: #cbd3de;\n  --fg: #141a22;\n  --fg-2: #4b5563;          /* \u6b21\u8981\u6587\u5b57 */\n  --fg-3: #8a94a3;          /* \u8f14\u52a9\u6587\u5b57\u3001placeholder */\n  --accent: #0b6e74;        /* \u6df1\u9752 */\n  --accent-hover: #095a5f;\n  --accent-soft: #e4f3f3;\n  --on-accent: #ffffff;\n  --ok: #1f7a4d;   --ok-soft: #e6f4ec;\n  --warn: #9a5b00; --warn-soft: #fdf1dc;\n  --fail: #b42318; --fail-soft: #fde9e7;\n  --skip: #64707f; --skip-soft: #eef1f5;\n  --focus: #0b6e74;\n  --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(20, 26, 34, .06);\n  --radius: 10px; --radius-sm: 6px;\n  --sidebar: 232px;\n  --font: -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", system-ui, \"Noto Sans TC\", \"PingFang TC\", \"Microsoft JhengHei\", sans-serif;\n  --mono: ui-monospace, \"SF Mono\", \"Cascadia Code\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n  color-scheme: light;\n}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n  :root:not([data-theme=\"light\"]) {\n    --bg: #0e1217; --surface: #151a21; --surface-2: #1b212a; --line: #262e39; --line-strong: #34404e;\n    --fg: #e6eaf0; --fg-2: #a7b1be; --fg-3: #6f7a89;\n    --accent: #3fb3b9; --accent-hover: #5cc3c8; --accent-soft: #123237; --on-accent: #06181a;\n    --ok: #4fc47f; --ok-soft: #10281b; --warn: #e9a73b; --warn-soft: #2d2208;\n    --fail: #f27a70; --fail-soft: #331513; --skip: #8d98a7; --skip-soft: #1d242d;\n    --focus: #3fb3b9; --shadow: none;\n    color-scheme: dark;\n  }\n}\n\n/* ---------- reset / base ---------- */\n*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\nhtml, body { height: 100%; }\nbody { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 14px/1.55 var(--font); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }\na { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; } a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\nh1, h2, h3 { margin: 0; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.01em; text-wrap: balance; }\nh1 { font-size: 20px; } h2 { font-size: 14px; } h3 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--fg-3); font-weight: 600; }\np { margin: 0; }\ncode, .mono { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; }\ncode { background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 5px; }\n.num, table td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n.muted { color: var(--fg-2); } .faint { color: var(--fg-3); }\n.small { font-size: 12.5px; } .tiny { font-size: 11.5px; }\n.ok { color: var(--ok); } .warn { color: var(--warn); } .err, .fail { color: var(--fail); }\n:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 4px; }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; } }\n\n/* ---------- app shell ---------- */\n.shell { display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--sidebar) 1fr; min-height: 100%; }\n.sidebar { position: sticky; top: 0; height: 100vh; background: var(--surface); border-right: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 18px 14px; gap: 18px; }\n.brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 0 8px; color: var(--fg); } .brand:hover { text-decoration: none; }\n.brand .mark { width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); display: grid; place-items: center; font: 700 12px var(--mono); flex: none; }\n.brand b { font-size: 14px; display: block; line-height: 1.2; } .brand span { display: block; font-size: 11px; color: var(--fg-3); }\n.nav { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }\n.nav a, .nav .soon { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 8px 10px; border-radius: 8px; color: var(--fg-2); font-weight: 500; }\n.nav a:hover { background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; }\n.nav a.on { background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent); }\n.nav svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; flex: none; stroke: currentColor; fill: none; stroke-width: 1.8; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }\n.nav .soon { color: var(--fg-3); cursor: not-allowed; }\n.side-foot { margin-top: auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; padding: 0 4px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-3); }\n.side-foot .chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }\n.side-foot .dot { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ok); } .side-foot .dot.open { background: var(--warn); }\n\n.main { min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }\n.page-head { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 22px 32px 14px; }\n.page-head .t { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; min-width: 0; }\n.page-head .sub { color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 13px; max-width: 72ch; }\n.page-head .actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n.content { padding: 0 32px 40px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }\n.notices { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; padding: 0 32px; }\n.notices:empty { display: none; }\n.notice { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start; padding: 9px 12px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font-size: 13px; border: 1px solid; margin-bottom: 8px; }\n.notice.warn { background: var(--warn-soft); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 30%, transparent); color: var(--warn); }\n.notice.fail { background: var(--fail-soft); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fail) 30%, transparent); color: var(--fail); }\n.notice.info { background: var(--accent-soft); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 30%, transparent); color: var(--accent); }\n.notice.ok { background: var(--ok-soft); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ok) 30%, transparent); color: var(--ok); }\n.notice svg { width: 15px; height: 15px; flex: none; margin-top: 2px; stroke: currentColor; fill: none; stroke-width: 1.8; }\n.notice a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; }\n\n/* ---------- layout helpers ---------- */\n.grid { display: grid; gap: 16px; }\n.grid.cols-2 { grid-template-columns: 1.45fr 1fr; } .grid.cols-eq { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }\n.stack { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; min-width: 0; }\n.row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; } .row.between { justify-content: space-between; }\n.right { text-align: right; }\n\n/* ---------- cards ---------- */\n.card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); box-shadow: var(--shadow); min-width: 0; }\n.card > .hd, .card > form > .hd { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 12px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n.card > .hd .meta, .card > form > .hd .meta { color: var(--fg-3); font-size: 12.5px; }\n.card > .bd, .card > form > .bd { padding: 14px 16px; } .card > .bd.flush, .card > form > .bd.flush { padding: 0; }\n.card > .bd + .bd { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }\n.card.narrow { max-width: 400px; width: 100%; }\n.empty { padding: 26px 16px; text-align: center; color: var(--fg-3); font-size: 13px; }\n\n/* ---------- stat tiles ---------- */\n.tiles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 12px; }\n.tile { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 14px 16px 12px 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }\n.tile::before { content: \"\"; position: absolute; inset: 0 auto 0 0; width: 4px; background: var(--skip); }\n.tile.ok::before { background: var(--ok); } .tile.warn::before { background: var(--warn); } .tile.fail::before { background: var(--fail); }\n.tile .n { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1.1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n.tile .l { font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-3); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; }\n.tile.ok .n { color: var(--ok); } .tile.warn .n { color: var(--warn); } .tile.fail .n { color: var(--fail); } .tile.skip .n { color: var(--skip); }\n\n/* ---------- status pill ---------- */\n.pill { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 999px; font: 600 11px/18px var(--mono); letter-spacing: .02em; white-space: nowrap; background: var(--skip-soft); color: var(--skip); }\n.pill::before { content: \"\"; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: currentColor; }\n.pill.st-ok { background: var(--ok-soft); color: var(--ok); } .pill.st-warn { background: var(--warn-soft); color: var(--warn); }\n.pill.st-fail { background: var(--fail-soft); color: var(--fail); } .pill.st-skip { background: var(--skip-soft); color: var(--skip); }\n.pill.src-env { background: var(--warn-soft); color: var(--warn); } .pill.src-file { background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent); } .pill.src-default { background: var(--skip-soft); color: var(--skip); }\n.pill.plain::before { display: none; }\n\n/* ---------- tables ---------- */\ntable.tbl { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }\ntable.tbl th { text-align: left; font-weight: 500; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--fg-3); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; padding: 8px 16px; background: var(--surface-2); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); white-space: nowrap; }\ntable.tbl td { padding: 9px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }\ntable.tbl tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }\ntable.tbl tbody tr:hover td, table.tbl tr:hover td { background: var(--surface-2); }\ntable.tbl tr.grp:hover td { background: var(--surface-2); }\ntable.tbl td.k { white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 500; }\ntable.tbl td.v { color: var(--fg-2); word-break: break-word; }\ntable.tbl td.st { width: 1%; white-space: nowrap; }\ntable.tbl td.r { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }\ntable.tbl tr.grp td { background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--fg-3); font-size: 11.5px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; padding: 6px 16px; font-weight: 600; }\n.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }\n\n/* ---------- buttons / forms ---------- */\n.btn, button { font: 500 13px/1 var(--font); border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); background: var(--surface); color: var(--fg); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 7px 12px; cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; transition: background .12s, border-color .12s; }\n.btn:hover, button:hover { background: var(--surface-2); text-decoration: none; }\n.btn.primary, button.primary { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }\n.btn.primary:hover, button.primary:hover { background: var(--accent-hover); }\n.btn.ghost, button.ghost { background: transparent; border-color: transparent; color: var(--fg-2); }\n.btn.ghost:hover, button.ghost:hover { background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--fg); }\n.btn.danger, button.danger { color: var(--fail); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fail) 35%, transparent); } .btn.danger:hover, button.danger:hover { background: var(--fail-soft); }\n.btn.sm, button.sm { padding: 4px 9px; font-size: 12px; }\n.btn.xs, button.xs { padding: 2px 7px; font-size: 11.5px; }\nbutton[disabled] { opacity: .5; cursor: default; }\n.btn svg, button svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; stroke: currentColor; fill: none; stroke-width: 1.8; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }\nform.inline { display: inline; }\ninput[type=text], input[type=number], input[type=password], select, textarea { font: 13px var(--font); width: 100%; padding: 7px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--surface); color: var(--fg); transition: border-color .12s; }\ninput:focus, select:focus { border-color: var(--accent); outline: none; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--accent-soft); }\ninput::placeholder { color: var(--fg-3); }\n.field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; } .field label { font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-2); font-weight: 500; }\n.form-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; } .form-row > input, .form-row > select { width: auto; flex: 1 1 160px; }\n\n/* switch */\n.switch { position: relative; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; cursor: pointer; user-select: none; }\n.switch input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 0; height: 0; }\n.switch .track { width: 34px; height: 20px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--line-strong); position: relative; transition: background .15s; flex: none; }\n.switch .track::after { content: \"\"; position: absolute; top: 2px; left: 2px; width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; background: #fff; transition: transform .15s; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.25); }\n.switch input:checked + .track { background: var(--accent); } .switch input:checked + .track::after { transform: translateX(14px); }\n.switch input:focus-visible + .track { outline: 2px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 2px; }\n.switch .val { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-2); min-width: 36px; }\n\n/* ---------- settings ---------- */\n.toc { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n.toc a { padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--fg-2); } .toc a:hover { color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; border-color: var(--line-strong); }\n.group .hd .doc { color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 400; }\ntable.fields { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }\ntable.fields tr + tr td, table.fields tr + tr th { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }\ntable.fields th, table.fields td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 12px 16px; }\ntable.fields th { width: 44%; font-weight: 400; }\ntable.fields th .k { font: 600 12.5px var(--mono); color: var(--fg); }\ntable.fields th .d { color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 12.5px; margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45; }\ntable.fields th .def { color: var(--fg-3); font-size: 11.5px; margin-top: 3px; }\ntable.fields td.ctl input[type=text], table.fields td.ctl input[type=number], table.fields td.ctl select { max-width: 460px; }\ntable.fields td.src { width: 1%; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right; }\ntr.locked td.ctl { color: var(--fg-2); } tr.locked .mono { color: var(--fg); }\ntr.has-err td.ctl input, tr.has-err td.ctl select { border-color: var(--fail); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--fail-soft); }\n.ferr { color: var(--fail); font-size: 12px; margin-top: 5px; }\n.hint { color: var(--fg-3); font-size: 11.5px; margin-top: 4px; }\n.hint svg, .saved svg, .meta svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; vertical-align: -2px; stroke: currentColor; fill: none; stroke-width: 1.8; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }\n.confirm { display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--warn); }\n.confirm input { width: auto; }\n.saved { color: var(--ok); font-size: 12.5px; display: inline-flex; gap: 5px; align-items: center; }\n\n/* ---------- lists ---------- */\n.item { padding: 12px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; } .item:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }\n.item .ttl { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n.item .ttl b { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; }\n.item ul { margin: 4px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--fg-2); } .item li { margin: 2px 0; }\n.item .meta { font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-3); }\ndetails summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 12.5px; list-style: none; display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\ndetails summary::before { content: \"\u25b8\"; font-size: 10px; } details[open] summary::before { content: \"\u25be\"; }\ndetails summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }\npre { margin: 0; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 12px 14px; overflow: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; font: 12.5px/1.5 var(--mono); }\npre.tall { max-height: 70vh; }\n.kv { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 6px 14px; font-size: 13px; margin: 0; } .kv dt { color: var(--fg-3); } .kv dd { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-2); min-width: 0; word-break: break-word; }\n.sev { font: 600 11px var(--mono); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; } .sev.error { background: var(--fail-soft); color: var(--fail); } .sev.warning { background: var(--warn-soft); color: var(--warn); } .sev.info { background: var(--skip-soft); color: var(--skip); }\n.tag { font: 11.5px var(--mono); color: var(--fg-3); }\n\n/* ---------- setup ---------- */\n.step { border-left: 4px solid var(--skip); } .step.st-ok { border-left-color: var(--ok); } .step.st-warn { border-left-color: var(--warn); } .step.st-fail { border-left-color: var(--fail); }\n.step .hd .idx { width: 24px; height: 24px; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-grid; place-items: center; font: 600 12px var(--mono); background: var(--skip-soft); color: var(--skip); margin-right: 8px; vertical-align: middle; }\n.step.st-ok .hd .idx { background: var(--ok-soft); color: var(--ok); } .step.st-warn .hd .idx { background: var(--warn-soft); color: var(--warn); } .step.st-fail .hd .idx { background: var(--fail-soft); color: var(--fail); }\n\n/* ---------- login ---------- */\n.login { display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 100vh; padding: 24px; }\n\n/* ---------- responsive ---------- */\n@media (max-width: 1100px) { .grid.cols-2, .grid.cols-eq { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .tiles { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }\n@media (max-width: 820px) {\n  .shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  .sidebar { position: static; height: auto; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 10px 14px; gap: 10px; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  .brand span { display: none; }\n  .nav { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px; } .nav a, .nav .soon { padding: 6px 9px; } .nav a span, .nav .soon span { display: none; }\n  .side-foot { margin-top: 0; margin-left: auto; flex-direction: row; }\n  .page-head, .content, .notices { padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px; }\n  table.fields th { width: 50%; } .mono, code { word-break: break-all; }\n}\n\n\n/* ======================================================================\n   v2 \u7248\u9762\uff1a\u72c0\u614b\u9801\u8207\u8a2d\u5b9a\u9801\u4e0d\u518d\u662f\u300c\u4e00\u5806\u5361\u7247\u300d\u3002\n   \u72c0\u614b\u9801 = \u4e00\u53e5\u7d50\u8ad6 \u2192 \u9700\u8981\u8655\u7406 \u2192 \u9935\u6599 \uff5c \u53f3\u6b04\u6d3b\u52d5\u6642\u9593\u8ef8\u3001\u6392\u7a0b\u3002\n   \u8a2d\u5b9a\u9801 = \u5de6\u5074\u6bb5\u843d\u7d22\u5f15 \uff5c \u4f9d\u4efb\u52d9\u5206\u6bb5\u3001\u6bcf\u6b04\u4e00\u5217\u4e09\u683c\uff08\u8aaa\u660e / \u63a7\u4ef6 / \u72c0\u614b\uff09\u3001\u5e95\u90e8\u672a\u5957\u7528\u5217\u3002\n   ====================================================================== */\n\n/* ---- \u72c0\u614b\uff1a\u7d50\u8ad6\u5e36 ---- */\n.verdict { display: flex; align-items: stretch; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; padding: 22px 26px; border-radius: var(--radius); border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); border-left-width: 6px; }\n.verdict.ok { border-left-color: var(--ok); } .verdict.degraded { border-left-color: var(--warn); } .verdict.down { border-left-color: var(--fail); }\n.verdict-title { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1.15; }\n.verdict.ok .verdict-title { color: var(--ok); } .verdict.degraded .verdict-title { color: var(--warn); } .verdict.down .verdict-title { color: var(--fail); }\n.verdict-why { color: var(--fg-2); margin-top: 6px; max-width: 60ch; }\n.verdict-side { display: flex; gap: 28px; align-items: center; }\n.verdict-side > div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; min-width: 72px; }\n.verdict-side .num { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1.1; }\n.verdict-side span:last-child { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--fg-3); }\n\n/* ---- \u72c0\u614b\uff1a\u5169\u6b04 ---- */\n.two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(300px, 1fr); gap: 32px; align-items: start; }\n.col-main, .col-side { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 28px; min-width: 0; }\n.block { min-width: 0; }\n.block-hd { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); margin-bottom: 10px; }\n.block-hd h2 { font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em; color: var(--fg-2); font-weight: 600; }\n.quiet { color: var(--fg-3); padding: 10px 0; }\n\n/* ---- \u9700\u8981\u8655\u7406 ---- */\nol.todo { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }\nol.todo li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 10px minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 14px; align-items: start; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\nol.todo li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }\n.todo-mark { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; margin-top: 5px; background: var(--warn); }\nol.todo li.fail .todo-mark { background: var(--fail); }\n.todo-title { font-weight: 600; }\n.todo-detail { color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 12.5px; margin-top: 2px; word-break: break-word; }\n.tag-block { display: inline-block; margin-left: 6px; font: 600 10.5px var(--mono); letter-spacing: .04em; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--fail-soft); color: var(--fail); vertical-align: middle; }\ndetails.healthy { margin-top: 14px; }\ndetails.healthy summary { color: var(--fg-3); }\nul.healthy-list { margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 0 0 0 4px; list-style: none; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--fg-2); columns: 2; column-gap: 24px; }\nul.healthy-list li { padding: 2px 0; break-inside: avoid; }\n\n/* ---- \u9935\u6599 facts ---- */\ndl.facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 8px 18px; margin: 0; font-size: 13px; }\ndl.facts dt { color: var(--fg-3); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; padding-top: 1px; }\ndl.facts dd { margin: 0; min-width: 0; word-break: break-word; }\n\n/* ---- \u6d3b\u52d5\u6642\u9593\u8ef8 ---- */\nol.feed { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\nol.feed li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px; padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\nol.feed li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }\n.feed-when { color: var(--fg-3); font-size: 11.5px; padding-top: 2px; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n.feed-body { padding-left: 12px; border-left: 2px solid var(--line); min-width: 0; }\nol.feed li.ok .feed-body { border-left-color: var(--ok); } ol.feed li.fail .feed-body { border-left-color: var(--fail); }\n.feed-title { font-size: 13px; } .feed-title a { color: var(--fg); } .feed-title a:hover { color: var(--accent); }\n.feed-detail { color: var(--fg-3); font-size: 12px; margin-top: 1px; word-break: break-word; }\nul.plain { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }\n\n/* ---- \u8a2d\u5b9a\uff1a\u7248\u9762 ---- */\n.settings-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 180px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 32px; align-items: start; }\n.section-index { position: sticky; top: 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }\n.section-index a { padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 6px; color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 13px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }\n.section-index a:hover { background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; }\n.section-index .count { font: 600 10.5px var(--mono); background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent); border-radius: 999px; padding: 1px 6px; }\n.index-foot { margin-top: 12px; padding: 0 10px; word-break: break-all; }\n.settings-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 36px; min-width: 0; }\n.task-hd { margin-bottom: 10px; } .task-hd h2 { font-size: 16px; } .task-hd p { margin-top: 2px; }\n.task { scroll-margin-top: 16px; }\nsection.group { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 12px 0 6px; }\nsection.group.dirty { border-top-color: var(--accent); }\n.group-hd { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding-bottom: 8px; }\n.group-name { font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px; color: var(--fg); }\n.fields { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }\n.field-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr) 118px; gap: 20px; align-items: start; padding: 11px 0; border-top: 1px dashed var(--line); }\n.field-row:first-child { border-top: 0; }\n.field-row[hidden] { display: none; }\n.field-label label { font-weight: 500; display: block; }\n.field-env { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--fg-3); margin-top: 1px; }\n.field-desc { font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-2); margin-top: 4px; line-height: 1.45; }\n.field-ctl input[type=text], .field-ctl input[type=number], .field-ctl select { max-width: 420px; }\n.field-state { text-align: right; padding-top: 6px; white-space: nowrap; }\n.field-row.locked .field-ctl { color: var(--fg-2); }\n.field-row.modified .field-label label { color: var(--accent); }\n.field-row.has-err .field-ctl input, .field-row.has-err .field-ctl select { border-color: var(--fail); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--fail-soft); }\n.search { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 0 8px; background: var(--surface); }\n.search svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; stroke: var(--fg-3); fill: none; stroke-width: 1.8; }\n.search input { border: 0; width: 280px; padding: 6px 2px; background: transparent; } .search input:focus { box-shadow: none; }\n.toggle-mod { display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--fg-2); } .toggle-mod input { width: auto; }\n.dirty-bar { position: sticky; bottom: 0; margin: 0 -32px -40px; padding: 10px 32px; background: var(--surface); border-top: 1px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; box-shadow: 0 -4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,.06); z-index: 5; }\n.dirty-bar[hidden] { display: none; }\n\n@media (max-width: 1100px) { .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .settings-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .section-index { position: static; flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; } ul.healthy-list { columns: 1; } }\n@media (max-width: 820px) { .verdict { flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; } .field-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; } .field-state { text-align: left; } .search input { width: 160px; } .dirty-bar { margin: 0 -16px -40px; padding: 10px 16px; } }\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/static/console.js","perm":"0644","sha":"3e2cebe8097239fb4eb4e8a4fd5ecfd5833a69fc562b519de4be819f12e46c16","data":"/* console.js \u2014\u2014 \u7121\u4f9d\u8cf4\u3002\u4e09\u4ef6\u4e8b\uff1a\u8868\u55ae\u975e\u540c\u6b65\u5957\u7528\u3001\u8a2d\u5b9a\u9801\u7684\u641c\u5c0b / \u53ea\u770b\u5df2\u4fee\u6539 / \u9084\u539f / \u672a\u5957\u7528\u5217\u3001switch \u6587\u5b57\u3002 */\n(function () {\n  function swapTemplates(root) {\n    root.querySelectorAll('template[data-swap]').forEach(function (t) {\n      var target = document.querySelector(t.getAttribute('data-swap'));\n      if (target) target.innerHTML = t.innerHTML;\n      t.remove();\n    });\n  }\n\n  /* ---- \u975e\u540c\u6b65\u5957\u7528\uff1aPOST \u5f8c\u7528\u56de\u4f86\u7684 HTML \u53d6\u4ee3\u8a72 group ---- */\n  function submitAsync(form) {\n    var btn = form.querySelector('.group-hd button:not([type=button])') || form.querySelector('button.primary');\n    if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = '\u5957\u7528\u4e2d\u2026'; }\n    return fetch(form.action, { method: 'POST', body: new FormData(form), credentials: 'same-origin' })\n      .then(function (r) { if (r.redirected) { location.href = r.url; return ''; } return r.text(); })\n      .then(function (html) {\n        if (!html) return;\n        var box = document.createElement('div');\n        box.innerHTML = html;\n        swapTemplates(box);\n        var fresh = box.querySelector('section.group') || box.firstElementChild;\n        var old = form.closest('section.group');\n        old.replaceWith(fresh);\n        bind(fresh);\n        applyFilters();\n        updateDirty();\n      })\n      .catch(function (e) { if (btn) { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = '\u5957\u7528'; } console.error(e); });\n  }\n\n  /* ---- \u672a\u5957\u7528\u5075\u6e2c ---- */\n  function currentValue(el) {\n    if (el.type === 'checkbox') return el.checked ? 'on' : '';\n    return el.value;\n  }\n  function dirtyGroups() {\n    var out = [];\n    document.querySelectorAll('section.group').forEach(function (g) {\n      var dirty = false;\n      g.querySelectorAll('[data-initial]').forEach(function (el) {\n        if (currentValue(el) !== el.getAttribute('data-initial')) dirty = true;\n      });\n      g.classList.toggle('dirty', dirty);\n      if (dirty) out.push(g);\n    });\n    return out;\n  }\n  function updateDirty() {\n    var bar = document.getElementById('dirty-bar');\n    if (!bar) return;\n    var d = dirtyGroups();\n    bar.hidden = d.length === 0;\n    var t = document.getElementById('dirty-text');\n    if (t && d.length) t.textContent = d.length + ' \u500b\u5340\u6bb5\u6709\u672a\u5957\u7528\u8b8a\u66f4\uff1a' + d.map(function (g) { return g.getAttribute('data-group'); }).join('\u3001');\n  }\n\n  /* ---- \u641c\u5c0b / \u53ea\u770b\u5df2\u4fee\u6539 ---- */\n  function applyFilters() {\n    var q = (document.getElementById('settings-search') || {}).value || '';\n    q = q.trim().toLowerCase();\n    var onlyMod = (document.getElementById('only-modified') || {}).checked;\n    document.querySelectorAll('section.task').forEach(function (task) {\n      var taskVisible = false;\n      task.querySelectorAll('section.group').forEach(function (g) {\n        var any = false;\n        g.querySelectorAll('.field-row').forEach(function (row) {\n          var hit = (!q || (row.getAttribute('data-search') || '').indexOf(q) >= 0)\n                 && (!onlyMod || row.classList.contains('modified') || row.classList.contains('dirty'));\n          row.hidden = !hit;\n          if (hit) any = true;\n        });\n        g.hidden = !any;\n        if (any) taskVisible = true;\n      });\n      if (task.id !== 'changes') task.hidden = !taskVisible;\n    });\n  }\n\n  function bind(root) {\n    root.querySelectorAll('form[data-async]').forEach(function (form) {\n      form.addEventListener('submit', function (ev) { ev.preventDefault(); submitAsync(form); });\n    });\n    root.querySelectorAll('label.switch input').forEach(function (cb) {\n      cb.addEventListener('change', function () {\n        var v = cb.parentElement.querySelector('.val');\n        if (v) v.textContent = cb.checked ? 'true' : 'false';\n      });\n    });\n    root.querySelectorAll('[data-initial]').forEach(function (el) {\n      el.addEventListener('input', updateDirty);\n      el.addEventListener('change', updateDirty);\n    });\n    root.querySelectorAll('button.reset').forEach(function (b) {\n      b.addEventListener('click', function () {\n        var row = b.closest('.field-row');\n        var el = row.querySelector('[data-initial]');\n        if (!el) return;\n        var def = b.getAttribute('data-default') || '';\n        if (el.type === 'checkbox') { el.checked = def === 'true'; el.dispatchEvent(new Event('change')); }\n        else { el.value = ''; el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input')); }\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  bind(document);\n  var s = document.getElementById('settings-search');\n  if (s) s.addEventListener('input', applyFilters);\n  var m = document.getElementById('only-modified');\n  if (m) m.addEventListener('change', applyFilters);\n  var apply = document.getElementById('dirty-apply');\n  if (apply) apply.addEventListener('click', function () {\n    var forms = dirtyGroups().map(function (g) { return g.querySelector('form[data-async]'); });\n    (function next() { var f = forms.shift(); if (f) submitAsync(f).then(next); })();\n  });\n  var discard = document.getElementById('dirty-discard');\n  if (discard) discard.addEventListener('click', function () { location.reload(); });\n})();\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/status.py","perm":"0644","sha":"852733a992dd02a840bd2e5d0a5575b86800e35a8931f0b62de4eb679068084b","data":"\"\"\"status \u2014\u2014 \u628a\u300c\u6aa2\u67e5\u7d50\u679c\u300d\u7ffb\u6210\u7dad\u904b\u8005\u8981\u7684\u4e09\u500b\u7b54\u6848\uff1a\u73fe\u5728\u80fd\u4e0d\u80fd\u5be9\uff1f\u8981\u8655\u7406\u4ec0\u9ebc\uff1f\u6700\u8fd1\u767c\u751f\u4ec0\u9ebc\uff1f\n\ndoctor \u56de\u7684\u662f\u4e00\u5f35\u8868\uff08group / name / OK|WARN|FAIL|SKIP / detail\uff09\uff0c\u90a3\u662f\u5de5\u7a0b\u5e2b\u7684\u8996\u89d2\u3002\n\u7dad\u904b\u8005\u6253\u958b\u9996\u9801\u8981\u7684\u662f\uff1a\n  1. \u4e00\u53e5\u7d50\u8ad6\uff1a\u53ef\u4ee5\u5be9\u67e5 / \u53ef\u4ee5\u5be9\u67e5\u4f46\u6709\u72c0\u6cc1 / \u73fe\u5728\u7121\u6cd5\u5be9\u67e5\uff0c\u52a0\u4e00\u53e5\u70ba\u4ec0\u9ebc\u3002\n  2. \u9700\u8981\u8655\u7406\u7684\u6e05\u55ae\uff1a\u6bcf\u4e00\u9805\u7528\u4eba\u8a71\u8aaa\u662f\u4ec0\u9ebc\u554f\u984c\u3001\u56b4\u91cd\u5230\u4ec0\u9ebc\u7a0b\u5ea6\u3001\u6309\u54ea\u88e1\u53bb\u8655\u7406\u3002\n     \u6b63\u5e38\u7684\u9805\u76ee\u6536\u8d77\u4f86\uff0c\u4e0d\u4f54\u7248\u9762\u3002\n  3. \u6700\u8fd1\u6d3b\u52d5\uff1areview\u3001\u5c0d ADO \u7684\u5beb\u5165\u3001\u6392\u7a0b\u3001\u8a2d\u5b9a\u6539\u52d5\u5408\u6210\u4e00\u689d\u6642\u9593\u8ef8\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport time\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom shared import doctor\n\n# FAIL \u5728\u9019\u5e7e\u7d44 = \u9019\u4e00\u523b\u4e00\u689d review \u90fd\u8dd1\u4e0d\u4e86\nBLOCKING_GROUPS = {\"settings\", \"services\", \"llm\", \"ado\", \"python\"}\n\n# (group, name) \u2192 (\u4eba\u8a71\u6a19\u984c, \u52d5\u4f5c\u6a19\u7c64, \u52d5\u4f5c\u9023\u7d50)\u3002\u6c92\u5217\u7684\u7528 fallback\u3002\n_HUMAN: dict[tuple[str, str], tuple[str, str, str]] = {\n    (\"settings\", \"parse\"): (\"\u8a2d\u5b9a\u89e3\u6790\u5931\u6557\", \"\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings\"),\n    (\"settings\", \"smell\"): (\"\u8a2d\u5b9a\u542b\u77db\u76fe\u6216\u5df2\u5ee2\u68c4\u7684\u8b8a\u6578\", \"\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings\"),\n    (\"python\", \"interpreter\"): (\"Python \u7248\u672c\u4e0d\u7b26\uff08\u9700 \u2265 3.10\uff09\", \"\", \"\"),\n    (\"python\", \"dependencies\"): (\"Python \u4f9d\u8cf4\u7f3a\u5931\", \"\", \"\"),\n    (\"python\", \"semgrep\"): (\"semgrep \u4e0d\u5728 PATH\uff1b\u975c\u614b\u6383\u63cf\u505c\u7528\", \"\u975c\u614b\u6383\u63cf\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-static\"),\n    (\"python\", \"ruff\"): (\"ruff \u4e0d\u5728 PATH\uff1bPython \u975c\u614b\u6383\u63cf\u505c\u7528\", \"\u975c\u614b\u6383\u63cf\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-static\"),\n    (\"paths\", \"REPOS_ROOT\"): (\"REPOS_ROOT \u7121\u6548\", \"\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-repos\"),\n    (\"paths\", \"RULES_ROOT\"): (\"RULES_ROOT \u7121\u6548\", \"\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-rules\"),\n    (\"paths\", \"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT\"): (\"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u7121\u6548\", \"\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-knowledge\"),\n    (\"paths\", \"DATA_DIR\"): (\"DATA_DIR \u4e0d\u53ef\u5beb\uff1breview \u8a18\u9304\u505c\u7528\", \"\u670d\u52d9\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-orchestrator\"),\n    (\"services\", \"orchestrator\"): (\"orchestrator \u7121\u56de\u61c9\", \"\", \"\"),\n    (\"services\", \"code graph \u2463\"): (\"code graph \u7121\u6cd5\u9023\u7dda\uff1bimpact radius \u505c\u7528\", \"graph \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-graph\"),\n    (\"jobs\", \"repo-sync\"): (\"repo-sync \u4e0a\u6b21\u57f7\u884c\u5931\u6557\", \"\u6aa2\u8996\", \"/console/sources#repos\"),\n    (\"jobs\", \"harvest\"): (\"harvest \u4e0a\u6b21\u57f7\u884c\u5931\u6557\", \"\u6aa2\u8996\", \"/console/knowledge\"),\n    (\"langfuse\", \"health\"): (\"Langfuse \u7121\u6cd5\u9023\u7dda\", \"Langfuse \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-langfuse\"),\n    (\"langfuse\", \"keys\"): (\"Langfuse \u6191\u8b49\u9a57\u8b49\u5931\u6557\", \"Langfuse \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-langfuse\"),\n    (\"llm\", \"gateway\"): (\"LLM gateway \u7121\u6cd5\u9023\u7dda\", \"LLM \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-llm\"),\n    (\"llm\", \"LLM_MODEL\"): (\"LLM_MODEL \u4e0d\u5728 gateway \u6a21\u578b\u6e05\u55ae\", \"LLM \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-llm\"),\n    (\"llm\", \"LLM_MODEL_ADVERSARY\"): (\"LLM_MODEL_ADVERSARY \u4e0d\u5728 gateway \u6a21\u578b\u6e05\u55ae\", \"LLM \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-llm\"),\n    (\"llm\", \"LLM_MODEL_DIGEST\"): (\"LLM_MODEL_DIGEST \u4e0d\u5728 gateway \u6a21\u578b\u6e05\u55ae\", \"LLM \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-llm\"),\n    (\"ado\", \"ADO_PAT\"): (\"ADO_PAT \u672a\u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"ADO \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-ado\"),\n    (\"ado\", \"reach\"): (\"Azure DevOps API \u7121\u6cd5\u5b58\u53d6\", \"ADO \u8a2d\u5b9a\", \"/console/settings#g-ado\"),\n    (\"systemd\", \"retired units\"): (\"\u5df2\u5ee2\u68c4\u7684 systemd unit \u4ecd\u555f\u7528\", \"\", \"\"),\n}\n\n_SEV_RANK = {\"FAIL\": 0, \"WARN\": 1}\n\n\ndef headline(checks: list[doctor.Check]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    fails = [c for c in checks if c.status == doctor.FAIL]\n    warns = [c for c in checks if c.status == doctor.WARN]\n    hard = [c for c in fails if c.group in BLOCKING_GROUPS]\n    if hard:\n        why = _title(hard[0])\n        more = f\"\uff1b\u53e6 {len(hard) - 1} \u9805\" if len(hard) > 1 else \"\"\n        return {\"state\": \"down\", \"title\": \"\u670d\u52d9\u4e0d\u53ef\u7528\", \"why\": f\"{why}{more}\u3002review \u7121\u6cd5\u57f7\u884c\u3002\",\n                \"fails\": len(fails), \"warns\": len(warns)}\n    if fails or warns:\n        parts = []\n        if fails:\n            parts.append(f\"{len(fails)} \u9805\u6545\u969c\")\n        if warns:\n            parts.append(f\"{len(warns)} \u9805\u8b66\u544a\")\n        return {\"state\": \"degraded\", \"title\": \"\u964d\u7d1a\u904b\u4f5c\", \"why\": \"\u3001\".join(parts) + \"\u3002review \u53ef\u57f7\u884c\uff0c\u90e8\u5206\u80fd\u529b\u505c\u7528\u3002\",\n                \"fails\": len(fails), \"warns\": len(warns)}\n    return {\"state\": \"ok\", \"title\": \"\u670d\u52d9\u5c31\u7dd2\", \"why\": \"\u6240\u6709\u6aa2\u67e5\u901a\u904e\u3002\", \"fails\": 0, \"warns\": 0}\n\n\ndef _title(c: doctor.Check) -> str:\n    h = _HUMAN.get((c.group, c.name))\n    if h:\n        return h[0]\n    if c.group == \"systemd\":\n        return f\"systemd unit {c.name} \u975e active\"\n    return f\"{c.group}\uff1a{c.name}\"\n\n\ndef blockers(checks: list[doctor.Check]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"FAIL \u8207 WARN\uff0c\u6309\u56b4\u91cd\u5ea6\u3001\u518d\u6309\u300c\u64cb\u4e0d\u64cb review\u300d\u6392\u3002\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for c in checks:\n        if c.status not in _SEV_RANK:\n            continue\n        h = _HUMAN.get((c.group, c.name), (_title(c), \"\", \"\"))\n        out.append({\"sev\": c.status, \"blocking\": c.group in BLOCKING_GROUPS and c.status == doctor.FAIL,\n                    \"title\": h[0], \"detail\": c.detail, \"action\": h[1], \"href\": h[2],\n                    \"group\": c.group, \"name\": c.name})\n    out.sort(key=lambda b: (_SEV_RANK[b[\"sev\"]], not b[\"blocking\"]))\n    return out\n\n\ndef healthy(checks: list[doctor.Check]) -> list[doctor.Check]:\n    return [c for c in checks if c.status in (doctor.OK, doctor.SKIP)]\n\n\ndef feed(reviews: list[dict], audit: list[dict], jobs: dict[str, dict],\n         changes: list[dict], limit: int = 20) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\u56db\u7a2e\u4e8b\u4ef6\u5408\u6210\u4e00\u689d\u6642\u9593\u8ef8\uff0c\u65b0\u7684\u5728\u524d\u3002\u6bcf\u7b46\uff1ats / kind / title / detail / href / tone\u3002\"\"\"\n    ev: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for r in reviews:\n        tone = {\"done\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"fail\"}.get(r[\"status\"], \"neutral\")\n        if r[\"status\"] == \"done\":\n            detail = f\"{r['n_error']} error \u00b7 {r['n_warning']} warning \u00b7 {r['n_info']} info\"\n            if r.get(\"duration\"):\n                detail += f\" \u00b7 {int(r['duration'])}s\"\n        elif r[\"status\"] == \"error\":\n            detail = (r.get(\"error\") or \"\")[:120]\n        else:\n            detail = \"\u57f7\u884c\u4e2d\"\n        ev.append({\"ts\": r[\"started\"], \"kind\": \"review\", \"tone\": tone,\n                   \"title\": f\"Review {r['repo']}#{r['pr_id']}\" + (f\" \u00b7 {r['title']}\" if r.get(\"title\") else \"\"),\n                   \"detail\": detail, \"href\": f\"/console/reviews/{r['id']}\"})\n    for a in audit:\n        ev.append({\"ts\": a[\"ts\"], \"kind\": \"write\", \"tone\": \"ok\" if a[\"posted\"] else \"neutral\",\n                   \"title\": (\"\u5df2\u767c\u5e03 \" if a[\"posted\"] else \"Dry-run \u00b7 \") + (\"review comment\" if a[\"kind\"] == \"review\" else \"knowledge draft\"),\n                   \"detail\": f\"PR {a['pr_url'].rsplit('/', 1)[-1]} \u00b7 {a['note']}\", \"href\": \"\"})\n    for name, st in jobs.items():\n        if st.get(\"last_end\"):\n            ev.append({\"ts\": st[\"last_end\"], \"kind\": \"job\", \"tone\": \"ok\" if st.get(\"last_ok\") else \"fail\",\n                       \"title\": f\"{name} \u57f7\u884c\u5b8c\u6210\" if st.get(\"last_ok\") else f\"{name} \u57f7\u884c\u5931\u6557\",\n                       \"detail\": (st.get(\"last_error\") or f\"{len(st.get('last_detail') or [])} \u9805\")[:120],\n                       \"href\": \"/console/sources#repos\" if name == \"repo-sync\" else \"/console/knowledge\"})\n    for c in changes:\n        ev.append({\"ts\": c[\"ts\"], \"kind\": \"config\", \"tone\": \"neutral\",\n                   \"title\": f\"\u8a2d\u5b9a\u8b8a\u66f4 {c['env']}\", \"detail\": f\"{c['old']} \u2192 {c['new']} \u00b7 {c['actor']}\",\n                   \"href\": \"/console/settings#changes\"})\n    ev.sort(key=lambda e: e[\"ts\"], reverse=True)\n    return ev[:limit]\n\n\ndef ago(ts: float, now: float | None = None) -> str:\n    d = int((now or time.time()) - ts)\n    if d < 60:\n        return \"\u525b\u525b\"\n    if d < 3600:\n        return f\"{d // 60} \u5206\u524d\"\n    if d < 86400:\n        return f\"{d // 3600} \u5c0f\u6642\u524d\"\n    return f\"{d // 86400} \u5929\u524d\"\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/_changes.html","perm":"0644","sha":"2bdf6f697af07ab3683d6b47f72b88481c1102adae235f3e6d07bf43c7209c20","data":"<div id=\"changes-body\">\n{% if not changes %}<div class=\"empty\">\u5c1a\u7121\u8b8a\u66f4\u7d00\u9304\u3002</div>{% else %}\n<table class=\"tbl\">\n  <tr><th>\u6642\u9593</th><th>\u4f86\u6e90</th><th>\u8b8a\u6578</th><th>\u820a\u503c \u2192 \u65b0\u503c</th></tr>\n  {% for c in changes %}\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"faint\">{{ c.ts | int | datetime }}</td>\n    <td>{{ c.actor }}</td>\n    <td><code>{{ c.env }}</code></td>\n    <td class=\"v\"><span class=\"mono\">{{ c.old }}</span> \u2192 <span class=\"mono\">{{ c.new }}</span></td>\n  </tr>\n  {% endfor %}\n</table>{% endif %}\n</div>\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/_group.html","perm":"0644","sha":"962afcb5b413d00a248e07f05ef00840fc97d0328bc3d3fb06914082d46f3eba","data":"{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n<section class=\"group\" data-group=\"{{ g.name }}\">\n  <form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/settings/{{ g.name }}\" data-async>\n    <div class=\"group-hd\">\n      <div><span class=\"group-name mono\">{{ g.name }}</span> <span class=\"faint small\">{{ g.doc }}</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\">\n        {% if g.saved %}<span class=\"saved\">{{ ic.icon('check') }}\u5df2\u5957\u7528{% if g.applied %}\uff08{{ g.applied|length }} \u9805\uff09{% else %}\uff08\u7121\u8b8a\u52d5\uff09{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}\n        {% if g.restart_needed %}<span class=\"pill st-warn plain\">\u9700\u91cd\u555f\u751f\u6548</span>{% endif %}\n        <button class=\"sm\">\u5957\u7528</button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"fields\">\n      {% for f in g.fields %}\n      <div class=\"field-row {{ 'has-err' if f.error else '' }} {{ 'locked' if f.locked else '' }} {{ 'modified' if f.source == 'file' else '' }}\" data-search=\"{{ f.env|lower }} {{ f.label|lower }} {{ f.description|lower }}\">\n        <div class=\"field-label\">\n          <label for=\"{{ g.name }}-{{ f.name }}\">{{ f.label }}</label>\n          <div class=\"field-env mono\">{{ f.env }}</div>\n          {% if f.more %}<div class=\"field-desc\">{{ f.more }}</div>{% endif %}\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field-ctl\">\n          {% if f.kind == 'secret' %}\n            <span class=\"mono\">{{ f.masked }}</span>\n            <div class=\"hint\">{{ ic.icon('lock') }} Secret\uff1a\u50c5\u80fd\u7531 secrets.env \u8a2d\u5b9a</div>\n          {% elif f.locked %}\n            <span class=\"mono\">{{ f.value or '(unset)' }}</span>\n            <div class=\"hint\">\u7531\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\u8986\u5beb\uff08\u552f\u8b80\uff09\u3002\u79fb\u9664\u8a72\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\u5f8c\u65b9\u53ef\u7531\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u7ba1\u7406\u3002</div>\n          {% elif f.kind == 'bool' %}\n            <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_b_{{ f.name }}\" value=\"1\">\n            <label class=\"switch\"><input id=\"{{ g.name }}-{{ f.name }}\" type=\"checkbox\" name=\"{{ f.name }}\" data-initial=\"{{ 'on' if f.value == 'true' else '' }}\" {{ 'checked' if f.value == 'true' else '' }}><span class=\"track\"></span><span class=\"val\">{{ f.value }}</span></label>\n            {% if f.dangerous %}<label class=\"confirm\"><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"confirm_{{ f.name }}\"> \u78ba\u8a8d\uff1a\u6b64\u8b8a\u66f4\u5c07\u5c0d\u5916\u5beb\u5165\u6216\u505c\u7528\u5b89\u5168\u9632\u8b77</label>{% endif %}\n          {% elif f.kind == 'choice' %}\n            <select id=\"{{ g.name }}-{{ f.name }}\" name=\"{{ f.name }}\" data-initial=\"{{ f.value }}\">{% for c in f.choices %}<option value=\"{{ c }}\" {{ 'selected' if c == f.value else '' }}>{{ c }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>\n          {% elif f.kind == 'number' %}\n            <input id=\"{{ g.name }}-{{ f.name }}\" type=\"number\" name=\"{{ f.name }}\" value=\"{{ f.value }}\" data-initial=\"{{ f.value }}\" step=\"any\" {% if f.min is not none %}min=\"{{ f.min }}\"{% endif %} {% if f.max is not none %}max=\"{{ f.max }}\"{% endif %}>\n          {% else %}\n            <input id=\"{{ g.name }}-{{ f.name }}\" type=\"text\" name=\"{{ f.name }}\" value=\"{{ f.value }}\" data-initial=\"{{ f.value }}\" placeholder=\"{{ '\u5fc5\u586b' if f.required else '\u7559\u7a7a = \u9810\u8a2d\u503c' }}\">\n          {% endif %}\n          {% if f.error %}<div class=\"ferr\">{{ f.error }}</div>{% endif %}\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field-state\">\n          {% if f.source == 'file' %}<span class=\"pill plain src-file\">\u5df2\u8986\u5beb</span> <button type=\"button\" class=\"ghost xs reset\" data-default=\"{{ f.default_raw }}\" title=\"\u9084\u539f\u9810\u8a2d\u503c {{ f.default }}\">\u9084\u539f\u9810\u8a2d</button>\n          {% elif f.source.startswith('env:') %}<span class=\"pill plain src-env\" title=\"{{ f.source }}\">env</span>\n          {% else %}<span class=\"faint tiny\">\u9810\u8a2d {{ f.default }}</span>{% endif %}\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      {% endfor %}\n    </div>\n  </form>\n</section>\n{% if g.saved %}\n<template data-swap=\"#changes-body\">{% include \"_changes.html\" %}</template>\n<template data-swap=\"#notices\">{% for w in warnings %}<div class=\"notice warn\">{{ ic.icon('warn') }}<div>{{ w }}</div></div>{% endfor %}</template>\n{% endif %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/_icons.html","perm":"0644","sha":"ff96a946eb5e6015a7c2f8b9477ce212f32475a6f72f6f59a4fb6e21a4787c97","data":"{% macro icon(name) -%}\n{%- if name == 'overview' or name == 'status' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"7\" height=\"9\" rx=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"3\" width=\"7\" height=\"5\" rx=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"12\" width=\"7\" height=\"9\" rx=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"16\" width=\"7\" height=\"5\" rx=\"1.5\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'settings' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 7h10M18 7h2M4 17h4M12 17h8\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"7\" r=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"17\" r=\"2.5\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'sources' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"6\" r=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"18\" r=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"12\" r=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M6 8.5v7M8.3 7l7.4 4M8.3 17l7.4-4\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'reviews' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M5 4h10l4 4v12H5z\"/><path d=\"M15 4v4h4M8 13h8M8 17h5\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'knowledge' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 5.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 3H20v15H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 0 4 20.5z\"/><path d=\"M4 18.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 16H20\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'setup' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 3l1.8 3.6 4 .6-2.9 2.8.7 4L12 12.1 8.4 14l.7-4L6.2 7.2l4-.6z\"/><path d=\"M5 20h14\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'refresh' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M20 12a8 8 0 1 1-2.3-5.7\"/><path d=\"M20 4v5h-5\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'play' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M7 5l12 7-12 7z\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'warn' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M12 4l9 16H3z\"/><path d=\"M12 10v4M12 17v.5\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'lock' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"5\" y=\"11\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'check' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'search' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"11\" r=\"6.5\"/><path d=\"M20 20l-4.2-4.2\"/></svg>\n{%- elif name == 'ext' -%}<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M14 4h6v6M20 4l-9 9\"/><path d=\"M19 14v5a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H5a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5\"/></svg>\n{%- endif -%}\n{%- endmacro %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/base.html","perm":"0644","sha":"37a8d5cbc3bf3cf137576580656de602452fe7ebb3bf4e683d5f0552882d61fc","data":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"zh-Hant\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>{% block title %}{{ page }}{% endblock %} \u00b7 pr-review</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/console/static/console.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n{% if page == 'login' %}\n<div class=\"login\">{% block login %}{% endblock %}</div>\n{% else %}\n<div class=\"shell\">\n  <aside class=\"sidebar\">\n    <a class=\"brand\" href=\"/console\"><span class=\"mark\">PR</span><b>pr-review</b></a>\n    <nav class=\"nav\">\n      {% for key, label, href in nav %}\n      <a href=\"{{ href }}\" class=\"{{ 'on' if page == key else '' }}\">{{ ic.icon(key) }}<span>{{ label }}</span></a>\n      {% endfor %}\n    </nav>\n    <div class=\"side-foot\">\n      {% if open_mode %}<span class=\"chip\" title=\"ORCH_API_KEY \u672a\u8a2d\uff1a\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u5c0d\u5167\u7db2\u958b\u653e\"><span class=\"dot open\"></span>\u958b\u653e\u6a21\u5f0f</span>\n      {% else %}<span class=\"chip\"><span class=\"dot\"></span>\u5df2\u767b\u5165</span>\n      <form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/logout\" class=\"inline\"><button class=\"ghost xs\">\u767b\u51fa</button></form>{% endif %}\n    </div>\n  </aside>\n  <div class=\"main\">\n    <header class=\"page-head\">\n      <div class=\"t\">\n        <h1>{% block heading %}{{ page }}{% endblock %}</h1>\n        {% block subheading %}{% endblock %}\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"actions\">{% block actions %}{% endblock %}</div>\n    </header>\n    <div class=\"notices\" id=\"notices\">{% block notices %}{% endblock %}</div>\n    <main class=\"content\">\n    {% block body %}{% endblock %}\n    </main>\n  </div>\n</div>\n{% endif %}\n<script src=\"/console/static/console.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/knowledge.html","perm":"0644","sha":"cb2c033323deec54326bb12feb4c828221c59b184ba38b6eaa041912cd64afe2","data":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n{% block title %}\u77e5\u8b58\u5e33\u672c{% endblock %}\n{% block heading %}\u77e5\u8b58\u5e33\u672c{% endblock %}\n{% block subheading %}<div class=\"sub\">\u5f85\u88c1\u6c7a\u8349\u7a3f\u7b49\u5f85 PR \u7d42\u614b\uff1b\u66ab\u5b58\u689d\u76ee\u7b49\u5f85 release\u2192master \u9a57\u6536 PR \u6536\u53e3\uff08\u6c89\u9ed8\u5373\u843d\u5730\uff09\u3002\u6b64\u8655\u7684 reject / keep \u8207 PR comment \u7b49\u6548\u3002</div>{% endblock %}\n{% block actions %}\n{% if job %}<span class=\"faint small\">harvest {% if not job.enabled %}\u505c\u7528{% elif job.running %}\u57f7\u884c\u4e2d{% elif job.last_end %}\u4e0a\u6b21 {{ ((now - job.last_end)/60)|int }} min \u524d{% if job.last_ok %}\u6210\u529f{% else %}<span class=\"err\">\u5931\u6557</span>{% endif %}{% else %}\u5c1a\u672a\u57f7\u884c{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}\n<form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/jobs/harvest/run?back=/console/knowledge\" class=\"inline\"><button>{{ ic.icon('play') }}\u624b\u52d5\u57f7\u884c harvest</button></form>\n{% endblock %}\n{% block notices %}\n{% if not root %}<div class=\"notice warn\">{{ ic.icon('warn') }}<div>KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\u5b9a\u6216\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\uff1a\u77e5\u8b58\u8ff4\u5708\u505c\u7528\u3002<a href=\"/console/settings#g-knowledge\">\u524d\u5f80\u8a2d\u5b9a</a>\u3002</div></div>{% endif %}\n{% if msg %}<div class=\"notice ok\">{{ ic.icon('check') }}<div>{{ msg }}</div></div>{% endif %}\n{% endblock %}\n{% block body %}\n{% macro verdict(repo, kind, token, label, cls='xs') -%}\n<form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/knowledge/verdict\" class=\"inline\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"repo\" value=\"{{ repo }}\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"kind\" value=\"{{ kind }}\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"token\" value=\"{{ token }}\"><button class=\"{{ cls }} {{ 'danger' if kind == 'reject' else '' }}\">{{ label }}</button></form>\n{%- endmacro %}\n<div class=\"grid cols-2\">\n<div class=\"stack\">\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><h2>\u5f85\u88c1\u6c7a\u8349\u7a3f</h2><span class=\"meta\">_pending \u00b7 {{ pending|length }} \u7b46 \u00b7 active \u7b49\u5f85 / abandoned \u6368\u68c4 / completed \u9032\u5165\u66ab\u5b58</span></div>\n  <div class=\"bd flush\">\n  {% if not pending %}<div class=\"empty\">\u7121\u3002</div>{% endif %}\n  {% for p in pending %}\n  <div class=\"item\">\n    <div class=\"ttl\"><b>{{ p.repo }}#{{ p.pr_id }}</b>\n      <span class=\"row small\">\n        {% if p.posted %}<span class=\"pill st-ok plain\">\u5df2\u767c\u5e03</span>{% elif p.dry_run %}<span class=\"pill st-skip plain\">dry-run</span>{% elif p.post_failed %}<span class=\"pill st-fail plain\">\u767c\u5e03\u5931\u6557</span>{% endif %}\n        {% if p.redistilled %}<span class=\"pill plain\">\u5df2\u91cd\u65b0\u84b8\u993e</span>{% elif p.redistill_attempts %}<span class=\"pill st-warn plain\">\u91cd\u65b0\u84b8\u993e {{ p.redistill_attempts }}/2</span>{% endif %}\n        <span class=\"faint\">{{ p.created[:16] }}</span> <a href=\"{{ p.pr_url }}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PR</a>\n      </span></div>\n    <div class=\"small\">\u2192 {{ p.target_branch }} \u00b7 <span class=\"mono\">{{ p.draft.primary_entity }}</span> \u00b7 {{ p.draft.decisions|length }} \u6c7a\u7b56 \u00b7 {{ p.draft.invariants|length }} \u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f{% if p.contradicted %} \u00b7 <span class=\"warn\">\u9055\u53cd {{ p.contradicted|join(', ') }}</span>{% endif %}{% if p.dropped %} \u00b7 <span class=\"warn\">{{ p.dropped|length }} \u689d decision \u56e0\u8b49\u64da\u9a57\u8b49\u5931\u6557\u88ab\u6368\u68c4</span>{% endif %}</div>\n    <div class=\"meta\">{{ p.draft.ledger_line }}</div>\n  </div>\n  {% endfor %}\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><h2>\u66ab\u5b58\u689d\u76ee</h2><span class=\"meta\">_cycle \u00b7 {{ staged|length }} \u7b46 \u00b7 \u7b49\u5f85\u9a57\u6536 PR \u6536\u53e3\uff1b\u6c89\u9ed8\u5373\u843d\u5730</span></div>\n  <div class=\"bd flush\">\n  {% if not staged %}<div class=\"empty\">\u7121\u3002</div>{% endif %}\n  {% for it in staged %}\n  <div class=\"item\">\n    <div class=\"ttl\"><b>{{ it.repo }}#{{ it.pr_id }}</b>\n      <span class=\"row small\"><span class=\"pill plain\">{{ it.provenance }}</span><span class=\"faint\">\u2192 {{ it.target_branch }}</span> <a href=\"{{ it.pr_url }}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PR</a> {{ verdict(it.repo, 'reject', 'PR' ~ it.pr_id, 'reject entry') }}</span></div>\n    <div class=\"small\"><span class=\"mono\">{{ it.draft.primary_entity }}</span> \u2014 {{ it.draft.ledger_line }}</div>\n    <ul>\n      {% for d in it.draft.decisions %}<li>{{ d.text }} {% if d.id %}{{ verdict(it.repo, 'reject', d.id, 'reject') }}{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}\n      {% for i in it.draft.invariants %}<li>{{ i.text }} <code>{{ i.id }}</code> {{ verdict(it.repo, 'reject', i.id, 'reject') }}</li>{% endfor %}\n    </ul>\n    {% if it.contradicted %}\n    <div class=\"small warn\">\u5408\u4f75\u7684\u5be6\u4f5c\u9055\u53cd\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f {{ it.contradicted|join(', ') }}\uff1a\u6536\u53e3\u6642\u5c07\u8a3b\u92b7\uff0c\u9664\u975e keep\uff1a\n      {% for iid in it.contradicted %}{{ verdict(it.repo, 'keep', iid, 'keep ' ~ iid) }}{% endfor %}</div>\n    {% endif %}\n    {% if it.author_note %}<div class=\"meta\">\ud83d\udcac author: {{ it.author_note }}</div>{% endif %}\n  </div>\n  {% endfor %}\n  </div>\n</section>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"stack\">\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><h2>\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u88c1\u6c7a</h2><span class=\"meta\">\u5f85\u4e0b\u6b21 harvest \u5957\u7528</span></div>\n  <div class=\"bd flush\">\n  {% set any = namespace(v=false) %}\n  <table class=\"tbl\">\n  {% for repo, kinds in verdicts.items() %}{% for kind, toks in kinds.items() %}{% for tok, meta in toks.items() %}{% set any.v = true %}\n  <tr><td class=\"k mono\">{{ repo }}</td><td class=\"st\"><span class=\"pill plain {{ 'st-fail' if kind == 'reject' else 'st-ok' }}\">{{ kind }}</span></td><td><code>{{ tok }}</code> <span class=\"faint small\">{{ meta.by }} {{ meta.ts[:16] }}</span></td>\n    <td class=\"r\"><form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/knowledge/verdict/remove\" class=\"inline\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"repo\" value=\"{{ repo }}\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"kind\" value=\"{{ kind }}\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"token\" value=\"{{ tok }}\"><button class=\"ghost xs\">\u64a4\u56de</button></form></td></tr>\n  {% endfor %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}\n  </table>\n  {% if not any.v %}<div class=\"empty\">\u7121\u5f85\u5957\u7528\u88c1\u6c7a\u3002</div>{% endif %}\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"bd\">\n    <form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/knowledge/verdict\" class=\"form-row\">\n      <input type=\"text\" name=\"repo\" placeholder=\"repo\" required style=\"flex:0 1 140px\">\n      <select name=\"kind\" style=\"flex:0 1 110px\"><option>reject</option><option>keep</option></select>\n      <input type=\"text\" name=\"token\" placeholder=\"\u5be6\u9ad4\u540d / PR12 / PR12-I1\" required>\n      <button class=\"sm\">\u65b0\u589e</button>\n    </form>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><h2>\u9a57\u6536\u7a97</h2><span class=\"meta\">_state/cycle.json</span></div>\n  <div class=\"bd flush\">\n  {% if not cycle %}<div class=\"empty\">\u5c1a\u7121\u9a57\u6536 PR\u3002</div>{% else %}\n  <table class=\"tbl\">\n    {% for key, st in cycle.items() %}\n    <tr><td class=\"st\"><span class=\"pill {{ 'st-skip' if st.closed else 'st-ok' }}\">{{ '\u5df2\u6536\u53e3' if st.closed else '\u958b\u7a97\u4e2d' }}</span></td><td class=\"k mono\">{{ key }}</td><td class=\"v\">{% if st.listed %}\u5df2\u5217\u51fa {{ st.listed|join(', ') }}{% endif %}{% if st.note %} \u00b7 {{ st.note }}{% endif %}</td></tr>\n    {% endfor %}\n  </table>{% endif %}\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><h2>Digest \u9810\u89bd</h2><span class=\"meta\">\u8207\u9a57\u6536 PR \u4e0a\u7684 digest \u76f8\u540c\u6e32\u67d3\uff08\u4e0d\u542b LLM \u9867\u554f\u6bb5\uff09</span></div>\n  <div class=\"bd\">\n    <form method=\"get\" action=\"/console/knowledge\" class=\"form-row\">\n      <input type=\"text\" name=\"digest_repo\" value=\"{{ digest_repo }}\" placeholder=\"repo\" style=\"flex:0 1 200px\"><button class=\"sm\">\u9810\u89bd</button>\n    </form>\n    {% if digest %}<pre style=\"margin-top:12px\">{{ digest }}</pre>{% elif digest_repo %}<p class=\"muted small\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">\u6b64 repo \u7121\u66ab\u5b58\u689d\u76ee\u3002</p>{% endif %}\n  </div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n{% endblock %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/login.html","perm":"0644","sha":"c4f9421e0d39652b9f2d090d4b943b08e149afbf60ce804c06f15b7871d5a5cd","data":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% block title %}\u767b\u5165{% endblock %}\n{% block login %}\n<section class=\"card narrow\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><div class=\"brand\"><span class=\"mark\">PR</span><div><b>pr-review</b><span>operations console</span></div></div></div>\n  <div class=\"bd stack\">\n    <p class=\"muted small\">\u8f38\u5165 secrets.env \u4e2d\u7684 <code>ORCH_API_KEY</code>\u3002</p>\n    {% if error %}<div class=\"notice fail\">API key \u9a57\u8b49\u5931\u6557\u3002</div>{% endif %}\n    <form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/login\" class=\"stack\">\n      <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"next\" value=\"{{ next }}\">\n      <div class=\"field\"><label for=\"token\">ORCH_API_KEY</label><input id=\"token\" type=\"password\" name=\"token\" autofocus required></div>\n      <button class=\"primary\">\u767b\u5165</button>\n    </form>\n  </div>\n</section>\n{% endblock %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/review_detail.html","perm":"0644","sha":"c216ece6e83948fab450007ea81820af3d185294644dff5de79c2d4f75ca9beb","data":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n{% block title %}Review {{ r.id }}{% endblock %}\n{% block heading %}<a href=\"/console/reviews\" class=\"faint\">Reviews</a> / <span class=\"mono\">{{ r.repo }}#{{ r.pr_id }}</span>{% endblock %}\n{% block subheading %}<div class=\"sub\">{{ r.title or '' }}{% if r.title %} \u00b7 {% endif %}{{ r.started|datetime }} \u00b7 {{ r.user }} \u00b7 {{ r.pipeline or '' }}{% if r.duration %} \u00b7 {{ r.duration|int }}s{% endif %}</div>{% endblock %}\n{% block actions %}\n<a class=\"btn\" href=\"{{ r.pr_url }}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">{{ ic.icon('ext') }}PR</a>\n{% if r.trace_id %}<a class=\"btn\" href=\"{{ langfuse_host }}/trace/{{ r.trace_id }}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">{{ ic.icon('ext') }}trace</a>{% endif %}\n{% endblock %}\n{% block body %}\n{% if r.status == 'running' %}\n<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"3\">\n<section class=\"card\"><div class=\"bd\"><span class=\"pill st-skip\">running</span> \u57f7\u884c\u4e2d\uff08{{ (now - r.started)|int }} s\uff09\uff1b\u6bcf 3 \u79d2\u81ea\u52d5\u66f4\u65b0\u3002</div></section>\n{% elif r.status == 'error' %}\n<section class=\"card\"><div class=\"bd\"><span class=\"pill st-fail\">error</span> <span class=\"err\">\u57f7\u884c\u5931\u6557\uff1a{{ r.error }}</span></div></section>\n{% else %}\n<div class=\"grid cols-2\">\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><h2>Findings</h2><span class=\"meta\"><span class=\"sev error\">{{ r.n_error }}</span> error \u00b7 <span class=\"sev warning\">{{ r.n_warning }}</span> warning \u00b7 <span class=\"sev info\">{{ r.n_info }}</span> info</span></div>\n  <div class=\"bd flush\">\n  {% if not r.findings %}<div class=\"empty\">\u7121 finding\u3002</div>{% else %}\n  <table class=\"tbl\">\n    {% for f in r.findings %}\n    <tr>\n      <td class=\"st\"><span class=\"pill plain st-{{ 'fail' if f.severity == 'error' else ('warn' if f.severity == 'warning' else 'skip') }}\">F{{ loop.index }}</span></td>\n      <td class=\"k\"><div class=\"mono\">{{ f.rule }}</div><div class=\"tag\">{{ f.source }}{% if f.dimension %} \u00b7 {{ f.dimension }}{% endif %} \u00b7 {{ '%.2f'|format(f.confidence) }}</div></td>\n      <td class=\"v\"><div class=\"mono\" style=\"color:var(--fg)\">{{ f.file }}{% if f.line %}:{{ f.line }}{% endif %}</div>{{ f.note }}\n        {% if f.rule_ref %}<div class=\"tag\">rule: {{ f.rule_ref }}</div>{% endif %}\n        {% if f.knowledge_ref %}<div class=\"tag\">knowledge: {{ f.knowledge_ref|join(', ') }}</div>{% endif %}</td>\n    </tr>\n    {% endfor %}\n  </table>{% endif %}\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><h2>\u8f38\u5165\u8207\u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587</h2></div>\n  <div class=\"bd\">\n  {% set st = r.stats or {} %}\n  <dl class=\"kv\">\n    <dt>diff</dt><dd>{{ st.files }} \u6a94 \u00b7 {{ st.added_lines }} \u65b0\u589e\u884c \u00b7 {{ st.hunks }} hunks{% if st.skipped %} \u00b7 {{ st.skipped }} \u6a94\u88ab\u7565\u904e{% endif %}</dd>\n    <dt>static</dt><dd>{{ st.static_findings }} \u689d{% if st.static_notes %} \u00b7 {{ st.static_notes|join('\uff1b') }}{% endif %}</dd>\n    <dt>base \u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587</dt><dd>{% if st.base_available %}{{ st.base_files }} \u6a94{% else %}\u7121\uff08\u7121\u672c\u5730 clone\uff09{% endif %}</dd>\n    <dt>rules</dt><dd>{% if st.rules_sha %}\u7248\u672c <span class=\"mono\">{{ st.rules_sha }}</span>{% if st.rules_files %} \u00b7 {{ st.rules_files|length }} \u6a94{% endif %}{% if st.rules_truncated %} \u00b7 <span class=\"warn\">\u88ab\u622a\u65b7</span>{% endif %}{% else %}\u7121{% endif %}</dd>\n    <dt>knowledge</dt><dd>{% if st.knowledge_entries %}{{ st.knowledge_entries }} \u689d\u6ce8\u5165{% if st.knowledge_injected %}\uff1a<span class=\"mono\">{{ st.knowledge_injected|join(', ') }}</span>{% endif %}{% if st.knowledge_grounded %} \u00b7 {{ st.knowledge_grounded }} \u689d finding \u5f15\u7528\u4e86{% endif %}{% else %}\u7121{% endif %}</dd>\n    <dt>graph</dt><dd>{% if st.graph_used %}\u6709\uff08{{ st.graph_impacted|length }} \u500b\u53d7\u6ce2\u53ca\uff09{% else %}{{ st.graph_note or '\u7121' }}{% endif %}</dd>\n    {% if st.dimension_names %}<dt>dimensions</dt><dd>{{ st.dimension_names|join(' \u00b7 ') }}{% if st.plan != 'ok' %} <span class=\"warn\">\uff08planner \u964d\u7d1a\u70ba\u56fa\u5b9a\u9762\u5411\uff09</span>{% endif %}</dd>{% endif %}\n    {% if st.adversary %}<dt>adversary</dt><dd>{{ st.adversary }}</dd>{% endif %}\n    {% if st.dropped_low_conf or st.dropped_over_cap %}<dt>synthesis</dt><dd>\u904e\u6ffe {{ st.dropped_low_conf or 0 }} \u689d\uff08\u4f4e\u65bc\u4fe1\u5fc3\u9580\u6abb\uff09\u3001{{ st.dropped_over_cap or 0 }} \u689d\uff08\u8d85\u904e\u6578\u91cf\u4e0a\u9650\uff09</dd>{% endif %}\n  </dl>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"bd\"><details><summary>\u5b8c\u6574 stats\uff08JSON\uff09</summary><pre style=\"margin-top:8px\">{{ r.stats|tojson(indent=1) }}</pre></details></div>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"hd\"><h2>Review \u5831\u544a</h2><span class=\"meta\">\u767c\u5e03\u81f3 PR \u7684 markdown</span></div>\n  <div class=\"bd\"><pre class=\"tall\">{{ r.markdown }}</pre></div>\n</section>\n{% endif %}\n{% endblock %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/reviews.html","perm":"0644","sha":"2c158b5479ec01d3d7104cf55ccc4a5f6ce73b7e20cb4ae9ca95281148d94044","data":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n{% block title %}Review \u8a18\u9304{% endblock %}\n{% block heading %}Review \u8a18\u9304{% endblock %}\n{% block subheading %}<div class=\"sub\">{{ summary.days }} \u5929\u5167 {{ summary.n }} \u7b46{% if summary.errors %} \u00b7 <span class=\"err\">{{ summary.errors }} \u7b46\u5931\u6557</span>{% endif %}{% if summary.avg_seconds %} \u00b7 \u5e73\u5747\u8017\u6642 {{ summary.avg_seconds|int }} s \u00b7 \u5e73\u5747 {{ summary.avg_findings|round(1) }} finding{% endif %}</div>{% endblock %}\n{% block notices %}\n{% if not store_ok %}<div class=\"notice warn\">{{ ic.icon('warn') }}<div>Review \u8a18\u9304\u505c\u7528\uff1a{{ store_reason }}\uff08DATA_DIR \u4e0d\u53ef\u5beb\uff1breview \u672c\u8eab\u4e0d\u53d7\u5f71\u97ff\uff09</div></div>{% endif %}\n{% if run_error %}<div class=\"notice fail\">{{ ic.icon('warn') }}<div>{{ run_error }}</div></div>{% endif %}\n{% endblock %}\n{% block body %}\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"bd\">\n    <form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/reviews/run\" class=\"form-row\">\n      <input type=\"text\" name=\"pr_url\" placeholder=\"PR URL\uff08https://\u2026/_git/<repo>/pullrequest/<id>\uff09\" required style=\"flex:1 1 420px\">\n      <button class=\"primary\">{{ ic.icon('play') }}\u57f7\u884c review</button>\n      <span class=\"hint\" style=\"margin:0\">\u8207 chat \u5165\u53e3\u76f8\u540c\u7684 pipeline\uff1b{% if auto_post %}<span class=\"warn\">AUTO_POST=true\uff1a\u5c07\u767c\u5e03 comment \u81f3 PR</span>{% else %}AUTO_POST=false\uff1a\u4e0d\u767c\u5e03 comment{% endif %}</span>\n    </form>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"bd flush scroll\">\n  {% if not reviews %}<div class=\"empty\">\u5c1a\u7121 review \u8a18\u9304\u3002</div>{% else %}\n  <table class=\"tbl\">\n    <tr><th>\u6642\u9593</th><th>PR</th><th>\u6a19\u984c</th><th>\u72c0\u614b</th><th>pipeline</th><th>findings</th><th class=\"r\">\u8017\u6642</th><th></th></tr>\n    {% for r in reviews %}\n    <tr>\n      <td class=\"faint\" style=\"white-space:nowrap\">{{ r.started|datetime }}</td>\n      <td class=\"k\"><a href=\"/console/reviews/{{ r.id }}\" class=\"mono\">{{ r.repo }}#{{ r.pr_id }}</a></td>\n      <td class=\"v\">{{ r.title or '' }}</td>\n      <td class=\"st\"><span class=\"pill st-{{ 'fail' if r.status == 'error' else ('skip' if r.status == 'running' else 'ok') }}\">{{ r.status }}</span></td>\n      <td class=\"faint\">{{ r.pipeline or '' }}</td>\n      <td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">{% if r.status == 'done' %}<span class=\"sev error\">{{ r.n_error }}</span> <span class=\"sev warning\">{{ r.n_warning }}</span> <span class=\"sev info\">{{ r.n_info }}</span>{% endif %}</td>\n      <td class=\"r faint\">{% if r.duration %}{{ r.duration|int }}s{% elif r.status == 'running' %}{{ (now - r.started)|int }}s\u2026{% endif %}</td>\n      <td class=\"r\"><a href=\"/console/reviews/{{ r.id }}\">\u8a73\u60c5</a></td>\n    </tr>\n    {% endfor %}\n  </table>{% endif %}\n  </div>\n</section>\n{% endblock %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/settings.html","perm":"0644","sha":"5e1c435ff9ebcd8a3a10896974cadb941f9ceb3557870fb7ba156bfe88d7ce00","data":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n{% block title %}\u8a2d\u5b9a{% endblock %}\n{% block heading %}\u8a2d\u5b9a{% endblock %}\n{% block subheading %}<div class=\"sub\">\u5957\u7528\u5f8c\u5373\u6642\u751f\u6548\uff0c\u7121\u9700\u91cd\u555f\u3002\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\u8986\u5beb\u7684\u503c\u70ba\u552f\u8b80\uff1bsecrets \u50c5\u5b58\u65bc <code>secrets.env</code>\u3002</div>{% endblock %}\n{% block actions %}\n<label class=\"search\">{{ ic.icon('search') }}<input type=\"search\" id=\"settings-search\" placeholder=\"\u641c\u5c0b\uff08\u6a19\u7c64\u3001\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\u3001\u8aaa\u660e\uff09\"></label>\n<label class=\"toggle-mod\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"only-modified\"> \u50c5\u986f\u793a\u5df2\u8986\u5beb</label>\n{% endblock %}\n{% block notices %}\n{% for w in warnings %}<div class=\"notice warn\">{{ ic.icon('warn') }}<div>{{ w }}</div></div>{% endfor %}\n{% endblock %}\n{% block body %}\n<div class=\"settings-layout\">\n  <nav class=\"section-index\" id=\"section-index\">\n    {% for t in tasks %}\n    <a href=\"#t-{{ loop.index }}\">{{ t.title }}{% if t.modified %}<span class=\"count\">{{ t.modified }}</span>{% endif %}</a>\n    {% endfor %}\n    <a href=\"#changes\">\u8b8a\u66f4\u7d00\u9304</a>\n    <div class=\"index-foot faint tiny\">{{ config_path }}{% if not config_exists %}<br>\uff08\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\uff1b\u9996\u6b21\u5957\u7528\u6642\u5efa\u7acb\uff09{% endif %}</div>\n  </nav>\n\n  <div class=\"settings-body\">\n    {% for t in tasks %}\n    <section class=\"task\" id=\"t-{{ loop.index }}\">\n      <header class=\"task-hd\">\n        <h2>{{ t.title }}</h2>\n        <p class=\"faint small\">{{ t.why }}{% if t.link %} \u00b7 <a href=\"{{ t.link }}\">{{ t.link_label }}</a>{% endif %}</p>\n      </header>\n      {% for g in t.groups %}\n      <div id=\"g-{{ g.name }}\">{% include \"_group.html\" %}</div>\n      {% endfor %}\n    </section>\n    {% endfor %}\n\n    <section class=\"task\" id=\"changes\">\n      <header class=\"task-hd\"><h2>\u8b8a\u66f4\u7d00\u9304</h2><p class=\"faint small\">\u6700\u8fd1 20 \u7b46\u5beb\u5165 config.toml \u7684\u8b8a\u66f4\uff08\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u6216 --migrate\uff09\u3002</p></header>\n      {% include \"_changes.html\" %}\n    </section>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"dirty-bar\" id=\"dirty-bar\" hidden>\n  <span id=\"dirty-text\">\u6709\u672a\u5957\u7528\u8b8a\u66f4</span>\n  <div class=\"row\">\n    <button class=\"ghost sm\" id=\"dirty-discard\">\u653e\u68c4\u8b8a\u66f4</button>\n    <button class=\"primary sm\" id=\"dirty-apply\">\u5957\u7528\u5168\u90e8</button>\n  </div>\n</div>\n{% endblock %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/setup.html","perm":"0644","sha":"ab64a904a0ef872795418c77eb57abf2c37bcf8bfb52dc61eb9066c19b835d76","data":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n{% block title %}Setup{% endblock %}\n{% block heading %}\u8a2d\u5b9a\u7cbe\u9748{% endblock %}\n{% block subheading %}<div class=\"sub\">\u6bcf\u4e00\u6b65\u5c0d\u61c9 doctor \u7684\u4e00\u7d44\u6aa2\u67e5\uff0c\u4f9d\u5e8f\u5b8c\u6210\u5373\u53ef\u6295\u5165\u670d\u52d9\u3002\u8a2d\u5b9a\u503c\u65bc <a href=\"/console/settings\">\u8a2d\u5b9a</a> \u9801\u4fee\u6539\uff1bsecrets \u65bc <code>secrets.env</code> \u4fee\u6539\u5f8c\u91cd\u555f\u3002</div>{% endblock %}\n{% block actions %}<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/console/setup?refresh=1\">{{ ic.icon('refresh') }}\u91cd\u65b0\u6aa2\u67e5</a>{% endblock %}\n{% block notices %}\n{% if not config_exists %}<div class=\"notice info\">{{ ic.icon('setup') }}<div><code>{{ config_path }}</code> \u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\uff1a\u9996\u6b21\u65bc\u8a2d\u5b9a\u9801\u5957\u7528\u6642\u5efa\u7acb\uff0c\u6216\u5148\u57f7\u884c <code>python -m shared.install</code>\u3002</div></div>{% endif %}\n{% endblock %}\n{% block body %}\n{% for s in steps %}\n<section class=\"card step st-{{ s.status|lower }}\">\n  <div class=\"hd\">\n    <h2><span class=\"idx\">{{ loop.index }}</span>{{ s.title }} <span class=\"pill st-{{ s.status|lower }}\" style=\"margin-left:8px\">{{ s.status }}</span></h2>\n    <div class=\"row small\">\n      {% for g in s.groups %}<a class=\"btn sm\" href=\"/console/settings#g-{{ g }}\">\u8a2d\u5b9a {{ g }}</a>{% endfor %}\n      {% if s.link %}<a class=\"btn sm\" href=\"{{ s.link }}\">{{ s.link_label }}</a>{% endif %}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"bd\"><p class=\"muted small\">{{ s.why }}</p>{% if s.secrets %}<p class=\"hint\">{{ ic.icon('lock') }} Secrets\uff1a{{ s.secrets|join('\u3001') }}\uff08secrets.env\uff09</p>{% endif %}</div>\n  <div class=\"bd flush\">\n  <table class=\"tbl\">\n    {% for c in s.checks %}\n    <tr><td class=\"st\"><span class=\"pill st-{{ c.status|lower }}\">{{ c.status }}</span></td><td class=\"k\">{{ c.name }}</td><td class=\"v\">{{ c.detail }}</td></tr>\n    {% endfor %}\n  </table>\n  </div>\n</section>\n{% endfor %}\n{% endblock %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/sources.html","perm":"0644","sha":"45112779ef6a762b10e66485e35006a24ebe0cdd23036bc459ea5e340f01c401","data":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n{% block title %}\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90{% endblock %}\n{% block heading %}\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90{% endblock %}\n{% block subheading %}<div class=\"sub\">repos\uff08base \u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\uff09\u3001rules\uff08\u5718\u968a\u898f\u5247\uff09\u3001knowledge\uff08\u6c7a\u7b56\u5e33\u672c\uff09\u4e09\u500b git \u8cc7\u6599\u57df\u7684\u72c0\u614b\u8207\u6ce8\u5165\u9810\u89bd\u3002\u552f\u4e00\u7684\u5beb\u5165\u64cd\u4f5c\u70ba\u65b0\u589e repo\u3002</div>{% endblock %}\n{% block notices %}{% if add_result %}<div class=\"notice info\">{{ ic.icon('check') }}<div>{% for ln in add_result %}{{ ln }}<br>{% endfor %}</div></div>{% endif %}{% endblock %}\n{% block body %}\n\n{# ---------- repos ---------- #}\n<section class=\"card\" id=\"repos\">\n  <div class=\"hd\">\n    <h2>repos <span class=\"doc mono\">{{ v.repos.root or 'REPOS_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d' }}</span></h2>\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      {% if jobs['repo-sync'] %}\n      <span class=\"meta\">repo-sync {% if not jobs['repo-sync'].enabled %}\u505c\u7528{% elif jobs['repo-sync'].running %}\u57f7\u884c\u4e2d{% elif jobs['repo-sync'].last_end %}\u4e0a\u6b21 {{ ((now - jobs['repo-sync'].last_end)/60)|int }} min \u524d{% if jobs['repo-sync'].last_ok %}\u6210\u529f{% else %}<span class=\"err\">\u5931\u6557</span>{% endif %}{% else %}\u5c1a\u672a\u57f7\u884c{% endif %}</span>\n      <form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/jobs/repo-sync/run?back=/console/sources\" class=\"inline\"><button class=\"sm\">{{ ic.icon('refresh') }}Sync now</button></form>\n      {% endif %}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  {% if v.repos.note %}<div class=\"bd\"><p class=\"warn small\">{{ v.repos.note }}</p></div>{% endif %}\n  {% if v.repos.items %}\n  <div class=\"bd flush\"><table class=\"tbl\">\n    <tr><th>repo</th><th>branch @ sha</th><th>\u6700\u65b0 commit</th><th class=\"r\">\u4e0a\u6b21 fetch</th></tr>\n    {% for r in v.repos.items %}\n    <tr>\n      <td class=\"k\">{{ r.name }}</td>\n      {% if r.git and not r.error %}\n      <td class=\"mono\">{{ r.branch }}@{{ r.sha }}{% if r.dirty %} <span class=\"pill st-warn plain\">\u5de5\u4f5c\u6a39\u6709\u672a\u63d0\u4ea4\u8b8a\u66f4</span>{% endif %}</td>\n      <td class=\"v\">{{ r.date }} \u00b7 {{ r.subject }}</td>\n      <td class=\"r faint\">{% if r.last_touch %}{{ ((now - r.last_touch)/3600)|round(1) }} \u5c0f\u6642\u524d{% else %}\u2014{% endif %}</td>\n      {% else %}<td colspan=\"3\" class=\"v warn\">{{ r.note or r.error }}</td>{% endif %}\n    </tr>\n    {% endfor %}\n  </table></div>\n  {% elif v.repos.exists %}<div class=\"empty\">\u76ee\u9304\u70ba\u7a7a\u3002</div>{% endif %}\n  {% if v.repos.exists %}\n  <div class=\"bd\">\n    {% if jobs['repo-sync'] and jobs['repo-sync'].last_detail %}\n    <details><summary>\u4e0a\u6b21 repo-sync \u660e\u7d30</summary><ul class=\"small\">{% for ln in jobs['repo-sync'].last_detail %}<li>{{ ln }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>\n    {% endif %}\n    <details><summary>\u65b0\u589e repo\uff08git clone \u5230 REPOS_ROOT\uff09</summary>\n      <form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/sources/repos/add\" class=\"form-row\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"name\" placeholder=\"\u76ee\u9304\u540d = PR URL \u88e1 _git/<\u9019\u6bb5> \u7684\u5c0f\u5beb\" required>\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"url\" placeholder=\"https://<ADO>/<collection>/<project>/_git/<repo>\" required style=\"flex:2 1 320px\">\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"branch\" placeholder=\"target branch\uff08\u9810\u8a2d main\uff09\" style=\"flex:0 1 200px\">\n        <button class=\"primary sm\">Clone</button>\n      </form>\n      <p class=\"hint\">\u4ee5 ADO_PAT \u8a8d\u8b49\uff1bPAT \u6703\u5beb\u5165\u8a72 clone \u7684 .git/config\uff08\u50c5\u670d\u52d9\u5e33\u865f\u53ef\u8b80\uff09\u3002\u5927\u578b repo \u9700\u6578\u5206\u9418\uff0c\u9801\u9762\u6703\u7b49\u5f85\u5b8c\u6210\u3002</p>\n    </details>\n  </div>\n  {% endif %}\n</section>\n\n{# ---------- rules ---------- #}\n<section class=\"card\" id=\"rules\">\n  <div class=\"hd\">\n    <h2>rules <span class=\"doc mono\">{{ v.rules.root or 'RULES_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d' }}</span></h2>\n    {% if v.rules.exists %}<span class=\"meta\">\u7248\u672c <span class=\"mono\">{{ v.rules.head.sha }}</span> \u00b7 {{ v.rules.head.date }} \u00b7 {{ v.rules.counts.md }} \u689d md\uff08common {{ v.rules.counts.common }}\u3001{{ v.rules.counts.repos }} \u500b repo \u5c08\u5c6c\uff09\u00b7 {{ v.rules.counts.semgrep }} \u500b semgrep \u898f\u5247\u6a94</span>{% endif %}\n  </div>\n  {% if v.rules.note %}<div class=\"bd\"><p class=\"warn small\">{{ v.rules.note }}</p></div>{% endif %}\n  {% if v.rules.exists %}\n  <div class=\"bd flush\">\n  <div class=\"grid cols-eq\" style=\"gap:0\">\n    <div class=\"scroll\" style=\"border-right:1px solid var(--line)\">\n      <table class=\"tbl\">\n        <tr><th>\u7bc4\u570d</th><th>\u6a94</th><th class=\"r\">chars</th></tr>\n        {% for f in v.rules.items %}\n        <tr><td class=\"st\"><span class=\"pill plain {{ 'st-ok' if f.kind == 'common' else ('st-skip' if f.kind == 'semgrep' else 'src-file') }}\">{{ f.kind }}</span></td><td class=\"mono\">{{ f.path }}</td><td class=\"r faint\">{{ f.chars or '' }}</td></tr>\n        {% endfor %}\n      </table>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bd\">\n      <h3>\u6ce8\u5165\u9810\u89bd</h3>\n      <p class=\"small muted\" style=\"margin:4px 0 10px\">\u6a21\u64ec\u6307\u5b9a repo \u7684 review \u6703\u8f09\u5165\u54ea\u4e9b\u898f\u5247\uff08\u5be6\u969b\u547c\u53eb load_rules\uff09\u3002</p>\n      <form method=\"get\" action=\"/console/sources\" class=\"form-row\">\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"rules_repo\" value=\"{{ rules_repo }}\" placeholder=\"repo\uff08\u7559\u7a7a = \u50c5 common\uff09\">\n        <button class=\"sm\">\u9810\u89bd</button>\n      </form>\n      {% if rp %}\n      <p class=\"small\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">\u8f09\u5165 {{ rp.files|length }} \u6a94\u3001{{ rp.chars }} / {{ rp.cap }} chars{% if rp.truncated %} \u00b7 <span class=\"warn\">\u8d85\u904e RULES_MAX_CHARS\uff0c\u5f8c\u7e8c\u6a94\u6848\u5df2\u622a\u65b7</span>{% endif %} \u00b7 \u7248\u672c <span class=\"mono\">{{ rp.sha }}</span></p>\n      <ul class=\"small mono\" style=\"margin:6px 0 0; padding-left:18px\">{% for s in rp.sections %}<li>{{ s.path }} <span class=\"faint\">{{ s.chars }}</span></li>{% endfor %}</ul>\n      {% if not rp.loaded %}<p class=\"muted small\">\u672a\u8f09\u5165\u4efb\u4f55\u898f\u5247\u3002</p>{% endif %}\n      {% endif %}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  </div>\n  {% endif %}\n</section>\n\n{# ---------- knowledge ---------- #}\n<section class=\"card\" id=\"knowledge\">\n  <div class=\"hd\">\n    <h2>knowledge <span class=\"doc mono\">{{ v.knowledge.root or 'KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d' }}</span></h2>\n    {% if v.knowledge.exists %}<span class=\"meta\">{% if v.knowledge.head.sha %}\u7248\u672c <span class=\"mono\">{{ v.knowledge.head.sha }}</span> \u00b7 {{ v.knowledge.head.date }} \u00b7 {% endif %}{{ v.knowledge.counts.pages }} \u9801\uff08{{ v.knowledge.counts.repos }} \u500b repo\uff09\u00b7 {{ v.knowledge.counts.pending }} \u5f85\u88c1\u6c7a \u00b7 {{ v.knowledge.counts.staged }} \u66ab\u5b58 \u00b7 <a href=\"/console/knowledge\">Knowledge \u2192</a></span>{% endif %}\n  </div>\n  {% if v.knowledge.note %}<div class=\"bd\"><p class=\"warn small\">{{ v.knowledge.note }}</p></div>{% endif %}\n  {% if v.knowledge.exists %}\n  <div class=\"bd flush\">\n  <div class=\"grid cols-eq\" style=\"gap:0\">\n    <div class=\"scroll\" style=\"border-right:1px solid var(--line)\">\n      <table class=\"tbl\">\n        <tr><th>repo</th><th>\u9801</th><th class=\"r\">\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f</th></tr>\n        {% for p in v.knowledge.items[:60] %}\n        <tr><td class=\"st faint\">{{ p.repo }}</td><td class=\"mono\">{{ p.path }}</td><td class=\"r faint\">{{ p.invariants }}{% if p.retired %}\uff08{{ p.retired }} \u5df2\u8a3b\u92b7\uff09{% endif %}</td></tr>\n        {% endfor %}\n      </table>\n      {% if v.knowledge.items|length > 60 %}<div class=\"empty\">\u53ea\u5217\u524d 60 \u9801\u3002</div>{% endif %}\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bd\">\n      <h3>\u6ce8\u5165\u9810\u89bd</h3>\n      <p class=\"small muted\" style=\"margin:4px 0 10px\">\u6a21\u64ec\u8b8a\u66f4\u6307\u5b9a\u6a94\u6848\u6642\u6ce8\u5165\u7684\u77e5\u8b58\u689d\u76ee\uff08\u5be6\u969b\u547c\u53eb load_for\uff09\u3002</p>\n      <form method=\"get\" action=\"/console/sources\" class=\"form-row\">\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"k_repo\" value=\"{{ k_repo }}\" placeholder=\"repo\" style=\"flex:0 1 160px\">\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"k_paths\" value=\"{{ k_paths }}\" placeholder=\"\u8b8a\u66f4\u6a94\u6848\u8def\u5f91\uff0c\u9017\u865f\u5206\u9694\">\n        <button class=\"sm\">\u9810\u89bd</button>\n      </form>\n      {% if kp %}\n      <p class=\"small\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">{{ kp.stats.knowledge_entries }} \u689d\u76ee \u00b7 {{ kp.chars }} / {{ kp.cap }} chars{% if kp.stats.knowledge_omitted %} \u00b7 <span class=\"warn\">{{ kp.stats.knowledge_omitted|length }} \u689d\u8d85\u51fa\u9810\u7b97\u88ab\u7701\u7565</span>{% endif %}</p>\n      {% if kp.text %}<pre style=\"margin-top:8px\">{{ kp.text }}</pre>{% else %}<p class=\"muted small\">\u7121\u547d\u4e2d\u689d\u76ee\u3002</p>{% endif %}\n      {% endif %}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  </div>\n  {% endif %}\n</section>\n{% endblock %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/console/templates/status.html","perm":"0644","sha":"96cc42899e0f8446348748410afc8a55b7ba473c9bb43d36492b15f752340293","data":"{% extends \"base.html\" %}\n{% import \"_icons.html\" as ic %}\n{% block title %}\u7cfb\u7d71\u72c0\u614b{% endblock %}\n{% block heading %}\u7cfb\u7d71\u72c0\u614b{% endblock %}\n{% block actions %}<span class=\"faint small\">\u4e0a\u6b21\u6aa2\u67e5 {{ (now - checked_at) | int }} s \u524d</span><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/console?refresh=1\">{{ ic.icon('refresh') }}\u91cd\u65b0\u6aa2\u67e5</a>{% endblock %}\n{% block body %}\n\n<section class=\"verdict {{ hl.state }}\">\n  <div class=\"verdict-main\">\n    <div class=\"verdict-title\">{{ hl.title }}</div>\n    <div class=\"verdict-why\">{{ hl.why }}</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"verdict-side\">\n    <div><span class=\"num\">{{ summary.n }}</span><span>review \u00b7 {{ summary.days }} \u5929\u5167</span></div>\n    <div><span class=\"num\">{{ sources.repos.counts.clones if sources.repos.exists else 0 }}</span><span>repo clone</span></div>\n    <div><span class=\"num\">{{ sources.knowledge.counts.pending if sources.knowledge.exists else 0 }}</span><span>\u5f85\u88c1\u6c7a\u8349\u7a3f</span></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<div class=\"two-col\">\n<div class=\"col-main\">\n  <section class=\"block\">\n    <div class=\"block-hd\">\n      <h2>\u5f85\u8655\u7406\u9805\u76ee</h2>\n      <span class=\"faint small\">{% if blockers %}{{ blockers|length }} \u9805{% if not config_exists %} \u00b7 config.toml \u4e0d\u5b58\u5728{% endif %} \u00b7 <a href=\"/console/setup\">\u8a2d\u5b9a\u7cbe\u9748</a>{% else %}\u7121{% endif %}</span>\n    </div>\n    {% if not blockers %}\n    <p class=\"quiet\">\u7121\u5f85\u8655\u7406\u9805\u76ee\u3002</p>\n    {% else %}\n    <ol class=\"todo\">\n      {% for b in blockers %}\n      <li class=\"{{ b.sev|lower }}{% if b.blocking %} blocking{% endif %}\">\n        <div class=\"todo-mark\"></div>\n        <div class=\"todo-body\">\n          <div class=\"todo-title\">{{ b.title }}{% if b.blocking %} <span class=\"tag-block\">BLOCKING</span>{% endif %}</div>\n          <div class=\"todo-detail\">{{ b.detail }}</div>\n        </div>\n        {% if b.href %}<a class=\"btn sm\" href=\"{{ b.href }}\">{{ b.action or '\u6aa2\u8996' }}</a>{% endif %}\n      </li>\n      {% endfor %}\n    </ol>\n    {% endif %}\n    <details class=\"healthy\">\n      <summary>{{ healthy|length }} \u9805\u6aa2\u67e5\u901a\u904e</summary>\n      <ul class=\"healthy-list\">\n        {% for c in healthy %}<li><span class=\"faint\">{{ c.group }}</span> {{ c.name }} <span class=\"faint\">\u00b7 {{ c.detail }}</span></li>{% endfor %}\n      </ul>\n    </details>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"block\">\n    <div class=\"block-hd\"><h2>\u8cc7\u6599\u4f86\u6e90</h2><a class=\"small\" href=\"/console/sources\">\u8a73\u7d30\u72c0\u614b\u8207\u6ce8\u5165\u9810\u89bd</a></div>\n    <dl class=\"facts\">\n      <dt>repos</dt><dd>{% if sources.repos.exists %}{{ sources.repos.counts.clones }} \u9846 clone{% if sources.repos.counts.others %}\u3001{{ sources.repos.counts.others }} \u500b\u975e git \u76ee\u9304{% endif %}{% if jobs['repo-sync'] and jobs['repo-sync'].last_end %} \u00b7 \u4e0a\u6b21\u540c\u6b65 {{ ago(jobs['repo-sync'].last_end) }}{% endif %}{% else %}<span class=\"faint\">{{ sources.repos.note }}</span>{% endif %}</dd>\n      <dt>rules</dt><dd>{% if sources.rules.exists %}{{ sources.rules.counts.md }} \u689d\u898f\u5247 \u00b7 \u7248\u672c <span class=\"mono\">{{ sources.rules.head.sha }}</span> \u00b7 {{ sources.rules.head.date }}{% else %}<span class=\"faint\">{{ sources.rules.note }}</span>{% endif %}</dd>\n      <dt>knowledge</dt><dd>{% if sources.knowledge.exists %}{{ sources.knowledge.counts.pages }} \u9801 \u00b7 {{ sources.knowledge.counts.pending }} \u5f85\u88c1\u6c7a \u00b7 {{ sources.knowledge.counts.staged }} \u66ab\u5b58{% else %}<span class=\"faint\">{{ sources.knowledge.note }}</span>{% endif %}</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </section>\n</div>\n\n<aside class=\"col-side\">\n  <section class=\"block\">\n    <div class=\"block-hd\"><h2>\u6d3b\u52d5\u7d00\u9304</h2><a class=\"small\" href=\"/console/reviews\">\u5168\u90e8 review \u8a18\u9304</a></div>\n    {% if not feed %}<p class=\"quiet\">\u5c1a\u7121\u6d3b\u52d5\u8a18\u9304\u3002</p>{% else %}\n    <ol class=\"feed\">\n      {% for e in feed %}\n      <li class=\"{{ e.tone }}\">\n        <div class=\"feed-when\">{{ ago(e.ts) }}</div>\n        <div class=\"feed-body\">\n          <div class=\"feed-title\">{% if e.href %}<a href=\"{{ e.href }}\">{{ e.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ e.title }}{% endif %}</div>\n          {% if e.detail %}<div class=\"feed-detail\">{{ e.detail }}</div>{% endif %}\n        </div>\n      </li>\n      {% endfor %}\n    </ol>\n    {% endif %}\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"block\">\n    <div class=\"block-hd\"><h2>\u6392\u7a0b\u5de5\u4f5c</h2></div>\n    <ul class=\"plain\">\n      {% for name, st in jobs.items() %}\n      <li class=\"row between\">\n        <span><b class=\"mono\">{{ name }}</b> <span class=\"faint small\">{% if not st.enabled %}\u505c\u7528{% elif st.running %}\u57f7\u884c\u4e2d{% elif st.last_end %}\u4e0a\u6b21 {{ ago(st.last_end) }}{% if not st.last_ok %} <span class=\"err\">\u5931\u6557</span>{% endif %}{% else %}\u6bcf {{ st.interval_min }} min \u00b7 \u5c1a\u672a\u57f7\u884c{% endif %}</span></span>\n        <form method=\"post\" action=\"/console/jobs/{{ name }}/run\" class=\"inline\"><button class=\"ghost xs\" {% if st.running %}disabled{% endif %}>\u624b\u52d5\u57f7\u884c</button></form>\n      </li>\n      {% endfor %}\n    </ul>\n  </section>\n</aside>\n</div>\n{% endblock %}\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/context.py","perm":"0644","sha":"def24910682d9ffa3bbe80b10251992477d8bd261695e08b4c7260e5b046a262","data":"\"\"\"context\uff08v2 \u7684\u9935\u6599\u5de5\u7a0b\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u9810\u6293\uff0c\u4e0d\u505a agentic tool loop\u3002\n\n\u523b\u610f\u7684\u8a2d\u8a08\u6c7a\u7b56\uff1areviewer \u4e0d\u62ff\u5de5\u5177\u81ea\u5df1\u901b\uff0c\u800c\u662f\u7531 code \u5148\u628a\u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\u5099\u597d\u9935\u9032\u53bb\u3002\n\u7406\u7531\uff1a(1) \u5167\u90e8 gateway \u7684 native tool calling \u652f\u63f4\u672a\u77e5\uff08README \u5df2\u8a18\u8f09\u9019\u662f\nLLM-as-judge \u7684\u963b\u7919\uff09\uff0c\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u9810\u6293\u4e0d\u5403\u9019\u500b\u80fd\u529b\uff1b(2) \u53ef\u91cd\u73fe \u2014\u2014 \u540c\u4e00\u4efd diff\n\u6c38\u9060\u62ff\u5230\u540c\u4e00\u4efd\u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\uff1b(3) \u96e2\u7dda eval \u512a\u96c5\u964d\u7d1a\uff08\u6c92\u6709 clone/graph \u5c31\u5c11\u9019\u584a\uff0c\n\u4e0d\u70b8\uff09\u3002\u4e4b\u5f8c\u8981\u5347\u7d1a\u6210 agentic loop\uff0c\u518d\u628a \u2461\u2463 \u63a5\u7d66\u6a21\u578b\u5373\u53ef\uff0c\u4ecb\u9762\u90fd\u5099\u8457\u3002\n\n\u5169\u500b\u4f86\u6e90\uff1a\n  A. \u672c\u5730\u4e7e\u6de8 clone\uff08target branch / base \u5074\uff09\uff1aREPOS_ROOT/<repo\u5c0f\u5beb>/\n     \u2014\u2014 \u53d6\u6bcf\u500b hunk \u820a\u884c\u865f\u9644\u8fd1 \u00b1N \u884c\u3002\u5206\u5de5\u539f\u5247\uff1a\u6539\u4e86\u4ec0\u9ebc\u770b diff\uff0c\n     \u5468\u908a\u9577\u4ec0\u9ebc\u6a23\u770b base\u3002\n  B. code graph\uff08\u9078\u914d\uff09\uff1aGRAPH_TOOLS_URL \u8a2d\u5b9a\u5f8c\uff0c\u7528 clients.graph_blast\n     \u62ff\u53d7\u5f71\u97ff\u7bc4\u570d\u6458\u8981\u3002\u5de5\u5177\u540d/\u53c3\u6578\u6a23\u677f\u7528 env \u8a2d\u5b9a\uff08\u88dd\u597d\u5f8c list tools \u518d\u586b\uff09\u3002\n\n\u8a2d\u5b9a\uff1asettings().repos\uff08REPOS_ROOT / CONTEXT_LINES / CONTEXT_MAX_CHARS\uff09\u8207 settings().graph\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom orchestrator.anatomy import Anatomy, FileChange\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\n\ndef _repo_root(repo: str | None) -> Path | None:\n    return settings().repos.root_for(repo)\n\n\ndef _safe(root: Path, rel: str) -> Path | None:\n    p = (root / rel.lstrip(\"/\")).resolve()\n    return p if (root == p or root in p.parents) else None\n\n\ndef _excerpt(root: Path, fc: FileChange, ctx: int) -> str | None:\n    p = _safe(root, fc.path)\n    if p is None or not p.is_file():\n        return None\n    try:\n        lines = p.read_text(errors=\"replace\").splitlines()\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n    wanted: set[int] = set()\n    for h in fc.hunks:\n        lo = max(1, h.old_start - ctx)\n        hi = min(len(lines), h.old_start + max(h.old_count, 1) + ctx)\n        wanted.update(range(lo, hi + 1))\n    if not wanted:\n        return None\n    out: list[str] = [f\"### base\uff08target branch\uff09{fc.path}\"]\n    prev = None\n    for i in sorted(wanted):\n        if prev is not None and i != prev + 1:\n            out.append(\"      \u2026\")\n        out.append(f\"{i:>5}  {lines[i - 1]}\")\n        prev = i\n    return \"\\n\".join(out)\n\n\ndef base_context(repo: str | None, ana: Anatomy) -> tuple[str, dict]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de\u50b3 (\u7d44\u597d\u7684\u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\u6587\u5b57, \u7d71\u8a08)\u3002clone \u4e0d\u5728 = \u7a7a\u5b57\u4e32 + \u8a3b\u8a18\uff0c\u4e0d\u70b8\u3002\"\"\"\n    root = _repo_root(repo)\n    stats = {\"base_files\": 0, \"base_available\": root is not None}\n    if root is None:\n        return \"\", stats\n    ctx = settings().repos.context_lines\n    budget = settings().repos.context_max_chars\n    parts: list[str] = []\n    total = 0\n    for fc in ana.files:\n        ex = _excerpt(root, fc, ctx)\n        if not ex:\n            continue\n        if total + len(ex) > budget:\n            parts.append(\"\uff08base \u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\u9054\u9810\u7b97\u4e0a\u9650\uff0c\u5176\u9918\u7701\u7565\uff09\")\n            break\n        parts.append(ex)\n        total += len(ex)\n        stats[\"base_files\"] += 1\n    return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts), stats\n\n\nasync def graph_context(repo: str | None, ana: Anatomy) -> tuple[str, dict]:\n    \"\"\"\u9078\u914d\uff1acode graph \u7684 blast radius \u6458\u8981\u3002\u4efb\u4f55\u5931\u6557 = \u7a7a\u5b57\u4e32 + \u8a3b\u8a18\u3002\"\"\"\n    stats = {\"graph_used\": False, \"graph_note\": \"\"}\n    g = settings().graph\n    if not g.tools_url:\n        stats[\"graph_note\"] = \"GRAPH_TOOLS_URL \u672a\u8a2d\u5b9a\"\n        return \"\", stats\n    bound = g.bound_repo\n    if bound and (repo or \"\").strip().lower() != bound:\n        # graph server \u4e00\u6b21\u53ea\u670d\u52d9\u4e00\u500b repo\uff1b\u5225\u7684 repo \u5be7\u53ef\u6c92\u6709 graph\uff0c\n        # \u4e5f\u4e0d\u80fd\u62ff\u932f\u7684\u5716\u51fa\u300c\u7121\u8de8\u6a94\u5f71\u97ff\u300d\u7684\u5047\u8b49\u8a5e\n        stats[\"graph_note\"] = f\"graph \u7d81\u5b9a repo '{bound}'\uff0c\u672c repo \u672a\u9644\u639b\"\n        return \"\", stats\n    try:\n        from orchestrator import clients\n        files = [fc.path.lstrip(\"/\") for fc in ana.files]\n        out = await clients.graph_blast(files=files, repo=repo)\n    except Exception as e:  # graph \u662f\u52a0\u5206\u9805\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u4f9d\u8cf4\n        stats[\"graph_note\"] = f\"graph \u547c\u53eb\u5931\u6557\uff1a{type(e).__name__}\"\n        return \"\", stats\n    if not out:\n        stats[\"graph_note\"] = \"graph \u7121\u56de\u61c9\u6216\u5de5\u5177\u540d\u672a\u8a2d\u5b9a\"\n        return \"\", stats\n    impacted: list[str] = []\n    if isinstance(out, dict):        # \u4f8b\u5982 get_impact_radius_tool \u7684\u56de\u50b3\n        summary = str(out.get(\"summary\") or \"\").strip()\n        for key in (\"impacted_files\", \"additional_files\", \"affected_files\",\n                    \"impacted_nodes\", \"affected_nodes\"):\n            for item in out.get(key) or []:\n                name = (item.get(\"qualified_name\") or item.get(\"name\")\n                        or item.get(\"file_path\")\n                        ) if isinstance(item, dict) else str(item)\n                if name:\n                    impacted.append(str(name))\n        detail = json.dumps(out, ensure_ascii=False, default=str)\n        text = (summary + \"\\n\" + detail) if summary else detail\n        if not summary:\n            summary = detail\n    else:\n        text = out if isinstance(out, str) else str(out)\n        summary = text.strip()\n    budget = settings().repos.context_max_chars\n    stats[\"graph_used\"] = True\n    stats[\"graph_summary\"] = summary           # \u5831\u544a\uff1a\u8840\u8108\u6458\u8981\n    stats[\"graph_impacted\"] = list(dict.fromkeys(impacted))[:12]  # \u5831\u544a\uff1a\u53d7\u6ce2\u53ca\u6e05\u55ae\n    return \"### code graph\uff08\u53d7\u5f71\u97ff\u7bc4\u570d\uff09\\n\" + text[:budget], stats\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/core.py","perm":"0644","sha":"8adf35a30e6dd3ac5f6c77ba579480b655d140a45fae5b3e19209b1cf0ea077e","data":"\"\"\"Orchestrator \u7684\u6838\u5fc3\uff1arun_review \u2014\u2014 \u4e5f\u662f eval \u7684\u6ce8\u5165\u53e3\u3002\n\nrun_review(diff) \u662f\u7d14\u51fd\u5f0f\u98a8\u683c\uff1a\u9935\u51cd\u7d50\u7684 diff \u5c31\u51fa\u7d50\u679c\uff0c\u4e0d\u78b0 \u2460\u2461\u2462\u3001\n\u4e0d\u78b0\u7db2\u8def\u4e0a\u7684 PR \u2014\u2014 eval \u53ef\u91cd\u73fe\u7684\u5730\u57fa\u3002\u7c3d\u540d\u6c38\u9060\u4e0d\u52d5\u3002\n\nREVIEW_PIPELINE \u6c7a\u5b9a\u809a\u5b50\u88e1\u8dd1\u54ea\u689d\u8def\uff1a\n  v1\uff08\u9810\u8a2d\uff09  \u55ae\u6b21 LLM \u547c\u53eb\uff08\u539f\u59cb\u884c\u70ba\uff0c\u4e00\u9375\u56de\u6efe\u7528\uff09\n  v2          anatomy \u2192 static \u2192 plan \u2192 \u5e73\u884c reviewer \u2192 adversary \u2192\n              synthesis \u2192 render\uff08\u898b orchestrator/pipeline.py\uff09\n\n\u8a2d\u5b9a\u5168\u90e8\u4f4f shared/settings.py\uff08REVIEW_PIPELINE \u5728 settings().orchestrator.pipeline\uff09\uff1b\n\u6bcf\u6b21 review \u7684\u65cb\u9215\u5feb\u7167\u4ee5 settings().knobs() \u9032 trace metadata\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport re\n\nfrom langfuse import get_client, observe\n\nfrom orchestrator.llm import complete, prompt_or\nfrom orchestrator.models import Finding, ReviewResult\nfrom orchestrator.rules import load_rules, rules_context\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\nPROMPT_NAME = \"pr-review-system\"\n\n# Langfuse \u4e0a\u9084\u6c92\u5efa prompt \u6642\u7684\u5167\u5efa\u5f8c\u5099\u7248\uff1bseed_langfuse.py \u6703\u628a\u540c\u4e00\u4efd\u63a8\u4e0a\u53bb\u53d7\u7248\u63a7\nDEFAULT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a senior code reviewer. Review the unified diff provided by the user, focusing on four categories:\n1. BUG \u2014 logic errors, boundary conditions, behavior contradicting intent\n2. MISSING-TEST \u2014 new or changed behavior without corresponding test changes\n3. NAMING \u2014 unclear or misleading identifiers\n4. SECURITY \u2014 credential exposure, injection, unsafe defaults\n\nRules:\n- Write in clear, professional English. Comment only on the changed lines; do not lecture on pre-existing code.\n- If nothing significant is found, state that explicitly. Never reply with a bare \"LGTM\".\n- Give file and line for every finding (best effort).\n\nOutput format (strict): first the human-readable markdown review, then one fenced JSON block containing the findings array:\n```json\n[{\"rule\": \"BUG\", \"file\": \"src/x.py\", \"line\": 12, \"severity\": \"error\", \"note\": \"...\"}]\n```\nOutput `[]` when there are no findings.\"\"\"\n\n_JSON_BLOCK = re.compile(r\"```json\\s*(\\[.*?\\])\\s*```\", re.DOTALL)\n\n\ndef _parse_findings(markdown: str) -> list[Finding]:\n    m = None\n    for m in _JSON_BLOCK.finditer(markdown):  # \u53d6\u300c\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u500b\u300djson \u5340\u584a\n        pass\n    if not m:\n        return []\n    try:\n        raw = json.loads(m.group(1))\n        return [Finding(**f) for f in raw if isinstance(f, dict)]\n    except Exception:\n        return []\n\n\ndef _meta_block(meta: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u6709\u6599\u7684\u6b04\u4f4d\u624d\u7d44\u9032\u53bb \u2014\u2014 eval \u53ea\u5e36 repo \u6642\u4e0d\u6703\u751f\u51fa\u7a7a\u6b04\u4f4d\u96dc\u8a0a\u3002\"\"\"\n    lines: list[str] = []\n    if meta.get(\"title\"):\n        lines.append(f\"Title: {meta['title']}\")\n    if meta.get(\"description\"):\n        lines.append(f\"Description: {meta['description']}\")\n    if meta.get(\"source_branch\") or meta.get(\"target_branch\"):\n        lines.append(f\"{meta.get('source_branch', '')} \u2192 {meta.get('target_branch', '')}\")\n    return (\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\") if lines else \"\"\n\n\nasync def _run_v1(diff: str, meta: dict, rules) -> ReviewResult:\n    \"\"\"\u539f\u59cb\u55ae\u547c\u53eb\u8def\u5f91\uff08\u4fdd\u7559 = \u4e00\u9375\u56de\u6efe + eval A/B \u7684\u5c0d\u7167\u7d44\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    md = await complete(\n        prompt_or(PROMPT_NAME, DEFAULT_SYSTEM_PROMPT) + rules_context(rules),\n        f\"{_meta_block(meta)}Review the following diff:\\n\\n{diff}\",\n    )\n    return ReviewResult(markdown=md, findings=_parse_findings(md),\n                        stats={\"pipeline\": \"v1\"})\n\n\n@observe()\nasync def run_review(diff: str, metadata: dict | None = None) -> ReviewResult:\n    \"\"\"\u7d66\u4e00\u6bb5 diff\uff08\u53ef\u9644 PR metadata\uff09\uff0c\u56de ReviewResult(markdown + findings)\u3002\n\n    metadata \u8a8d\u5f97\u7684\u9375\u5168\u662f\u9078\u914d\uff1atitle / description / source_branch /\n    target_branch \u9032 prompt\uff1brepo \u7528\u4f86\u8f09 per-repo \u898f\u5247\u3001\u627e\u672c\u5730 clone\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    meta = metadata or {}\n    rules = load_rules(meta.get(\"repo\"))\n    mode = settings().orchestrator.pipeline\n\n    if mode == \"v2\":\n        from orchestrator.pipeline import run_pipeline\n        result = await run_pipeline(diff, meta, rules)\n    else:\n        result = await _run_v1(diff, meta, rules)\n\n    get_client().update_current_span(\n        output={\"findings_count\": len(result.findings),\n                \"pipeline\": result.stats.get(\"pipeline\", mode)},\n        metadata={\n            \"rules_sha\": rules.sha or None,\n            \"rules_files\": rules.files,\n            \"rules_truncated\": rules.truncated,\n            \"config\": settings().knobs(),\n            **{k: v for k, v in result.stats.items() if k != \"rules_sha\"},\n        },\n    )\n    return result\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/jobs.py","perm":"0644","sha":"6b138375070be4b45c1868dff2308dfbdcd020788a6b14b9ee83d20d908c8eda","data":"\"\"\"jobs \u2014\u2014 \u884c\u7a0b\u5167\u6392\u7a0b\uff0c\u53d6\u4ee3\u5169\u7d44 systemd timer\uff08repo-sync\u3001knowledge-harvest\uff09\u3002\n\n\u70ba\u4ec0\u9ebc\u642c\u9032\u884c\u7a0b\uff1a\u5169\u500b oneshot timer \u5404\u8981\u4e00\u500b service + \u4e00\u500b timer \u55ae\u5143\u3001\u5404\u81ea\u7684\nEnvironmentFile \u8207 PATH override\uff0c\u5931\u6557\u53ea\u9032 journal\uff0c\u6c92\u6709\u4efb\u4f55\u5730\u65b9\u80fd\u4e00\u773c\u770b\u5230\n\u300c\u4e0a\u6b21\u540c\u6b65\u662f\u5e7e\u9ede\u3001\u6210\u4e0d\u6210\u529f\u300d\u3002\u642c\u9032 orchestrator \u7684 event loop \u4e4b\u5f8c\uff1a\n  - \u4e00\u500b systemd unit \u7ba1\u5168\u90e8\uff1b\n  - \u6bcf\u500b job \u7684 last_run / last_ok / last_error \u4f4f\u5728\u8a18\u61b6\u9ad4\uff0c/healthz \u76f4\u63a5\u56de\u3001\n    doctor \u76f4\u63a5\u8b80\u3001S3 \u7684\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u76f4\u63a5\u756b\uff1b\n  - \u300charvester \u662f\u552f\u4e00 commit \u8005\u300d\u7684\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u7531\u55ae\u4e00 event loop \u4fdd\u8b49\uff1a\u540c\u4e00\u500b job\n    \u5728\u4e0a\u4e00\u8f2a\u7d50\u675f\u524d\u4e0d\u6703\u518d\u958b\u7b2c\u4e8c\u8f2a\uff08run_forever \u662f\u9806\u5e8f\u7684\uff09\u3002\n\n\u5169\u500b job \u90fd\u662f\u540c\u6b65\u3001\u6703\u6253 git / HTTP \u7684\u51fd\u5f0f\uff0c\u7528 asyncio.to_thread \u8dd1\uff0c\u4e0d\u5361 SSE\u3002\n\nCLI\uff08\u904e\u6e21\u671f\u8207\u624b\u52d5\u89f8\u767c\uff09\uff1a\n    python -m orchestrator.jobs repo-sync     \u8dd1\u4e00\u6b21 repo-sync \u5c31\u9000\u51fa\uff08\u539f repo-sync.sh\uff09\n    python -m orchestrator.jobs harvest       \u8dd1\u4e00\u6b21 harvest\uff08\u540c python -m orchestrator.knowledge_harvest\uff09\n\n\u8a2d\u5b9a\uff1asettings().jobs \u2014\u2014 REPO_SYNC_INTERVAL_MIN\uff08\u9810\u8a2d 10\uff1b0 = \u95dc\uff09\u3001\nHARVEST_INTERVAL_MIN\uff08\u9810\u8a2d 30\uff1b0 = \u95dc\uff09\u3001REPO_SYNC_GRAPH_REBUILD\uff08auto/on/off\uff09\u3002\njob \u53ea\u5728\u5c0d\u61c9\u7684 root \u6709\u8a2d\u6642\u624d\u6392\u7a0b\uff08REPOS_ROOT / KNOWLEDGE_ROOT\uff09\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Callable\n\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass JobState:\n    name: str\n    interval_min: int\n    enabled: bool\n    running: bool = False\n    runs: int = 0\n    last_start: float | None = None\n    last_end: float | None = None\n    last_ok: bool | None = None\n    last_error: str = \"\"\n    last_detail: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)   # \u6700\u8fd1\u4e00\u8f2a\u6bcf\u500b\u9805\u76ee\u4e00\u884c\n    next_run: float | None = None\n\n\n_STATE: dict[str, JobState] = {}\n_TASKS: set[asyncio.Task] = set()\n\n\ndef snapshot() -> dict[str, dict]:\n    \"\"\"\u7d66 /healthz\u3001doctor\u3001\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u3002\"\"\"\n    return {k: asdict(v) for k, v in _STATE.items()}\n\n\n# ---------- repo-sync\uff08\u539f deploy/bin/repo-sync.sh\uff09 ----------\n\ndef _git(path: Path, *args: str, timeout: int = 300) -> tuple[int, str]:\n    try:\n        r = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(path), *args], capture_output=True,\n                           text=True, timeout=timeout)\n        return r.returncode, (r.stdout or r.stderr).strip()\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return 127, f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\"\n\n\ndef repo_sync_once() -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u540c\u6b65 REPOS_ROOT \u5e95\u4e0b\u6240\u6709\u4e7e\u6de8 clone \u5230 target branch \u6700\u65b0\uff0c\u4e26\uff08\u9078\u914d\uff09\n    \u589e\u91cf\u91cd\u5efa code graph\u3002\u6bcf\u500b repo \u4e00\u884c\u7d50\u679c\uff1bpull \u5931\u6557\u7684 repo \u7dad\u6301\u539f\u72c0\u3001\u4e0d\u64cb\u5225\u4eba\u3002\"\"\"\n    s = settings()\n    root = s.repos.repos_root\n    lines: list[str] = []\n    if root is None or not root.is_dir():\n        return [f\"REPOS_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\u6216\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\uff08{root}\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u7121\u4e8b\u53ef\u505a\"]\n    graph_bin = shutil.which(\"code-review-graph\") if s.jobs.graph_rebuild != \"off\" else None\n    for d in sorted(p for p in root.iterdir() if (p / \".git\").exists()):\n        rc, out = _git(d, \"pull\", \"--ff-only\", \"--quiet\")\n        if rc != 0:\n            lines.append(f\"{d.name}: pull \u5931\u6557\uff08\u5206\u652f\u767c\u6563\u6216\u7db2\u8def\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u7dad\u6301\u539f\u72c0\uff1a{out[:160]}\")\n            continue\n        _rc, sha = _git(d, \"rev-parse\", \"--short\", \"HEAD\", timeout=15)\n        line = f\"{d.name} -> {sha}\"\n        if graph_bin:\n            try:\n                r = subprocess.run([graph_bin, \"build\"], cwd=str(d), capture_output=True,\n                                   text=True, timeout=1800)\n                line += \"; graph \u589e\u91cf\u91cd\u5efa\u5b8c\u6210\" if r.returncode == 0 else \\\n                    f\"; graph build \u5931\u6557\uff08\u4e0d\u5f71\u97ff review\uff09\uff1a{(r.stderr or r.stdout)[-160:]}\"\n            except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n                line += f\"; graph build \u4f8b\u5916\uff1a{type(e).__name__}\"\n        lines.append(line)\n    return lines or [\"REPOS_ROOT \u5e95\u4e0b\u6c92\u6709\u4efb\u4f55 clone\"]\n\n\n# ---------- knowledge-harvest ----------\n\ndef harvest_once() -> list[str]:\n    from orchestrator import knowledge_harvest\n    return knowledge_harvest.main()\n\n\n# ---------- \u6392\u7a0b ----------\n\nJOBS: dict[str, Callable[[], list[str]]] = {\n    \"repo-sync\": repo_sync_once,\n    \"harvest\": harvest_once,\n}\n\n\ndef _schedule(name: str) -> tuple[int, bool]:\n    \"\"\"(\u9593\u9694\u5206, \u73fe\u5728\u8a72\u4e0d\u8a72\u8dd1) \u2014\u2014 \u6bcf\u8f2a\u91cd\u8b80\uff0c\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u6539\u8a2d\u5b9a\u4e0d\u7528 restart\u3002\"\"\"\n    s = settings()\n    if name == \"repo-sync\":\n        iv = s.jobs.repo_sync_interval_min\n        return iv, iv > 0 and s.repos.repos_root is not None\n    iv = s.jobs.harvest_interval_min\n    return iv, iv > 0 and s.knowledge.root is not None\n\n\ndef _plan() -> list[JobState]:\n    return [JobState(name, *_schedule(name)) for name in JOBS]\n\n\nasync def run_once(name: str) -> JobState:\n    \"\"\"\u8dd1\u4e00\u8f2a\u4e26\u66f4\u65b0\u72c0\u614b\uff08\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u7684\u300c\u7acb\u523b\u57f7\u884c\u300d\u4e5f\u8d70\u9019\u88e1\uff09\u3002\u540c\u540d job \u6b63\u5728\u8dd1\u5c31\u76f4\u63a5\u56de\u3002\"\"\"\n    st = _STATE.setdefault(name, JobState(name, 0, enabled=False))\n    if st.running:\n        return st\n    st.running, st.last_start = True, time.time()\n    try:\n        st.last_detail = await asyncio.to_thread(JOBS[name])\n        st.last_ok, st.last_error = True, \"\"\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        st.last_ok, st.last_error = False, f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\"\n        st.last_detail = []\n    finally:\n        st.running, st.last_end, st.runs = False, time.time(), st.runs + 1\n    for ln in st.last_detail:\n        print(f\"[{name}] {ln}\")\n    if st.last_error:\n        print(f\"[{name}] \u5931\u6557\uff1a{st.last_error}\")\n    return st\n\n\nDISABLED_POLL_S = 60.0     # \u95dc\u8457\u7684 job \u6bcf\u5206\u9418\u770b\u4e00\u6b21\u8a2d\u5b9a\u6709\u6c92\u6709\u628a\u5b83\u6253\u958b\n\n\nasync def _run_forever(st: JobState, first_delay_s: float) -> None:\n    await asyncio.sleep(first_delay_s)\n    while True:\n        st.interval_min, st.enabled = _schedule(st.name)\n        if not st.enabled:\n            st.next_run = None\n            await asyncio.sleep(DISABLED_POLL_S)\n            continue\n        await run_once(st.name)\n        st.interval_min, st.enabled = _schedule(st.name)      # \u8dd1\u7684\u9014\u4e2d\u53ef\u80fd\u88ab\u6539\n        st.next_run = time.time() + st.interval_min * 60\n        await asyncio.sleep(st.interval_min * 60)\n\n\ndef start(first_delay_s: float = 60.0) -> list[JobState]:\n    \"\"\"\u7531 app \u7684 lifespan \u547c\u53eb\u3002\u6bcf\u500b job \u90fd\u6392\u4e00\u500b\u8ff4\u5708\uff1b\u95dc\u8457\u7684\u53ea\u662f\u6bcf\u5206\u9418\u770b\u4e00\u6b21\u8a2d\u5b9a\u3002\"\"\"\n    _STATE.clear()\n    for st in _plan():\n        _STATE[st.name] = st\n        st.next_run = time.time() + first_delay_s if st.enabled else None\n        t = asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task(_run_forever(st, first_delay_s))\n        _TASKS.add(t)\n        t.add_done_callback(_TASKS.discard)\n    return list(_STATE.values())\n\n\ndef stop() -> None:\n    for t in list(_TASKS):\n        t.cancel()\n    _TASKS.clear()\n\n\n# ---------- CLI ----------\n\ndef _main(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    if len(argv) != 1 or argv[0] not in JOBS:\n        print(f\"\u7528\u6cd5\uff1apython -m orchestrator.jobs {{{'|'.join(JOBS)}}}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    from shared.settings import fail_fast\n    fail_fast()\n    for ln in JOBS[argv[0]]():\n        print(f\"[{argv[0]}] {ln}\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(_main(sys.argv[1:]))\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/knowledge.py","perm":"0644","sha":"44944df1bcac021165c653ab8bc341c81791e357e0e944514fc675f7dbcb2091","data":"\"\"\"\u77e5\u8b58\u8ff4\u5708\uff08K \u6bb5\uff09\u2014\u2014 rules.py \u7684\u5b7f\u751f + distiller \u524d\u6bb5\u3002\n\n\u5b9a\u4f4d\uff1a\u6c7a\u7b56\u5e33\u672c\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u6587\u4ef6\u7db2\u7ad9\u3002\u4e09\u9435\u5f8b\uff1a\n  \u6aa2\u7d22\u512a\u5148 \u2014\u2014 \u7b2c\u4e00\u8b80\u8005\u662f\u6211\u5011\u81ea\u5df1\u7684 reviewer\uff08Stage 04 targeted \u6ce8\u5165\uff09\n  \u8b49\u64da\u512a\u5148 \u2014\u2014 \u689d\u76ee\u6bcf\u53e5\u8a71\u639b PR / file:line\uff0c\u7121\u9023\u7d50\u7684\u53e5\u5b50\u4e0d\u5f97\u51fa\u73fe\n  \u9328\u5728\u5be6\u9ad4 \u2014\u2014 \u9801\u9762\u9328 code \u5be6\u9ad4\u4e0d\u9328 PR\uff1b\u540c\u5be6\u9ad4\u65b0\u6c7a\u7b56\u63a5\u7e8c\u5beb\u9032\u540c\u4e00\u9801\n\n\u672c\u6a21\u7d44\u7ba1\u56db\u4ef6\u4e8b\uff1a\n  load_for()            \u8b80\u53d6\u8def\uff1a\u8b8a\u66f4\u6a94 \u2192 \u76f8\u95dc\u689d\u76ee \u2192 \u6ce8\u5165\u5340\u584a\uff08\u82f1\u6587\u3001\u5206\u7d1a\u964d\u8f09\uff09\n  gate()                K1 \u9598\u9580\uff1a\u76ee\u6a19\u5206\u652f \u2208 KNOWLEDGE_BRANCHES\u3001\u6392\u9664 bump/merge-sync\n  distill_once()        \u84b8\u993e\u4e00\u6b21\uff1a\u540c\u4e00\u4efd diff \u5207\u7247 \u2192 LLM \u2192 \u8b49\u64da\u9a57\u8b49 \u2192 \u88dc ID\n  distill_and_stage()   K2+K3 \u524d\u6bb5\uff1adistill_once \u2192 \u8349\u7a3f\u7559\u8a00\u8cbc\u4e0a PR \u2192 \u5beb _pending/\n  redistill()           stale \u88dc\u6551\uff1a\u7528\u6700\u7d42 diff \u91cd\u84b8\u4e00\u6b21\uff0c\u8986\u5beb _pending/\n                        \uff08\u7d42\u614b\u88c1\u6c7a\u8207\u843d\u5730\u5728 knowledge_harvest.py\uff0ctimer \u662f\u552f\u4e00 commit \u8005\uff09\n\n\u8b49\u64da\u5730\u677f\uff08Phase 1\uff09\uff1adistiller \u5403\u7684\u662f reviewer \u770b\u904e\u7684\u540c\u4e00\u4efd numbered slices\uff0c\n\u7522\u51fa\u7684\u6bcf\u4e00\u689d decision \u90fd\u8981\u80fd\u5f15\u5230\u300cexcerpt \u88e1\u770b\u5f97\u5230\u7684\u884c / \u9019\u6b21 review \u7684 finding\n\u7de8\u865f / \u6709\u5167\u5bb9\u7684 PR description\u300d\u2014\u2014\u9a57\u4e0d\u904e\u7684 evidence \u525d\u6389\uff0c\u525d\u5149\u7684 decision \u6574\u689d\n\u4e0d\u5165\u7a3f\uff0c\u6578\u5b57\u9032 stats\u3001\u75d5\u8de1\u9032\u8349\u7a3f\u7559\u8a00 footer\u3002\u8a9e\u610f\u5224\u65b7\u5728\u6a21\u578b\u3001\u9a57\u8b49\u5728 code\u3002\n\n\u8a2d\u5b9a\uff1asettings().knowledge\uff08KNOWLEDGE_ROOT / KNOWLEDGE_BRANCHES / KNOWLEDGE_MAX_CHARS /\nDISTILL_DIFF_MAX_CHARS / KNOWLEDGE_REDISTILL \u2026\uff09\uff1bKNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d = \u6574\u500b K \u6bb5\u975c\u9ed8\u505c\u7528\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport fnmatch\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom langfuse import observe\n\nfrom orchestrator import clients\nfrom orchestrator.anatomy import (Anatomy, line_in_view, match_path,\n                                  numbered_slice, parse_diff)\nfrom orchestrator.llm import complete, extract_json, prompt_or\nfrom orchestrator.static_pass import DECL_RE, TEST_PATH_RE\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\nDISTILLER_PROMPT_NAME = \"pr-review-distiller\"\n\nDEFAULT_DISTILLER_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are the knowledge distiller of an automated code-review system. A pull request has just been reviewed; your job is to distill it into one decision-ledger entry so future reviewers inherit what was decided here.\n\nHard rules:\n- Every statement must be supported by the material provided (PR description, diff summary, review report). Never invent intent: if the PR text does not state why the change was made, set \"intent_stated\": false and describe only the mechanics.\n- Write for a reviewer who will read this months from now while reviewing a change to the same code: decisions and invariants they must not break, not a narrative of the diff.\n- Prefer few, load-bearing statements over completeness. A ledger entry with two real decisions beats ten paraphrased diff lines.\n- \"evidence\" items are short locators and are verified mechanically \u2014 an item that cannot be resolved is stripped, and a decision left with no evidence is discarded before anyone reads it. Exactly three forms are accepted:\n  - \"<file>:<line>\" \u2014 the line must be one you can actually see in the annotated diff excerpt below (the number in the left-hand column of a \"+\" or context line). Never cite a line that is not in the excerpt, and never guess a number.\n  - \"F<n>\" \u2014 a finding id from the review report below, exactly as numbered there.\n  - \"PR\" \u2014 only when the statement rests on the PR description; do not use it when the description is empty.\n- If the PR text or review discussion explicitly reverses or retires a previously established rule, record it in \"supersedes\" (entity + what is being retired). Only when explicitly stated \u2014 never infer retirement.\n- Lines under \"Existing ledger invariants\" below start with a bracketed id such as [PR12-I1]. When the retired rule is one of those lines, put that id (without brackets) in \"retires_id\" \u2014 the id is how the system strikes the old entry. If the line is marked [no-id], copy its text into \"retires_verbatim\" character for character instead. Never invent an id; omit both fields if unsure.\n- \"Existing ledger invariants\" is reference material for supersede detection only. Never restate those lines as this PR's own decisions or invariants.\n- If the material mentions alternatives that were considered and rejected, capture that as a decision (\"chose X over Y because Z\") \u2014 rejected paths are knowledge a diff cannot show. Such a decision is normally carried by \"PR\" evidence; that is what the \"PR\" form is for.\n- \"primary_entity\" must be copied verbatim from the changed-files list \u2014 it is the page this entry is filed under. Pick the file that carries the change's meaning, not a test or a build file. \"affected\" may name neighbours that this diff does not touch.\n- Write all output in clear, professional English.\n\nOutput a single JSON object only \u2014 the first character must be \"{\" and the last \"}\":\n{\"summary\": \"One or two sentences: what this change establishes.\",\n \"type\": \"bugfix|feature|refactor|revert|other\",\n \"intent_stated\": true,\n \"primary_entity\": \"src/main/java/.../SessionCache.java\",\n \"decisions\": [{\"text\": \"The decision and its rationale as stated\", \"evidence\": [\"PR\", \"CacheConfig.java:24\"]}],\n \"invariants\": [\"A constraint future changes must preserve\"],\n \"supersedes\": [{\"entity\": \"path/or/ClassName\", \"what\": \"the rule being retired\", \"retires_id\": \"PR12-I1 (the id of the existing invariant this replaces; omit if none)\", \"retires_verbatim\": \"only for [no-id] lines: the exact text, copied character for character (omit otherwise)\"}],\n \"affected\": [\"other/entities/touched\"],\n \"ledger_line\": \"One line for the history table, e.g. 'TTL unit changed to milliseconds; margin fixed at 5000ms'\"}\"\"\"\n\n# ---------- \u689d\u76ee ID\uff08\u84b8\u993e\u6642\u5373\u5b9a\uff0c\u66ab\u5b58\u2192\u843d\u5730\u4e00\u8def\u4e0d\u8b8a\uff09 ----------\n#\n# \u5f62\u5f0f\uff1aPR<pr_id>-D<n>\uff08decision\uff09/ PR<pr_id>-I<n>\uff08invariant\uff09\u3002PR id + \u5e8f\u865f\n# \u5929\u7136\u5168\u57df\u552f\u4e00\uff0c\u4e0d\u9700\u8981\u4e2d\u592e\u8a08\u6578\u5668\uff1bdigest \u7684 LLM \u5206\u6790\u3001`reject <ID>`\u3001supersede\n# \u7684 retires_id \u5168\u90e8\u8a8d\u9019\u500b\u5b57\u4e32\uff0c\u843d\u5730\u7aef\u53ea\u505a\u7cbe\u78ba\u6bd4\u5c0d\u2014\u2014\u4e0d\u518d\u9760 stem \u731c\u3001\u4e0d\u518d\u9760\n# \u9010\u5b57\u8907\u88fd\u3002\u9801\u9762\u88e1\u4ee5\u884c\u5c3e `PR12-I1`\uff08\u53cd\u5f15\u865f\uff09\u6a19\u8a18\uff0cwiki \u53ef\u8b80\u3001regex \u53ef\u89e3\u3002\n\nID_RE = re.compile(r\"^PR(\\d+)-([DI])(\\d+)$\", re.I)\n_ID_TAIL = re.compile(r\"\\s*`(PR\\d+-[DI]\\d+)`\\s*$\", re.I)\n\n\ndef norm_id(tok: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"'pr12-i1' \u2192 'PR12-I1'\uff1b\u4e0d\u662f ID \u5f62\u5f0f\u56de\u7a7a\u5b57\u4e32\u3002\"\"\"\n    m = ID_RE.match((tok or \"\").strip())\n    return f\"PR{m.group(1)}-{m.group(2).upper()}{m.group(3)}\" if m else \"\"\n\n\ndef split_id(body: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"'text `PR12-I1`' \u2192 ('text', 'PR12-I1')\uff1b\u7121\u6a19\u8a18 \u2192 (text, '')\u3002\"\"\"\n    m = _ID_TAIL.search(body or \"\")\n    if not m:\n        return (body or \"\").strip(), \"\"\n    return body[:m.start()].strip(), norm_id(m.group(1))\n\n\ndef inv_text(x) -> str:\n    \"\"\"invariant \u53ef\u80fd\u662f\u820a\u7a3f\u7684\u7d14\u5b57\u4e32\u6216\u65b0\u7a3f\u7684 {id, text}\u3002\"\"\"\n    return (x.get(\"text\", \"\") if isinstance(x, dict) else str(x or \"\")).strip()\n\n\ndef inv_id(x) -> str:\n    return (x.get(\"id\", \"\") if isinstance(x, dict) else \"\").strip()\n\n\ndef assign_ids(data: dict, pr_id: int) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\u5c31\u5730\u88dc ID\uff08\u51aa\u7b49\uff09\uff1a\u5df2\u6709 id \u7684\u4e0d\u52d5\uff1b\u7d14\u5b57\u4e32 invariant \u5347\u683c\u6210 {id, text}\u3002\n    \u820a\u7a3f\uff08\u7121 id\uff09\u5728 staging \u6216\u843d\u5730\u6642\u7d93\u904e\u9019\u88e1\u4e00\u6b21\u5373\u53ef\u5c0d\u9f4a\u65b0\u683c\u5f0f\u3002\"\"\"\n    decs = data.get(\"decisions\") or []\n    for i, d in enumerate(decs, 1):\n        if isinstance(d, dict) and not (d.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip():\n            d[\"id\"] = f\"PR{pr_id}-D{i}\"\n    invs = []\n    for i, x in enumerate(data.get(\"invariants\") or [], 1):\n        text = inv_text(x)\n        if not text:\n            continue\n        iid = inv_id(x) or f\"PR{pr_id}-I{i}\"\n        invs.append({\"id\": iid, \"text\": text})\n    data[\"invariants\"] = invs\n    return data\n\n\ndef entry_ids(data: dict, pr_id: int) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u4e00\u689d\u689d\u76ee\u53ef\u88ab reject / \u5f15\u7528\u7684\u5168\u90e8 ID\uff1aPR<id> \u672c\u8eab + \u5404\u884c\u3002\"\"\"\n    out = {f\"PR{pr_id}\"}\n    out.update(d.get(\"id\", \"\") for d in (data.get(\"decisions\") or [])\n               if isinstance(d, dict) and d.get(\"id\"))\n    out.update(inv_id(x) for x in (data.get(\"invariants\") or []) if inv_id(x))\n    return out\n\n\n# ---------- \u8b49\u64da\u5730\u677f\uff08Phase 1.2\uff09\uff1aLLM \u8aaa\u7684\u6bcf\u4e00\u53e5\u90fd\u8981\u6307\u5f97\u56de\u6750\u6599 ----------\n#\n# \u578b\u5225\u5408\u7d04\uff1aevidence \u662f\u300c\u5f15\u7528\u7cfb\u7d71\u7d66\u7684\u5ea7\u6a19\u300d\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u81ea\u7531\u5b57\u4e32\u3002\u4e09\u7a2e\u5f62\u5f0f\u5404\u6709\u4e00\u500b\n# \u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u6aa2\u67e5\uff0c\u9a57\u4e0d\u904e\u5c31\u525d\u6389\uff1b\u4e00\u689d decision \u7684 evidence \u88ab\u525d\u5149 = \u5b83\u6c92\u6709\u4efb\u4f55\u53ef\n# \u56de\u6eaf\u7684\u4f9d\u64da \u2192 \u6574\u689d\u4e0d\u5165\u7a3f\uff08\u8ddf\u300c\u5f15\u4e0d\u51fa\u884c\u865f\u7684 reject \u4e0d\u914d \u00d70.35\u300d\u540c\u4e00\u500b\u56b4\u683c\u5ea6\uff09\u3002\n#\n# invariants \u6c92\u6709 evidence \u6b04\u4f4d\uff0c\u9019\u88e1\u4e0d\u9a57\u2014\u2014\u5b83\u5011\u662f\u898f\u5247\u4e0d\u662f\u4e3b\u5f35\uff0c\u9a57\u8b49\u4ea4\u7d66\n# reviewer \u7aef\u7684\u5f15\u7528\u7387\uff08Phase 2\uff09\u8207\u84b8\u993e\u8003\u5377\u7684\u5e7b\u89ba\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u9677\u9631\u984c\uff08Phase 4\uff09\u3002\n# \u9019\u662f\u660e\u6587\u63a5\u53d7\u7684\u6b98\u9918\u98a8\u96aa\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u6f0f\u6389\u3002\n\nEV_PR_MIN_CHARS = 40           # description \u81f3\u5c11\u8981\u6709\u9019\u9ebc\u591a\u975e\u7a7a\u767d\u5b57\u5143\u624d\u6490\u5f97\u8d77 \"PR\"\n_EV_FINDING_RE = re.compile(r\"^F\\d+$\", re.I)\n\n\ndef _evidence_ok(tok: str, ana: Anatomy, ids: set[str], desc_chars: int) -> bool:\n    t = (tok or \"\").strip().strip(\"[]`\")\n    if not t:\n        return False\n    if t.upper() == \"PR\":\n        return desc_chars >= EV_PR_MIN_CHARS\n    if _EV_FINDING_RE.match(t):\n        return t.upper() in ids\n    path, sep, line = t.rpartition(\":\")\n    if sep and path.strip() and line.strip().isdigit():\n        # line_in_view \u5167\u542b match_path\uff1a\u6a94\u6848\u8981\u5728\u9019\u4efd diff \u88e1\uff0c\u884c\u8981\u5728\u5207\u7247\u770b\u5f97\u5230\u7684\n        # \u7bc4\u570d\uff08added \u222a context\uff09\u00b12 \u2014\u2014 decision \u5e38\u5e38\u6307\u8457\u88ab\u6539\u52d5\u90a3\u4e00\u6bb5\u7684\u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\u884c\u3002\n        return line_in_view(ana, path.strip(), int(line))\n    return False\n\n\ndef verify_evidence(data: dict, ana: Anatomy, finding_ids: set[str] | None,\n                    description: str) -> tuple[dict, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\u5c31\u5730\u9a57\u8b49 decisions \u7684 evidence\u3002\u56de (data, \u88ab\u6574\u689d\u4e1f\u6389\u7684 decision \u6587\u5b57)\u3002\n\n    ana \u70ba\u7a7a\uff08\u6c92\u6709 diff \u53ef\u6bd4\u5c0d\uff09\u6642 file:line \u4e00\u5f8b\u9a57\u4e0d\u904e\u2014\u2014\u5be7\u53ef\u5c11\u6536\uff0c\u4e0d\u53ef\u5047\u8b49\u64da\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    desc_chars = len(\"\".join((description or \"\").split()))\n    ids = {str(x).strip().upper() for x in (finding_ids or set())}\n    kept: list = []\n    dropped: list[str] = []\n    for d in data.get(\"decisions\") or []:\n        if not isinstance(d, dict):\n            continue\n        good = [str(e).strip() for e in (d.get(\"evidence\") or [])\n                if _evidence_ok(str(e), ana, ids, desc_chars)]\n        if not good:\n            dropped.append(\" \".join((d.get(\"text\") or \"(no text)\").split())[:200])\n            continue\n        d[\"evidence\"] = good\n        kept.append(d)\n    data[\"decisions\"] = kept\n    return data, dropped\n\n\n# ---------- \u84b8\u993e\u5207\u7247\uff08Phase 1.1\uff09\uff1adistiller \u5403 reviewer \u770b\u904e\u7684\u540c\u4e00\u4efd\u5ea7\u6a19\u7cfb ----------\n\ndef _distill_order(ana: Anatomy, finding_files: list[str] | None) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\u512a\u5148\u5e8f\uff1a\u2460 \u65b0\u589e\u884c\u6700\u591a\u7684\u90a3\u500b\u6a94 \u2461 \u88ab review findings \u6307\u5230\u7684\u6a94\n    \u2462 \u542b\u65b0\u5ba3\u544a\uff08DECL_RE\uff09\u7684\u6a94 \u2463 \u5176\u9918\u3002\u540c\u7d1a\u4ee5 (\u65b0\u589e\u884c\u6578 desc, \u8def\u5f91) \u5b9a\u5e8f\uff0c\n    \u540c\u4e00\u4efd diff \u6c38\u9060\u5207\u51fa\u540c\u4e00\u4efd\u5207\u7247\u3002\"\"\"\n    if not ana.files:\n        return []\n    refs = [f for f in (finding_files or []) if f]\n    top = max(ana.files, key=lambda fc: (len(fc.added), fc.path))\n\n    def rank(fc) -> int:\n        if fc.path == top.path:\n            return 0\n        if any(match_path(fc.path, r) for r in refs):\n            return 1\n        if any(DECL_RE.match(t) for _, t in fc.added):\n            return 2\n        return 3\n\n    return sorted(ana.files, key=lambda fc: (rank(fc), -len(fc.added), fc.path))\n\n\ndef distill_slices(ana: Anatomy,\n                   finding_files: list[str] | None = None) -> tuple[str, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de (\u5207\u7247\u6587, \u8d85\u9810\u7b97\u88ab\u7701\u7565\u7684\u6a94\u6848)\u3002\u7701\u7565\u5c0d\u6a21\u578b\u6709\u8a3b\u8a18\u3001\u5c0d\u6211\u5011\u9032 stats\u2014\u2014\n    \u964d\u7d1a\u53ef\u898b\uff0c\u4e0d\u5b89\u975c\u84b8\u767c\u3002\"\"\"\n    budget = settings().knowledge.distill_diff_max_chars\n    parts: list[str] = []\n    skipped: list[str] = []\n    used = 0\n    for fc in _distill_order(ana, finding_files):\n        chunk = numbered_slice(fc)\n        if parts and used + len(chunk) > budget:\n            skipped.append(fc.path)\n            continue\n        parts.append(chunk)\n        used += len(chunk)\n    if skipped:\n        shown = \", \".join(skipped[:6]) + (\", \u2026\" if len(skipped) > 6 else \"\")\n        parts.append(f\"({len(skipped)} file(s) omitted from the diff excerpt: \"\n                     f\"{shown}) \u2014 do not cite line numbers from these files\")\n    return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts), skipped\n\n\ndef pick_primary_entity(ana: Anatomy, paths: list[str]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u9801\u9762\u9328\u9ede\u7684 fallback\uff1a\u975e lockfile\u3001\u975e\u6e2c\u8a66\u6a94\u4e2d\u300c\u65b0\u589e\u884c\u6578\u6700\u591a\u300d\u7684\u6a94\u3002\n    \uff08\u820a\u7248\u53d6\u300e\u8def\u5f91\u6700\u9577\u300f\u2014\u2014\u9801\u9762\u9328\u9ede\u537b\u7528\u6700\u5f31\u7684\u555f\u767c\u5f0f\u3002\uff09\"\"\"\n    def usable(p: str) -> bool:\n        name = Path(p).name.lower()\n        return name not in _EXCLUDE_BASENAMES \\\n            and not TEST_PATH_RE.search(p.lstrip(\"/\"))\n\n    cands = [fc for fc in ana.files if usable(fc.path)]\n    if cands:\n        return max(cands, key=lambda fc: (len(fc.added), fc.path)).path\n    if ana.files:                       # \u5168\u662f\u6e2c\u8a66/lockfile\uff1a\u7167\u6a23\u8981\u6709\u9328\n        return max(ana.files, key=lambda fc: (len(fc.added), fc.path)).path\n    usable_paths = [p for p in paths if usable(p)]\n    return max(usable_paths or paths, key=len) if (usable_paths or paths) else \"\"\n\n\ndef fix_primary_entity(data: dict, ana: Anatomy, paths: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"distiller \u81ea\u9078\u7684 primary_entity \u5fc5\u9808\u662f\u9019\u6b21\u771f\u7684\u6539\u5230\u7684\u6a94\uff08suffix \u8a9e\u610f\uff09\uff1b\n    \u9a57\u4e0d\u904e\u624d fallback\u3002\u56de True = \u88ab\u4fee\u6b63\u904e\u3002\"\"\"\n    ent = (data.get(\"primary_entity\") or \"\").strip()\n    if ent and ana.files and any(match_path(fc.path, ent) for fc in ana.files):\n        return False\n    if ent and not ana.files and ent in paths:\n        return False                     # \u6c92\u6709 diff \u53ef\u6bd4\u5c0d\u6642\u9000\u56de\u820a\u8a9e\u610f\n    data[\"primary_entity\"] = pick_primary_entity(ana, paths)\n    return True\n\n\ndef write_json_atomic(path: Path, obj) -> None:\n    \"\"\"tmp + os.replace\uff1aharvester \u7684 git add / rglob \u649e\u5230\u5beb\u4e00\u534a\u7684\u6a94\u4e5f\u53ea\u6703\u770b\u5230\n    \u5b8c\u6574\u820a\u7248\u6216\u5b8c\u6574\u65b0\u7248\uff0c\u4e0d\u6703\u8b80\u5230\u534a\u622a JSON\u3002\uff08.tmp \u4e0d\u7b26 pr-*.json \u7684 glob\u3002\uff09\"\"\"\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tmp = path.with_name(path.name + \".tmp\")\n    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    os.replace(tmp, path)\n\n\n_EXCLUDE_BASENAMES = {\"pom.xml\", \"build.gradle\", \"build.gradle.kts\", \"package.json\",\n                      \"package-lock.json\", \"yarn.lock\", \"changelog.md\", \"version.txt\",\n                      \"gradle.properties\"}\n_SKIP_DIRS = {\"_pending\", \"_state\", \"_overview\"}\n_AFFECTED_RE = re.compile(r\"## Affected entities\\n(.*?)(\\n#|\\Z)\", re.S)\n\n\ndef _suffix_eq(a: str, b: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\u8def\u5f91\u5f8c\u7db4\u76f8\u7b49\uff0c\u4f46\u53ea\u5728\u8def\u5f91\u6bb5\u908a\u754c\u6210\u7acb\u3002\"\"\"\n    return bool(a) and bool(b) and (\n        a == b or a.endswith(\"/\" + b) or b.endswith(\"/\" + a))\n\n\ndef _affected_block(body: str) -> str:\n    m = _AFFECTED_RE.search(body)\n    return m.group(1) if m else \"\"\n\n\ndef _root() -> Path | None:\n    return settings().knowledge.root\n\n\ndef _norm(p: str) -> str:\n    p = (p or \"\").strip().lstrip(\"/\")\n    if p[:2] in (\"a/\", \"b/\"):\n        p = p[2:]\n    return p.lower()\n\n\n# ---------- \u9801\u9762\u6bd4\u5c0d\uff08\u6aa2\u7d22\u8def\u8207 supersede \u76ee\u9304\u5171\u7528\uff0c\u907f\u514d\u5169\u4efd\u908f\u8f2f\u6f02\u79fb\uff09 ----------\n#\n# \u547d\u4e2d\u5f37\u5ea6\u662f tier \u4e0d\u662f\u5e03\u6797\uff08Phase 3\uff09\uff1a\u6ce8\u5165\u9810\u7b97\u6709\u9650\u6642\uff0c\u300c\u9019\u4e00\u9801\u5c31\u662f\u8b1b\u4f60\u6b63\u5728\u6539\n# \u7684\u90a3\u500b\u6a94\u300d\u5fc5\u9808\u6392\u5728\u300c\u4f60\u6539\u7684\u6a94\u7684\u9130\u5c45\u63d0\u904e\u4e00\u53e5\u300d\u524d\u9762\u3002\u5168\u90e8\u662f ordinal\u2014\u2014\u6c92\u6709\u5206\u6578\n# \u5e38\u6578\u3001\u4e0d\u9700\u8981\u6821\u6e96\uff0c\u540c\u4e00\u4efd diff \u5c0d\u540c\u4e00\u500b\u5e33\u672c SHA \u6c38\u9060\u6ce8\u5165\u540c\u4e00\u7d44\u3002\n#\n#   4  primary \u7cbe\u78ba\u8def\u5f91\uff08\u9801\u9762\u7684 `> entity:` \u5c31\u662f\u9019\u6b21\u8b8a\u66f4\u7684\u6a94\uff09\n#   3  (parent, stem) \u6a94\u540d\u547d\u4e2d\n#   2  Affected entities \u9130\u63a5\uff08graph \u7d66\u7684\u771f\u9130\u5c45\uff09\n#   1  _module \u4eba\u985e\u624b\u5beb\u9801\u7684\u8def\u5f91\u6bb5\u547d\u4e2d\n#   0  \u672a\u547d\u4e2d\n\nTIER_PRIMARY, TIER_FILENAME, TIER_AFFECTED, TIER_MODULE = 4, 3, 2, 1\n\n_ENTITY_LINE = re.compile(r\"^> entity: (.+)$\", re.M)\n\n\nclass _MatchCtx:\n    \"\"\"\u628a\u300c\u9019\u6b21\u8b8a\u66f4\u7684\u6a94\u6848\u300d\u9810\u8655\u7406\u6210\u6bd4\u5c0d\u7528\u7684\u9375\u3002\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, changed_paths: list[str]):\n        self.segs: set[str] = set()\n        self.fname_keys: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()   # (parent_dir, stem)\n        for p in changed_paths:\n            parts = _norm(p).split(\"/\")\n            self.segs.update(parts)\n            if parts:\n                stem = parts[-1].rsplit(\".\", 1)[0]\n                parent = parts[-2] if len(parts) >= 2 else \"\"\n                self.fname_keys.add((parent, stem))\n        self.changed_norm = [_norm(p) for p in changed_paths]\n\n    def entry_tier(self, primary: str, affected: list[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\uff08_cycle/\uff09\u7684\u547d\u4e2d\u5f37\u5ea6 \u2014\u2014 \u8207\u6b63\u5f0f\u9801\u540c\u4e00\u628a\u5c3a\uff0c\u4e00\u8d77\u6392\u5e8f\u3002\"\"\"\n        pn = _norm(primary)\n        if pn and any(_suffix_eq(c, pn) for c in self.changed_norm):\n            return TIER_PRIMARY\n        stem = pn.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1].rsplit(\".\", 1)[0]\n        if stem and any(s2 == stem for _, s2 in self.fname_keys):\n            return TIER_FILENAME\n        if any(self._aff_hit(aff) for aff in affected):\n            return TIER_AFFECTED\n        return 0\n\n    def _aff_hit(self, aff: str) -> bool:\n        a = _norm(aff)\n        if \"/\" in a:\n            return any(_suffix_eq(c, a) for c in self.changed_norm)\n        token = re.split(r\"[.(]\", a, 1)[0].strip()\n        return bool(token) and any(s2 == token for _, s2 in self.fname_keys)\n\n    def page_hit(self, page: Path, rel: Path, body: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\u56de\u547d\u4e2d\u5f37\u5ea6 tier\uff080 = \u6c92\u4e2d\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n        stem = page.stem.lower()\n        if rel.parts and rel.parts[0] == \"_module\":\n            # \u4eba\u985e\u624b\u5beb\u7684\u6a21\u7d44\u9801\uff1a\u8def\u5f91\u6bb5\u547d\u4e2d\uff0c\u5f37\u5ea6\u6700\u4f4e\uff08\u6574\u500b\u6a21\u7d44\u7d1a\u7684\u6cdb\u8ac7\uff09\n            return TIER_MODULE if stem in self.segs else 0\n        m = _ENTITY_LINE.search(body)\n        ent = _norm(m.group(1)) if m else \"\"\n        if ent and any(_suffix_eq(c, ent) for c in self.changed_norm):\n            return TIER_PRIMARY            # \u9019\u4e00\u9801\u8b1b\u7684\u5c31\u662f\u4f60\u6b63\u5728\u6539\u7684\u90a3\u500b\u6a94\n        parent = page.parent.name.lower()\n        if any(stem == s and (not parent or parent == pa or parent in self.segs)\n               for pa, s in self.fname_keys) or (parent, stem) in self.fname_keys:\n            return TIER_FILENAME\n        # \u526f\u9375\uff1a\u689d\u76ee\u7684 Affected entities\uff08graph \u7d66\u7684\u771f\u9130\u63a5\uff09\u2014\u2014\n        # \u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u4f4f\u5728 A\u3001\u958b\u767c\u8005\u6539\u7684\u662f\u9130\u5c45 B\uff0c\u7167\u6a23\u8981\u88ab\u63d0\u9192\u3002\n        if any(self._aff_hit(a)\n               for a in re.findall(r\"`([^`]+)`\", _affected_block(body))):\n            return TIER_AFFECTED\n        return 0\n\n\ndef _matching_pages(base: Path, ctx: _MatchCtx):\n    \"\"\"\u8d70\u8a2a repo \u5e95\u4e0b\u7684\u5e33\u672c\u9801\uff0cyield \u547d\u4e2d\u7684 (page, body, tier)\u3002\"\"\"\n    if not base.is_dir():\n        return\n    for page in sorted(base.rglob(\"*.md\")):\n        rel = page.relative_to(base)\n        if rel.parts and rel.parts[0] in _SKIP_DIRS:\n            continue\n        body = page.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        tier = ctx.page_hit(page, rel, body)\n        if tier:\n            yield page, body, tier\n\n\n_INVARIANT_BLOCK = re.compile(r\"^## Invariants\\n(.*?)(?=\\n## |\\Z)\", re.M | re.S)\n\n\ndef existing_invariants(repo: str | None, changed_paths: list[str]\n                        ) -> list[tuple[str, list[tuple[str, str]]]]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de [(\u9801\u9762\u76f8\u5c0d\u8def\u5f91, [(ID, \u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u539f\u6587)])]\uff0c\u7d66 distiller \u8207 digest \u5206\u6790\u7528\u3002\n\n    \u53ea\u56de\u300c\u9084\u6709\u6548\u300d\u7684\u689d\u76ee\u2014\u2014\u5df2\u7d93\u88ab\u756b\u6389\u7684\uff08`~~\u2026~~`\uff09\u4e0d\u518d\u5217\u5165\uff0c\u5426\u5247\u6a21\u578b\u6703\u88ab\n    \u5f15\u5c0e\u53bb\u91cd\u8907\u8a3b\u92b7\u540c\u4e00\u689d\u3002ID \u4f86\u81ea\u884c\u5c3e `PR12-I1` \u6a19\u8a18\uff1b\u820a\u683c\u5f0f\u7684\u884c ID \u70ba\u7a7a\uff0c\n    \u4ecd\u4ee5\u9010\u5b57\u539f\u6587\u65b9\u5f0f\uff08retires_verbatim\uff09\u53ef\u88ab\u8a3b\u92b7\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None or not repo or not changed_paths:\n        return []\n    base = root / repo.strip().lower()\n    ctx = _MatchCtx(changed_paths)\n    out: list[tuple[str, list[tuple[str, str]]]] = []\n    for page, body, _tier in _matching_pages(base, ctx):\n        m = _INVARIANT_BLOCK.search(body)\n        if not m:\n            continue\n        pairs: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n        for ln in m.group(1).splitlines():\n            ln = ln.strip()\n            if not ln.startswith(\"- \"):\n                continue\n            text, iid = split_id(ln[2:].strip())\n            if text and not text.startswith(\"~~\"):\n                pairs.append((iid, text))\n        if pairs:\n            out.append((page.relative_to(root).as_posix(), pairs))\n    return out\n\n\ndef catalogue_text(cat: list[tuple[str, list[tuple[str, str]]]], header: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u628a existing_invariants \u7684\u7d50\u679c\u6392\u6210\u7d66\u6a21\u578b\u770b\u7684\u6e05\u55ae\uff1a`- [PR12-I1] text`\u3002\"\"\"\n    if not cat:\n        return \"\"\n    blocks = []\n    for rel, pairs in cat:\n        blocks.append(\"## \" + rel + \"\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(\n            f\"- [{iid or 'no-id'}] {text}\" for iid, text in pairs))\n    return header + \"\\n\\n\".join(blocks)\n\n\n# ---------- \u8b80\u53d6\u8def\uff1aStage 04 \u6ce8\u5165 ----------\n\n_ID_ANY = re.compile(r\"\\bPR\\d+-[DI]\\d+\\b\", re.I)\n_RETIRED_LINE = re.compile(r\"^- ~~\", re.M)\n\n\ndef strip_retired(body: str) -> tuple[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"\u628a\u5df2\u8a3b\u92b7\u7684\u884c\uff08`- ~~text~~ \u26a0 retired by PR#nn`\uff09\u5f9e**\u6ce8\u5165\u7528**\u7684\u6587\u5b57\u88e1\u62ff\u6389\u3002\n\n    \u9801\u9762\u4e0a\u4fdd\u7559\uff08\u8a3b\u92b7\u662f\u6a19\u8a18\u4e0d\u662f\u84b8\u767c\uff0c\u4eba\u8981\u770b\u5f97\u5230\u8840\u7de3\uff09\uff1b\u4f46\u9935\u7d66 reviewer \u7684\u5340\u584a\n    \u4e0d\u8a72\u5e36\u8457\u5b83\u2014\u2014\u6a21\u578b\u6703\u7167\u6a23\u62ff\u5b83\u5831 violation\uff0c\u800c\u8aa4\u5831\u6bd4\u6f0f\u5831\u66f4\u5feb\u628a\u4fe1\u4efb\u71d2\u5149\u3002\n    \u9023\u5e36\u6548\u679c\uff1a\u5b83\u7684 id \u4e5f\u5c31\u4e0d\u5728 knowledge_ids \u88e1\uff0creviewer \u4e0d\u80fd\u62ff\u4e00\u689d\u6b7b\u6389\u7684\n    \u898f\u5247\u7576 grounding\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    keep, n = [], 0\n    for ln in body.splitlines():\n        if _RETIRED_LINE.match(ln):\n            n += 1\n            continue\n        keep.append(ln)\n    return (\"\\n\".join(keep), n) if n else (body, 0)\n\n\ndef _short_form(body: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u964d\u8f09\u7248\u672c\uff1a\u53ea\u7559 Invariants \u6bb5\uff08\u6c92\u6709\u5c31\u9000 Summary\uff09\u2014\u2014\u689d\u76ee\u6700\u50cf\u898f\u5247\u7684\u90a3\u90e8\u5206\u3002\"\"\"\n    m = _INVARIANT_BLOCK.search(body)\n    if m and m.group(1).strip():\n        return \"## Invariants\\n\" + m.group(1).strip()\n    m = re.search(r\"^## Summary\\n(.*?)(?=\\n## |\\Z)\", body, re.M | re.S)\n    return (\"## Summary\\n\" + m.group(1).strip()[:1200]) if m else body.strip()[:1200]\n\n\ndef load_for(repo: str | None, changed_paths: list[str]) -> tuple[str, dict]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de (\u6ce8\u5165\u5340\u584a, stats)\u3002\u7121 root / \u7121 repo / \u7121\u547d\u4e2d \u2192 (\"\", {entries:0})\u3002\n\n    \u6392\u5e8f\u8207\u964d\u8f09\uff08Phase 3\uff09\uff1a\n      \u00b7 \u4f9d (-tier, \u8def\u5f91) \u6392 \u2014\u2014 \u7cbe\u78ba\u547d\u4e2d\u7684\u9801\u6392\u5728\u9130\u63a5\u547d\u4e2d\u7684\u524d\u9762\uff0c\u53ef\u91cd\u73fe\u3002\n      \u00b7 tier 4\uff08primary \u7cbe\u78ba\u8def\u5f91\uff09\u4fdd\u8b49\u5165\u5834\uff1a\u585e\u4e0d\u4e0b\u5168\u6587\u5c31\u6ce8\u5165 Invariants \u6bb5\u3002\n      \u00b7 \u5176\u9918\u4f9d\u5e8f\u6ce8\u5165\u5168\u6587\uff1b\u7b2c\u4e00\u6b21\u585e\u4e0d\u4e0b\u5c31\u5207\u6210\u300c\u53ea\u6ce8\u5165 Invariants \u6bb5\u300d\u7e8c\u6392\uff1b\n        \u9023\u77ed\u7248\u90fd\u585e\u4e0d\u4e0b\u624d\u505c\uff0c\u5c3e\u7aef\u5217\u51fa\u88ab\u7701\u7565\u7684\u689d\u76ee\u540d\uff08\u964d\u7d1a\u53ef\u898b\uff09\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    stats = {\"knowledge_entries\": 0}\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None or not repo or not changed_paths:\n        return \"\", stats\n    base = root / repo.strip().lower()\n    cyc_dir = root / \"_cycle\" / repo.strip().lower()\n    if not base.is_dir() and not cyc_dir.is_dir():\n        return \"\", stats\n\n    ctx = _MatchCtx(changed_paths)\n    retired = 0\n    picked: list[tuple[int, str, str, str]] = []      # (tier, sort_key, title, body)\n    for page, body, tier in _matching_pages(base, ctx):\n        body, n = strip_retired(body)                 # \u5df2\u8a3b\u92b7\u7684\u884c\u4e0d\u9032 reviewer\n        retired += n\n        picked.append((tier, page.relative_to(base).as_posix(), page.stem, body))\n\n    if cyc_dir.is_dir():\n        for f in sorted(cyc_dir.glob(\"pr-*.json\")):\n            try:\n                d = json.loads(f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n            draft = d.get(\"draft\") or {}\n            tier = ctx.entry_tier(draft.get(\"primary_entity\", \"\"),\n                                  list(draft.get(\"affected\") or []))\n            if tier:\n                # \u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\u8207\u6b63\u5f0f\u9801\u5957\u540c\u4e00\u628a\u5c3a\u4e00\u8d77\u6392\uff1a\u5b83\u53ef\u80fd\u6b63\u662f\u6700\u76f8\u95dc\u7684\u90a3\u4e00\u689d\n                picked.append((\n                    tier, f.name,\n                    f\"{Path(draft.get('primary_entity', 'entry')).stem} \"\n                    f\"(staged, pending cycle acceptance)\",\n                    render_entry(draft, int(d.get(\"pr_id\", 0)), \"staged\",\n                                 author_note=d.get(\"author_note\", \"\"))))\n\n    if not picked:\n        return \"\", stats\n    picked.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[0], x[1]))\n    cap_total = settings().knowledge.max_chars\n    parts_out = [f\"# Knowledge ({len(picked)} entr\"\n                 f\"{'y' if len(picked) == 1 else 'ies'} relevant to this change)\"]\n    used = 0\n    injected: list[str] = []\n    full = short = 0\n    omitted: list[str] = []\n    degraded = False                     # \u4e00\u65e6\u964d\u8f09\u5c31\u4e0d\u518d\u56de\u982d\uff08\u9806\u5e8f\u5373\u512a\u5148\u5e8f\uff09\n    ids: set[str] = set()\n    for tier, _key, title, body in picked:\n        if omitted:                      # \u5df2\u7d93\u505c\u4e86\uff1a\u5176\u9918\u5168\u90e8\u5217\u9032\u7701\u7565\u540d\u55ae\n            omitted.append(title)\n            continue\n        chunk = f\"\\n## {title}\\n{body.strip()}\"\n        if degraded or used + len(chunk) > cap_total:\n            degraded = True\n            chunk = (f\"\\n## {title} (invariants only \u2014 context budget)\\n\"\n                     f\"{_short_form(body)}\")\n            if used + len(chunk) > cap_total and tier != TIER_PRIMARY:\n                omitted.append(title)\n                continue\n            # tier 4 \u7684\u4fdd\u8b49\u5165\u5834\u512a\u5148\u65bc\u9810\u7b97\uff1a\u9801\u9762\u8b1b\u7684\u5c31\u662f\u9019\u6b21\u6539\u7684\u6a94\uff0c\n            # \u5c11\u6ce8\u5165\u5b83\u7b49\u65bc\u9019\u6b21 review \u767d\u5e36\u4e86\u77e5\u8b58\u5c64\u3002\n            short += 1\n        else:\n            full += 1\n        parts_out.append(chunk)\n        used += len(chunk)\n        injected.append(title)\n        # \u5f15\u7528\u7387\u7684\u5206\u6bcd\uff08Phase 2.1\uff09\uff1a\u53ea\u8a8d\u300c\u771f\u7684\u88ab\u6ce8\u5165\u7684\u90a3\u4e00\u6bb5\u6587\u5b57\u300d\u88e1\u7684 id\u2014\u2014\n        # \u5c3e\u8a3b\u8981\u8209\u4f8b\u8aaa\u660e\u683c\u5f0f\uff0c\u4f8b\u5b50\u4e0d\u80fd\u56e0\u6b64\u8b8a\u6210\u5408\u6cd5\u5f15\u7528\u3002\n        ids.update(m.upper() for m in _ID_ANY.findall(chunk))\n    if omitted:\n        shown = \", \".join(omitted[:8]) + (\", \u2026\" if len(omitted) > 8 else \"\")\n        parts_out.append(f\"\\n({len(omitted)} more matched entries omitted \"\n                         f\"(context budget): {shown})\")\n    stats[\"knowledge_ids\"] = sorted(ids)\n    parts_out.append(\"\\n(evidence-linked team knowledge; treat as leads, not \"\n                     \"limits \u2014 verify against the diff. When a finding rests on \"\n                     \"one of the invariants above, cite its id \u2014 the backticked \"\n                     \"marker at the end of the line \u2014 in knowledge_ref.)\")\n    text = \"\\n\".join(parts_out)\n    stats[\"knowledge_entries\"] = len(picked)\n    stats[\"knowledge_injected\"] = injected      # \u6708\u5ea6 staleness \u62bd\u6a23\u7684\u5206\u6bcd\n    stats[\"knowledge_full\"] = full\n    stats[\"knowledge_invariants_only\"] = short\n    stats[\"knowledge_omitted\"] = len(omitted)\n    if retired:\n        stats[\"knowledge_retired_hidden\"] = retired   # \u964d\u7d1a\u53ef\u898b\uff1a\u88ab\u64cb\u6389\u7684\u6b7b\u898f\u5247\n    return text, stats\n\n\n# ---------- K1 \u9598\u9580 ----------\n\ndef _branch_patterns() -> list[str]:\n    return list(settings().knowledge.branches)\n\n\ndef gate(meta: dict, changed_paths: list[str]) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n    \"\"\"(\u8981\u4e0d\u8981\u84b8\u993e, \u539f\u56e0)\u3002\u539f\u56e0\u9032 journal\uff0c\u4e0d\u9032\u4f7f\u7528\u8005\u9762\u3002\"\"\"\n    if _root() is None:\n        return False, \"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\u5b9a\"\n    target = (meta.get(\"target_branch\") or \"\").replace(\"refs/heads/\", \"\").strip()\n    if not target or not any(fnmatch.fnmatch(target, pat)\n                             for pat in _branch_patterns()):\n        return False, f\"\u76ee\u6a19\u5206\u652f {target or '?'} \u4e0d\u5728 KNOWLEDGE_BRANCHES\"\n    src = (meta.get(\"source_branch\") or \"\").replace(\"refs/heads/\", \"\").strip()\n    cyc_src = settings().knowledge.cycle_source\n    cyc_tgt = settings().knowledge.cycle_target\n    if cyc_src and fnmatch.fnmatch(src, cyc_src) \\\n            and fnmatch.fnmatch(target, cyc_tgt):\n        return False, \"cycle checkpoint PR\uff08\u9a57\u6536\u5100\u5f0f\uff0c\u4e0d\u84b8\u993e\uff09\"\n    title = (meta.get(\"title\") or \"\").strip()\n    if re.match(r\"^Merge (branch|remote-tracking)\", title) \\\n            or re.match(r\"^Merge .+ (into|to) .+\", title, re.I):\n        return False, \"\u5206\u652f\u540c\u6b65 merge PR\"\n    if title.lower().startswith(\"revert\"):\n        return True, \"revert\uff08\u5fc5\u6536\uff09\"\n    paths = [_norm(p) for p in changed_paths]\n    if paths and all(p.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1] in _EXCLUDE_BASENAMES for p in paths):\n        return False, \"\u7d14 version-bump / lockfile\"\n    return True, \"release-bound\"\n\n\n# ---------- \u689d\u76ee\u6e32\u67d3\uff08distiller \u8207 harvester \u5171\u7528\uff09 ----------\n\ndef decision_line(d: dict, pr_id: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"`- text [ev] \\\\`PR12-D1\\\\``\uff1b\u7121 id \u7684\u820a\u7a3f\u9000\u56de `(PR#12)` \u8840\u7de3\u6a19\u8a18\u3002\"\"\"\n    ev = \" \".join(f\"[{e}]\" for e in (d.get(\"evidence\") or []))\n    body = f\"{(d.get('text') or '').strip()} {ev}\".rstrip()\n    did = (d.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n    return f\"- {body} `{did}`\" if did else f\"- {body} (PR#{pr_id})\"\n\n\ndef invariant_line(x) -> str:\n    text, iid = inv_text(x), inv_id(x)\n    return f\"- {text} `{iid}`\" if iid else f\"- {text}\"\n\n\ndef render_entry(data: dict, pr_id: int, provenance: str,\n                 author_note: str = \"\", history_rows: list[str] | None = None) -> str:\n    day = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    ent = data.get(\"primary_entity\") or \"(entity unspecified)\"\n    lines = [f\"# {Path(ent).stem or ent}\", \"\",\n             f\"> entity: {ent}\",\n             f\"> approval: {provenance} \u00b7 last: PR#{pr_id} \u00b7 {day}\", \"\",\n             \"## Summary\", data.get(\"summary\", \"\").strip() or \"(none)\", \"\"]\n    if not data.get(\"intent_stated\", True):\n        lines += [\"> intent: not stated in the PR \u2014 mechanics only.\", \"\"]\n    decs = data.get(\"decisions\") or []\n    if decs:\n        lines.append(\"## Decisions\")\n        lines += [decision_line(d, pr_id) for d in decs if isinstance(d, dict)]\n        lines.append(\"\")\n    inv = data.get(\"invariants\") or []\n    if inv:\n        lines.append(\"## Invariants\")\n        lines += [invariant_line(x) for x in inv if inv_text(x)]\n        lines.append(\"\")\n    if author_note:\n        lines += [\"## Author note\", f\"> {author_note.strip()}\", \"\"]\n    sup = data.get(\"supersedes\") or []\n    if sup:\n        lines.append(\"## Supersedes\")\n        lines += [f\"- \u26a0 `{x.get('entity', '?')}` \u2014 {x.get('what', '')}\" for x in sup]\n        lines.append(\"\")\n    aff = data.get(\"affected\") or []\n    if aff:\n        lines += [\"## Affected entities\", \", \".join(f\"`{a}`\" for a in aff[:8]), \"\"]\n    row = (f\"| PR#{pr_id} | {day} | {data.get('ledger_line', '').strip() or '\u2014'}\"\n           f\" ({data.get('type', 'other')}) \u00b7 {provenance} |\")\n    lines += [\"## History\", \"| PR | Date | Entry |\", \"|---|---|---|\", row]\n    lines += (history_rows or [])\n    lines.append(\"\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ---------- K2 + \u8cbc\u7a3f + _pending ----------\n\ndef _draft_comment(data: dict, pr_id: int, dropped: int = 0) -> str:\n    body = render_entry(data, pr_id, provenance=\"draft\")\n    ask_why = (\"\" if data.get(\"intent_stated\", True) else\n               \"\\n**The PR text does not state why this change was made** \u2014 \"\n               \"reply with one line of intent \u2014 especially any alternative you \"\n               \"considered and rejected \u2014 and it will be recorded verbatim.\\n\")\n    # \u88ab\u4e1f\u6389\u7684 decision \u4e5f\u8981\u770b\u5f97\u898b\uff1a\u4f5c\u8005\u77e5\u9053\u5c11\u4e86\u4ec0\u9ebc\uff0c\u624d\u6709\u6a5f\u6703\u7528\u4e00\u884c note \u88dc\u56de\u4f86\n    dropped_note = (f\"\\n_{dropped} decision(s) dropped: evidence could not be \"\n                    \"verified against this diff._\\n\") if dropped else \"\"\n    return (\"**Knowledge draft \u2014 decision ledger entry**\\n\\n\"\n            \"This will be committed to the team knowledge base when the PR \"\n            \"completes.\\n\" + ask_why + \"\\n---\\n\" + body + \"\\n---\\n\"\n            + dropped_note +\n            \"Reply to add an author note (recorded verbatim) \u00b7 reply `reject` \"\n            \"to discard \u00b7 merging silently records it as-is.\")\n\n\ndef _catalogue_for_paths(repo: str, paths: list[str]) -> str:\n    return catalogue_text(\n        existing_invariants(repo, paths),\n        \"# Existing ledger invariants for the entities this PR touches\\n\"\n        \"# (supersede detection only \u2014 do NOT restate these as your own \"\n        \"decisions; put the bracketed id in retires_id if one is retired)\\n\")\n\n\n@observe(name=\"knowledge-distill-llm\")\nasync def distill_once(pr_id: int, repo: str, meta: dict, ana: Anatomy,\n                       ana_files: list[str], review_markdown: str = \"\",\n                       graph_impacted: list[str] | None = None,\n                       finding_ids: set[str] | None = None,\n                       finding_files: list[str] | None = None,\n                       extra_blocks: list[str] | None = None,\n                       catalogue: str | None = None\n                       ) -> tuple[dict, dict]:\n    \"\"\"\u84b8\u993e\u4e00\u6b21\uff1a\u7d44\u6750\u6599 \u2192 LLM \u2192 \u8b49\u64da\u9a57\u8b49 \u2192 primary \u4fee\u6b63 \u2192 \u88dc ID\u3002\n\n    \u56de (data, info)\u3002info \u5e36 slices_skipped / dropped / evidence_stripped /\n    primary_fixed \u2014\u2014 \u5168\u662f\u300c\u88ab\u964d\u7d1a\u6216\u88ab\u4fee\u6b63\u6389\u7684\u6771\u897f\u300d\uff0c\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u8ca0\u8cac\u5beb\u9032 _pending\n    \u8207 journal\uff08\u84b8\u993e\u8003\u5377\u4e5f\u8b80\u9019\u5e7e\u500b\u6578\uff09\u3002\u5931\u6557\u76f4\u63a5 raise\uff0c\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u6c7a\u5b9a\u964d\u7d1a\u3002\n\n    catalogue \u7d66\u5b9a\u6642\u7528\u5b83\u53d6\u4ee3\u300c\u5f9e KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u8b80\u65e2\u6709\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u300d\u2014\u2014\u53ea\u6709\u96e2\u7dda\u8003\u5377\n    \u6703\u7528\uff08\u8003\u7684\u662f\u84b8\u993e\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u6aa2\u7d22\uff1b\u6aa2\u7d22\u6709\u81ea\u5df1\u7684\u91cf\u5c3a\uff09\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    slices_text, slices_skipped = distill_slices(ana, finding_files)\n    user = \"\\n\\n\".join(filter(None, [\n        f\"# PR #{pr_id}: {meta.get('title', '')}\",\n        f\"Target branch: {meta.get('target_branch', '')}\",\n        (\"Description:\\n\" + (meta.get(\"description\") or \"\"))\n        if meta.get(\"description\") else \"Description: (empty)\",\n        \"Changed files:\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(f\"- {p}\" for p in ana_files),\n        (\"Graph impact outside this diff:\\n\"\n         + \"\\n\".join(f\"- {g}\" for g in (graph_impacted or [])))\n        if graph_impacted else \"\",\n        # reviewer \u770b\u904e\u7684\u540c\u4e00\u4efd\u5ea7\u6a19\u7cfb\uff1afile:line evidence \u5fc5\u9808\u6307\u5f97\u5230\u9019\u88e1\u7684\u884c\n        (\"# Diff excerpt (line numbers annotated \u2014 every file:line you cite \"\n         \"must be visible here)\\n\" + slices_text) if slices_text else \"\",\n        catalogue if catalogue is not None\n        else _catalogue_for_paths(repo, ana_files),\n        *(extra_blocks or []),\n        # \u5831\u544a\u5b8c\u6574\u9935\u5165\uff1a\u84b8\u993e\u7684\u539f\u6599\u5c31\u662f\u300c\u5df2\u7d93\u639b\u597d\u8b49\u64da\u300d\u7684 review \u7d50\u679c\uff0c\n        # \u5f9e\u4e2d\u9593\u5207\u65b7\u6703\u8b93\u6700\u5f8c\u5e7e\u689d finding \u6574\u500b\u6d88\u5931\u3001\u4e14\u7121\u75d5\u3002\n        (\"# Review report (already evidence-linked)\\n\" + review_markdown)\n        if review_markdown else \"\",\n    ]))\n    raw = await complete(prompt_or(DISTILLER_PROMPT_NAME,\n                                   DEFAULT_DISTILLER_PROMPT), user)\n    data = extract_json(raw)\n    if not (isinstance(data, dict) and data.get(\"summary\")):\n        raise ValueError(\"distiller \u8f38\u51fa\u4e0d\u662f\u5408\u7d04 JSON\uff08\u7f3a summary\uff09\")\n    def _ev_count(d: dict) -> int:\n        return sum(len(x.get(\"evidence\") or []) for x in (d.get(\"decisions\") or [])\n                   if isinstance(x, dict))\n\n    before = _ev_count(data)\n    data, dropped = verify_evidence(data, ana, finding_ids,\n                                    meta.get(\"description\") or \"\")\n    primary_fixed = fix_primary_entity(data, ana, ana_files)\n    assign_ids(data, pr_id)          # \u8cbc\u7a3f\u524d\u5c31\u5b9a ID\uff1a\u4f5c\u8005\u770b\u5230\u7684\u548c\u843d\u5730\u7684\u662f\u540c\u4e00\u7d44\n    return data, {\"slices_skipped\": slices_skipped, \"dropped\": dropped,\n                  \"evidence_stripped\": before - _ev_count(data),\n                  \"primary_fixed\": primary_fixed}\n\n\n@observe(name=\"knowledge-distill\")\nasync def distill_and_stage(pr_url: str, meta: dict, ana_files: list[str],\n                            review_markdown: str, graph_impacted: list[str],\n                            diff: str = \"\",\n                            finding_ids: set[str] | None = None,\n                            finding_files: list[str] | None = None,\n                            contradicted: set[str] | None = None) -> None:\n    \"\"\"review \u5b8c\u975e\u540c\u6b65\u8dd1\uff1b\u4efb\u4f55\u5931\u6557\u53ea\u9032 journal\uff08print\uff09\uff0c\u7d55\u4e0d\u5f71\u97ff\u4f7f\u7528\u8005\u3002\n\n    diff / finding_ids / finding_files \u7531 app \u76f4\u63a5\u905e\u4f86\uff08reviewer \u624b\u4e0a\u90a3\u4e00\u4efd\uff09\u2014\u2014\n    \u4e0d\u53e6\u9020 diff \u8868\u793a\u3001\u4e0d\u91cd parse markdown\u3002\u7701\u7565\u6642\u9000\u5316\u6210\u7121\u5207\u7247\u7684\u820a\u884c\u70ba\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    ok, why = gate(meta, ana_files)\n    root = _root()\n    if not ok or root is None:\n        print(f\"[knowledge] \u8df3\u904e\u84b8\u993e\uff1a{why}\")\n        return\n    from shared.azdo import parse_pr_url\n    ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n\n    ana = parse_diff(diff) if diff else Anatomy()\n    try:\n        data, info = await distill_once(\n            ref.pr_id, ref.repo, meta, ana, ana_files,\n            review_markdown=review_markdown, graph_impacted=graph_impacted,\n            finding_ids=finding_ids, finding_files=finding_files)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[knowledge] \u84b8\u993e\u5931\u6557\uff08{e}\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u672c\u689d PR \u4e0d\u7559\u7a3f\")\n        return\n    _log_distill(ref.pr_id, info)\n\n    thread_id = None\n    posted = False\n    dry_run = False\n    post_failed = False\n    try:\n        out = await clients.post_knowledge_draft(\n            pr_url, _draft_comment(data, ref.pr_id, len(info[\"dropped\"])))\n        posted = bool(out and out.get(\"posted\"))\n        dry_run = bool(out and out.get(\"dry_run\"))\n        thread_id = (out or {}).get(\"thread_id\")\n        if dry_run:\n            print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u5f71\u5b50\u6a21\u5f0f\uff08KNOWLEDGE_POST=false\uff09\"\n                  \"\u2014\u2014 \u7a3f\u5165 _pending\uff0c\u4e0d\u6703\u88ab\u4efb\u4f55\u4eba\u88dc\u8cbc\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        post_failed = True                    # \u771f\u5617\u8a66\u3001\u771f\u5931\u6557 \u2192 harvest \u624d\u88dc\u8cbc\n        print(f\"[knowledge] \u8cbc\u7a3f\u5931\u6557\uff08{e}\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u4ecd\u5beb _pending\uff0charvest \u6703\u91cd\u8a66\u4e00\u6b21\")\n\n    pend_dir = root / \"_pending\" / ref.repo.lower()\n    write_json_atomic(pend_dir / f\"pr-{ref.pr_id}.json\", {\n        \"pr_url\": pr_url, \"pr_id\": ref.pr_id, \"repo\": ref.repo.lower(),\n        \"target_branch\": (meta.get(\"target_branch\") or \"\")\n        .replace(\"refs/heads/\", \"\").strip(),\n        \"base_url\": ref.base_url, \"distilled_commit\": meta.get(\"source_commit\"),\n        \"author\": meta.get(\"author\", \"\"), \"thread_id\": thread_id,\n        \"posted\": posted, \"dry_run\": dry_run, \"post_failed\": post_failed,\n        \"draft\": data, \"created\": time.strftime(\"%FT%T\"),\n        # \u9019\u6b21 review \u88e1\u300c\u88ab\u5be6\u4f5c\u8e29\u5230\u300d\u7684\u65e2\u6709\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\uff08\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\uff0c\u4f86\u81ea knowledge_ref\uff09\n        \"contradicted\": sorted({str(x).upper() for x in (contradicted or set())}),\n        **_provenance_fields(info),\n    })\n    repos_f = root / \"_state\" / \"repos.json\"\n    repos = json.loads(repos_f.read_text()) if repos_f.exists() else {}\n    repos[ref.repo.lower()] = ref.base_url\n    write_json_atomic(repos_f, repos)\n    print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u84b8\u993e\u7a3f\u5df2\u5165 _pending\uff08posted={posted}\uff09\")\n\n\ndef _provenance_fields(info: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\u7a3f\u88e1\u81ea\u5e36\u300c\u9019\u4e00\u7a3f\u88ab\u9a57\u904e\u3001\u88ab\u4e1f\u904e\u4ec0\u9ebc\u300d\u2014\u2014\u5f71\u5b50\u671f\u9a57\u6536\u770b\u9019\u5e7e\u500b\u6b04\u4f4d\u3002\"\"\"\n    return {\"evidence_verified\": True,\n            \"distill_dropped\": info.get(\"dropped\") or [],\n            \"distill_slices_skipped\": info.get(\"slices_skipped\") or []}\n\n\ndef _log_distill(pr_id: int, info: dict) -> None:\n    if info.get(\"dropped\"):\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{pr_id} \u8b49\u64da\u9a57\u8b49\uff1a\u4e1f\u6389 {len(info['dropped'])} \u689d \"\n              f\"decision \u2014\u2014 \" + \" | \".join(info[\"dropped\"][:3]))\n    if info.get(\"slices_skipped\"):\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{pr_id} \u84b8\u993e\u5207\u7247\u8d85\u9810\u7b97\uff0c{len(info['slices_skipped'])} \"\n              f\"\u6a94\u672a\u9032 excerpt\uff1a{', '.join(info['slices_skipped'][:5])}\")\n    if info.get(\"primary_fixed\"):\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{pr_id} primary_entity \u4e0d\u5728\u8b8a\u66f4\u6a94\u5167 \u2014\u2014 \u5df2\u6539\u7528\"\n              \"\u65b0\u589e\u884c\u6578\u6700\u591a\u7684\u6a94\")\n\n\n# ---------- Phase 5\uff1astale \u91cd\u84b8\uff08harvester \u53ea\u5075\u6e2c\uff0c\u9019\u88e1\u505a\u5168\u90e8\uff09 ----------\n\ndef redistill_enabled() -> bool:\n    return settings().knowledge.redistill\n\n\ndef _clear_cycle_traces(root: Path, repo: str, pr_id: int) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u91cd\u84b8\u6703\u7522\u751f\u540c ID\u3001\u4e0d\u540c\u5167\u5bb9\u7684\u884c\u2014\u2014\u820a\u7684\u300c\u5df2\u5217 / \u5df2 reject\u300d\u8a18\u9304\u4e00\u5f8b\u4f5c\u5ee2\u3002\n\n    \u00b7 \u4efb\u4f55\u9031\u671f state \u7684 listed \u79fb\u9664 PR<n> \u2192 \u4e0b\u4e00\u5247 delta \u6703\u91cd\u65b0\u5217\u5b83\n      \uff08\u6c92\u4eba\u770b\u904e\u7684\u65b0\u5167\u5bb9\u4e0d\u6703\u9802\u8457\u300c\u5df2\u5217\u300d\u72c0\u614b\u7121\u8072\u843d\u5730\uff09\n    \u00b7 \u6c60\u88e1\u82e5\u5df2\u6709\u540c\u4e00\u689d PR \u7684\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\uff08\u624b\u52d5\u88dc\u84b8\u7684\u60c5\u5883\uff09\u9023\u540c\u5b83\u7684 rejected_ids\n      \u4e00\u8d77\u79fb\u9664\u2014\u2014reject \u6307\u7684\u662f\u820a\u884c\uff0c\u5957\u5230\u65b0\u884c\u662f\u8aa4\u6bba\n    \"\"\"\n    out: list[str] = []\n    staged = root / \"_cycle\" / repo / f\"pr-{pr_id}.json\"\n    if staged.exists():\n        staged.unlink()\n        out.append(f\"\u79fb\u9664\u820a\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f _cycle/{repo}/pr-{pr_id}.json\uff08\u542b rejected_ids\uff09\")\n    state_f = root / \"_state\" / \"cycle.json\"\n    if state_f.exists():\n        try:\n            state = json.loads(state_f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        except Exception:\n            return out\n        key = f\"PR{pr_id}\"\n        touched = False\n        for ck, st in state.items():\n            if key in (st.get(\"listed\") or []):\n                st[\"listed\"] = [x for x in st[\"listed\"] if x != key]\n                touched = True\n                out.append(f\"{ck} \u7684 listed \u79fb\u9664 {key}\uff08\u4e0b\u4e00\u5247 digest \u91cd\u65b0\u5217\uff09\")\n        if touched:\n            write_json_atomic(state_f, state)\n    return out\n\n\n@observe(name=\"knowledge-redistill\")\nasync def redistill(pr_url: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\u7528\u6700\u7d42 diff \u91cd\u84b8\u4e00\u6b21\u3001\u8986\u5beb _pending/\u3002\n\n    \u6750\u6599\u523b\u610f\u6bd4\u9996\u84b8\u7a84\uff1a\u6700\u7d42 diff \u5207\u7247 + title/branch/description + \u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u76ee\u9304\n    + \u65e2\u6536\u7684 author replies\uff08\u9010\u5b57\uff09\u3002**\u4e0d\u542b\u820a review \u5831\u544a**\u3001graph \u7d66\u7a7a\u3001\n    finding_ids \u7d66\u7a7a\u96c6\u5408\u2014\u2014\u90a3\u4efd\u5831\u544a\u662f\u5c0d\u820a diff \u5beb\u7684\uff0cF \u7de8\u865f\u5df2\u7d93 stale\uff0c\n    \u5bb9\u8a31\u5b83\u9032\u4f86\u53ea\u6703\u8b93 evidence \u6307\u5411\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\u7684\u6771\u897f\u3002\u7a84\u4e00\u9ede\u63db\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None:\n        print(\"[knowledge] \u91cd\u84b8\u8df3\u904e\uff1aKNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\u5b9a\")\n        return\n    if not redistill_enabled():\n        print(\"[knowledge] \u91cd\u84b8\u8df3\u904e\uff1aKNOWLEDGE_REDISTILL=false\")\n        return\n    from shared.azdo import parse_pr_url\n    ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n    pend = root / \"_pending\" / ref.repo.lower() / f\"pr-{ref.pr_id}.json\"\n    try:\n        info = json.loads(pend.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[knowledge] \u91cd\u84b8\u8df3\u904e\uff1a\u8b80\u4e0d\u5230 _pending \u7a3f\uff08{e}\uff09\")\n        return\n    if info.get(\"redistilled\"):\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u5df2\u91cd\u84b8\u904e\u4e00\u6b21\uff0c\u4e0d\u518d\u91cd\u84b8\")\n        return\n\n    try:\n        meta = await clients.fetch_pr_metadata(pr_url)\n        diff = await clients.fetch_pr_diff(pr_url)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u91cd\u84b8\u53d6\u4ef6\u5931\u6557\uff08{e}\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u7a3f\u4fdd\u7559\uff0c\"\n              \"harvester \u4e0b\u4e00\u8f2a\u6c7a\u5b9a\u8981\u4e0d\u8981\u518d\u8a66\")\n        return\n    ana = parse_diff(diff)\n    ana_files = [fc.path for fc in ana.files]\n    replies = (info.get(\"author_note\") or \"\").strip()\n    extra = ([f\"# Author's reply to an earlier draft of this entry (verbatim)\"\n              f\"\\n{replies}\"] if replies else [])\n    try:\n        data, dinfo = await distill_once(\n            ref.pr_id, ref.repo, meta, ana, ana_files,\n            review_markdown=\"\", graph_impacted=[],\n            finding_ids=set(), finding_files=[], extra_blocks=extra)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u91cd\u84b8\u5931\u6557\uff08{e}\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u7a3f\u4fdd\u7559\uff08stale\uff09\uff0c\"\n              \"harvester \u4e0b\u4e00\u8f2a\u6309\u91cd\u8a66\u4e0a\u9650\u8655\u7406\")\n        return\n    _log_distill(ref.pr_id, dinfo)\n    merged = (info.get(\"redistill_requested\") or {}).get(\"commit\") \\\n        or meta.get(\"source_commit\")\n    posted, dry_run, post_failed = info.get(\"posted\", False), False, False\n    try:\n        out = await clients.post_knowledge_draft(\n            pr_url, _draft_comment(data, ref.pr_id, len(dinfo[\"dropped\"])),\n            thread_id=info.get(\"thread_id\"))\n        posted = bool(out and out.get(\"posted\")) or posted\n        dry_run = bool(out and out.get(\"dry_run\"))\n    except Exception as e:\n        post_failed = True\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u91cd\u84b8\u7a3f\u56de\u8cbc\u5931\u6557\uff08{e}\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u7a3f\u7167\u6a23\u66f4\u65b0\")\n\n    if not pend.exists():\n        # \u6211\u5011\u84b8\u7684\u671f\u9593 harvester \u5df2\u7d93\u628a\u9019\u689d\u5224\u6b7b\uff08\u91cd\u8a66\u4e0a\u9650\u7528\u76e1 / \u4e16\u4ee3\u8b8a\u66f4\uff09\u2014\u2014\n        # \u9019\u88e1\u518d\u5beb\u56de\u53bb\u7b49\u65bc\u8b93\u4e00\u4efd\u5df2\u7d93\u88ab\u88c1\u6c7a\u6389\u7684\u7a3f\u5fa9\u6d3b\u3002\u653e\u68c4\uff0c\u53ea\u7559 journal\u3002\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u91cd\u84b8\u5b8c\u6210\u4f46\u7a3f\u5df2\u88ab\u6536\u5272\u5668\u4e1f\u68c4 \u2014\u2014 \u4e0d\u5fa9\u6d3b\")\n        return\n    # \u820a\u75d5\u8de1\u7684\u4f5c\u5ee2\u7dca\u8cbc\u8457\u5beb\u5165\u505a\uff1a\u78ba\u5b9a\u8981\u8986\u5beb\u4e86\u624d\u52d5\u5225\u4eba\u7684\u72c0\u614b\n    for line in _clear_cycle_traces(root, ref.repo.lower(), ref.pr_id):\n        print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u91cd\u84b8\uff1a{line}\")\n    info.update({\n        \"draft\": data, \"distilled_commit\": merged,\n        # \u91cd\u84b8\u6c92\u6709 review \u5831\u544a\u53ef\u8b80\uff0c\u9a57\u4e0d\u4e86\u300c\u90a3\u4e9b\u77db\u76fe\u662f\u4e0d\u662f\u9084\u5728\u300d\u2014\u2014\u9a57\u4e0d\u4e86\u5c31\u4e0d\u63d0\u6848\u3002\n        # \u4f5c\u8005\u82e5\u662f\u7167 review \u628a code \u6539\u56de\u4f86\u624d push\uff0c\u77db\u76fe\u672c\u4f86\u5c31\u8a72\u6d88\u5931\uff0c\u9019\u662f\u6b63\u78ba\u65b9\u5411\u3002\n        \"contradicted\": [],\n        \"redistilled\": True, \"redistill_of\": info.get(\"distilled_commit\"),\n        \"posted\": posted, \"dry_run\": dry_run, \"post_failed\": post_failed,\n        \"redistilled_at\": time.strftime(\"%FT%T\"),\n        **_provenance_fields(dinfo),\n    })\n    info.pop(\"redistill_requested\", None)     # \u6233\u6e05\u6389 = \u9019\u4e00\u8f2a\u8acb\u6c42\u5df2\u7d93\u88ab\u6d88\u5316\n    write_json_atomic(pend, info)\n    print(f\"[knowledge] PR#{ref.pr_id} \u91cd\u84b8\u5b8c\u6210 \u2192 _pending \u8986\u5beb\"\n          f\"\uff08commit {str(merged)[:8]}\uff09\")\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/knowledge_digest.py","perm":"0644","sha":"f8f466188571e61f08ac8df9cef6bbd096b315fa1aaac1078d644a7b100c61fc","data":"\"\"\"Cycle digest \u2014\u2014 \u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u7684\u4ecb\u9762\uff08render\uff09\uff0b LLM \u8f14\u52a9\u7684\u9867\u554f\u5206\u6790\uff08analyze\uff09\u3002\n\n\u5b9a\u4f4d\uff1adigest \u662f**\u63d0\u6848**\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u5e33\u672c\u3002\u9019\u88e1\u7684 LLM \u53ea\u505a\u4e09\u4ef6\u4e8b\uff0c\u800c\u4e14\u5168\u662f\u552f\u8b80\uff1a\n  1) \u6309\u5be6\u9ad4\u770b\u6574\u9031\u671f\u7684\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\uff08distiller \u662f\u9010\u689d PR \u770b\u7684\uff0c\u770b\u4e0d\u5230\u540c\u9031\u671f\u9130\u5c45\uff09\n  2) \u6a19\u51fa\u4e92\u76f8\u77db\u76fe / \u8fd1\u91cd\u8907 / \u8a72\u8a3b\u92b7\u537b\u6c92\u9ede\u540d\u7684\u689d\u76ee\n  3) \u5efa\u8b70 release owner \u8a72 reject \u54ea\u500b ID\n\u8f38\u51fa\u53ea\u5f15\u7528\u7cfb\u7d71\u7d66\u5b83\u7684 ID\uff1b\u9a57\u8b49\u4e0d\u904e\u7684 ID \u4e00\u5f8b\u4e1f\uff1b\u5206\u6790\u5931\u6557\u5c31\u9000\u56de\u7d14\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\n\u6e05\u55ae\u2014\u2014\u843d\u5730\u8def\u5f91\uff08_land\uff09\u6c38\u9060\u4e0d\u8b80\u9019\u88e1\u7684\u4efb\u4f55\u8f38\u51fa\u3002\u300cLLM \u63d0\u3001\u4eba\u88c1\u3001code \u57f7\u884c\u300d\uff0c\n\u8207 adversary \u2192 synthesis \u662f\u540c\u4e00\u500b\u6a21\u5f0f\u3002\n\n\u8a2d\u5b9a\uff1asettings().knowledge.digest_llm / digest_max_flags\u3001settings().llm.model_digest\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom orchestrator.knowledge import (assign_ids, catalogue_text, decision_line, entry_ids,\n                                    existing_invariants, inv_id, inv_text,\n                                    norm_id)\nfrom orchestrator.llm import complete_sync, extract_json, prompt_or\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\nKMARK = \"<!-- pr-review-knowledge-digest -->\"\nDIGEST_PROMPT_NAME = \"pr-review-digest\"\n\nDEFAULT_DIGEST_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are the knowledge-cycle auditor of an automated code-review system. Over one release cycle, each merged pull request was distilled into a decision-ledger entry (decisions and invariants, each with a stable id such as PR12-D1 or PR12-I1). Before these entries are committed to the team knowledge base, a release owner will skim a digest and may reject entries by id. Your job is to tell that person where to look.\n\nYou receive:\n- the staged entries of this cycle, grouped by PR, each line prefixed with its id;\n- the invariants already in the ledger for the same code entities, each prefixed with its id (or [no-id] for legacy lines).\n\nFind, and only report:\n- \"conflict\": two lines (staged vs staged, or staged vs already-landed) that cannot both be true.\n- \"duplicate\": two staged lines that state the same rule, possibly paraphrased \u2014 say which one to keep (prefer the one with an author note, the more specific wording, or the later PR).\n- \"retire_check\": a staged entry declares that it supersedes something, but no landed invariant is pointed at by id even though one clearly matches \u2014 name the landed id it should retire.\n- \"unclear\": a staged invariant that is a narrative of the diff rather than a checkable constraint (low priority; report at most two).\n\nHard rules:\n- Reference ONLY ids that appear in the material. Never invent ids, never paraphrase an id.\n- One sentence per note. No praise, no summary of entries that are fine.\n- If nothing needs attention, return an empty \"flags\" list. Silence is a valid answer.\n- Suggestions must be phrased as reject commands, e.g. \"reject PR12-I1\"; suggest at most one command per flag.\n\nOutput a single JSON object only \u2014 the first character must be \"{\" and the last \"}\":\n{\"headline\": \"One sentence: what this cycle establishes overall.\",\n \"flags\": [{\"kind\": \"conflict|duplicate|retire_check|unclear\",\n            \"ids\": [\"PR12-I1\", \"PR15-I2\"],\n            \"note\": \"Why these need a look, one sentence.\",\n            \"suggest\": \"reject PR12-I1\"}]}\"\"\"\n\n_KINDS = (\"conflict\", \"retire_check\", \"duplicate\", \"unclear\")\n\n\n# ---------- \u8f38\u5165\u7d44\u88dd ----------\n\ndef _stem(ent: str) -> str:\n    return Path(ent or \"entry\").stem or (ent or \"entry\")\n\n\ndef catalogue_for(repo: str, items: list[dict]):\n    \"\"\"\u6574\u9031\u671f\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\u89f8\u53ca\u7684\u5be6\u9ad4\uff0c\u5176\u6b63\u5f0f\u9801\u4e0a\u9084\u6709\u6548\u7684\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\uff08\u53bb\u91cd\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    out = []\n    for it in items:\n        d = it.get(\"draft\") or {}\n        paths = [d.get(\"primary_entity\", \"\")] + list(d.get(\"affected\") or [])\n        for rel, pairs in existing_invariants(repo, [p for p in paths if p]):\n            if rel not in seen:\n                seen.add(rel)\n                out.append((rel, pairs))\n    return out\n\n\ndef known_ids(items: list[dict], catalogue) -> set[str]:\n    ids: set[str] = set()\n    for it in items:\n        ids |= entry_ids(it.get(\"draft\") or {}, int(it.get(\"pr_id\", 0)))\n    for _, pairs in catalogue:\n        ids.update(iid for iid, _ in pairs if iid)\n    return {i.upper() for i in ids}\n\n\ndef analysis_input(items: list[dict], catalogue) -> str:\n    blocks = [\"# Staged entries of this cycle (pending acceptance)\"]\n    for it in items:\n        d = it.get(\"draft\") or {}\n        pid = it.get(\"pr_id\")\n        lines = [f\"## PR#{pid} \u2014 {d.get('primary_entity', '?')} \"\n                 f\"(provenance: {it.get('provenance', 'silent')})\",\n                 f\"summary: {(d.get('summary') or '').strip()}\"]\n        for x in d.get(\"decisions\") or []:\n            if isinstance(x, dict):\n                lines.append(decision_line(x, int(pid or 0)))\n        for x in d.get(\"invariants\") or []:\n            if inv_text(x):\n                lines.append(f\"- {inv_text(x)} `{inv_id(x) or 'no-id'}`\")\n        for s in d.get(\"supersedes\") or []:\n            lines.append(f\"supersedes: `{s.get('entity', '?')}` \u2014 {s.get('what', '')}\"\n                         + (f\" (retires_id: {s.get('retires_id')})\"\n                            if s.get(\"retires_id\") else \" (no retires_id)\"))\n        if it.get(\"author_note\"):\n            lines.append(\"author note: \" + it[\"author_note\"].strip())\n        blocks.append(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n    cat = catalogue_text(\n        catalogue, \"# Invariants already in the ledger for the same entities\\n\")\n    if cat:\n        blocks.append(cat)\n    return \"\\n\\n\".join(blocks)\n\n\n# ---------- \u9a57\u8b49\uff08\u5e7b\u89ba\u5728\u9019\u88e1\u88ab\u64cb\u6389\uff09 ----------\n\ndef validate(raw, known: set[str], max_flags: int | None = None) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"\u56de {\"headline\": str, \"flags\": [...]} \u6216 None\uff08\u7d50\u69cb\u4e0d\u5c0d = \u6574\u4efd\u4e0d\u7528\uff09\u3002\n    \u6bcf\u500b flag\uff1akind \u6b63\u898f\u5316\u3001ids \u53ea\u7559\u7cfb\u7d71\u8a8d\u5f97\u7684\u3001\u4e00\u500b\u90fd\u4e0d\u5269\u5c31\u4e1f\u3002\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(raw, dict):\n        return None\n    cap = max_flags if max_flags is not None else \\\n        settings().knowledge.digest_max_flags\n    flags = []\n    for f in (raw.get(\"flags\") or []):\n        if not isinstance(f, dict):\n            continue\n        kind = str(f.get(\"kind\") or \"\").strip().lower()\n        if kind not in _KINDS:\n            continue\n        ids = []\n        for x in (f.get(\"ids\") or []):\n            t = str(x).strip().upper()\n            if t in known and t not in ids:\n                ids.append(t)\n        if not ids:\n            continue\n        note = \" \".join(str(f.get(\"note\") or \"\").split())\n        sug = \" \".join(str(f.get(\"suggest\") or \"\").split())\n        # \u5efa\u8b70\u5fc5\u9808\u662f reject <\u5df2\u77e5 ID>\uff0c\u5426\u5247\u53ea\u7559 note\n        st = sug.split()\n        if not (len(st) == 2 and st[0].lower() == \"reject\"\n                and st[1].upper() in known):\n            sug = \"\"\n        flags.append({\"kind\": kind, \"ids\": ids, \"note\": note, \"suggest\": sug})\n    flags.sort(key=lambda f: _KINDS.index(f[\"kind\"]))\n    return {\"headline\": \" \".join(str(raw.get(\"headline\") or \"\").split()),\n            \"flags\": flags[:cap]}\n\n\n# ---------- LLM \u547c\u53eb\uff08\u5931\u6557 = None\uff0c\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u9000\u56de\u7d14\u6e05\u55ae\uff09 ----------\n\ndef analyze(repo: str, items: list[dict], log=print) -> dict | None:\n    if not settings().knowledge.digest_llm:\n        return None\n    if not items:\n        return None\n    try:\n        for it in items:                       # \u9632\u5446\uff1a\u672a\u88dc ID \u7684\u7a3f\u5148\u5c0d\u9f4a\n            assign_ids(it.get(\"draft\") or {}, int(it.get(\"pr_id\", 0)))\n        cat = catalogue_for(repo, items)\n        known = known_ids(items, cat)\n        raw = complete_sync(prompt_or(DIGEST_PROMPT_NAME, DEFAULT_DIGEST_PROMPT),\n                            analysis_input(items, cat),\n                            model=settings().llm.model_digest)\n        out = validate(extract_json(raw), known)\n        if out is None:\n            log(f\"[digest] {repo}: \u5206\u6790\u8f38\u51fa\u4e0d\u662f\u5408\u7d04 JSON \u2014\u2014 \u9000\u56de\u7d14\u6e05\u55ae\")\n        return out\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        log(f\"[digest] {repo}: \u5206\u6790\u5931\u6557\uff08{e}\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u9000\u56de\u7d14\u6e05\u55ae\")\n        return None\n\n\n# ---------- \u6e32\u67d3 ----------\n\ndef _involves(flag: dict, prs: set[str]) -> bool:\n    return any(i.split(\"-\", 1)[0] in prs for i in flag[\"ids\"])\n\n\ndef render(items: list[dict], new_prs: set[str] | None,\n           analysis: dict | None, total: int | None = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"new_prs=None \u2192 \u9996\u6b21 digest\uff08\u5168\u5217\uff09\uff1b\u7d66\u5b9a \u2192 delta\uff08\u53ea\u5217\u65b0\u9032\u7684\u3001\u65d7\u6a19\u53ea\u7559\n    \u727d\u6d89\u65b0\u9032 PR \u7684\uff09\u3002\u65d7\u6a19\u8207\u8a3b\u92b7\u7d05\u5340\u6392\u5728\u689d\u76ee\u6e05\u55ae\u524d\u9762\uff1a\u6383\u7684\u4eba\u5148\u770b\u8981\u8655\u7406\u7684\u3002\"\"\"\n    shown = items if new_prs is None else \\\n        [it for it in items if f\"PR{it.get('pr_id')}\" in new_prs]\n    n = len(shown)\n    if new_prs is None:\n        head = [KMARK, f\"**Knowledge cycle digest \u2014 pending acceptance** \"\n                       f\"({n} entr{'y' if n == 1 else 'ies'})\", \"\"]\n    else:\n        head = [KMARK, f\"**Knowledge cycle digest \u2014 update: {n} new \"\n                       f\"entr{'y' if n == 1 else 'ies'} since the last digest**\"\n                       + (f\" ({total} total this cycle)\" if total else \"\"), \"\"]\n    head += [\"The entries below were distilled from this cycle's PRs and will \"\n             \"be committed to the team knowledge base when this PR completes. \"\n             \"Reply `reject <EntityName>` or `reject PR12` to drop an entry, \"\n             \"`reject PR12-I1` to drop one line, `keep PR12-I1` to veto the \"\n             \"retirement of an existing rule. Merging silently accepts the rest.\",\n             \"\"]\n    lines = head\n\n    if analysis:\n        flags = analysis[\"flags\"] if new_prs is None else \\\n            [f for f in analysis[\"flags\"] if _involves(f, new_prs)]\n        if analysis.get(\"headline\") and new_prs is None:\n            lines += [f\"_{analysis['headline']}_\", \"\"]\n        if flags:\n            lines += [\"**\ud83d\udd0e Needs a look** \u2014 LLM-assisted, advisory only; \"\n                      \"nothing is dropped automatically:\"]\n            for f in flags:\n                ids = \" \u2194 \".join(f\"`{i}`\" for i in f[\"ids\"])\n                lines.append(f\"- **{f['kind']}** {ids} \u2014 {f['note']}\"\n                             + (f\" \u2192 `{f['suggest']}`\" if f[\"suggest\"] else \"\"))\n            lines.append(\"\")\n\n    retiring = []\n    for it in shown:\n        for x in (it.get(\"draft\") or {}).get(\"supersedes\") or []:\n            retiring.append(\n                f\"- \u26a0 **{x.get('entity', '?')}** \u2014 {x.get('what', '')}\"\n                + (f\" (retires `{x.get('retires_id')}`)\"\n                   if x.get(\"retires_id\") else \"\")\n                + f\" (by PR#{it.get('pr_id')})\")\n    if retiring:\n        lines += [\"**\u26a0 Rules being retired this cycle** \u2014 removals are riskier \"\n                  \"than additions; review these first:\", *retiring, \"\"]\n\n    # \u77db\u76fe\u7d05\u5340\uff1a\u898f\u5247\u88ab\u5408\u4f75\u7684\u5be6\u4f5c\u63a8\u7ffb\u4e86\u3002\u9019\u662f\u63d0\u6848\u4e0d\u662f\u65e2\u6210\u4e8b\u5be6\u2014\u2014\u6c89\u9ed8\u5373\u63a5\u53d7\n    # \uff08\u8207\u65b0\u689d\u76ee\u540c\u4e00\u5957\u6838\u51c6\u8a9e\u610f\uff09\uff0c\u4efb\u4f55\u4eba\u56de `keep <ID>` \u5c31\u5426\u6c7a\u672c\u6b21\u62d4\u9664\u3002\n    contra = []\n    for it in shown:\n        for iid in (it.get(\"contradicted\") or []):\n            contra.append(f\"- \u26a0 `{iid}` \u2014 contradicted by the code merged in \"\n                          f\"PR#{it.get('pr_id')}\"\n                          f\" ({_stem((it.get('draft') or {}).get('primary_entity', ''))})\"\n                          f\" \u2192 reply `keep {iid}` to keep the rule\")\n    if contra:\n        lines += [\"**\u26a0 Invariants contradicted by merged code** \u2014 the review \"\n                  \"flagged these and the change merged anyway, so they are \"\n                  \"proposed for retirement at close. They will be struck \"\n                  \"through (never deleted) unless someone objects:\", *contra, \"\"]\n\n    for it in shown:\n        d = it.get(\"draft\") or {}\n        pid = it.get(\"pr_id\")\n        lines.append(f\"- **{_stem(d.get('primary_entity', 'entry'))}** \"\n                     f\"(PR#{pid} \u00b7 {it.get('provenance', 'silent')}) \u2014 \"\n                     f\"{(d.get('ledger_line') or d.get('summary') or '').strip()}\")\n        for x in d.get(\"decisions\") or []:\n            if isinstance(x, dict):\n                lines.append(\"  \" + decision_line(x, int(pid or 0)))\n        for x in d.get(\"invariants\") or []:\n            if inv_text(x):\n                lines.append(f\"  - {inv_text(x)}\"\n                             + (f\" `{inv_id(x)}`\" if inv_id(x) else \"\"))\n        if it.get(\"author_note\"):\n            lines.append(\"  - \ud83d\udcac author: \" + \" \".join(it[\"author_note\"].split()))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines).rstrip() + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef parse_reject_token(tok: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de ('entry', 'PR12') / ('line', 'PR12-I1') / ('name', \u539f token)\u3002\"\"\"\n    t = (tok or \"\").strip()\n    iid = norm_id(t)\n    if iid:\n        return \"line\", iid\n    if t.upper().startswith(\"PR\") and t[2:].isdigit():\n        return \"entry\", t.upper()\n    return \"name\", t\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/knowledge_harvest.py","perm":"0644","sha":"b6cd95e6f0daaac4199ad1a7197138aca4437a988275f31b0bcdd665a377d1a1","data":"\"\"\"K \u6bb5\u6536\u5272\u5668 \u2014\u2014 \u552f\u4e00 commit \u8005\u3002timer \u6bcf 30 \u5206\u8dd1\u4e00\u6b21\uff1a\n\n  1) git add/commit \u6536\u650f\u65b0 _pending\uff08distiller \u53ea\u5beb\u6a94\u3001\u4e0d\u78b0 git \u2192 \u7121\u4f75\u767c\u885d\u7a81\uff09\n  2) \u9010\u689d pending \u554f PR \u7d42\u614b\uff1a\n       active     \u2192 \u966a\u7b49\uff08\u7121\u904e\u671f\u6a5f\u5236\uff1aPR \u958b\u591a\u4e45\u6211\u5011\u966a\u591a\u4e45\uff09\n       abandoned  \u2192 \u4e1f\u7a3f\uff08\u5f9e\u672a\u767c\u751f\u7684\u6c7a\u7b56\u4e0d\u5165\u5e33\u672c\uff09\n       completed  \u2192 \u8b80\u6211\u5011\u90a3\u689d thread \u5206\u985e\uff1a\n           \u4f5c\u8005\u56de\u8986\u542b reject          \u2192 \u4e1f\n           \u4f5c\u8005\u6709\u56de\u8986\uff08\u5176\u4ed6\uff09          \u2192 explicit\uff1a\u56de\u8986\u9010\u5b57\u5165 Author note\n           \u6c89\u9ed8 + code \u672a\u518d\u52d5         \u2192 silent\uff1a\u539f\u7a3f\u7167\u55ae\u843d\u5730\n           draft \u4e4b\u5f8c\u53c8\u6709\u65b0 push      \u2192 stale\uff1a\u8acb\u6c42 orchestrator \u7528\u6700\u7d42 diff\n                                       \u91cd\u84b8\uff08\u8acb\u6c42\u6233 + attempts \u2264 2\uff1b\u95dc\u6389\n                                       KNOWLEDGE_REDISTILL \u5c31\u56de\u5230\u76f4\u63a5\u4e1f\u7a3f\uff09\n  3) watermark \u6383\u63cf\uff1a\u76ee\u6a19\u5206\u652f\u4e0a\u300c\u6c92\u7d93\u904e bot\u300d\u5c31 completed \u7684 PR \u2192 \u88dc\u4e00\u689d\n     History \u5e33\u672c\u884c\uff08provenance=unreviewed\uff09\uff0crelease \u53f2\u96f6\u907a\u6f0f\n  4) \u9031\u671f\u6536\u53e3\uff08release \u2192 master \u9a57\u6536 PR\uff09\uff1a\n       active     \u2192 \u8cbc digest\uff08\u9996\u6b21\u5168\u5217\uff1b\u4e4b\u5f8c\u6bcf\u6709\u65b0\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\u88dc\u4e00\u5247 delta\u2014\u2014\n                    release owner \u6c92\u770b\u904e\u7684\u689d\u76ee\u4e0d\u6703\u7121\u8072\u843d\u5730\uff09\uff0b \u6536 reject\n       completed  \u2192 \u6536\u53e3\u524d\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u6b21\u6536 reject \u2192 \u6279\u6b21\u843d\u5730 \u2192 _cycles/ \u6536\u64da\n                    \uff08\u5f9e\u672a\u51fa\u73fe\u5728\u4efb\u4f55 digest \u7684\u689d\u76ee provenance \u5e36 +unlisted\uff09\n  5) \u7d71\u4e00 git commit\n\nreject \u4e09\u7a2e\u7c92\u5ea6\uff08\u884c\u9996\u547d\u4ee4\u5f0f\uff0c\u4efb\u4f55\u4eba\u53ef\u56de\uff09\uff1a\n  reject <EntityName|\u8def\u5f91\u5f8c\u7db4>   \u6574\u689d\uff08\u65e2\u6709\uff1b\u649e\u540d\u6642\u56de\u8cbc\u6d88\u6b67\u7fa9\uff09\n  reject PR12                    \u6574\u689d\uff08\u4e0d\u6703\u649e\u540d\uff09\n  reject PR12-I1 / PR12-D2       \u53ea\u4e1f\u90a3\u4e00\u884c\uff08ID \u5728\u84b8\u993e\u6642\u5b9a\uff0cdigest \u9010\u884c\u5217\u51fa\uff09\n\ndigest \u88e1\u7684\u300cNeeds a look\u300d\u6bb5\u7531 LLM \u7522\u751f\uff08knowledge_digest.analyze\uff09\uff0c\u53ea\u662f\u63d0\u6848\uff1a\n\u843d\u5730\u8def\u5f91\u4e0d\u8b80\u5b83\uff0c\u5931\u6557\u5c31\u9000\u56de\u7d14\u6e05\u55ae\u3002harvester \u7684**\u5beb\u5165\u8def\u5f91**\u7dad\u6301\u96f6 LLM\u3002\n\n**\u91cd\u84b8\u7684\u5206\u5de5**\uff1a\u6536\u5272\u5668\u53ea\u5075\u6e2c\u300cmerge commit \u2260 distilled_commit\u300d\u4e26\u6253\u4e00\u689d\n`POST {ORCH_URL}/knowledge/redistill`\uff0c\u84b8\u993e\u8207\u5beb\u7a3f\u6574\u500b\u7559\u5728 orchestrator\u2014\u2014\n`_land` \u7dad\u6301\u96f6 LLM\uff0c\u4e5f\u4e0d\u5fc5\u628a\u534a\u500b orchestrator \u642c\u9032\u9019\u652f oneshot\u3002\n\n\u7528\u6cd5\uff1apython -m orchestrator.knowledge_harvest\n\u8a2d\u5b9a\uff1asettings().knowledge\uff08KNOWLEDGE_*\uff09\u3001settings().ado\uff08ADO_PAT\uff09\u3001\n     settings().orchestrator\uff08ORCH_URL / ORCH_API_KEY\uff0c\u91cd\u84b8\u8acb\u6c42\u7528\uff09\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport fnmatch\nimport json\nimport re\nimport hashlib\nimport subprocess\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom shared.azdo import PrRef, client, get_json\nfrom shared.settings import fail_fast, settings\n\nfrom orchestrator import knowledge_digest as digest\nfrom orchestrator import ledger\nfrom orchestrator.knowledge import (_branch_patterns, _draft_comment,\n                                    _suffix_eq, assign_ids, decision_line,\n                                    inv_id, inv_text, invariant_line,\n                                    redistill_enabled, split_id,\n                                    write_json_atomic)\n\nKMARK = digest.KMARK\n\n\ndef _load_json(path: Path) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"\u8b80\u4e0d\u51fa\u4f86\u56de None\uff08\u5beb\u4e00\u534a / \u58de\u6a94\uff09\uff0c\u7531\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u6c7a\u5b9a\u7565\u904e\u9084\u662f\u4fdd\u7559\u3002\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\n\ndef _load_staged(path: Path) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"\u8b80\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\u4e26\u4fdd\u8b49 draft \u6709 ID\u3002\u5347\u7d1a\u524d\u5c31\u9032\u6c60\u7684\u820a\u7a3f\u5728\u6b64\u88dc ID \u4e26\u5beb\u56de\u2014\u2014\n    digest \u5217\u51fa\u7684 ID \u8207\u4e4b\u5f8c reject / \u843d\u5730\u7528\u7684\u5fc5\u9808\u662f\u540c\u4e00\u7d44\u3002\"\"\"\n    it = _load_json(path)\n    if not it or not isinstance(it.get(\"draft\"), dict):\n        return None\n    before = json.dumps(it[\"draft\"], sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n    assign_ids(it[\"draft\"], int(it.get(\"pr_id\", 0)))\n    if json.dumps(it[\"draft\"], sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) != before:\n        write_json_atomic(path, it)\n    return it\n\n\ndef _cycle_pat() -> tuple[str, str]:\n    k = settings().knowledge\n    return (k.cycle_source, k.cycle_target)\n\n_HISTORY_ROW = re.compile(r\"^\\| PR#(\\d+) \\|.*\\|$\", re.M)\n\n\n# ---------- \u53ef\u66ff\u63db\u7684 ADO \u8584\u5c01\u88dd\uff08\u6e2c\u8a66 stub \u9ede\uff09 ----------\n\ndef _get_pr(c, ref: PrRef) -> dict:\n    return get_json(c, ref.pr_api)\n\n\ndef _get_threads(c, ref: PrRef) -> list[dict]:\n    return get_json(c, f\"{ref.pr_api}/threads\").get(\"value\", [])\n\n\ndef _list_active(c, ref: PrRef) -> list[dict]:\n    return get_json(c, f\"{ref.repo_api}/pullrequests\",\n                    **{\"searchCriteria.status\": \"active\",\n                       \"$top\": \"50\"}).get(\"value\", [])\n\n\ndef _post_thread(c, ref: PrRef, content: str):\n    r = c.post(f\"{ref.pr_api}/threads\", params={\"api-version\": \"7.1\"},\n               json={\"comments\": [{\"parentCommentId\": 0, \"content\": content,\n                                   \"commentType\": 1}],\n                     \"status\": \"active\"})\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    try:\n        return r.json().get(\"id\")\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\n\ndef _list_completed(c, ref: PrRef) -> list[dict]:\n    return get_json(c, f\"{ref.repo_api}/pullrequests\",\n                    **{\"searchCriteria.status\": \"completed\",\n                       \"$top\": \"100\"}).get(\"value\", [])\n\n\n# ---------- \u843d\u5730\u5beb\u5165 ----------\n\ndef _page_path(root: Path, repo: str, entity: str) -> Path:\n    ent = Path((entity or \"misc\").lstrip(\"/\"))\n    parent = ent.parent.name or \"misc\"\n    return root / repo / parent / f\"{ent.stem or 'misc'}.md\"\n\n\ndef _entity_stems(entity: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"entity \u53ef\u80fd\u662f\u8def\u5f91\u3001\u6a94\u540d\u3001\u985e\u540d\u6216 FQN \u2014\u2014 \u56de\u6240\u6709\u5408\u7406\u7684\u6a94\u540d\u5019\u9078\uff08\u4f9d\u512a\u5148\u5e8f\uff09\u3002\n\n      src/main/java/.../LockService.java \u2192 LockService\n      LockService                        \u2192 LockService\n      com.acme.lock.LockService          \u2192 com.acme.lock\uff08Path.stem \u7684\u7522\u7269\uff0c\u5148\u8a66\uff09\n                                         \u2192 LockService\uff08\u9ede\u865f\u5c3e\u6bb5\uff0c\u5be6\u969b\u6703\u4e2d\u7684\uff09\n      LockService.applyLock()            \u2192 LockService\n    \"\"\"\n    e = (entity or \"\").strip().lstrip(\"/\")\n    if not e:\n        return []\n    tail = re.split(r\"[(#]\", e.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1], 1)[0].strip()\n    out = [Path(tail).stem]\n    if \".\" in tail:\n        last = tail.rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1].strip()\n        # \u5927\u5beb\u958b\u982d = \u985e\u540d\uff1b\u5c0f\u5beb\u591a\u534a\u662f\u526f\u6a94\u540d\uff08.java/.py\uff09\uff0c\u4e0d\u7576\u5019\u9078\n        if last[:1].isupper():\n            out.append(last)\n    out.append(tail)\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    return [s for s in out if s and not (s in seen or seen.add(s))]\n\n\ndef _resolve_page(root: Path, repo: str, entity: str) -> tuple[Path | None, str]:\n    \"\"\"\u627e\u51fa entity \u5c0d\u61c9\u7684\u5e33\u672c\u9801\u3002\u56de (\u9801\u9762 \u6216 None, \u8aaa\u660e)\u3002\n\n    supersedes.entity \u662f\u6a21\u578b\u81ea\u7531\u586b\u7684\u5b57\u4e32\uff0c\u800c\u5efa\u9801\u6642\u7528\u7684\u662f primary_entity \u7684\u5b8c\u6574\n    \u8def\u5f91\u2014\u2014\u5169\u8005\u5f62\u5f0f\u4e0d\u4e00\u81f4\u5c31\u7b97\u4e0d\u51fa\u540c\u4e00\u500b\u4f4d\u7f6e\u3002\u7cbe\u78ba\u8def\u5f91\u4e0d\u4e2d\u6642\uff0c\u9000\u5230\u300c\u540c\u6a94\u540d stem\u300d\n    \u5168\u57df\u641c\uff1b\u649e\u540d\u4e00\u5f8b\u4e0d\u84cb\u6233\u2014\u2014\u8a3b\u92b7\u6bd4\u65b0\u589e\u98a8\u96aa\u9ad8\uff0c\u84cb\u932f\u9801\u7b49\u65bc\u8aa4\u6bba\u4e00\u689d\u9084\u6709\u6548\u7684\u898f\u5247\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    exact = _page_path(root, repo, entity)\n    if exact.exists():\n        return exact, \"\"\n    base = root / repo\n    if not base.is_dir():\n        return None, f\"repo \u76ee\u9304\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\uff08{repo}\uff09\"\n    stems = _entity_stems(entity)\n    if not stems:\n        return None, \"entity \u7a7a\u767d\"\n    pages = sorted(base.rglob(\"*.md\"))\n    for stem in stems:\n        # \u540c stem\uff0c\u6216 _land \u649e\u540d\u5206\u9801\u6642\u52a0\u7684 stem-<md5 \u524d\u56db\u78bc>\n        cands = [p for p in pages\n                 if p.stem == stem or p.stem.startswith(stem + \"-\")]\n        if len(cands) == 1:\n            return cands[0], f\"\uff08\u7cbe\u78ba\u8def\u5f91\u672a\u4e2d\uff0c\u4ee5 {stem} \u6bd4\u5c0d\u5230 {cands[0].relative_to(root)}\uff09\"\n        if len(cands) > 1:\n            names = \", \".join(str(p.relative_to(root)) for p in cands[:4])\n            return None, f\"{stem} \u649e\u540d {len(cands)} \u9801\uff08{names}\uff09\u2014 \u4e0d\u84cb\u6233\uff0c\u907f\u514d\u84cb\u932f\"\n    return None, f\"\u67e5\u7121\u6b64\u9801\uff08\u8a66\u904e {', '.join(stems)}\uff09\"\n\n\n_SEC_RE = re.compile(r\"^## (.+)$\", re.M)\n\n\ndef _parse_page(text: str) -> tuple[list[str], dict[str, list[str]], str]:\n    \"\"\"(\u9802\u7aef\u5ee2\u9664\u6233 banners, \u6bb5\u540d\u2192\u5167\u5bb9\u884c, entity \u884c)\u3002\u53ea\u89e3\u6790\u6211\u5011\u81ea\u5df1\u5beb\u7684\u683c\u5f0f\u3002\"\"\"\n    banners = [ln for ln in text.splitlines()\n               if ln.startswith(\"> \u26a0 **Superseded\")]\n    entity = \"\"\n    m = re.search(r\"^> entity: (.+)$\", text, re.M)\n    if m:\n        entity = m.group(1).strip()\n    sections: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    parts = _SEC_RE.split(text)\n    for i in range(1, len(parts) - 1, 2):\n        name = parts[i].strip()\n        body = [ln for ln in parts[i + 1].strip().splitlines() if ln.strip()]\n        sections[name] = body\n    return banners, sections, entity\n\n\ndef _land(root: Path, repo: str, pr_id: int, data: dict,\n          provenance: str, author_note: str,\n          rejected_ids: list[str] | None = None) -> tuple[str, Path | None]:\n    \"\"\"\u7d2f\u7a4d\u5408\u4f75\u843d\u5730\uff08F1\uff09\uff1a\u5e33\u672c\u662f\u63a5\u7e8c\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u5feb\u7167\u3002\n    \u820a\u9801\u7684 Decisions / Invariants / Supersedes / Author notes \u524d\u6efe\u53bb\u91cd\uff0c\n    Summary \u53d6\u6700\u65b0\uff0c\u5ee2\u9664\u6233 banner \u4fdd\u7559\uff0cHistory \u758a\u884c\u3002\n    rejected_ids\uff1a\u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u88ab\u9010\u884c reject \u6389\u7684 ID\uff0c\u53ea\u7559\u75d5\u5728 History\uff08\u5167\u5bb9\u5df2\u4e0d\u5728 draft\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    page = _page_path(root, repo, data.get(\"primary_entity\") or \"\")\n    banners: list[str] = []\n    acc: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    history: list[str] = []\n    if page.exists():\n        old = page.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        if re.search(rf\"\\| PR#{pr_id} \\|\", old):\n            return f\"skip\uff08PR#{pr_id} \u5df2\u5728 {page.name} \u7684 History\uff09\", page\n        banners, acc, old_entity = _parse_page(old)\n        new_entity = (data.get(\"primary_entity\") or \"\").strip()\n        if old_entity and new_entity and old_entity != new_entity:\n            # \u4e0d\u540c\u5b50\u6a39\u540c parent+stem \u7684\u5be6\u9ad4\uff1a\u5206\u9801\uff0c\u5225\u628a\u5169\u500b\u5be6\u9ad4\u652a\u6210\u4e00\u934b\n            tag = hashlib.md5(new_entity.encode()).hexdigest()[:4]\n            page = page.with_name(f\"{page.stem}-{tag}.md\")\n            banners, acc, history = [], {}, []\n            if page.exists():\n                old = page.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n                if re.search(rf\"\\| PR#{pr_id} \\|\", old):\n                    return f\"skip\uff08PR#{pr_id} \u5df2\u5728 {page.name} \u7684 History\uff09\", page\n                banners, acc, _ = _parse_page(old)\n                history = [m.group(0) for m in _HISTORY_ROW.finditer(old)]\n        else:\n            history = [m.group(0) for m in _HISTORY_ROW.finditer(old)]\n\n    day = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    ent = data.get(\"primary_entity\") or \"(entity unspecified)\"\n    assign_ids(data, pr_id)              # \u820a\u7a3f\uff08\u7121 ID\uff09\u843d\u5730\u6642\u88dc\u9f4a\uff0c\u683c\u5f0f\u5c0d\u9f4a\n\n    def _body(ln: str) -> str:\n        return ln[2:].strip() if ln.startswith(\"- \") else ln.strip()\n\n    def merge(name: str, new_lines: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n        seen = list(acc.get(name, []))\n        # \u820a\u683c\u5f0f\u9077\u79fb\uff1a\u55ae\u6578 Author note \u4f75\u5165\u8907\u6578\n        if name == \"Author notes\" and \"Author note\" in acc:\n            seen = acc[\"Author note\"] + seen\n        if name == \"Invariants\":\n            # \u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u4ee5\u300c\u6587\u5b57\u300d\u53bb\u91cd\uff08\u5ffd\u7565\u884c\u5c3e ID\uff09\uff1a\u540c\u4e00\u689d\u898f\u5247\u88ab\u5169\u689d PR \u5404\u8b1b\u4e00\u6b21\n            # \u53ea\u7559\u5148\u843d\u5730\u7684\u90a3\u689d\uff1bID \u4e0d\u540c\u4e0d\u4ee3\u8868\u898f\u5247\u4e0d\u540c\u3002\n            seen_text = {split_id(_body(s))[0] for s in seen}\n            fresh = [ln for ln in new_lines\n                     if split_id(_body(ln))[0] not in seen_text]\n        else:\n            fresh = [ln for ln in new_lines if ln not in seen]\n        if name in (\"Decisions\", \"Supersedes\", \"Author notes\"):\n            return fresh + seen          # \u6642\u5e8f\u6bb5\uff1a\u65b0\u5728\u524d\uff08\u6ce8\u5165\u622a\u65b7\u4fdd\u4f4f\u6700\u65b0\uff09\n        return seen + fresh              # Invariants \u7b49\u7121\u6642\u5e8f\u6bb5\uff1aappend \u5373\u53ef\n\n    decs = merge(\"Decisions\", [decision_line(d, pr_id)\n                               for d in (data.get(\"decisions\") or [])\n                               if isinstance(d, dict)])\n    invs = merge(\"Invariants\", [invariant_line(x)\n                                for x in (data.get(\"invariants\") or [])\n                                if inv_text(x)])\n    # \u88ab\u672c\u6b21 supersede \u9ede\u540d\u7684\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\uff1a\u5c31\u5730\u6a19\u8a18\uff0c\u4e0d\u522a\u9664\u3002\n    # \u4e3b\u8def\u5f91\u662f ID \u7cbe\u78ba\u6bd4\u5c0d\uff08retires_id\uff09\uff1b\u9010\u5b57\u76f8\u7b49\uff08retires_verbatim\uff09\u53ea\u670d\u52d9\n    # \u9084\u6c92\u6709 ID \u7684\u820a\u884c\u3002\u5c0d\u4e0d\u4e0a\u5c31\u4ec0\u9ebc\u90fd\u4e0d\u505a\u2014\u2014\u6f0f\u6a19\u7684\u4ee3\u50f9\u662f\u5169\u689d\u4e26\u5b58\uff0c\n    # \u8aa4\u6a19\u7684\u4ee3\u50f9\u662f\u8aa4\u6bba\u4e00\u689d\u6709\u6548\u898f\u5247\u3002\n    retired_ids = {(x.get(\"retires_id\") or \"\").strip().upper()\n                   for x in (data.get(\"supersedes\") or [])\n                   if (x.get(\"retires_id\") or \"\").strip()}\n    retired_txt = {(x.get(\"retires_verbatim\") or \"\").strip()\n                   for x in (data.get(\"supersedes\") or [])\n                   if (x.get(\"retires_verbatim\") or \"\").strip()}\n    if retired_ids or retired_txt:\n        marked: list[str] = []\n        for ln in invs:\n            body = _body(ln)\n            text, iid = split_id(body)\n            if text.startswith(\"~~\"):\n                marked.append(ln)              # \u5df2\u6a19\u8a18\u904e\n            elif (iid and iid in retired_ids) or (not iid and text in retired_txt):\n                marked.append(f\"- ~~{text}~~ \u26a0 retired by PR#{pr_id}\"\n                              + (f\" `{iid}`\" if iid else \"\"))\n            else:\n                marked.append(ln)\n        invs = marked\n    sups = merge(\"Supersedes\", [\n        f\"- \u26a0 `{x.get('entity', '?')}` \u2014 {x.get('what', '')} (PR#{pr_id})\"\n        for x in (data.get(\"supersedes\") or [])])\n    notes = merge(\"Author notes\",\n                  [f\"- (PR#{pr_id}) {author_note.strip()}\"] if author_note else [])\n    aff = merge(\"Affected entities\",\n                [\", \".join(f\"`{a}`\" for a in (data.get(\"affected\") or [])[:8])]\n                if data.get(\"affected\") else [])\n\n    lines = [f\"# {Path(ent).stem or ent}\", \"\"]\n    lines += banners + ([\"\"] if banners else [])\n    lines += [f\"> entity: {ent}\",\n              f\"> approval: {provenance} \u00b7 last: PR#{pr_id} \u00b7 {day}\", \"\",\n              \"## Summary\", (data.get(\"summary\", \"\") or \"(none)\").strip(), \"\"]\n    if not data.get(\"intent_stated\", True):\n        lines += [\"> intent: not stated in the PR \u2014 mechanics only.\", \"\"]\n    for name, body in ((\"Decisions\", decs), (\"Invariants\", invs),\n                       (\"Supersedes\", sups), (\"Author notes\", notes),\n                       (\"Affected entities\", aff)):\n        if body:\n            lines += [f\"## {name}\", *body, \"\"]\n    _known = {\"Summary\", \"Decisions\", \"Invariants\", \"Supersedes\",\n              \"Author notes\", \"Author note\", \"Affected entities\", \"History\"}\n    for name, body_lines in acc.items():\n        if name not in _known and body_lines:      # \u4eba\u5de5\u88dc\u5beb\u7684\u6bb5\u843d\uff1a\u524d\u6efe\u4fdd\u7559\n            lines += [f\"## {name}\", *body_lines, \"\"]\n    row = (f\"| PR#{pr_id} | {day} | {data.get('ledger_line', '').strip() or '\u2014'}\"\n           f\" ({data.get('type', 'other')}) \u00b7 {provenance}\"\n           + (\" \u00b7 rejected: \" + \", \".join(f\"`{r}`\" for r in rejected_ids)\n              if rejected_ids else \"\") + \" |\")\n    lines += [\"## History\", \"| PR | Date | Entry |\", \"|---|---|---|\", row]\n    lines += history + [\"\"]\n    page.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    page.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return f\"landed \u2192 {page.relative_to(root)}\uff08{provenance}\uff09\", page\n\n\ndef _mark_superseded(root: Path, repo: str, sup: dict, pr_id: int,\n                     landed: Path | None = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u5728\u88ab\u5ee2\u9664\u7684\u9801\u9762\u9802\u7aef\u84cb\u6233 + History \u7559\u884c\u3002\u5167\u5bb9\u4fdd\u7559 \u2014\u2014 \u975c\u9ed8\u84b8\u767c\u662f\u5927\u5fcc\u3002\n\n    landed \u7d66\u5b9a\u6642\u4ee3\u8868\u300c\u9019\u689d supersede \u6307\u5411\u672c\u6b21\u525b\u5beb\u7684\u540c\u4e00\u9801\u300d\u2014\u2014\u90a3\u7a2e\u60c5\u6cc1\u6574\u9801\u84cb\u6233\n    \u6703\u8aa4\u5c0e\u8b80\u8005\u4ee5\u70ba\u5168\u9801\u4f5c\u5ee2\uff0c\u4ea4\u7d66 _land \u7684\u9010\u689d\u522a\u9664\u7dda\u8655\u7406\u5373\u53ef\uff0c\u9019\u88e1\u4e0d\u91cd\u8907\u6a19\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    ent = sup.get(\"entity\") or \"\"\n    page, why = None, \"\"\n    rid = (sup.get(\"retires_id\") or \"\").strip().upper()\n    if rid:\n        # ID \u662f\u7cbe\u78ba\u9375\uff1a\u54ea\u4e00\u9801\u542b `PR12-I1` \u5c31\u662f\u54ea\u4e00\u9801\uff0c\u4e0d\u7528\u731c stem\n        hits = [p for p in sorted((root / repo).rglob(\"*.md\"))\n                if f\"`{rid}`\" in p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")] \\\n            if (root / repo).is_dir() else []\n        if len(hits) == 1:\n            page, why = hits[0], f\"\uff08\u4ee5 {rid} \u5b9a\u4f4d\uff09\"\n    if page is None:\n        page, why = _resolve_page(root, repo, ent)\n    if page is None:\n        # \u65b0\u9801\u5df2\u5beb\u4e0b Supersedes \u5ba3\u544a\u3001\u820a\u9801\u537b\u6c92\u84cb\u5230 \u2014\u2014 \u5e33\u672c\u9032\u5165\u4e0d\u4e00\u81f4\u72c0\u614b\uff0c\n        # \u9019\u4e0d\u662f\u7121\u5bb3\u7684\u7565\u904e\uff0c\u63aa\u8fad\u8981\u8b93\u4eba\u770b\u5f97\u51fa\u8981\u8655\u7406\u3002\n        return f\"\u26a0 supersede \u672a\u84cb\u6233\uff08{ent}\uff09\uff1a{why}\"\n    if landed is not None and page.resolve() == landed.resolve():\n        return f\"supersede \u540c\u9801\uff08{page.name}\uff09\u2014 \u5df2\u65bc\u689d\u76ee\u5c64\u7d1a\u6a19\u8a18\uff0c\u4e0d\u84cb\u9801\u9762\u6233\"\n    txt = page.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    if f\"Superseded (PR#{pr_id}\" in txt:\n        return \"supersede \u5df2\u84cb\u6233\uff08\u51aa\u7b49\u7565\u904e\uff09\"\n    day = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    banner = (f\"> \u26a0 **Superseded (PR#{pr_id}, {day})** \u2014 \"\n              f\"{sup.get('what', '')}\\n\")\n    nl = txt.find(\"\\n\") + 1\n    txt = txt[:nl] + \"\\n\" + banner + txt[nl:]\n    if \"## History\" in txt:\n        txt = txt.rstrip() + (f\"\\n| PR#{pr_id} | {day} | \u26a0 superseded: \"\n                              f\"{sup.get('what', '')[:80]} |\\n\")\n    page.write_text(txt, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return f\"supersede \u84cb\u6233 \u2192 {page.relative_to(root)}{why}\"\n\n\ndef _ledger_only(root: Path, repo: str, pr: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u672a\u7d93 bot \u7684 completed PR\uff1a\u53ea\u88dc\u4e00\u689d\u5e33\u672c\u884c\uff08\u6c92\u6709 review \u7522\u7269\u53ef\u84b8\uff0c\u8aa0\u5be6\u7559\u75d5\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    pr_id = pr.get(\"pullRequestId\")\n    title = (pr.get(\"title\") or \"\").strip()[:100]\n    page = root / repo / \"_module\" / \"unreviewed-ledger.md\"\n    day = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    row = f\"| PR#{pr_id} | {day} | {title or '\u2014'} \u00b7 unreviewed |\"\n    if page.exists():\n        old = page.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        if f\"PR#{pr_id} \" in old:\n            return \"skip\"\n        page.write_text(old.rstrip() + \"\\n\" + row + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    else:\n        page.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        page.write_text(\"# Unreviewed release ledger\\n\\n\"\n                        \"PRs that reached a knowledge branch without passing \"\n                        \"through the review bot.\\n\\n\"\n                        \"| PR | Date | Entry |\\n|---|---|---|\\n\"\n                        + row + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return f\"ledger \u884c \u2192 PR#{pr_id}\"\n\n\n# ---------- \u5206\u985e ----------\n\ndef _author_reply(threads: list[dict], thread_id, author_id: str,\n                  marker: str = \"pr-review-knowledge-draft\") -> tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de (\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u5247\u4f5c\u8005\u56de\u8986, 'reject'|'reply'|'silent')\u3002\"\"\"\n    ours = None\n    for t in threads:\n        if thread_id and t.get(\"id\") == thread_id:\n            ours = t\n            break\n        if not thread_id and any(marker in (c.get(\"content\") or \"\")\n                                 for c in t.get(\"comments\", [])):\n            ours = t\n            break\n    if ours is None:\n        return \"\", \"silent\"\n    replies = [c[\"content\"].strip() for c in ours.get(\"comments\", [])[1:]\n               if (c.get(\"author\") or {}).get(\"id\") == author_id\n               and (c.get(\"content\") or \"\").strip()]\n    if not replies:\n        return \"\", \"silent\"\n    if re.search(r\"(?m)^\\s*reject\\b\", replies[-1], re.I):\n        return replies[-1], \"reject\"\n    return \"\\n\\n\".join(replies), \"reply\"      # \u5168\u90e8\u56de\u8986\u9010\u5b57\u5165\u5e33\uff0c\u4e0d\u53ea\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u5247\n\n\n# ---------- stale \u91cd\u84b8\u7684\u8acb\u6c42\u7aef\uff08\u5075\u6e2c\u5728\u9019\u88e1\uff0c\u84b8\u993e\u6574\u500b\u5728 orchestrator\uff09 ----------\n\ndef _orch_url() -> str:\n    return settings().orchestrator.base_url\n\n\ndef _request_redistill(pr_url: str) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n    \"\"\"POST {ORCH}/knowledge/redistill\u3002\u56de (\u6210\u529f?, \u8aaa\u660e)\u3002\n\n    trust_env=False\uff1a\u9019\u662f\u540c\u6a5f loopback \u547c\u53eb\uff0c\u516c\u53f8\u7684 HTTPS_PROXY \u4e0d\u8a72\u63a5\u7ba1\u5b83\n    \uff08ADO \u90a3\u689d\u624d\u9700\u8981 proxy\uff09\u3002\u7aef\u9ede\u6536\u5230\u5373\u56de 202\uff0c\u6240\u4ee5 timeout \u958b\u5c0f\u5373\u53ef\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    import httpx\n    key = settings().orchestrator.api_key.get_secret_value()\n    headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {key}\"} if key else {}\n    try:\n        r = httpx.post(f\"{_orch_url()}/knowledge/redistill\",\n                       json={\"pr_url\": pr_url}, headers=headers,\n                       timeout=15.0, trust_env=False)\n        r.raise_for_status()\n        return True, \"\u5df2\u8acb\u6c42\u91cd\u84b8\"\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return False, f\"\u8acb\u6c42\u5931\u6557\uff08{type(e).__name__}: {e}\uff09\"\n\n\ndef _handle_stale(pend: Path, info: dict, merged: str,\n                  note: str, kind: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"draft \u4e4b\u5f8c\u53c8\u6709 push\uff1a\u8acb\u6c42\u91cd\u84b8\uff0c\u4e26\u7528\u300c\u8acb\u6c42\u6233 + attempts \u2264 2\u300d\u5c01\u6b7b\u91cd\u8a66\u8ff4\u5708\u3002\n\n        \u7121\u6233                \u2192 \u84cb\u6233(attempts=1) \u2192 POST\uff08\u9023\u7dda\u5931\u6557\u4e5f\u7b97\u4e00\u6b21\uff09\n        \u6709\u6233\u3001commit \u76f8\u540c    \u2192 attempts 1 \u2192 2 \u518d\u8a66\u4e00\u6b21\uff1b\u22652 \u2192 \u4e1f\u7a3f\n        \u6709\u6233\u3001commit \u53c8\u8b8a\u4e86  \u2192 \u91cd\u84b8\u671f\u9593\u53c8 push\uff08\u4e16\u4ee3\u8b8a\u66f4\uff09\u2192 \u4e1f\u7a3f\n\n    30 \u5206\u9418\u4e00\u8f2a\u7684 timer \u5728\u4efb\u4f55\u5931\u6557\u6a21\u5f0f\u4e0b\u90fd\u4e0d\u53ef\u80fd\u8b8a\u6210\u7121\u754c\u7684 LLM \u91cd\u8a66\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    tail = \"\uff08\u4f5c\u8005\u56de\u8986\u4e00\u4f75\u6368\u68c4\uff09\" if kind == \"reply\" else \"\"\n    if not redistill_enabled():\n        pend.unlink()\n        return f\"completed + draft \u5f8c\u53c8\u6709 push \u2192 stale \u4e1f\u7a3f{tail}\" \\\n               \"\uff08KNOWLEDGE_REDISTILL=false\uff09\"\n    stamp = info.get(\"redistill_requested\") or {}\n    attempts = int(stamp.get(\"attempts\") or 0)\n    if stamp and stamp.get(\"commit\") != merged:\n        pend.unlink()\n        return (\"completed + \u91cd\u84b8\u671f\u9593\u53c8\u6709\u65b0 push\uff08\u4e16\u4ee3\u8b8a\u66f4\uff09\u2192 stale \u4e1f\u7a3f\"\n                f\"{tail}\uff08\u6233 {str(stamp.get('commit'))[:8]} \u2192 \"\n                f\"\u73fe\u5728 {str(merged)[:8]}\uff09\")\n    if attempts >= 2:\n        pend.unlink()\n        return f\"completed + \u91cd\u84b8\u5169\u6b21\u672a\u6210 \u2192 stale \u4e1f\u7a3f{tail}\"\n    info[\"redistill_requested\"] = {\"commit\": merged, \"attempts\": attempts + 1}\n    if kind == \"reply\" and note:\n        info[\"author_note\"] = note      # \u9010\u5b57\u7559\u8457\uff1a\u91cd\u84b8\u7684\u6750\u6599\u8981\u5e36\u4f5c\u8005\u8aaa\u904e\u7684\u8a71\n    write_json_atomic(pend, info)       # \u5148\u84cb\u6233\u518d POST\uff1a\u5931\u6557\u4e5f\u7b97\u4e00\u6b21 attempt\n    ok, why = _request_redistill(info.get(\"pr_url\") or \"\")\n    return (f\"completed + draft \u5f8c\u53c8\u6709 push \u2192 \u8acb\u6c42\u91cd\u84b8\"\n            f\"\uff08\u7b2c {attempts + 1}/2 \u6b21\uff0ccommit {str(merged)[:8]}\uff09\uff1a{why}\")\n\n\ndef _process_pending(c, root: Path, pend: Path) -> str:\n    info = json.loads(pend.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    ref = PrRef(base_url=info[\"base_url\"], repo=info[\"repo\"],\n                pr_id=int(info[\"pr_id\"]))\n    pr = _get_pr(c, ref)\n    status = (pr.get(\"status\") or \"\").lower()\n    if status == \"active\":\n        if not info.get(\"posted\") and info.get(\"post_failed\") \\\n                and not info.get(\"post_retried\"):\n            # \u53ea\u6709\u300c\u771f\u5617\u8a66\u904e\u4e14\u5931\u6557\u300d\u624d\u88dc\u8cbc\u3002dry_run \u7a3f\u8207\u7121\u6a19\u8a18\u7684\u5b58\u91cf\u820a\u7a3f\n            # \u4e00\u5f8b\u6c89\u9ed8\u2014\u2014\u5f71\u5b50\u6a21\u5f0f\u7684\u975c\u9ed8\u627f\u8afe\u7531\u9019\u884c\u5b88\u4f4f\uff08\u96d9\u958b\u95dc\u7e31\u6df1\u4e0d\u7e5e\u9053\uff09\u3002\n            info[\"post_retried\"] = True          # \u8cbc\u7a3f\u5931\u6557\u88dc\u6551\uff1a\u53ea\u91cd\u8a66\u4e00\u6b21\n            try:\n                tid = _post_thread(\n                    c, ref, \"<!-- pr-review-knowledge-draft -->\\n\"\n                    + _draft_comment(info[\"draft\"], info[\"pr_id\"]))\n                info[\"posted\"] = True\n                info[\"thread_id\"] = tid\n                write_json_atomic(pend, info)\n                return \"active\uff08\u8cbc\u7a3f\u88dc\u6551\u6210\u529f\u2014\u2014harvester \u4ee3\u8cbc\uff09\"\n            except Exception as e:\n                write_json_atomic(pend, info)\n                return f\"active\uff08\u8cbc\u7a3f\u88dc\u6551\u5931\u6557\uff1a{e}\uff1b\u4e0d\u518d\u91cd\u8a66\uff09\"\n        return \"active\uff08\u966a\u7b49\uff09\"\n    if status == \"abandoned\":\n        pend.unlink()\n        return \"abandoned \u2192 \u4e1f\u7a3f\"\n    if status != \"completed\":\n        return f\"\u672a\u77e5\u72c0\u614b {status}\uff08\u4fdd\u7559\uff09\"\n\n    merged = (pr.get(\"lastMergeSourceCommit\") or {}).get(\"commitId\")\n    author_id = (pr.get(\"createdBy\") or {}).get(\"id\", \"\")\n    note, kind = _author_reply(_get_threads(c, ref), info.get(\"thread_id\"),\n                               author_id)\n    if kind == \"reject\":\n        pend.unlink()\n        return \"completed + \u4f5c\u8005 reject \u2192 \u4e1f\u7a3f\"\n    if info.get(\"distilled_commit\") and merged \\\n            and info[\"distilled_commit\"] != merged:\n        return _handle_stale(pend, info, merged, note, kind)\n    # \u9032 release \u2260 \u9032\u5e33\u672c\uff1a\u66ab\u5b58\u5230 _cycle/\uff0c\u7b49 release\u2192master \u9a57\u6536 PR \u6536\u53e3\n    assign_ids(info[\"draft\"], int(info[\"pr_id\"]))   # \u5347\u7d1a\u524d\u7684\u820a\u7a3f\u5728\u6b64\u88dc ID\n    # \u91cd\u84b8\u904e\u7684\u7a3f\u88e1\u7559\u8457\u4f5c\u8005\u5c0d\u300c\u66f4\u65e9\u90a3\u7248\u8349\u7a3f\u300d\u7684\u56de\u8986\u2014\u2014thread \u8b80\u4e0d\u5230\u6642\uff08\u4f8b\u5982\n    # thread \u88ab\u522a\uff09\u4ecd\u4ee5\u5b83\u70ba\u6e96\uff0cprovenance \u8ddf\u8457\u8aaa\u5be6\u8a71\uff1a\u4f5c\u8005\u78ba\u5be6\u8aaa\u904e\u8a71\u3002\n    author_note = note if kind == \"reply\" else info.get(\"author_note\", \"\")\n    prov = \"explicit\" if author_note else \"silent\"\n    if info.get(\"redistilled\"):\n        prov += \"\u00b7redistilled\"          # \u9019\u689d\u7684\u5167\u5bb9\u662f\u7528\u6700\u7d42 diff \u91cd\u84b8\u4f86\u7684\n    write_json_atomic(root / \"_cycle\" / info[\"repo\"] / pend.name, {\n        **{k: info[k] for k in (\"pr_url\", \"pr_id\", \"repo\", \"base_url\", \"draft\")},\n        \"target_branch\": info.get(\"target_branch\", \"\"),\n        \"author_note\": author_note,\n        \"provenance\": prov,\n        # \u5e36\u8457\u77db\u76fe\u5b8c\u6210 = \u5be6\u4f5c\u63a8\u7ffb\u4e86\u65e2\u6709\u898f\u5247\uff0c\u7559\u7d66\u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u88c1\u6c7a\uff08\u898b _apply_contradictions\uff09\n        \"contradicted\": list(info.get(\"contradicted\") or []),\n    })\n    pend.unlink()\n    return f\"completed \u2192 staged\uff08{prov}\uff0c\u7b49\u9031\u671f\u9a57\u6536\uff09\"\n\n\n# ---------- watermark \u6383\u63cf ----------\n\ndef _watermark_scan(c, root: Path) -> list[str]:\n    state = root / \"_state\"\n    repos_f = state / \"repos.json\"\n    if not repos_f.exists():\n        return []\n    wm_f = state / \"watermark.json\"\n    wm = json.loads(wm_f.read_text()) if wm_f.exists() else {}\n    pats = _branch_patterns()\n    seen_pending: set[str] = set()\n    if (root / \"_pending\").is_dir():\n        for p in (root / \"_pending\").rglob(\"pr-*.json\"):\n            info = _load_json(p)           # \u5beb\u4e00\u534a\u7684\u7a3f\uff1a\u9019\u8f2a\u7565\u904e\uff0c\u4e0d\u62d6\u57ae\u6574\u500b\u6383\u63cf\n            if info and info.get(\"pr_id\") is not None:\n                seen_pending.add(f\"{p.parent.name}#{info['pr_id']}\")\n    lines: list[str] = []\n    for repo, base in json.loads(repos_f.read_text()).items():\n        key = f\"{base}|{repo}\"\n        ref = PrRef(base_url=base, repo=repo, pr_id=0)\n        if key not in wm:                    # F6\uff1a\u9996\u898b\u5373\u5b9a\u6c34\u4f4d\uff0c\u4e0d\u704c\u6b77\u53f2\n            wm[key] = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\", time.gmtime())\n            lines.append(f\"{repo}: \u9996\u898b\uff0cwatermark \u5b9a\u65bc\u73fe\u5728\uff08\u6b77\u53f2 PR \u4e0d\u56de\u586b\uff09\")\n            continue\n        newest = wm.get(key, \"\")\n        for pr in _list_completed(c, ref):\n            closed = pr.get(\"closedDate\") or \"\"\n            target = (pr.get(\"targetRefName\") or \"\").replace(\"refs/heads/\", \"\")\n            if closed <= wm.get(key, \"\") or not any(\n                    fnmatch.fnmatch(target, p) for p in pats):\n                continue\n            src = (pr.get(\"sourceRefName\") or \"\").replace(\"refs/heads/\", \"\")\n            if fnmatch.fnmatch(src, _cycle_pat()[0]):\n                newest = max(newest, closed)\n                continue          # \u9a57\u6536\u5100\u5f0f\u672c\u8eab\u4e0d\u662f\u300c\u6f0f\u7db2 PR\u300d\n            if f\"{repo}#{pr.get('pullRequestId')}\" in seen_pending:\n                newest = max(newest, closed)\n                continue\n            lines.append(f\"{repo}: {_ledger_only(root, repo, pr)}\")\n            newest = max(newest, closed)\n        if newest:\n            wm[key] = newest\n    write_json_atomic(wm_f, wm)\n    return lines\n\n\n# ---------- \u9031\u671f\u6536\u53e3\uff08release \u2192 master \u9a57\u6536 PR\uff09 ----------\n\ndef _collect_rejects(threads: list[dict]) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u884c\u9996\u547d\u4ee4\u5f0f\uff1a`reject <Entity\u6216\u8def\u5f91\u5f8c\u7db4>`\uff1b\u300edon't reject X\u300f\u4e0d\u7b97\u3002\"\"\"\n    tokens: set[str] = set()\n    for t in threads:\n        for cm in t.get(\"comments\", []):\n            for m in re.finditer(r\"(?m)^\\s*reject\\s+([\\w./$-]+)\",\n                                 cm.get(\"content\") or \"\", re.I):\n                tokens.add(m.group(1).lower())\n    return tokens\n\n\n# ---------- \u77db\u76fe\u88c1\u6c7a\uff08\u5be6\u4f5c\u63a8\u7ffb\u898f\u5247 \u2192 \u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u6c7a\u5b9a\u8981\u4e0d\u8981\u62d4\u6389\u90a3\u689d\u898f\u5247\uff09 ----------\n#\n# \u70ba\u4ec0\u9ebc\u4e0d\u662f\u300cPR \u5b8c\u6210\u5c31\u81ea\u52d5\u62d4\u300d\uff1amerge \u904e\u4e00\u500b\u8b66\u544a\uff0c\u8ddf\u300c\u4f5c\u8005\u6839\u672c\u6c92\u770b\u90a3\u689d\u7559\u8a00\n# \u5c31\u6309 Complete\u300d\u5728\u8cc7\u6599\u4e0a\u9577\u5f97\u4e00\u6a23\u3002\u81ea\u52d5\u62d4\u7684\u8a71\uff0c\u6bcf\u4e00\u6b21\u771f\u7684 regression \u90fd\u6703\u9806\u624b\n# \u522a\u6389\u90a3\u689d\u672c\u4f86\u6703\u6293\u5230\u5b83\u7684\u898f\u5247\u2014\u2014\u932f\u8aa4\u81ea\u6211\u62b9\u9664\uff0c\u800c\u4e14\u7121\u8072\u3002\n#\n# \u70ba\u4ec0\u9ebc\u4e5f\u4e0d\u662f\u300c\u4e0d\u80fd\u62d4\u300d\uff1a\u5e33\u672c\u53ea\u9032\u4e0d\u51fa\u5c31\u6703\u721b\u3002\u52a0\u4e00\u689d\u898f\u5247\u53ea\u8981\u6c89\u9ed8 merge\uff0c\u62d4\u4e00\u689d\n# \u537b\u8981\u4f5c\u8005\u7528\u525b\u597d\u7684\u53e5\u5f0f\u660e\u793a\u2014\u2014\u9019\u500b\u4e0d\u5c0d\u7a31\u662f\u53cd\u7684\uff0c\u932f\u8aa4\u7684\u898f\u5247\u6703\u6c38\u4e45\u88fd\u9020\u8aa4\u5831\u3002\n#\n# \u6240\u4ee5\uff1a\u5075\u6e2c\u662f\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u7684\uff08finding \u7684 knowledge_ref \u6307\u540d\u4e86\u662f\u54ea\u4e00\u689d\uff09\uff0c\u63d0\u6848\u9032 digest\n# \u7684\u7d05\u5340\u8b93\u4eba\u770b\u5f97\u5230\uff0c**\u6c89\u9ed8\u5373\u63a5\u53d7**\uff08\u8ddf\u300c\u65b0\u689d\u76ee\u6c89\u9ed8\u5373\u843d\u5730\u300d\u540c\u4e00\u5957\u6838\u51c6\u8a9e\u610f\uff09\uff0c\n# \u4efb\u4f55\u4eba\u56de `keep PR12-I1` \u5c31\u5426\u6c7a\u9019\u6b21\u62d4\u9664\u3002\u8207 reject \u540c\u4e00\u500b\u6a21\u5f0f\uff1a\u4eba\u88c1\u3001code \u57f7\u884c\u3002\n\ndef _retire_on_contradiction() -> bool:\n    return settings().knowledge.retire_on_contradiction\n\n\ndef _collect_keeps(threads: list[dict]) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u884c\u9996\u547d\u4ee4\u5f0f `keep PR12-I1`\uff1a\u5426\u6c7a\u672c\u9031\u671f\u5c0d\u8a72\u689d\u898f\u5247\u7684\u62d4\u9664\u3002\"\"\"\n    out: set[str] = set()\n    for t in threads:\n        for cm in t.get(\"comments\", []):\n            for m in re.finditer(r\"(?m)^\\s*keep\\s+(PR\\d+-[DI]\\d+)\",\n                                 cm.get(\"content\") or \"\", re.I):\n                out.add(m.group(1).upper())\n    return out\n\n\ndef _retire_by_id(root: Path, repo: str, iid: str, pr_id: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u5728\u5df2\u843d\u5730\u7684\u9801\u4e0a\u628a\u67d0\u689d\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u756b\u6389\uff08\u4e0d\u522a\u9664\uff09\uff0c\u4e26\u5728 History \u7559\u884c\u3002\n\n    \u5b9a\u4f4d\u65b9\u5f0f\u8207 _mark_superseded \u76f8\u540c\uff1a\u54ea\u4e00\u9801\u542b `PR12-I1` \u5c31\u662f\u54ea\u4e00\u9801\u2014\u2014ID \u662f\n    \u7cbe\u78ba\u9375\uff0c\u4e0d\u7528\u731c stem\u3002\u627e\u4e0d\u5230 / \u649e\u591a\u9801\u4e00\u5f8b\u4e0d\u52d5\uff0c\u53ea\u7559 journal\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    base = root / repo\n    if not base.is_dir():\n        return f\"\u26a0 \u62d4\u9664 {iid} \u5931\u6557\uff1arepo \u76ee\u9304\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\"\n    hits = [p for p in sorted(base.rglob(\"*.md\"))\n            if f\"`{iid}`\" in p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")]\n    if len(hits) != 1:\n        return (f\"\u26a0 \u62d4\u9664 {iid} \u672a\u57f7\u884c\uff1a{'\u67e5\u7121\u6b64 ID' if not hits else f'\u649e\u5230 {len(hits)} \u9801'}\")\n    page = hits[0]\n    txt = page.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    out, done = [], False\n    for ln in txt.splitlines():\n        body = ln[2:].strip() if ln.startswith(\"- \") else \"\"\n        text, line_id = split_id(body)\n        if not done and line_id.upper() == iid and not text.startswith(\"~~\"):\n            out.append(f\"- ~~{text}~~ \u26a0 retired by PR#{pr_id} \"\n                       f\"(contradicted by merged code) `{line_id}`\")\n            done = True\n        else:\n            out.append(ln)\n    if not done:\n        return f\"\u26a0 \u62d4\u9664 {iid} \u672a\u57f7\u884c\uff1a\u8a72\u884c\u5df2\u756b\u6389\u6216\u683c\u5f0f\u4e0d\u7b26\"\n    day = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    txt = \"\\n\".join(out).rstrip() + (\n        f\"\\n| PR#{pr_id} | {day} | \u26a0 retired `{iid}`: contradicted by merged \"\n        f\"code, accepted at cycle close |\\n\")\n    page.write_text(txt, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return f\"\u62d4\u9664 {iid} \u2192 {page.relative_to(root).as_posix()}\uff08\u5be6\u4f5c\u63a8\u7ffb\uff0c\u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u672a\u5426\u6c7a\uff09\"\n\n\ndef _apply_contradictions(root: Path, repo: str, items: list[tuple],\n                          keeps: set[str]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u6536\u53e3\u6642\u57f7\u884c\uff1a\u6bcf\u689d\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\u5e36\u4f86\u7684\u77db\u76fe id\uff0c\u6c92\u88ab keep \u5426\u6c7a\u7684\u5c31\u756b\u6389\u3002\"\"\"\n    if not _retire_on_contradiction():\n        return []\n    out: list[str] = []\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    for _x, it in items:\n        for iid in (it.get(\"contradicted\") or []):\n            iid = str(iid).upper()\n            if iid in seen:\n                continue\n            seen.add(iid)\n            if iid in keeps:\n                out.append(f\"\u77db\u76fe {iid} \u4fdd\u7559\uff08\u6709\u4eba\u56de keep\uff0c\u672c\u9031\u671f\u4e0d\u62d4\uff09\")\n                continue\n            out.append(_retire_by_id(root, repo, iid, int(it.get(\"pr_id\", 0))))\n    return out\n\n\ndef _reject_line(x: Path, iid: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\u5f9e\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\u62ff\u6389\u4e00\u884c\uff08decision \u6216 invariant\uff09\uff0c\u7559\u75d5\u5728 rejected_ids\u3002\n    \u547d\u4e2d\u56de True\u3002\u689d\u76ee\u672c\u8eab\u4fdd\u7559\u2014\u2014\u6458\u8981\u8207 History \u884c\u4ecd\u6703\u843d\u5730\u3002\"\"\"\n    info = _load_json(x)\n    if not info:\n        return False\n    d = info.get(\"draft\") or {}\n    assign_ids(d, int(info.get(\"pr_id\", 0)))\n    before = (len(d.get(\"decisions\") or []), len(d.get(\"invariants\") or []))\n    d[\"decisions\"] = [q for q in (d.get(\"decisions\") or [])\n                      if not (isinstance(q, dict)\n                              and (q.get(\"id\") or \"\").upper() == iid)]\n    d[\"invariants\"] = [q for q in (d.get(\"invariants\") or [])\n                       if inv_id(q).upper() != iid]\n    if before == (len(d[\"decisions\"]), len(d[\"invariants\"])):\n        return False\n    info[\"rejected_ids\"] = sorted(set(info.get(\"rejected_ids\") or []) | {iid})\n    write_json_atomic(x, info)\n    return True\n\n\ndef _apply_rejects(tokens: set[str], staged: list[Path],\n                   where: str) -> tuple[list[str], dict[str, list[str]]]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de (journal \u884c, \u6b67\u7fa9 token \u2192 \u5019\u9078\u8def\u5f91\u6e05\u55ae)\u3002\u6b67\u7fa9\u7684\u4e00\u5f8b\u4fdd\u7559\u4e0d\u57f7\u884c\u3002\n\n    \u4e09\u7a2e token\uff1a\u5be6\u9ad4\u540d / \u8def\u5f91\u5f8c\u7db4\uff08\u649e\u540d\u2192\u6b67\u7fa9\uff09\u3001PR12\uff08\u6574\u689d\uff0c\u7cbe\u78ba\uff09\u3001\n    PR12-I1\uff08\u55ae\u884c\uff0c\u7cbe\u78ba\uff09\u3002ID \u985e\u6c38\u9060\u4e0d\u6703\u6b67\u7fa9\u3002\"\"\"\n    out: list[str] = []\n    ambiguous: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    for tok in sorted(tokens):\n        kind, key = digest.parse_reject_token(tok)\n        if kind == \"line\":\n            pr_key = key.split(\"-\", 1)[0]\n            hit = False\n            for x in staged:\n                info = _load_json(x) if x.exists() else None\n                if info and f\"PR{info.get('pr_id')}\" == pr_key:\n                    hit = _reject_line(x, key) or hit\n            out.append(f\"reject {key} {where} \u2192 \"\n                       + (\"\u8a72\u884c\u5df2\u79fb\u9664\uff08\u689d\u76ee\u4fdd\u7559\uff09\" if hit else \"\u67e5\u7121\u6b64 ID\uff08\u7565\u904e\uff09\"))\n            continue\n        if kind == \"entry\":\n            hit = False\n            for x in list(staged):\n                info = _load_json(x)\n                if info and f\"PR{info.get('pr_id')}\" == key and x.exists():\n                    x.unlink()\n                    hit = True\n            out.append(f\"reject {key} {where} \u2192 \" + (\"\u6574\u689d\u4e1f\" if hit else \"\u67e5\u7121\u6b64 PR\uff08\u7565\u904e\uff09\"))\n            continue\n        hits, ents = [], []\n        for x in list(staged):\n            info = _load_json(x)\n            if not info:\n                continue\n            ent = (info.get(\"draft\") or {}).get(\"primary_entity\", \"\")\n            stem = Path(ent).stem.lower()\n            if (\"/\" in tok and _suffix_eq(ent.lower(), tok)) \\\n                    or (\"/\" not in tok and stem == tok):\n                hits.append(x)\n                ents.append(ent)\n        if len(hits) > 1:\n            ambiguous[tok] = ents\n            out.append(f\"reject '{tok}' \u5c0d\u5230 {len(hits)} \u689d\uff08\u540c\u540d stem\uff09\u2014\u2014\"\n                       \"\u5df2\u56de\u8cbc\u8acb\u6c42\u6d88\u6b67\u7fa9\uff0c\u672c\u8f2a\u5168\u6578\u4fdd\u7559\")\n            continue\n        for x in hits:\n            if x.exists():\n                x.unlink()\n                out.append(f\"staged {tok} {where} reject \u2192 \u4e1f\")\n    return out, ambiguous\n\n\ndef _post_ambiguity(c, ref: PrRef, state: dict, key: str,\n                    ambiguous: dict[str, list[str]]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u5c0d release owner \u8aaa\u4eba\u8a71\uff1a\u54ea\u500b token \u649e\u540d\u3001\u5019\u9078\u6709\u54ea\u4e9b\u3001\u8a72\u600e\u9ebc\u6253\u3002\n    state \u8a18\u5e33\uff08\u6bcf token \u53ea\u8cbc\u4e00\u6b21\uff09\uff0c30 \u5206\u9418\u4e00\u8f2a\u7684 timer \u4e0d\u6703\u8b8a\u6210\u9a37\u64fe\u3002\"\"\"\n    done = set(state.get(key, {}).get(\"ambig\", []))\n    fresh = {t: e for t, e in ambiguous.items() if t not in done}\n    out: list[str] = []\n    if not fresh:\n        return out\n    lines = [\"<!-- pr-review-knowledge-digest -->\",\n             \"**\u26a0 Reject ambiguity \u2014 no entry was dropped**\", \"\"]\n    for tok, ents in fresh.items():\n        lines.append(f\"- `reject {tok}` matches {len(ents)} entries: \"\n                     + \", \".join(f\"`{e}`\" for e in ents[:4])\n                     + \" \u2014 reply with the PR id shown in the digest \"\n                     + \"(e.g. `reject PR12`), or a path suffix, e.g. \"\n                     + f\"`reject {ents[0].split('/', 1)[-1] if '/' in ents[0] else ents[0]}`\")\n    try:\n        _post_thread(c, ref, \"\\n\".join(lines))\n        st = state.setdefault(key, {})\n        st[\"ambig\"] = sorted(done | set(fresh))\n        out.append(f\"\u6b67\u7fa9\u56de\u8cbc \u2192 PR#{ref.pr_id}\uff08{len(fresh)} \u500b token\uff09\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        out.append(f\"\u6b67\u7fa9\u56de\u8cbc\u5931\u6557\uff08{e}\uff09\u2014\u2014\u50c5 journal \u7559\u75d5\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _cycle_first_sight(repo: str, state: dict) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\u9019\u500b repo \u7684\u9031\u671f state \u662f\u4e0d\u662f\u5168\u65b0\u7684\uff08= \u6536\u5272\u5668\u7b2c\u4e00\u6b21\u770b\u5230\u5b83\uff09\u3002\n\n    \u300c\u54ea\u4e9b\u9a57\u6536 PR \u5df2\u7d93\u7d50\u7b97\u904e\u300d\u53ea\u8a18\u5728 `_state/cycle.json`\uff0c\u800c\u90a3\u500b\u6a94\u4f4f\u5728\n    KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u5e95\u4e0b\uff1b\u5e33\u672c\u88ab\u91cd\u65b0 clone\u3001_state \u6389\u4e86\u3001\u6216\u6e2c\u8a66\u6642\u6e05\u7a7a KB\uff0c\n    \u8a18\u61b6\u5c31\u6c92\u4e86\u2014\u2014\u4f46 ADO \u90a3\u908a\u7684\u6b77\u53f2\u4e00\u689d\u90fd\u6c92\u5c11\u3002\u5c11\u4e86\u9019\u500b\u5224\u65b7\uff0c\u6536\u5272\u5668\u6703\u628a\n    \u300c\u4e0a\u500b\u6708\u65e9\u5c31\u7d50\u7b97\u5b8c\u7684\u9a57\u6536 PR\u300d\u7576\u6210\u300c\u525b\u5b8c\u6210\u3001\u7b49\u7d50\u7b97\u300d\uff0c\u628a\u7576\u4e0b\u66ab\u5b58\u7684\u7a3f\n    \u7acb\u523b\u843d\u5730\uff0c\u800c\u90a3\u6279\u7a3f\u6c92\u6709\u4efb\u4f55\u4eba\u5728\u4efb\u4f55 digest \u4e0a\u770b\u904e\u3002\n\n    \u5c0d\u7b56\u8207 _watermark_scan \u540c\u4e00\u5957\uff1a\u9996\u898b\u5373\u5b9a\u6c34\u4f4d\uff0c\u6b77\u53f2\u4e0d\u56de\u586b\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    return not any(k.startswith(f\"{repo}#\") for k in state)\n\n\ndef _pending_for(root: Path, repo: str, branch: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\u9084\u5728 _pending\uff08\u5c0f PR \u672a completed\uff09\u4e14\u76ee\u6a19\u5206\u652f\u5c31\u662f\u672c\u9031\u671f src \u7684\u7a3f\u6578\u3002\n    \u9a57\u6536 PR \u5b8c\u6210\u6642\u82e5\u6c60\u5b50\u662f\u7a7a\u7684\u4f46\u9019\u88e1 > 0\uff0c\u4e0d\u80fd\u6a19 closed\u2014\u2014\u5426\u5247\u90a3\u5e7e\u689d\u7a3f\n    completed \u5f8c\u9032\u6c60\u5c31\u6c38\u9060\u6c92\u6709\u9a57\u6536 PR \u4f86\u6536\uff08\u539f\u300c\u5b64\u5152\u300d\u554f\u984c\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    d = root / \"_pending\" / repo\n    if not d.is_dir():\n        return 0\n    n = 0\n    for f in d.glob(\"pr-*.json\"):\n        info = _load_json(f)\n        if info and (info.get(\"target_branch\") or \"\") == branch:\n            n += 1\n    return n\n\n\ndef _staged(root: Path, repo: str, branch: str | None = None) -> list[Path]:\n    \"\"\"branch \u7d66\u5b9a\u6642\uff0c\u53ea\u56de\u300c\u76ee\u6a19\u5206\u652f == branch\u300d\u7684\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\uff08\u7121\u6a19\u8a18\u8996\u70ba\u842c\u7528\uff09\u3002\n    \u591a\u689d release \u5206\u652f\u4e26\u884c\u6642\uff0c\u5404\u9031\u671f\u53ea\u6536\u81ea\u5df1\u90a3\u6279\u2014\u2014\u4e0d\u8de8\u9031\u671f\u6c61\u67d3\u3002\"\"\"\n    d = root / \"_cycle\" / repo\n    files = sorted(d.glob(\"pr-*.json\")) if d.is_dir() else []\n    if branch is None:\n        return files\n    out = []\n    for f in files:\n        try:\n            tb = json.loads(f.read_text()).get(\"target_branch\", \"\")\n        except Exception:\n            tb = \"\"\n        if not tb or tb == branch:\n            out.append(f)\n    return out\n\n\ndef _listed(st: dict, staged_prs: list[str]) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u5df2\u51fa\u73fe\u5728\u67d0\u5247 digest \u88e1\u7684 PR \u96c6\u5408\u3002\n\n    \u5347\u7d1a\u76f8\u5bb9\uff1a\u820a state \u53ea\u6709 digest:true \u6c92\u6709 listed \u2014\u2014 \u90a3\u5247\u820a digest \u5217\u7684\u5c31\u662f\n    \u7576\u6642\u6240\u6709\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\uff0c\u9019\u88e1\u628a\u73fe\u5728\u6c60\u88e1\u7684\u8996\u70ba\u5df2\u5217\uff08\u5be7\u53ef\u5c11\u8cbc\u4e00\u5247 delta\uff0c\u4e5f\u4e0d\u628a\n    \u6574\u4efd digest \u91cd\u8cbc\u4e00\u6b21\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    if \"listed\" in st:\n        return set(st[\"listed\"])\n    return set(staged_prs) if st.get(\"digest\") else set()\n\n\ndef _post_digest(c, ref: PrRef, repo: str, items: list[dict],\n                 listed: set[str], log: list[str]) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u9996\u6b21\u5168\u5217\u3001\u4e4b\u5f8c\u53ea\u88dc\u65b0\u9032\u7684\uff08delta\uff09\u3002\u56de\u66f4\u65b0\u5f8c\u7684 listed\uff1b\u8cbc\u5931\u6557\u56de\u539f\u96c6\u5408\n    \uff08\u4e0b\u4e00\u8f2a\u518d\u8a66\u2014\u2014\u689d\u76ee\u6c92\u88ab\u4eba\u770b\u904e\u4e4b\u524d\u4e0d\u7b97\u300c\u5df2\u5217\u300d\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    all_prs = {f\"PR{it.get('pr_id')}\" for it in items}\n    new_prs = all_prs - listed\n    if not new_prs:\n        return listed\n    analysis = digest.analyze(repo, items, log=lambda m: log.append(f\"{repo}: {m}\"))\n    first = not listed\n    md = digest.render(items, None if first else new_prs, analysis,\n                       total=len(items))\n    try:\n        _post_thread(c, ref, md)\n    except Exception as e:\n        log.append(f\"{repo}: digest \u8cbc\u5931\u6557\uff08{e}\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u4e0b\u4e00\u8f2a\u91cd\u8a66\")\n        return listed\n    n_flags = len(analysis[\"flags\"]) if analysis else 0\n    log.append(f\"{repo}: digest{'' if first else '\uff08delta\uff09'} \u2192 \u9a57\u6536 PR#{ref.pr_id}\"\n               f\"\uff08{len(new_prs)} \u689d{'\u958b\u7a97' if first else '\u65b0\u9032'}\"\n               + (f\"\uff0c{n_flags} \u500b\u9867\u554f\u65d7\u6a19\" if analysis else \"\uff0c\u7121\u9867\u554f\u5206\u6790\") + \"\uff09\")\n    return listed | new_prs\n\n\ndef _cycle_close(c, root: Path) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u5c0d\u6bcf\u500b\u5df2\u77e5 repo\uff1aactive \u9a57\u6536 PR \u2192 \u8cbc digest\uff08\u9996\u6b21 / delta\uff09+ \u6536 reject\uff1b\n    completed \u9a57\u6536 PR \u2192 \u6536\u53e3\u524d\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u6b21\u6536 reject \u2192 \u6279\u6b21\u843d\u5730 + \u9031\u671f\u6536\u64da\u3002\"\"\"\n    state_f = root / \"_state\" / \"cycle.json\"\n    state = (_load_json(state_f) or {}) if state_f.exists() else {}\n    repos_f = root / \"_state\" / \"repos.json\"\n    if not repos_f.exists():\n        return []\n    src_pat, tgt_pat = _cycle_pat()\n    digest_on = settings().knowledge.digest\n    out: list[str] = []\n\n    def _is_cycle_pr(pr: dict) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n        src = (pr.get(\"sourceRefName\") or \"\").replace(\"refs/heads/\", \"\")\n        tgt = (pr.get(\"targetRefName\") or \"\").replace(\"refs/heads/\", \"\")\n        return (fnmatch.fnmatch(src, src_pat)\n                and fnmatch.fnmatch(tgt, tgt_pat)), src\n\n    for repo, base in (_load_json(repos_f) or {}).items():\n        ref0 = PrRef(base_url=base, repo=repo, pr_id=0)\n        # \u5728\u52d5\u4efb\u4f55 state \u4e4b\u524d\u5148\u554f\uff1a\u9019\u500b repo \u662f\u4e0d\u662f\u9996\u898b\uff1f\uff08\u4e0b\u9762\u7684 active \u8ff4\u5708\n        # \u6703 setdefault \u51fa key\uff0c\u554f\u665a\u4e86\u7b54\u6848\u5c31\u88ab\u81ea\u5df1\u6c59\u67d3\u4e86\uff09\n        first_sight = _cycle_first_sight(repo, state)\n        for pr in _list_active(c, ref0):\n            ok, src = _is_cycle_pr(pr)\n            if not ok:\n                continue\n            pid = pr.get(\"pullRequestId\")\n            ref = PrRef(base_url=base, repo=repo, pr_id=pid)\n            key = f\"{repo}#{pid}\"\n            st = state.setdefault(key, {})\n            staged = _staged(root, repo, src)      # \u53ea\u8a8d\u672c\u9031\u671f\uff08src \u5206\u652f\uff09\u90a3\u6279\n            items = [it for it in (_load_staged(x) for x in staged) if it]\n            listed = _listed(st, [f\"PR{it.get('pr_id')}\" for it in items])\n            if digest_on and items:\n                listed = _post_digest(c, ref, repo, items, listed, out)\n            if listed or st.get(\"digest\"):\n                st[\"listed\"] = sorted(listed)\n                st[\"digest\"] = True\n            # \u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u5167\u6536 reject\uff08\u884c\u9996\u547d\u4ee4\u5f0f\uff1b\u5be6\u9ad4\u540d / PR12 / PR12-I1\uff09+ \u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u88c1\u6c7a\uff08\u540c\u7fa9\uff09\n            msgs, ambiguous = _apply_rejects(\n                _collect_rejects(_get_threads(c, ref)) | ledger.peek_verdicts(root, repo)[0],\n                staged, \"\u9a57\u6536\u7a97\")\n            for line in msgs:\n                out.append(f\"{repo}: {line}\")\n            for line in _post_ambiguity(c, ref, state, key, ambiguous):\n                out.append(f\"{repo}: {line}\")\n        # completed \u9a57\u6536 PR \u2192 \u6536\u53e3\n        swallowed = 0\n        for pr in _list_completed(c, ref0):\n            ok, src = _is_cycle_pr(pr)\n            pid = pr.get(\"pullRequestId\")\n            key = f\"{repo}#{pid}\"\n            if not ok or state.get(key, {}).get(\"closed\"):\n                continue\n            st = state.setdefault(key, {})\n            if first_sight:\n                # \u9996\u898b\u6c34\u4f4d\uff1aADO \u56de\u7684\u662f\u300c\u6700\u8fd1 100 \u689d completed\u300d\uff0c\u6c92\u6709\u6642\u9593\u689d\u4ef6\uff0c\n                # \u6240\u4ee5\u9019\u4e9b\u591a\u534a\u662f\u6211\u5011\u958b\u59cb\u770b\u4e4b\u524d\u5c31\u7d50\u7b97\u5b8c\u7684\u3002\u6a19 closed\u3001\u4e0d\u843d\u5730\u3002\n                st[\"closed\"] = True\n                st[\"note\"] = \"\u9996\u898b\u6c34\u4f4d\uff1a\u672c\u8f2a\u4e4b\u524d\u5c31\u5df2\u5b8c\u6210\uff0c\u4e0d\u56de\u586b\u6536\u53e3\"\n                swallowed += 1\n                continue\n            staged = _staged(root, repo, src)      # \u672c\u9031\u671f\u90a3\u6279\n            if not staged:\n                n_wait = _pending_for(root, repo, src)\n                if n_wait:\n                    out.append(f\"{repo}: \u9a57\u6536 PR#{pid} \u5df2\u5b8c\u6210\u4f46\u4ecd\u6709 {n_wait} \u689d \"\n                               f\"_pending \u6307\u5411 {src} \u2014\u2014 \u66ab\u4e0d\u6536\u53e3\uff0c\u7b49\u5b83\u5011\u88c1\u6c7a\")\n                    continue\n                st[\"closed\"] = True\n                continue\n            # \u6536\u53e3\u524d\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u6b21\u6536 reject / keep\uff08\u9632\u300c\u56de\u5b8c\u99ac\u4e0a\u6309 Complete\u300d\u7684\u6642\u9593\u5dee\u6f0f\u770b\uff09\n            ref = PrRef(base_url=base, repo=repo, pr_id=pid)\n            keeps: set[str] = set()\n            try:\n                threads = _get_threads(c, ref)\n                tokens = _collect_rejects(threads)\n                keeps = _collect_keeps(threads)\n            except Exception:\n                tokens = set()\n            c_rej, c_keep = ledger.consume_verdicts(root, repo)   # \u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u88c1\u6c7a\uff1a\u6536\u53e3\u6642\u7528\u6389\n            tokens, keeps = tokens | c_rej, keeps | c_keep\n            msgs, ambiguous = _apply_rejects(tokens, staged, \"\u6536\u53e3\u524d\")\n            for line in msgs:\n                out.append(f\"{repo}: {line}\")\n            for line in _post_ambiguity(c, ref, state, key, ambiguous):\n                out.append(f\"{repo}: {line}\")\n            staged = _staged(root, repo, src)\n            if not staged:\n                st[\"closed\"] = True\n                continue\n            items = [(x, it) for x in staged for it in [_load_staged(x)] if it]\n            listed = _listed(st, [f\"PR{it.get('pr_id')}\" for _, it in items])\n            day = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n            rows = []\n            unlisted = 0\n            for x, it in items:\n                prov = f\"cycle/{it.get('provenance', 'silent')}\"\n                if f\"PR{it.get('pr_id')}\" not in listed:\n                    prov += \"+unlisted\"       # \u6c92\u4eba\u770b\u904e\u5c31\u843d\u5730\uff1a\u6524\u5728 provenance \u4e0a\n                    unlisted += 1\n                res, landed = _land(root, repo, it[\"pr_id\"], it[\"draft\"], prov,\n                                    author_note=it.get(\"author_note\", \"\"),\n                                    rejected_ids=it.get(\"rejected_ids\") or [])\n                for sup in it[\"draft\"].get(\"supersedes\") or []:\n                    out.append(f\"{repo}: \"\n                               f\"{_mark_superseded(root, repo, sup, it['pr_id'], landed)}\")\n                rows.append(f\"| PR#{it['pr_id']} | \"\n                            f\"{Path(it['draft'].get('primary_entity', '')).stem}\"\n                            f\" | {prov} |\")\n                x.unlink()\n            # \u843d\u5730\u4e4b\u5f8c\u624d\u8655\u7406\u77db\u76fe\uff1a\u65b0\u689d\u76ee\u5df2\u7d93\u5beb\u9032\u9801\u9762\uff0c\u9019\u6642\u518d\u628a\u88ab\u63a8\u7ffb\u7684\u820a\u884c\u756b\u6389\uff0c\n            # \u9806\u5e8f\u8207\u4eba\u7684\u76f4\u89ba\u4e00\u81f4\uff08\u5148\u8a18\u4e0b\u9019\u6b21\u6c7a\u5b9a\u4e86\u4ec0\u9ebc\uff0c\u518d\u5283\u6389\u5b83\u53d6\u4ee3\u7684\u6771\u897f\uff09\u3002\n            retired_lines = _apply_contradictions(root, repo, items, keeps)\n            for line in retired_lines:\n                out.append(f\"{repo}: {line}\")\n            cyc_page = root / repo / \"_cycles\" / f\"{day}-PR{pid}.md\"\n            cyc_page.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n            cyc_page.write_text(\n                f\"# Cycle acceptance \u2014 PR#{pid} ({day})\\n\\n\"\n                \"| Source PR | Entity | Provenance |\\n|---|---|---|\\n\"\n                + \"\\n\".join(rows) + \"\\n\"\n                + (\"\\n## Invariants retired this cycle\\n\"\n                   \"\uff08\u88ab\u5408\u4f75\u7684\u5be6\u4f5c\u63a8\u7ffb\uff0c\u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u672a\u5426\u6c7a\uff09\\n\\n\"\n                   + \"\\n\".join(f\"- {ln}\" for ln in retired_lines) + \"\\n\"\n                   if retired_lines else \"\"), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            st[\"closed\"] = True\n            out.append(f\"{repo}: \u9a57\u6536 PR#{pid} \u6536\u53e3 \u2192 \u843d\u5730 {len(rows)} \u689d + \u9031\u671f\u9801\"\n                       + (f\"\uff08{unlisted} \u689d\u5f9e\u672a\u51fa\u73fe\u5728 digest\uff0cprovenance \u5df2\u6a19 +unlisted\uff09\"\n                          if unlisted else \"\"))\n        if swallowed:\n            out.append(f\"{repo}: \u9996\u898b\uff0c{swallowed} \u689d\u6b77\u53f2\u9a57\u6536 PR \u6a19\u70ba\u5df2\u6536\u53e3\"\n                       \"\uff08\u4e0d\u56de\u586b\u843d\u5730\uff1b\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\u7559\u8457\u7b49\u4e0b\u4e00\u689d\u771f\u6b63\u5b8c\u6210\u7684\u9a57\u6536 PR\uff09\")\n    write_json_atomic(state_f, state)\n    return out\n\n\n# ---------- git\uff08\u552f\u4e00\u5beb\u624b\uff09 ----------\n\ndef _git(root: Path, *args) -> None:\n    r = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), *args],\n                       capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if r.returncode != 0 and \"commit\" in args:\n        msg = (r.stderr or r.stdout or \"\").strip()\n        if \"nothing to commit\" not in msg and \"nothing added\" not in msg:\n            print(f\"[harvest] git commit \u5931\u6557\uff08{msg.splitlines()[-1] if msg else '?'}\uff09\"\n                  \"\u2014\u2014 \u6a94\u6848\u5df2\u5beb\u5165\u4f46\u7121\u7248\u672c\u7d00\u9304\uff1b\u591a\u534a\u662f user.name/email \u672a\u8a2d\")\n\n\ndef main() -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\u8dd1\u4e00\u8f2a\uff1b\u56de\u50b3\u6bcf\u500b\u9805\u76ee\u4e00\u884c\uff08jobs \u5b58\u6210 last_detail\uff0cCLI \u76f4\u63a5\u5370\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    out: list[str] = []\n    root = settings().knowledge.root\n    if root is None:\n        out.append(\"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\u5b9a\uff0c\u6536\u5272\u5668\u4e0d\u8dd1\")\n        return out\n    if not root.is_dir():\n        out.append(f\"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\uff1a{root}\")\n        return out\n    _git(root, \"add\", \"-A\")\n    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-m\", \"knowledge: stage pendings\")\n\n    pendings = sorted((root / \"_pending\").rglob(\"pr-*.json\")) \\\n        if (root / \"_pending\").is_dir() else []\n    out.append(f\"pending {len(pendings)} \u689d\")\n    with client() as c:\n        for pend in pendings:\n            try:\n                out.append(f\"PR {pend.stem[3:]}\uff08{pend.parent.name}\uff09\uff1a\"\n                           f\"{_process_pending(c, root, pend)}\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                out.append(f\"{pend.name} \u5931\u6557\uff1a{e}\uff08\u4fdd\u7559\u5f85\u4e0b\u8f2a\uff09\")\n        out += _watermark_scan(c, root)\n        out += _cycle_close(c, root)\n\n    _git(root, \"add\", \"-A\")\n    _git(root, \"commit\", \"-m\",\n         f\"knowledge: harvest {time.strftime('%F %T')}\")\n    out.append(\"\u5b8c\u6210\")\n    return out\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    fail_fast()\n    for _ln in main():\n        print(f\"[harvest] {_ln}\")\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/ledger.py","perm":"0644","sha":"33a900edd6e739320bc273c881622c615a76c361b2f17cc80f68b556bffa6626","data":"\"\"\"ledger \u2014\u2014 \u63a7\u5236\u53f0 Knowledge \u9801\u7684\u8b80\u5beb\u5c64\uff1a\u770b\u5e33\u672c\u5728\u7b49\u8ab0\u3001\u66ff\u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u4e0b\u88c1\u6c7a\u3002\n\n\u8b80\uff1a_pending/\uff08\u84b8\u993e\u7a3f\uff0c\u7b49 PR \u7d42\u614b\uff09\u3001_cycle/\uff08\u66ab\u5b58\u7a3f\uff0c\u7b49 release\u2192master \u9a57\u6536 PR \u6536\u53e3\uff09\u3001\n    _state/cycle.json\uff08\u54ea\u4e9b\u9a57\u6536 PR \u958b\u4e86\u7a97\u3001\u5217\u904e\u8ab0\u3001\u6536\u53e3\u4e86\u6c92\uff09\u3001digest \u9810\u89bd\uff08\u7d14\u6e32\u67d3\uff0c\u96f6 LLM\uff09\u3002\n\u5beb\uff1a**\u53ea\u5beb\u4e00\u500b\u6a94** `_state/console-verdicts.json`\uff1a\n    {repo: {\"reject\": {token: {\"by\", \"ts\"}}, \"keep\": {ID: {\"by\", \"ts\"}}}}\n    harvester \u6536\u53e3\uff08\u8207\u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u5167\u6536 reject\uff09\u6642\u628a\u5b83\u8ddf PR \u7559\u8a00\u88e1\u7684 `reject \u2026` / `keep \u2026`\n    \u5408\u5728\u4e00\u8d77\u770b\uff0c\u8a9e\u610f\u5b8c\u5168\u76f8\u540c\uff08\u5be6\u9ad4\u540d / PR12 / PR12-I1 \u4e09\u7a2e\u7c92\u5ea6\u3001keep \u5426\u6c7a\u62d4\u9664\uff09\uff0c\n    \u7528\u6389\u4e4b\u5f8c\u6e05\u6389\u8a72 repo \u7684\u90a3\u4e00\u4efd\u3002\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u662f\u7b2c\u4e8c\u500b\u300c\u4eba\u88c1\u300d\u7684\u5165\u53e3\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u7b2c\u4e8c\u5957\u898f\u5247\u3002\n\n\u9019\u88e1\u4e0d\u78b0 git\u3001\u4e0d\u78b0 ADO\u3001\u4e0d\u547c\u53eb LLM\uff1bharvester \u4ecd\u662f\u552f\u4e00 commit \u8005\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom orchestrator.knowledge import assign_ids, decision_line, inv_id, inv_text, write_json_atomic\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\nVERDICTS = \"console-verdicts.json\"\n\n\ndef _root() -> Path | None:\n    r = settings().knowledge.root\n    return r if r is not None and r.is_dir() else None\n\n\ndef _load(p: Path) -> dict | None:\n    try:\n        return json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return None\n\n\ndef _draft_summary(d: dict, pr_id: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    d = dict(d or {})\n    assign_ids(d, pr_id)\n    return {\n        \"primary_entity\": d.get(\"primary_entity\", \"\"),\n        \"ledger_line\": (d.get(\"ledger_line\") or d.get(\"summary\") or \"\").strip(),\n        \"decisions\": [{\"id\": (x.get(\"id\") or \"\"), \"text\": decision_line(x, pr_id)}\n                      for x in d.get(\"decisions\") or [] if isinstance(x, dict)],\n        \"invariants\": [{\"id\": inv_id(x), \"text\": inv_text(x)} for x in d.get(\"invariants\") or [] if inv_text(x)],\n        \"supersedes\": d.get(\"supersedes\") or [],\n        \"intent\": d.get(\"intent\", \"\"),\n    }\n\n\n# ---------- \u8b80 ----------\n\ndef pending() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None:\n        return []\n    out = []\n    for f in sorted((root / \"_pending\").rglob(\"pr-*.json\")) if (root / \"_pending\").is_dir() else []:\n        info = _load(f)\n        if not info:\n            out.append({\"file\": f.name, \"repo\": f.parent.name, \"broken\": True})\n            continue\n        pid = int(info.get(\"pr_id\") or 0)\n        out.append({\n            \"file\": f.name, \"repo\": info.get(\"repo\") or f.parent.name, \"pr_id\": pid,\n            \"pr_url\": info.get(\"pr_url\", \"\"), \"created\": info.get(\"created\", \"\"),\n            \"target_branch\": info.get(\"target_branch\", \"\"), \"author\": info.get(\"author\", \"\"),\n            \"posted\": bool(info.get(\"posted\")), \"dry_run\": bool(info.get(\"dry_run\")),\n            \"post_failed\": bool(info.get(\"post_failed\")), \"thread_id\": info.get(\"thread_id\"),\n            \"redistilled\": bool(info.get(\"redistilled\")),\n            \"redistill_attempts\": (info.get(\"redistill_requested\") or {}).get(\"attempts\", 0),\n            \"contradicted\": info.get(\"contradicted\") or [],\n            \"dropped\": info.get(\"distill_dropped\") or [], \"slices_skipped\": info.get(\"distill_slices_skipped\") or [],\n            \"draft\": _draft_summary(info.get(\"draft\") or {}, pid),\n        })\n    return out\n\n\ndef staged() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None:\n        return []\n    out = []\n    for f in sorted((root / \"_cycle\").rglob(\"pr-*.json\")) if (root / \"_cycle\").is_dir() else []:\n        it = _load(f)\n        if not it:\n            continue\n        pid = int(it.get(\"pr_id\") or 0)\n        out.append({\n            \"file\": f.name, \"repo\": it.get(\"repo\") or f.parent.name, \"pr_id\": pid,\n            \"pr_url\": it.get(\"pr_url\", \"\"), \"target_branch\": it.get(\"target_branch\", \"\"),\n            \"provenance\": it.get(\"provenance\", \"silent\"), \"author_note\": it.get(\"author_note\", \"\"),\n            \"contradicted\": it.get(\"contradicted\") or [], \"rejected_ids\": it.get(\"rejected_ids\") or [],\n            \"draft\": _draft_summary(it.get(\"draft\") or {}, pid),\n            \"_raw\": it,\n        })\n    return out\n\n\ndef cycle_state() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None:\n        return {}\n    st = _load(root / \"_state\" / \"cycle.json\") or {}\n    return {k: v for k, v in st.items() if isinstance(v, dict)}\n\n\ndef digest_preview(repo: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u8ddf\u9a57\u6536 PR \u4e0a\u90a3\u5247 digest \u540c\u4e00\u500b\u6e32\u67d3\uff0c\u4f46\u96f6 LLM\uff08\u6c92\u6709\u9867\u554f\u6bb5\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    from orchestrator import knowledge_digest as digest\n    items = [it[\"_raw\"] for it in staged() if it[\"repo\"] == repo]\n    if not items:\n        return \"\"\n    for it in items:\n        assign_ids(it.get(\"draft\") or {}, int(it.get(\"pr_id\") or 0))\n    return digest.render(items, None, None, total=len(items))\n\n\n# ---------- \u88c1\u6c7a ----------\n\ndef verdicts() -> dict[str, dict[str, dict[str, dict]]]:\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None:\n        return {}\n    return _load(root / \"_state\" / VERDICTS) or {}\n\n\ndef add_verdict(repo: str, kind: str, token: str, by: str = \"console\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"kind \u2208 reject | keep\uff1btoken = \u5be6\u9ad4\u540d / PR12 / PR12-I1\uff08reject\uff09\u6216 PR12-I1\uff08keep\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None:\n        return \"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\u6216\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\"\n    repo = (repo or \"\").strip().lower()\n    token = (token or \"\").strip()\n    if kind not in (\"reject\", \"keep\") or not repo or not token:\n        return \"\u7f3a\u5c11 repo / kind / token\"\n    if kind == \"keep\" and not token.upper().startswith(\"PR\"):\n        return \"keep \u50c5\u63a5\u53d7\u689d\u76ee ID\uff08\u4f8b\u5982 PR12-I1\uff09\"\n    key = token.upper() if token.upper().startswith(\"PR\") else token.lower()\n    data = verdicts()\n    data.setdefault(repo, {}).setdefault(kind, {})[key] = {\"by\": by, \"ts\": time.strftime(\"%FT%T\")}\n    write_json_atomic(root / \"_state\" / VERDICTS, data)\n    return f\"{kind} {key} \u5df2\u8a18\u9304\uff1b\u4e0b\u6b21 harvest \u65bc\u9a57\u6536\u7a97 / \u6536\u53e3\u6642\u5957\u7528\"\n\n\ndef remove_verdict(repo: str, kind: str, token: str) -> str:\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None:\n        return \"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\u6216\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\"\n    data = verdicts()\n    repo = (repo or \"\").strip().lower()\n    key = token.upper() if token.upper().startswith(\"PR\") else token.lower()\n    if data.get(repo, {}).get(kind, {}).pop(key, None) is None:\n        return \"\u7121\u6b64\u88c1\u6c7a\"\n    write_json_atomic(root / \"_state\" / VERDICTS, data)\n    return f\"{kind} {key} \u5df2\u64a4\u56de\"\n\n\ndef consume_verdicts(root: Path, repo: str) -> tuple[set[str], set[str]]:\n    \"\"\"harvester \u7528\uff1a\u53d6\u51fa\u4e26\u6e05\u6389\u8a72 repo \u7684\u88c1\u6c7a\u3002\u56de (reject tokens, keep ids)\u3002\"\"\"\n    p = root / \"_state\" / VERDICTS\n    data = _load(p) or {}\n    mine = data.pop(repo.lower(), None) or {}\n    if mine:\n        write_json_atomic(p, data)\n    return (set(k.lower() for k in (mine.get(\"reject\") or {})),\n            set(k.upper() for k in (mine.get(\"keep\") or {})))\n\n\ndef peek_verdicts(root: Path, repo: str) -> tuple[set[str], set[str]]:\n    \"\"\"harvester \u9a57\u6536\u7a97\u5167\u7528\uff08\u4e0d\u6e05\u6389\u2014\u2014\u6536\u53e3\u6642\u624d\u7b97\u7528\u6389\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    mine = (_load(root / \"_state\" / VERDICTS) or {}).get(repo.lower()) or {}\n    return (set(k.lower() for k in (mine.get(\"reject\") or {})),\n            set(k.upper() for k in (mine.get(\"keep\") or {})))\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/llm.py","perm":"0644","sha":"eb61e37488664b1f14ea593a54a62ef64d07e2e805885aea5e43727ed9e21700","data":"\"\"\"LLM \u5171\u7528\u5c64\uff1aclient\u3001\u53d7\u7248\u63a7 prompt \u7684\u53d6\u7528\u3001\u5065\u58ef\u7684 JSON \u64f7\u53d6\u3002\n\nv2 pipeline \u7684\u9435\u5f8b\u5728\u9019\u88e1\u843d\u5be6\uff1a\u6bcf\u500b LLM \u968e\u6bb5\u90fd\u662f\u300cJSON \u8f38\u51fa + \u9a57\u8b49 +\n\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027 fallback\u300d\u2014\u2014LLM \u662f\u4e0d\u53ef\u9760\u96f6\u4ef6\uff0c\u4efb\u4f55\u968e\u6bb5\u6545\u969c\u90fd\u662f\u964d\u7d1a\u3001\u4e0d\u662f\u70b8\u6389\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport asyncio\nimport re\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom langfuse import get_client\nfrom langfuse.openai import AsyncOpenAI  # drop-in\uff1a\u547c\u53eb\u81ea\u52d5\u8b8a generation span\n\nfrom shared.settings import on_reload, settings\n\n_client: AsyncOpenAI | None = None\n\n\ndef _drop_client() -> None:\n    global _client\n    _client = None\n\n\non_reload(_drop_client)       # \u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u6539 LLM_BASE_URL / API key \u2192 \u4e0b\u4e00\u6b21\u547c\u53eb\u91cd\u5efa\n\n\ndef _llm() -> AsyncOpenAI:\n    \"\"\"\u9577\u99d0 client\uff08orchestrator \u7684 event loop \u7528\uff09\u3002\u7b2c\u4e00\u6b21\u547c\u53eb\u624d\u5efa\uff0c\n    \u8a2d\u5b9a\u503c\u7531 settings() \u4f86\u2014\u2014\u6a21\u7d44\u8f09\u5165\u6642\u4e0d\u518d\u5077\u8b80 env\u3002\"\"\"\n    global _client\n    if _client is None:\n        s = settings().llm\n        _client = AsyncOpenAI(base_url=s.base_url,\n                              api_key=s.api_key.get_secret_value())\n    return _client\n\n\ndef model_name() -> str:\n    return settings().llm.model\n\n\ndef prompt_or(name: str, default: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u512a\u5148\u7528 Langfuse \u53d7\u7248\u63a7\u7684 prompt\uff08UI \u6539\u7248\u3001code \u96f6\u6539\u52d5\uff09\uff1b\u62ff\u4e0d\u5230\u7528\u5167\u5efa\u7248\u3002\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return get_client().get_prompt(name).prompt\n    except Exception:\n        return default\n\n\nasync def complete(system: str, user: str, temperature: float = 0.2,\n                   model: str | None = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"model=None \u8d70 LLM_MODEL\uff1badversary \u53ef\u7528 LLM_MODEL_ADVERSARY \u63db\u4e00\u9846\u8166\n    \uff08\u6aa2\u5bdf\u5b98\u8207\u88ab\u544a\u5f8b\u5e2b\u5206\u5bb6\uff0c\u53bb\u6389\u81ea\u6211\u540c\u610f\u504f\u5dee\uff09\u3002\n    LLM_TIMEOUT_S\uff08\u9810\u8a2d 180\uff09+ \u4e00\u6b21\u91cd\u8a66\uff1agateway \u5361\u4f4f\u4e0d\u540a\u6b7b\u6574\u5834 review\u2014\u2014\n    \u91cd\u8a66\u4ecd\u5931\u6557\u5c31\u628a\u4f8b\u5916\u4ea4\u9084\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\uff0c\u8d70\u5404\u7ad9\u65e2\u6709\u7684\u964d\u7d1a\u8def\u5f91\u3002\"\"\"\n    timeout = settings().llm.timeout_s\n\n    async def _once() -> str:\n        resp = await _llm().chat.completions.create(\n            model=model or model_name(),\n            temperature=temperature,\n            messages=[{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system},\n                      {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user}],\n        )\n        return resp.choices[0].message.content or \"\"\n\n    try:\n        return await asyncio.wait_for(_once(), timeout=timeout)\n    except (asyncio.TimeoutError, Exception) as first:  # noqa: BLE001\n        await asyncio.sleep(1.5)\n        try:\n            return await asyncio.wait_for(_once(), timeout=timeout)\n        except Exception:\n            raise first\n\n\ndef complete_sync(system: str, user: str, temperature: float = 0.2,\n                  model: str | None = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u7d66\u975e async \u7684 oneshot \u7a0b\u5e8f\uff08knowledge_harvest\uff09\u7528\u3002\n\n    \u6bcf\u6b21\u547c\u53eb\u958b\u4e00\u500b\u65b0 event loop \u4e26\u5efa\u4e00\u500b\u65b0 client\uff1a\u6a21\u7d44\u5c64\u90a3\u9846 `llm` \u7684\u9023\u7dda\u6c60\n    \u7d81\u5728\u7b2c\u4e00\u500b loop \u4e0a\uff0c\u8de8 `asyncio.run` \u91cd\u7528\u6703\u70b8 \"Event loop is closed\"\u3002\n    \u540c\u6a23\u8d70 LLM_TIMEOUT_S + \u4e00\u6b21\u91cd\u8a66\uff1b\u5931\u6557\u628a\u4f8b\u5916\u4ea4\u9084\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u8d70\u964d\u7d1a\u3002\"\"\"\n    cfg = settings().llm\n    timeout = cfg.timeout_s\n\n    async def _go() -> str:\n        client = AsyncOpenAI(base_url=cfg.base_url,\n                             api_key=cfg.api_key.get_secret_value())\n\n        async def _once() -> str:\n            resp = await client.chat.completions.create(\n                model=model or model_name(), temperature=temperature,\n                messages=[{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system},\n                          {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user}])\n            return resp.choices[0].message.content or \"\"\n        try:\n            try:\n                return await asyncio.wait_for(_once(), timeout=timeout)\n            except (asyncio.TimeoutError, Exception) as first:  # noqa: BLE001\n                await asyncio.sleep(1.5)\n                try:\n                    return await asyncio.wait_for(_once(), timeout=timeout)\n                except Exception:\n                    raise first\n        finally:\n            close = getattr(client, \"close\", None)\n            if close is not None:\n                try:\n                    await close()\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n\n    return asyncio.run(_go())\n\n\n_FENCE = re.compile(r\"```(?:json)?\\s*([\\[{].*?[\\]}])\\s*```\", re.DOTALL)\n\n\ndef extract_json(text: str) -> Any | None:\n    \"\"\"\u5f9e\u6a21\u578b\u8f38\u51fa\u6488 JSON\uff1a\u5148\u8a66 fenced \u5340\u584a\uff08\u53d6\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u500b\uff09\uff0c\u518d\u8a66\u88f8 JSON\uff0c\n    \u6700\u5f8c\u8a66\u300c\u7b2c\u4e00\u500b [ \u6216 { \u5230\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u500b ] \u6216 }\u300d\u3002\u5168\u5931\u6557\u56de None\uff08\u547c\u53eb\u7aef\u8d70 fallback\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    m = None\n    for m in _FENCE.finditer(text):\n        pass\n    candidates = []\n    if m:\n        candidates.append(m.group(1))\n    candidates.append(text.strip())\n    start = min((i for i in (text.find(\"[\"), text.find(\"{\")) if i >= 0), default=-1)\n    end = max(text.rfind(\"]\"), text.rfind(\"}\"))\n    if start >= 0 and end > start:\n        candidates.append(text[start:end + 1])\n    for c in candidates:\n        try:\n            return json.loads(c)\n        except (json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError):\n            continue\n    return None\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/models.py","perm":"0644","sha":"11ec8a281ed9d5d79fdf39c78672562feaaff9be5429ac24c3b4591b7283c3c6","data":"\"\"\"\u8f38\u51fa\u5408\u7d04\uff08\u96d9\u8ecc\uff09\uff1amarkdown \u7d66\u4eba\u770b\uff0cfindings \u7d66\u6a5f\u5668\u8a55\u5206\u3002\u5f9e\u7b2c\u4e00\u5929\u5c31\u5b9a\u6b7b\u3002\n\nv2 \u8d77 Finding \u591a\u5169\u500b\u6b04\u4f4d\uff08\u90fd\u6709\u9810\u8a2d\u503c\uff0c\u5411\u5f8c\u76f8\u5bb9\uff09\uff1a\n  source      \"llm\" | \"static\" | \"graph\" \u2014\u2014 \u8ab0\u7522\u7684\uff08eval \u53ef per-source \u5207\u7247\uff09\n  confidence  0.0\u20131.0 \u2014\u2014 static \u6046\u70ba 1.0\uff1bLLM \u5f9e\u57fa\u790e\u503c\u8d77\u8df3\uff0c\u88ab adversary\n              \u78ba\u8a8d\u52a0\u6b0a\u3001\u63a8\u7ffb\u6253\u6298\uff1bsynthesis \u4f9d\u9580\u6abb\u904e\u6ffe\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\n\nclass Finding(BaseModel):\n    rule: str = Field(description=\"\u898f\u5247\u4ee3\u865f\uff0c\u4f8b\u5982 BUG / MISSING-TEST / NAMING / SECURITY / STYLE / PERF\")\n    file: str = \"\"\n    line: int | None = None\n    severity: str = \"info\"  # info | warning | error\n    note: str = \"\"\n    # \u4f9d\u64da\u7684\u5718\u968a\u898f\u5247\u6a94\u8def\u5f91\uff08\u4f8b\u5982 rules/common/naming.md\uff09\uff1b\u4e00\u822c\u767c\u73fe\u7559\u7a7a\u3002\n    rule_ref: str = \"\"\n    # \u4f9d\u64da\u7684\u77e5\u8b58\u689d\u76ee id\uff08\u4f8b\u5982 [\"PR12-I1\"]\uff09\u3002\u6e05\u55ae\u800c\u975e\u55ae\u503c\u662f\u523b\u610f\u7684\uff1a\u4e00\u689d finding\n    # \u53ef\u4ee5\u540c\u6642\u7ad9\u5728\u5169\u689d\u4e0d\u8b8a\u5f0f\u4e0a\u3002\u53ea\u6709\u300c\u672c\u6b21\u6ce8\u5165\u5340\u584a\u88e1\u771f\u7684\u51fa\u73fe\u904e\u300d\u7684 id \u7559\u5f97\u4e0b\u4f86\n    # \uff08synthesis \u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u9a57\u8b49\uff09\uff0c\u6240\u4ee5\u9019\u500b\u6b04\u4f4d\u662f\u5f15\u7528\u7387\u7684\u5206\u5b50\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u6a21\u578b\u7684\u81ea\u7531\u6b04\u3002\n    knowledge_ref: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\n    # \u5177\u9ad4\u4fee\u6cd5\u5efa\u8b70\uff08\u4e00\u5169\u53e5\uff0c\u53ef\u542b\u77ed\u78bc\uff09\uff1b\u5831\u544a\u6703\u4ee5\u300c\u21b3 \u5efa\u8b70\uff1a\u300d\u5448\u73fe\uff0c\u9078\u586b\n    suggestion: str = \"\"\n    source: str = \"llm\"      # llm | static | graph\n    # \u7522\u51fa\u9019\u689d finding \u7684\u5be9\u67e5\u9762\u5411\u540d\uff08\u5831\u544a\u7684 Dimensions \u8868\u4ea4\u53c9\u5f15\u7528\u7528\uff1bstatic \u7559\u7a7a\uff09\n    dimension: str = \"\"\n    confidence: float = 0.7\n\n\nclass ReviewResult(BaseModel):\n    markdown: str\n    findings: list[Finding] = []\n    stats: dict = {}         # pipeline \u5404\u968e\u6bb5\u7684\u7d71\u8a08\uff08\u9032 trace metadata / footer\uff09\n\n    def findings_summary(self) -> list[dict]:\n        return [f.model_dump() for f in self.findings]\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/pipeline.py","perm":"0644","sha":"c95aa983b0dd91b394dcc3b0a339c955b41a72fb995046e2155259e7e0f4d8de","data":"\"\"\"v2 pipeline \u2014\u2014 plan \u2192 coverage gate \u2192 parallel reviewers \u2192 adversary \u2192 synthesis\u3002\n\n\u5206\u5de5\u9435\u5f8b\uff08PR-AF \u7684\u6838\u5fc3\u6d1e\u898b\uff09\uff1a\u80fd\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u8a08\u7b97\u7684\u7d55\u4e0d\u7d66 LLM\u3002\n  anatomy / static / coverage gate / dedupe / \u4e58\u6578 / \u9580\u6abb / render = code\n  \u898f\u5283\u9762\u5411\u8207\u5047\u8aaa / \u627e\u554f\u984c / \u6311\u6230\u554f\u984c                              = LLM\n\u6bcf\u500b LLM \u968e\u6bb5\u90fd\u662f\u300cJSON + \u9a57\u8b49 + fallback\u300d\uff1a\u4efb\u4f55\u6545\u969c\u662f\u964d\u7d1a\u3001\u4e0d\u662f\u70b8\u6389\u3002\n\n\u672c\u7248\u4e09\u500b\u5347\u7d1a\uff08U1\u2013U3\uff09\uff1a\n  U1 \u539a brief\uff1aplanner \u5c0d\u6bcf\u500b\u9762\u5411\u7522\u300c\u5f85\u9a57\u8b49\u5047\u8aaa + \u6307\u6d3e\u898f\u5247\u300d\uff0creviewer \u6536\u5230\n     \u7684\u662f\u4efb\u52d9\u66f8\uff08\u5047\u8aaa\u9010\u689d\u9a57\u3001\u53ea\u5e36\u81ea\u5df1\u8a72\u7ba1\u7684\u898f\u5247\u5167\u5bb9 = targeted context\uff09\u3002\n  U2 \u8986\u84cb\u4fdd\u8b49\uff08\u7d14 code\uff09\uff1aplan \u5f8c\u6aa2\u67e5\u300c\u6bcf\u500b\u8b8a\u66f4\u6a94 \u2265 \u4e00\u500b\u9762\u5411\u300d\u300c\u6bcf\u689d md \u898f\u5247\n     \u2265 \u4e00\u500b\u9762\u5411\u300d\uff0c\u5b64\u5152\u81ea\u52d5\u88dc\u4e00\u500b Coverage Sweep \u9762\u5411\uff1bstats[\"coverage\"] \u8a18\u5e33\u3002\n  U3 adversary \u7cbe\u7dfb\u5316\uff1a\u5206\u584a\u5be9\uff08\u2264 ADVERSARY_CHUNK \u689d/\u6b21\uff0c\u9632\u6ce8\u610f\u529b\u7a00\u91cb\uff09\u3001\u5224\u6c7a\n     \u5fc5\u9644\u884c\u865f\u8b49\u64da\u8207\u6311\u6230\u7de8\u865f\u3001\u53ef\u7528 LLM_MODEL_ADVERSARY \u63db\u4e00\u9846\u8166\u53bb\u81ea\u6211\u540c\u610f\u504f\u5dee\u3002\n\n\u65cb\u9215\u5168\u90e8\u4f4f\u5728 shared/settings.py \u7684 Review \u7d44\uff08settings().review.*\uff09\uff0c\n\u6bcf\u9846\u90fd\u9032 trace metadata\uff1b\u540d\u5b57\u8207\u9810\u8a2d\u503c\u898b\u8a72\u6a94\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\n\nfrom langfuse import observe\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nfrom orchestrator import context as ctx\nfrom orchestrator import knowledge\nfrom orchestrator.anatomy import (Anatomy, line_in_view, line_near,\n                                 match_path, numbered_slice, parse_diff)\nfrom orchestrator.llm import complete, extract_json, prompt_or\nfrom orchestrator.models import Finding, ReviewResult\nfrom orchestrator.progress import note\nfrom orchestrator.render import render_markdown, sort_key\nfrom orchestrator.rules import RulesBundle\nfrom orchestrator.static_pass import run_static\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\n# ---------- \u53d7\u7248\u63a7 prompts\uff08Langfuse \u512a\u5148\uff0c\u5167\u5efa\u70ba\u5f8c\u5099\uff1bseed_langfuse \u6703\u63a8\u4e0a\u53bb\uff09 ----------\n\nPLANNER_PROMPT_NAME = \"pr-review-planner\"\nREVIEWER_PROMPT_NAME = \"pr-review-reviewer\"\nADVERSARY_PROMPT_NAME = \"pr-review-adversary\"\n\nDEFAULT_PLANNER_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are the review planner of an automated pull-request review system. Your output is the investigation brief that individual reviewers will execute, so be specific: a vague plan produces a vague review.\n\nGiven the structural summary of a pull request, decide which review dimensions this specific PR warrants. Derive the dimensions from the actual risk profile of the change \u2014 for example: database access warrants injection and transactional-integrity scrutiny; public API changes warrant input-validation and backward-compatibility scrutiny; pure refactors warrant behavior-preservation and consistency scrutiny. Do not apply a generic checklist.\n\nRequirements:\n- Define 2 to {max_dims} dimensions.\n- Taken together, the dimensions must give every category an owner: behavioral correctness (BUG), security (SECURITY), test adequacy (MISSING-TEST), naming/readability (NAMING/STYLE), and performance/resource efficiency (PERF). Fold these lenses into related dimensions or add one \u2014 do not leave a category unowned.\n- For each dimension provide:\n  - \"focus\": precisely what to investigate and why it matters for this PR.\n  - \"hypotheses\": 2 to 4 concrete, testable suspicions about what could be wrong in THIS change (e.g. \"deleteByName builds SQL from the raw name argument\", \"the new expiry check may treat the boundary instant incorrectly\"). Reviewers will verify each one.\n  - \"files\": target files, using the paths that appear in the diff.\n  - \"rules\": the team-rule file paths (from the provided rule index) this dimension is responsible for checking. Every rule plausibly relevant to this change must be assigned to at least one dimension.\n\nOutput JSON only \u2014 no prose, no code fences:\n{\"summary\": \"One or two sentences describing what this PR does, for the report header.\",\n \"dimensions\": [{\"name\": \"Dimension name\", \"focus\": \"...\", \"hypotheses\": [\"...\", \"...\"], \"files\": [\"/src/x.py\"], \"rules\": [\"rules/common/x.md\"]}]}\"\"\"\n\nDEFAULT_REVIEWER_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a senior software engineer performing a focused code review. You are responsible for exactly one review dimension and you have been handed an investigation brief; execute it exhaustively and ignore concerns outside it.\n\nGround rules:\n- Work through every listed hypothesis explicitly. Your \"assessment\" must state the outcome of each hypothesis (confirmed as a finding, or refuted and why). Hypotheses are leads, not limits \u2014 also report any defect within your dimension that no hypothesis anticipated.\n- Review only the changed lines shown in the annotated diff. Base-branch context is provided solely for understanding; do not raise issues about pre-existing code.\n- Report the line number shown in the left-hand annotation of the diff slice (these are true new-file line numbers).\n- Use uppercase category codes: BUG / SECURITY / MISSING-TEST / NAMING / STYLE / PERF.\n- Severity calibration: \"error\" = would cause incorrect behavior, data loss, or a security exposure \u2014 merging should be blocked; \"warning\" = a real defect or risk that should be addressed but need not block the merge; \"info\" = advisory.\n- MISSING-TEST is decided within the diff: if this diff adds or changes behavior (new or modified methods, endpoints, or logic) and no test file is touched in the same diff, report MISSING-TEST (severity: warning). Attach it to the changed file carrying the main new behavior; one finding is enough \u2014 do not repeat it per file. Do not require proof that no tests exist elsewhere. Pure refactors, renames, or formatting-only changes with no behavior change do not warrant it.\n- Category boundaries: NAMING is for identifiers whose name misstates their type, polarity, or content (e.g. a Map named accountList, a double-negative boolean method); STYLE is for formatting and layout only.\n- Be precise and factual. Every finding must be supported by the code shown. If you are not confident a finding is real, omit it \u2014 false positives erode trust in the review.\n- Where practical, include a concrete remediation in \"suggestion\" (one or two sentences; short code is acceptable).\n- Team rules: the rules assigned to this dimension are attached. For each assigned rule, take an explicit position. If the change violates it, raise a finding referencing it and add a \"violation\" entry to rule_checks. If you verified compliance, add a \"pass\" entry with one sentence of evidence (what you checked and why it is satisfied).\n- Team knowledge: a \"Knowledge\" block may be attached, carrying decisions and invariants distilled from earlier pull requests. Each line ends with an id such as `PR12-I1`. If a finding rests on one of those invariants, list that id in \"knowledge_ref\" (a list \u2014 a finding may stand on two). Cite only ids that appear in the attached block; an id that is not there is dropped. Knowledge entries are leads, not law: verify each against the diff before you rely on it.\n- Write all output in clear, professional English.\n\nOutput a single JSON object only. The first character of your reply must be \"{\" and the last must be \"}\". Never output a bare array. When there are no findings, output \"findings\": [] and still provide \"assessment\".\n{\"assessment\": \"Hypothesis-by-hypothesis outcome and overall conclusion\", \"findings\": [{\"rule\": \"BUG\", \"file\": \"/src/x.py\", \"line\": 12, \"severity\": \"error|warning|info\", \"note\": \"The defect and its consequence\", \"suggestion\": \"Concrete fix\", \"rule_ref\": \"\", \"knowledge_ref\": []}], \"rule_checks\": [{\"rule_ref\": \"rules/common/x.md\", \"verdict\": \"pass|violation\", \"evidence\": \"One sentence of evidence\"}]}\"\"\"\n\nDEFAULT_ADVERSARY_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are the adversarial validator of a code-review pipeline. Other reviewers proposed the findings below against the annotated diff. Attack every finding and keep only what survives scrutiny.\n\nChallenge each finding on:\n1. Pre-existence \u2014 is the issue visible only in base context rather than in the added lines? If so, it is out of scope.\n2. Convention \u2014 is this an established project pattern rather than a defect?\n3. Severity inflation \u2014 does the stated severity match the actual consequence?\n4. Substantiation \u2014 does the cited code actually support the claim?\n\nVerdicts: \"confirmed\" only when the finding is clearly real and correctly scoped; \"rejected\" when it fails any challenge above; otherwise \"uncertain\". Be strict \u2014 confirming a false positive is worse than marking it uncertain \u2014 but every \"rejected\" must cite the specific annotated line your reason relies on and name which challenge (1-4) it failed; if you cannot point to a line, use \"uncertain\" instead.\n\nOutput a JSON array only \u2014 no prose. \"id\" must match the input numbering.\n[{\"id\": 1, \"verdict\": \"confirmed|uncertain|rejected\", \"challenge\": 2, \"line\": 15, \"reason\": \"One sentence grounded in the cited line\"}]\"\"\"\n\n\nclass _Dim(BaseModel):\n    name: str\n    focus: str = \"\"\n    hypotheses: list[str] = []\n    files: list[str] = []\n    rules: list[str] = []\n\n\ndef _norm(p: str) -> str:\n    p = (p or \"\").strip().lstrip(\"/\")\n    if p[:2] in (\"a/\", \"b/\"):\n        p = p[2:]\n    return p.lower()\n\n\n# ---------- U1\uff1atargeted rules \u2014\u2014 \u53ea\u7d66\u6bcf\u500b reviewer \u5b83\u8a72\u7ba1\u7684\u898f\u5247 ----------\n\ndef _rules_for_dim(rules: RulesBundle, dim: _Dim) -> str:\n    if not rules.loaded:\n        return \"\"\n    cap = settings().review.reviewer_rules_max_chars\n    picked: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    for want in dim.rules:\n        for rel, body in rules.sections.items():\n            if match_path(rel, want):\n                picked.append((rel, body))\n                break\n    if picked:\n        body = \"\\n\\n\".join(f\"## {rel}\\n{b}\" for rel, b in picked)[:cap]\n        head = (f\"\\n\\n# Assigned Team Rules (version {rules.sha}; this dimension \"\n                \"is responsible for these \u2014 take an explicit pass/violation \"\n                \"position on each in rule_checks; reference the file path in \"\n                \"rule_ref for rule-based findings)\\n\\n\")\n    else:  # planner \u6c92\u6307\u6d3e\uff08\u6216 fallback\uff09\u2192 \u5168\u91cf\uff0c\u884c\u70ba\u540c\u524d\u7248\n        body = rules.text[:cap]\n        head = (f\"\\n\\n# Team Rules (version {rules.sha}; repo-specific overrides \"\n                \"common on conflict; reference the rule file path in rule_ref, \"\n                \"and record pass/violation positions in rule_checks for rules \"\n                \"relevant to your dimension)\\n\\n\")\n    return head + body + (\"\\n(Note: rules truncated at the length limit)\"\n                          if len(body) >= cap else \"\")\n\n\n# ---------- \u968e\u6bb5 2\uff1aplan\uff08U1 \u539a brief\uff09 ----------\n\n@observe(name=\"plan\")\nasync def _plan(ana: Anatomy, meta: dict, rules: RulesBundle,\n                graph_text: str, stats: dict) -> tuple[list[_Dim], str]:\n    max_dims = settings().review.max_dimensions\n    files = [fc.path for fc in ana.files]\n    fallback = [\n        _Dim(name=\"Correctness\",\n             focus=\"Logic errors, boundary conditions, behavior contradicting intent (BUG)\",\n             hypotheses=[\"A changed branch or boundary condition contradicts the stated intent\",\n                         \"A changed expression produces a wrong value on edge inputs\"],\n             files=files),\n        _Dim(name=\"Security\",\n             focus=\"Injection, credential exposure, unsafe defaults (SECURITY)\",\n             hypotheses=[\"Changed code builds a query or command from unvalidated input\",\n                         \"Changed code embeds or weakens a credential or trust setting\"],\n             files=files),\n        _Dim(name=\"Test Coverage\",\n             focus=\"New or changed behavior lacking corresponding tests (MISSING-TEST)\",\n             hypotheses=[\"This diff adds or changes behavior without touching any test file\"],\n             files=files),\n        _Dim(name=\"Readability\",\n             focus=\"Misleading names, inconsistent style (NAMING/STYLE)\",\n             hypotheses=[\"A new identifier misstates its type, polarity, or content\"],\n             files=files),\n    ][:max_dims]\n\n    summary = [f\"{ana.stats['files']} file(s) changed, \"\n               f\"{ana.stats['added_lines']} line(s) added\"]\n    if meta.get(\"title\"):\n        summary.append(f\"PR title: {meta['title']}\")\n    if meta.get(\"description\"):\n        summary.append(f\"Description: {meta['description']}\")\n    summary.append(\"Files: \" + \", \".join(files[:20]))\n    for fc in ana.files[:20]:\n        heads = [t.strip() for _, n, t in\n                 (fc.hunks[0].lines if fc.hunks else []) if n][:3]\n        summary.append(f\"- {fc.path} ({len(fc.added)} added lines), e.g.: \"\n                       + \" / \".join(heads))\n    if rules.files:\n        summary.append(\"Team rule index: \" + \", \".join(rules.files[:30]))\n    if graph_text:\n        summary.append(graph_text[:1500])\n\n    system = prompt_or(PLANNER_PROMPT_NAME,\n                       DEFAULT_PLANNER_PROMPT).replace(\"{max_dims}\", str(max_dims))\n    pr_summary = \"\"\n    try:\n        raw = await complete(system, \"\\n\".join(summary))\n        data = extract_json(raw) or {}\n        pr_summary = str(data.get(\"summary\", \"\")).strip()\n        dims = [_Dim(**d) for d in data.get(\"dimensions\", [])\n                if isinstance(d, dict)]\n        dims = [d for d in dims if d.name.strip()][:max_dims]\n    except Exception:\n        dims = []\n    if len(dims) < 2:\n        stats[\"plan\"] = \"fallback\"\n        return fallback, pr_summary\n    stats[\"plan\"] = \"ok\"\n    return dims, pr_summary\n\n\n# ---------- U2\uff1acoverage gate\uff08\u7d14 code \u7684\u8986\u84cb\u4fdd\u8b49\uff09 ----------\n\ndef _coverage_gate(dims: list[_Dim], ana: Anatomy,\n                   rules: RulesBundle, stats: dict) -> list[_Dim]:\n    \"\"\"\u4fdd\u8b49\uff1a\u6bcf\u500b\u8b8a\u66f4\u6a94\u3001\u6bcf\u689d md \u898f\u5247\uff0c\u81f3\u5c11\u843d\u5728\u4e00\u500b\u9762\u5411\u3002\u5b64\u5152 \u2192 Coverage Sweep\u3002\n    files \u70ba\u7a7a\u7684\u9762\u5411\u8996\u70ba\u6db5\u84cb\u5168\u90e8\u6a94\u6848\uff08planner \u660e\u793a\u7684\u5168 PR \u9762\u5411\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    all_files_dim = any(not d.files for d in dims)\n    orphan_files = [] if all_files_dim else [\n        fc.path for fc in ana.files\n        if not any(match_path(fc.path, w) for d in dims for w in d.files)]\n    all_rules_dim = any(not d.rules for d in dims)   # \u7a7a rules = \u6536\u5168\u91cf\u898f\u5247\n    assigned_rules = {w for d in dims for w in d.rules}\n    orphan_rules = [] if all_rules_dim else [\n        rel for rel in rules.files\n        if not any(match_path(rel, w) for w in assigned_rules)]\n\n    stats[\"coverage\"] = {\n        \"files\": \"full\" if not orphan_files else \"patched\",\n        \"rules\": \"full\" if (not rules.files or not orphan_rules) else \"patched\",\n        \"orphan_files\": orphan_files,\n        \"orphan_rules\": orphan_rules,\n    }\n    if not orphan_files and not orphan_rules:\n        return dims\n\n    sweep = _Dim(\n        name=\"Coverage Sweep\",\n        focus=(\"Deterministic coverage backstop: no planned dimension claimed \"\n               \"the files and/or team rules listed below. Review them with \"\n               \"the same rigor \u2014 nothing merges unexamined.\"),\n        hypotheses=[\"An unclaimed file contains a defect no dimension looked at\",\n                    \"An unassigned team rule is violated by this change\"],\n        files=orphan_files or [fc.path for fc in ana.files],\n        rules=orphan_rules,\n    )\n    return dims + [sweep]   # \u8986\u84cb\u4fdd\u8b49\u512a\u5148\u65bc REVIEW_MAX_DIMENSIONS\uff08\u6700\u591a +1\uff09\n\n\n# ---------- \u968e\u6bb5 3\uff1a\u5e73\u884c reviewer ----------\n\ndef _slices_for(dim: _Dim, ana: Anatomy) -> tuple[str, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de (\u5207\u7247\u6587, \u88ab\u9810\u7b97\u7701\u7565\u7684\u6a94\u6848\u6e05\u55ae)\u3002\u7701\u7565\u5c0d\u6a21\u578b\u6709\u8a3b\u8a18\u3001\u5c0d\u4eba\u985e\u9032 stats\u2014\u2014\n    \u300cnothing merges unexamined\u300d\u7684\u8aa0\u5be6\u7248\u672c\u662f\uff1a\u8d85\u9810\u7b97\u6a94\u6848\u964d\u7d1a\u70ba static-only\u3002\"\"\"\n    wanted = {_norm(f) for f in dim.files}\n    picked = [fc for fc in ana.files\n              if not wanted or any(match_path(fc.path, w) for w in wanted)]\n    if not picked:\n        picked = ana.files\n    budget = settings().review.reviewer_slices_max_chars\n    per_file = settings().review.reviewer_file_slice_max_chars\n    parts, used, skipped = [], 0, []\n    for fc in picked:\n        chunk = numbered_slice(fc, max_chars=per_file)\n        if used + len(chunk) > budget and parts:\n            skipped.append(fc.path)\n            continue\n        parts.append(chunk)\n        used += len(chunk)\n    if skipped:\n        parts.append(f\"({len(skipped)} more changed file(s) omitted \u2014 this \"\n                     f\"dimension's context budget was reached)\")\n    return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts), skipped\n\n\n@observe(name=\"review-dimension\")\nasync def _review_one(dim: _Dim, ana: Anatomy, rules: RulesBundle,\n                      base_text: str, graph_text: str):\n    system = prompt_or(REVIEWER_PROMPT_NAME, DEFAULT_REVIEWER_PROMPT) \\\n        + _rules_for_dim(rules, dim)\n    brief = [f\"# Review dimension: {dim.name}\",\n             f\"Investigative focus: {dim.focus}\"]\n    if dim.hypotheses:\n        brief.append(\"Hypotheses to test (address each in your assessment):\")\n        brief += [f\"  {i}. {h}\" for i, h in enumerate(dim.hypotheses, 1)]\n    slices_text, slices_skipped = _slices_for(dim, ana)\n    user_parts = [\"\\n\".join(brief),\n                  \"# Changes (line numbers annotated)\", slices_text]\n    if base_text:\n        user_parts += [\"# Base-branch context (for understanding only \u2014 \"\n                       \"do not comment on it)\", base_text]\n    if graph_text:\n        user_parts.append(graph_text)\n    raw = await complete(system, \"\\n\\n\".join(user_parts))\n    data = extract_json(raw)\n    assessment = \"\"\n    rule_checks: list[dict] = []\n    if isinstance(data, dict):                 # \u65b0\u683c\u5f0f\n        assessment = str(data.get(\"assessment\", \"\")).strip()\n        items = data.get(\"findings\", [])\n        rule_checks = [c for c in data.get(\"rule_checks\", [])\n                       if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get(\"rule_ref\")\n                       and c.get(\"verdict\") in (\"pass\", \"violation\")]\n    elif isinstance(data, list):               # \u820a\u683c\u5f0f\uff08\u88f8\u9663\u5217\uff09\u76f8\u5bb9\n        items = data\n    else:\n        return \"(unparseable reviewer output)\", [], [], \\\n            {\"location_dropped\": 0, \"location_flagged\": 0,\n             \"slices_skipped\": slices_skipped}\n    base_conf = settings().review.llm_base_conf\n    out: list[Finding] = []\n    loc = {\"location_dropped\": 0, \"location_flagged\": 0,\n           \"slices_skipped\": slices_skipped}\n    for f in items:\n        if not isinstance(f, dict):\n            continue\n        kr = f.get(\"knowledge_ref\")                   # \u578b\u5225\u6536\u6582\u5728\u5efa\u6a21\u524d\u505a\uff1a\n        if isinstance(kr, str):                       # \u5f15\u7528\u683c\u5f0f\u5beb\u6b6a\u4e0d\u8a72\u8b93\u6574\u689d\n            f[\"knowledge_ref\"] = [kr] if kr else []    # finding \u88ab pydantic \u4e1f\u6389\n        elif isinstance(kr, list):\n            f[\"knowledge_ref\"] = [str(x).strip() for x in kr if str(x).strip()]\n        elif kr is not None:\n            f.pop(\"knowledge_ref\", None)\n        try:\n            fin = Finding(**f)\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n        fin.source = \"llm\"\n        fin.dimension = dim.name\n        fin.confidence = base_conf\n        fin.rule = (fin.rule or \"BUG\").strip().upper()\n        if not any(match_path(fc.path, fin.file) for fc in ana.files):\n            loc[\"location_dropped\"] += 1        # \u5e7b\u89ba\u6a94\u6848\uff1a\u660e\u78ba drop\uff0c\u4e0d\u9032\u5831\u544a\n            continue\n        if not line_near(ana, fin.file, fin.line):\n            fin.confidence = round(fin.confidence * 0.8, 3)   # 0.7\u21920.56\uff1a\u904e\u7dda\u3001\u5e36\u6a19\u8a18\n            fin.note = \"[unverified location: line not in added set] \" + fin.note\n            loc[\"location_flagged\"] += 1\n        if fin.note:\n            out.append(fin)\n    return assessment, out, rule_checks, loc\n\n\nasync def _review_all(dims: list[_Dim], ana: Anatomy, rules: RulesBundle,\n                      base_text: str, graph_text: str,\n                      stats: dict) -> list[Finding]:\n    sem = asyncio.Semaphore(settings().review.max_parallel)\n\n    async def one(d: _Dim):\n        async with sem:\n            try:\n                assessment, out, checks, loc = await _review_one(\n                    d, ana, rules, base_text, graph_text)\n                for k, v in loc.items():\n                    if k == \"slices_skipped\":\n                        merged = set(stats.get(\"context_omitted\") or []) | set(v)\n                        stats[\"context_omitted\"] = sorted(merged)   # JSON \u53cb\u5584\n                    else:\n                        stats[k] = stats.get(k, 0) + v\n                await note(f\"Reviewing [{d.name}] \u2014 done, {len(out)} finding(s)\")\n                return out, {\"name\": d.name, \"assessment\": assessment,\n                             \"count\": len(out)}, checks\n            except Exception:\n                stats.setdefault(\"reviewer_errors\", 0)\n                stats[\"reviewer_errors\"] += 1\n                await note(f\"Reviewing [{d.name}] \u2014 failed, skipped\")\n                return [], {\"name\": d.name, \"assessment\": \"Failed to execute\",\n                            \"count\": 0}, []\n\n    results = await asyncio.gather(*(one(d) for d in dims))\n    stats[\"assessments\"] = [a for _, a, _ in results]     # \u4f9d dims \u539f\u9806\u5e8f\n    checks: dict[str, dict] = {}                          # violation \u84cb\u904e pass\n    for _, _, cs in results:\n        for c in cs:\n            ref = str(c[\"rule_ref\"]).strip()\n            if ref not in checks or c[\"verdict\"] == \"violation\":\n                checks[ref] = {\"verdict\": c[\"verdict\"],\n                               \"evidence\": str(c.get(\"evidence\", \"\"))}\n    stats[\"llm_rule_checks\"] = checks\n    return [f for fs, _, _ in results for f in fs]\n\n\n# ---------- \u968e\u6bb5 4\uff1aadversary\uff08U3 \u5206\u584a + \u884c\u865f\u8b49\u64da + \u53ef\u63db\u8166\uff09 ----------\n\n@observe(name=\"adversary\")\nasync def _adversary(llm_findings: list[Finding], ana: Anatomy,\n                     base_text: str, rules: RulesBundle, stats: dict) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\u5c31\u5730\u8abf\u6574 llm findings \u7684 confidence\u3002static\uff08\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\uff09\u4e0d\u9001\u5be9\u3001\u4e0d\u52d5\u3002\"\"\"\n    if not settings().review.adversary:\n        stats[\"adversary\"] = \"off\"\n        return\n    if not llm_findings:\n        stats[\"adversary\"] = \"n/a\"\n        return\n    fallback_diff = \"\\n\\n\".join(numbered_slice(fc, max_chars=3000)\n                                for fc in ana.files)[:12000]\n    base_block = (\"\\n\\n# Base-branch context\\n\" + base_text[:4000]) if base_text else \"\"\n\n    def _context_for(batch: list[Finding]) -> str:\n        # \u6aa2\u5bdf\u5b98\u81f3\u5c11\u8981\u770b\u5f97\u5230\u88ab\u6311\u6230\u767c\u73fe\u6240\u5728\u7684\u6a94 \u2014\u2014 \u5927 PR \u4e0d\u80fd\u9760\u5168\u57df\u622a\u65b7\u78b0\u904b\u6c23\n        picked, seen = [], set()\n        for f in batch:\n            for fc in ana.files:\n                if fc.path not in seen and match_path(fc.path, f.file):\n                    seen.add(fc.path)\n                    picked.append(numbered_slice(fc, max_chars=3000))\n        text = \"\\n\\n\".join(picked)[:15000]\n        rule_refs = sorted({f.rule_ref for f in batch if f.rule_ref})\n        excerpts = []\n        for ref in rule_refs:\n            for rel, body in rules.sections.items():\n                if (rel == ref or ref.endswith(\"/\" + rel)\n                        or rel.endswith(\"/\" + ref)):\n                    excerpts.append(f\"## {rel}\\n{body[:1500]}\")\n                    break\n        if excerpts:\n            text += (\"\\n\\n# Referenced team rules (verbatim \u2014 a finding that \"\n                     \"cites one of these is grounded in the rule itself; do not \"\n                     \"reject it as 'project convention' without reading it)\\n\"\n                     + \"\\n\\n\".join(excerpts)[:4500])\n        return text or fallback_diff\n    system = prompt_or(ADVERSARY_PROMPT_NAME, DEFAULT_ADVERSARY_PROMPT)\n    model = settings().llm.model_adversary\n    chunk = settings().review.adversary_chunk\n    chunks = [llm_findings[i:i + chunk]\n              for i in range(0, len(llm_findings), chunk)]\n\n    async def judge(batch: list[Finding]) -> list[dict] | None:\n        listing = \"\\n\".join(\n            f'{i + 1}. [{f.rule}] {f.file}:{f.line} ({f.severity}) {f.note}'\n            for i, f in enumerate(batch))\n        user = (\"# Diff (line numbers annotated)\\n\" + _context_for(batch)\n                + base_block + \"\\n\\n# Findings under challenge\\n\" + listing)\n        try:\n            raw = await complete(system, user, model=model)\n            data = extract_json(raw)\n            assert isinstance(data, list)\n        except Exception:\n            return None\n        slots: list[dict] = [{} for _ in batch]\n        for v in data:\n            if not isinstance(v, dict):\n                continue\n            try:\n                idx = int(v.get(\"id\")) - 1\n            except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                continue\n            if 0 <= idx < len(batch):\n                slots[idx] = v\n        return slots\n\n    sem = asyncio.Semaphore(settings().review.max_parallel)\n\n    async def _bounded(b):\n        async with sem:                      # \u6aa2\u5bdf\u5b98\u540c\u6a23\u53d7\u4f75\u767c\u4e0a\u9650\u7ba1\n            return await judge(b)\n\n    results = await asyncio.gather(*(_bounded(b) for b in chunks))\n    confirmed = rejected = degraded = demoted = 0\n    for batch, slots in zip(chunks, results):\n        if slots is None:\n            degraded += 1\n            continue                       # \u8a72\u584a\u5168\u7dad\u6301 uncertain\uff08\u4e2d\u7acb\uff09\n        for f, v in zip(batch, slots):\n            verdict = str(v.get(\"verdict\", \"uncertain\")).lower()\n            if verdict == \"confirmed\":\n                f.confidence = min(0.95, f.confidence * 1.25)\n                confirmed += 1\n            elif verdict == \"rejected\":\n                # \u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u57f7\u6cd5\uff1aprompt \u8aaa\u300c\u5fc5\u5f15\u884c\u865f+\u6311\u6230\u7de8\u865f\u300d\uff0c\u9019\u88e1\u9a57\u771f\u3002\n                # \u5f15\u4e0d\u51fa\u5408\u6cd5\u884c\u865f\u7684 reject \u4e0d\u914d \u00d70.35 \u2014\u2014 \u964d\u70ba uncertain\u3002\n                ch = str(v.get(\"challenge\", \"\")).strip()\n                line_ok = (line_in_view(ana, f.file, v.get(\"line\"))\n                           if ch == \"1\" else\n                           line_near(ana, f.file, v.get(\"line\")))\n                if ch in {\"1\", \"2\", \"3\", \"4\"} and line_ok:\n                    f.confidence = round(f.confidence * 0.35, 3)\n                    rejected += 1\n                else:\n                    demoted += 1\n    stats[\"adversary\"] = (f\"ok({confirmed} confirmed / {rejected} rejected\"\n                          f\" / {len(llm_findings)}; {len(chunks)} chunk(s)\"\n                          + (f\", {demoted} unproven-reject demoted\" if demoted else \"\")\n                          + (f\", {degraded} degraded\" if degraded else \"\")\n                          + (f\", model={model}\" if model else \"\") + \")\")\n\n\n# ---------- \u968e\u6bb5 5\uff1asynthesis\uff08\u7d14 code\uff09 ----------\n\ndef _dedupe(findings: list[Finding]) -> list[Finding]:\n    kept: list[Finding] = []\n    for f in sorted(findings, key=lambda x: -x.confidence):\n        dup = None\n        for k in kept:\n            if k.rule != f.rule:\n                continue\n            if k.rule == \"MISSING-TEST\":       # \u5168\u57df\u4e00\u689d\u5c31\u5920\uff08\u639b\u54ea\u500b\u6a94\u4e0d\u91cd\u8981\uff09\n                dup = k\n                break\n            if _norm(k.file) != _norm(f.file):\n                continue\n            if k.line is None or f.line is None:\n                if k.line == f.line:\n                    dup = k\n                    break\n            elif abs(k.line - f.line) <= 3:\n                dup = k\n                break\n        if dup is None:\n            kept.append(f)\n            continue\n        if f.knowledge_ref and not dup.knowledge_ref:\n            dup.knowledge_ref = f.knowledge_ref   # \u53bb\u91cd\u4e0d\u8a72\u5403\u6389\u5f15\u7528\uff08\u5f15\u7528\u7387\u5206\u5b50\uff09\n        if {dup.source, f.source} == {\"static\", \"llm\"}:\n            dup.confidence = 1.0\n            dup.note = dup.note + \" (corroborated: static + LLM)\"\n            dup.rule_ref = dup.rule_ref or f.rule_ref\n    return kept\n\n\ndef _verify_knowledge_refs(findings: list[Finding], stats: dict) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\u5f15\u7528\u7387\u7684\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u57f7\u6cd5\uff1aknowledge_ref \u2286 \u672c\u6b21\u6ce8\u5165\u5340\u584a\u88e1\u771f\u7684\u51fa\u73fe\u904e\u7684 id\u3002\n\n    \u4e0d\u5728\u540d\u55ae\u7684\u525d\u6389\uff08\u4e0d\u6263\u5206\u2014\u2014\u5f15\u932f\u4e0d\u4ee3\u8868 finding \u662f\u932f\u7684\uff0c\u53ea\u4ee3\u8868\u9019\u689d\u5f15\u7528\u4e0d\u7b97\u6578\uff09\u3002\n    \u5e7b\u89ba id \u82e5\u7559\u5728\u5831\u544a\u88e1\uff0c\u65e5\u5f8c\u6c92\u6709\u4eba\u80fd\u8ffd\u56de\u5b83\u6307\u7684\u662f\u4ec0\u9ebc\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    known = {str(i).upper() for i in (stats.get(\"knowledge_ids\") or [])}\n    stats[\"knowledge_ids_injected\"] = len(known)\n    stripped = 0\n    for f in findings:\n        if not f.knowledge_ref:\n            continue\n        keep, seen = [], set()\n        for ref in f.knowledge_ref:\n            r = str(ref).strip().upper()\n            if r in known and r not in seen:\n                seen.add(r)\n                keep.append(r)\n            else:\n                stripped += 1\n        f.knowledge_ref = keep\n    if stripped:\n        stats[\"knowledge_refs_stripped\"] = stripped\n\n\n@observe(name=\"synthesis\")\ndef _synthesize(findings: list[Finding], stats: dict) -> list[Finding]:\n    merged = _dedupe(findings)\n    _verify_knowledge_refs(merged, stats)\n    threshold = settings().review.min_confidence\n    passed = [f for f in merged if f.confidence >= threshold]\n    stats[\"dropped_low_conf\"] = len(merged) - len(passed)\n    cap = settings().review.max_findings\n    passed.sort(key=sort_key)\n    stats[\"dropped_over_cap\"] = max(0, len(passed) - cap)\n    final = passed[:cap]\n    # \u5f15\u7528\u7387\u7684\u5206\u5b50\uff1a\u6700\u7d42\u7559\u5728\u5831\u544a\u88e1\u3001\u4e14\u5f15\u7528\u6709\u6548\u7684\u689d\u6578\uff08\u7dda\u4e0a\u91cf\u5c3a\u7684\u4e0a\u754c\u2014\u2014\n    # \u5b83\u53ea\u8b49\u660e reviewer \u8b80\u5230\u4e86\u77e5\u8b58\uff0c\u4e0d\u8b49\u660e finding \u56e0\u5b83\u800c\u4f86\uff1b\u4e0b\u754c\u5728 eval \u7684\n    # knowledge_delta\uff09\n    stats[\"knowledge_grounded\"] = sum(1 for f in final if f.knowledge_ref)\n    return final\n\n\ndef _rule_audit(rules: RulesBundle, findings: list[Finding],\n                stats: dict) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"\u898f\u5247\u7a3d\u6838\u8868\uff1a\u6bcf\u689d\u8f09\u5165\u7684\u5718\u968a\u898f\u5247\u4e00\u5217 \u2014\u2014 \u9055\u53cd/\u901a\u904e/\u672a\u6aa2\u6838\u3002\n    \u8b49\u64da\u512a\u5148\u5e8f\uff1a\u6700\u7d42\u767c\u73fe\u7684\u9055\u53cd > semgrep \u6a5f\u68b0\u6383\u63cf(0 \u547d\u4e2d=\u901a\u904e) > LLM \u7684 pass \u8868\u614b\u3002\"\"\"\n    def norm(x: str) -> str:\n        return (x or \"\").strip().lstrip(\"/\").lower()\n\n    violated: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for f in findings:\n        if f.rule_ref:\n            violated.setdefault(norm(f.rule_ref),\n                                f\"See finding: {f.file}:{f.line} {f.note}\")\n    llm = {norm(k): v for k, v in (stats.get(\"llm_rule_checks\") or {}).items()}\n    rows: list[dict] = []\n    for ref in list(stats.get(\"static_rule_refs\") or []) + list(rules.files):\n        key = norm(ref)\n        if any(r[\"ref\"] == ref for r in rows):\n            continue\n        if key in violated:\n            rows.append({\"ref\": ref, \"verdict\": \"violation\",\n                         \"evidence\": violated[key]})\n        elif ref in (stats.get(\"static_rule_refs\") or []):\n            rows.append({\"ref\": ref, \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n                         \"evidence\": \"Static analysis (semgrep): 0 matches\"})\n        elif key in llm and llm[key][\"verdict\"] == \"pass\":\n            rows.append({\"ref\": ref, \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n                         \"evidence\": llm[key][\"evidence\"]\n                         or \"Verified by review dimension\"})\n        else:\n            rows.append({\"ref\": ref, \"verdict\": \"unchecked\", \"evidence\": \"\"})\n    return rows\n\n\n# ---------- \u5165\u53e3 ----------\n\nasync def run_pipeline(diff: str, meta: dict,\n                       rules: RulesBundle) -> ReviewResult:\n    stats: dict = {\"pipeline\": \"v2\", \"rules_sha\": rules.sha or None}\n\n    ana = parse_diff(diff)\n    stats.update(ana.stats)\n    stats[\"skipped_notes\"] = ana.skipped_notes\n    await note(f\"Parsing diff \u2014 {ana.stats['files']} file(s), \"\n               f\"{ana.stats['added_lines']} added line(s)\"\n               + (f\", {len(ana.skipped_notes)} skipped\"\n                  if ana.skipped_notes else \"\"))\n\n    static_finds, static_notes, static_refs = run_static(ana)\n    stats[\"static_rule_refs\"] = static_refs\n    stats[\"static_findings\"] = len(static_finds)\n    if static_notes:\n        stats[\"static_notes\"] = static_notes\n    await note(f\"Static analysis \u2014 {len(static_finds)} finding(s)\"\n               + (f\"; {static_notes[0]}\"\n                  if static_notes and not static_finds else \"\"))\n\n    base_text, base_stats = ctx.base_context(meta.get(\"repo\"), ana)\n    graph_text, graph_stats = await ctx.graph_context(meta.get(\"repo\"), ana)\n    know_text, know_stats = knowledge.load_for(\n        meta.get(\"repo\"), [fc.path for fc in ana.files])\n    stats.update(base_stats)\n    stats.update(graph_stats)\n    stats.update(know_stats)\n    if know_text:\n        graph_text = (graph_text + \"\\n\\n\" + know_text) if graph_text else know_text\n    await note(\"Context prefetch \u2014 base: \"\n               + (f\"{base_stats['base_files']} file(s)\"\n                  if base_stats.get(\"base_available\")\n                  else \"unavailable (no local clone)\")\n               + (\"; code graph: attached\"\n                  if graph_stats.get(\"graph_used\") else \"\")\n               + (f\"; knowledge: {know_stats['knowledge_entries']} entr\"\n                  + (\"y\" if know_stats[\"knowledge_entries\"] == 1 else \"ies\")\n                  if know_stats.get(\"knowledge_entries\") else \"\"))\n\n    dims, pr_summary = await _plan(ana, meta, rules, graph_text, stats)\n    dims = _coverage_gate(dims, ana, rules, stats)\n    stats[\"pr_summary\"] = pr_summary or (meta.get(\"title\") or \"\")\n    stats[\"file_table\"] = [\n        {\"path\": fc.path, \"added\": len(fc.added), \"hunks\": len(fc.hunks)}\n        for fc in ana.files]\n    stats[\"dimensions\"] = len(dims)\n    stats[\"dimension_names\"] = [d.name for d in dims]\n    cov = stats[\"coverage\"]\n    await note((\"Planning\" if stats.get(\"plan\") == \"ok\"\n                else \"Planning (degraded to fixed dimensions)\")\n               + f\" \u2014 {len(dims)} dimensions: \"\n               + \", \".join(d.name for d in dims))\n    await note(f\"Coverage gate \u2014 files: {cov['files']}; rules: {cov['rules']}\"\n               + (\" (+Coverage Sweep dimension)\"\n                  if cov[\"files\"] == \"patched\" or cov[\"rules\"] == \"patched\"\n                  else \"\"))\n\n    llm_finds = await _review_all(dims, ana, rules, base_text, graph_text, stats)\n    stats[\"llm_findings\"] = len(llm_finds)\n\n    await _adversary(llm_finds, ana, base_text, rules, stats)\n    await note(f\"Adversarial validation \u2014 {stats.get('adversary', 'n/a')}\")\n\n    final = _synthesize(static_finds + llm_finds, stats)\n    stats[\"final_findings\"] = len(final)\n    stats[\"rule_audit\"] = _rule_audit(rules, final, stats)\n    await note(f\"Synthesis \u2014 {len(final)} finding(s) retained\"\n               + (f\", {stats['dropped_low_conf']} filtered below confidence\"\n                  \" threshold\" if stats.get(\"dropped_low_conf\") else \"\"))\n\n    return ReviewResult(markdown=render_markdown(final, stats),\n                        findings=final, stats=stats)\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/progress.py","perm":"0644","sha":"34433e0c3524773f122ee02b80d4c077ebe9c14a079a0a75dff198cfe45fa89b","data":"\"\"\"\u4e32\u6d41\u65c1\u767d\u532f\u6d41\u6392\uff1apipeline \u5404\u7ad9\u5f80\u9019\u88e1\u4e1f\u4e00\u53e5\u8a71\uff0capp \u5c64\u6c7a\u5b9a\u64ad\u4e0d\u64ad\u3002\n\n\u7528 contextvars \u800c\u4e0d\u662f\u628a callback \u4e00\u8def\u50b3\u53c3\u2014\u2014run_review \u7684\u7c3d\u540d\uff08eval \u6ce8\u5165\u53e3\uff09\n\u4e00\u500b\u5b57\u90fd\u4e0d\u52d5\uff1b\u6c92\u4eba\u8a02\u95b1\u6642\uff08eval\uff0fCLI\uff0f\u975e\u4e32\u6d41 /review\uff09note() \u662f\u7121\u8072 no-op\uff0c\n\u800c\u4e14\u65c1\u767d\u4efb\u4f55\u5931\u6557\u90fd\u88ab\u541e\u6389\uff0c\u6c38\u4e0d\u5f71\u97ff\u4e3b\u6d41\u7a0b\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport contextvars\nfrom typing import Awaitable, Callable, Optional\n\nStatusCb = Optional[Callable[[str], Awaitable[None]]]\n\n_cb: contextvars.ContextVar[StatusCb] = contextvars.ContextVar(\n    \"review_status_cb\", default=None)\n\n\ndef set_status_cb(cb: StatusCb):\n    \"\"\"\u8a02\u95b1\u65c1\u767d\uff08app \u7684 SSE \u76f4\u64ad\u7528\uff09\u3002\u56de\u50b3 token \u7d66 reset \u7528\u3002\"\"\"\n    return _cb.set(cb)\n\n\ndef reset_status_cb(token) -> None:\n    _cb.reset(token)\n\n\nasync def note(msg: str) -> None:\n    cb = _cb.get()\n    if cb is None:\n        return\n    try:\n        await cb(msg)\n    except Exception:\n        pass  # \u65c1\u767d\u6c38\u4e0d\u5e72\u64fe\u4e3b\u6d41\u7a0b\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/render.py","perm":"0644","sha":"48081e3e51b6aa214885432b41234bdba128b7eb8bb1b8475b850d6960b885ca","data":"\"\"\"render\uff08v2 \u7b2c 6 \u6bb5\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u5c08\u696d\u82f1\u6587\u6a19\u6e96\u5831\u544a v3\uff0cmarkdown \u7531 code \u7522\u3001\u683c\u5f0f\u6046\u5b9a\u3002\n\nv3 \u5347\u7d1a\uff1afinding \u7de8\u865f\uff08F1..Fn\uff09\u5168\u5831\u544a\u4ea4\u53c9\u5f15\u7528\uff1bAt-a-glance \u7d71\u8a08\u884c +\nRequired actions\uff08blocking \u7684\u884c\u52d5\u6e05\u55ae\uff09\uff1bReview Dimensions \u6539\u8868\u683c\n\uff08Dimension / Verdict / Findings / Assessment\uff0c\u542b Static analysis \u5408\u6210\u5217\uff09\uff1b\nRule Compliance \u7684\u9055\u53cd\u4f9d\u64da\u76f4\u63a5\u5f15 F \u7de8\u865f\uff1bReview Coverage \u6539\u6210\u8868\u683c\u3002\n\u4e0d\u8b8a\u7684\u5e95\u7dda\uff1a\u96f6\u767c\u73fe\u7167\u6a23\u5b8c\u6574\u3001\u7121\u8b8a\u66f4\u53ef\u89e3\u6790\u660e\u8b1b\u4e0d\u4ee3\u8868\u901a\u904e\u3001\u5168\u7a0b\u7121 emoji\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom orchestrator.models import Finding\n\n_ORDER = {\"error\": 0, \"warning\": 1, \"info\": 2}\n_SEV_HDR = [(\"error\", \"Blocking \u2014 must fix\"),\n            (\"warning\", \"Non-blocking \u2014 should fix\"),\n            (\"info\", \"Informational\")]\n_SRC = {\"static\": \"static\", \"graph\": \"graph\"}\n_VERDICT_MARK = {\"pass\": \"Pass\", \"violation\": \"Violation\",\n                 \"unchecked\": \"Not assessed\"}\n\n\ndef sort_key(f: Finding) -> tuple:\n    return (_ORDER.get(f.severity, 2), -f.confidence)\n\n\ndef _norm(p: str) -> str:\n    return (p or \"\").strip().lstrip(\"/\").lower()\n\n\ndef _cell(text: str, limit: int | None = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u8868\u683c\u5132\u5b58\u683c\uff1a\u62d4\u6389\u6703\u62c6\u8868\u7684\u5b57\u5143\uff08\u88f8 | \u8207\u63db\u884c\u6703\u62c6\u6389 markdown \u8868\u683c\uff09\u3002\n\n    limit \u9810\u8a2d None\uff1d\u4e0d\u622a\u65b7\u2014\u2014\u8868\u683c\u5bec\u5ea6\u7531\u6e32\u67d3\u7aef\u81ea\u52d5\u63db\u884c\u8655\u7406\uff0c\u4e0d\u8a72\u5728\u9019\u88e1\u780d\u5167\u5bb9\u3002\n    \u53ea\u6709\u300c\u672c\u4f86\u5c31\u8a72\u77ed\u300d\u7684\u6b04\u4f4d\uff08\u4f8b\u5982\u79d1\u540d\uff09\u624d\u660e\u78ba\u50b3 limit\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    s = (text or \"\").replace(\"|\", \"/\").replace(\"\\n\", \" \").strip()\n    return s[:limit] if limit else s\n\n\ndef _partial(stats: dict) -> bool:\n    return bool(stats.get(\"context_omitted\") or stats.get(\"skipped_notes\"))\n\n\ndef _verdict(findings: list[Finding], stats: dict | None = None) -> str:\n    st = stats or {}\n    if not findings and st.get(\"reviewer_errors\") \\\n            and not st.get(\"static_findings\"):\n        n = st.get(\"reviewer_errors\")\n        return (f\"**REVIEW INCOMPLETE** \u2014 {n} reviewer pass(es) failed and \"\n                \"static analysis reported nothing; this is NOT an approval. \"\n                \"Re-run the review.\")\n    if any(f.severity == \"error\" for f in findings):\n        return (\"**REQUIRES CHANGES** \u2014 blocking issues must be resolved \"\n                \"before merge\")\n    if any(f.severity == \"warning\" for f in findings):\n        return \"**APPROVED WITH SUGGESTIONS** \u2014 non-blocking issues noted below\"\n    return \"**APPROVED** \u2014 no issues requiring action were identified\"\n\n\ndef _counts_line(findings: list[Finding]) -> str:\n    n = {\"error\": 0, \"warning\": 0, \"info\": 0}\n    for f in findings:\n        n[f.severity] = n.get(f.severity, 0) + 1\n    return (f\"Blocking {n['error']} \u00b7 Non-blocking {n['warning']} \u00b7 \"\n            f\"Informational {n['info']}\")\n\n\ndef _required_actions(ordered: list[Finding], ids: dict[int, str]) -> list[str]:\n    blocking = [f for f in ordered if f.severity == \"error\"]\n    if not blocking:\n        return []\n    out = [\"**Required actions before merge**:\", \"\"]\n    for i, f in enumerate(blocking, 1):\n        loc = f\"`{f.file}:{f.line}`\" if f.line else f\"`{f.file}`\"\n        action = f.suggestion or f.note\n        out.append(f\"{i}. {ids[id(f)]} {loc} \u2014 {_cell(action)}\")\n    out.append(\"\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _file_table(stats: dict) -> list[str]:\n    table = stats.get(\"file_table\") or []\n    if not table:\n        return []\n    out = [\"### Changed Files\", \"\",\n           \"| File | Lines added | Hunks |\", \"|---|---:|---:|\"]\n    for row in table[:15]:\n        out.append(f\"| `{row['path']}` | {row['added']} | {row['hunks']} |\")\n    if len(table) > 15:\n        out.append(f\"| \u2026 {len(table) - 15} more file(s) | | |\")\n    for n in (stats.get(\"skipped_notes\") or [])[:4]:\n        out.append(f\"\\n> Not reviewed: {n}\")\n    out.append(\"\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _graph_section(stats: dict) -> list[str]:\n    if not stats.get(\"graph_summary\"):\n        return []\n    out = [\"### Impact Analysis (Code Graph)\", \"\"]\n    out += [f\"> {ln}\" for ln in stats[\"graph_summary\"].strip().splitlines()[:4]]\n    impacted = stats.get(\"graph_impacted\") or []\n    if impacted:\n        out += [\"\", \"Affected outside this diff:\"]\n        out += [f\"- `{name}`\" for name in impacted]\n    else:\n        out += [\"\", \"**No cross-file impact detected** \u2014 the dependency graph \"\n                \"shows no other callers or files affected by these changes.\"]\n    out.append(\"\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _findings_section(ordered: list[Finding], ids: dict[int, str]) -> list[str]:\n    out = [f\"### Findings ({len(ordered)})\", \"\"]\n    for sev, hdr in _SEV_HDR:\n        group = [f for f in ordered if f.severity == sev]\n        if not group:\n            continue\n        out.append(f\"#### {hdr} ({len(group)})\")\n        for f in group:\n            loc = f\"`{f.file}:{f.line}`\" if f.line else f\"`{f.file}`\"\n            tag = f\" `[{_SRC[f.source]}]`\" if f.source in _SRC else \"\"\n            ref = f\" (per {f.rule_ref})\" if f.rule_ref else \"\"\n            # \u77e5\u8b58\u5f15\u7528\u6bd4\u7167 rule_ref\uff1a\u8b80\u8005\u770b\u5f97\u5230\u9019\u689d\u767c\u73fe\u7ad9\u5728\u54ea\u4e00\u689d\u65e2\u6709\u6c7a\u7b56\u4e0a\n            if f.knowledge_ref:\n                ref += \" (knowledge: \" + \", \".join(f.knowledge_ref) + \")\"\n            note = \" \".join(f.note.split())          # \u63db\u884c/\u63a7\u5236\u5b57\u5143\u6536\u6582\n            out.append(f\"- **{ids[id(f)]} \u00b7 {f.rule}** {loc}{tag} \u2014 \"\n                       f\"{note}{ref}\")\n            if f.suggestion:\n                out.append(f\"  Recommendation: {f.suggestion}\")\n        out.append(\"\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _dimension_table(stats: dict, ordered: list[Finding],\n                     ids: dict[int, str]) -> list[str]:\n    rows = stats.get(\"assessments\") or []\n    if not rows and not stats.get(\"static_findings\"):\n        return []\n    out = [\"### Review Dimensions\", \"\",\n           \"| Dimension | Verdict | Findings | Assessment |\",\n           \"|---|---|---|---|\"]\n    static_ids = [ids[id(f)] for f in ordered if f.source == \"static\"]\n    if stats.get(\"static_findings\") is not None:\n        verdict = \"Issues found\" if static_ids else \"Clear\"\n        out.append(\"| Static analysis (deterministic) | \" + verdict + \" | \"\n                   + (\", \".join(static_ids) or \"\u2014\")\n                   + \" | semgrep / ruff / heuristic checks; findings carry \"\n                     \"confidence 1.0 |\")\n    for a in rows:\n        fids = [ids[id(f)] for f in ordered\n                if f.source == \"llm\" and f.dimension == a[\"name\"]]\n        if a.get(\"assessment\") == \"Failed to execute\":\n            verdict = \"Failed\"\n        elif fids or a.get(\"count\"):\n            verdict = \"Issues found\"\n        else:\n            verdict = \"Clear\"\n        assessment = _cell(a.get(\"assessment\") or \"(no assessment provided)\")\n        out.append(f\"| {_cell(a['name'], 80)} | {verdict} | \"\n                   f\"{', '.join(fids) or '\u2014'} | {assessment} |\")\n    out.append(\"\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _rule_audit_section(stats: dict, ordered: list[Finding],\n                        ids: dict[int, str]) -> list[str]:\n    rows = stats.get(\"rule_audit\") or []\n    if not rows:\n        return []\n    sha = stats.get(\"rules_sha\") or \"?\"\n    out = [f\"### Rule Compliance (rules {sha})\", \"\",\n           \"| Rule | Status | Basis |\", \"|---|---|---|\"]\n    shown = [r for r in rows if r[\"verdict\"] != \"unchecked\"][:14]\n    for r in shown:\n        basis = r[\"evidence\"] or \"\u2014\"\n        if r[\"verdict\"] == \"violation\":\n            hit = next((f for f in ordered\n                        if _norm(f.rule_ref) == _norm(r[\"ref\"])), None)\n            if hit is not None:\n                basis = f\"{ids[id(hit)]} \u2014 {basis}\"\n        out.append(f\"| `{r['ref']}` | {_VERDICT_MARK[r['verdict']]} \"\n                   f\"| {_cell(basis)} |\")\n    unchecked = sum(1 for r in rows if r[\"verdict\"] == \"unchecked\")\n    if unchecked:\n        out.append(f\"| \u2026 {unchecked} more | Not assessed | Out of scope for \"\n                   \"this change or not covered by a dimension |\")\n    out.append(\"\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _coverage_table(stats: dict) -> list[str]:\n    rows: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    if stats.get(\"files\"):\n        rows.append((\"Scope\", f\"{stats['files']} file(s), \"\n                              f\"{stats.get('added_lines', 0)} added line(s)\"))\n    static = f\"{stats.get('static_findings', 0)} match(es)\"\n    if stats.get(\"static_findings\", 0) == 0 and stats.get(\"static_notes\"):\n        static += \" \u2014 \" + \"; \".join(stats[\"static_notes\"][:2])\n    rows.append((\"Static analysis\", static))\n    if stats.get(\"base_available\"):\n        rows.append((\"Base context\", f\"{stats.get('base_files', 0)} file(s)\"))\n    rows.append((\"Code graph\", \"enabled\" if stats.get(\"graph_used\")\n                 else \"not attached\"))\n    if stats.get(\"knowledge_entries\"):\n        detail = (f\"{stats['knowledge_entries']} entr\"\n                  + (\"y\" if stats[\"knowledge_entries\"] == 1 else \"ies\")\n                  + \" matched\")\n        if stats.get(\"knowledge_invariants_only\") or stats.get(\"knowledge_omitted\"):\n            # \u964d\u7d1a\u53ef\u898b\uff1a\u88ab\u7e2e\u6210 invariants-only \u6216\u6574\u689d\u6c92\u9032\u53bb\u7684\uff0c\u6524\u5728\u5831\u544a\u4e0a\n            detail += (f\" ({stats.get('knowledge_full', 0)} full, \"\n                       f\"{stats.get('knowledge_invariants_only', 0)} invariants \"\n                       f\"only, {stats.get('knowledge_omitted', 0)} omitted \"\n                       \"\u2014 context budget)\")\n        if stats.get(\"knowledge_grounded\"):\n            detail += (f\"; {stats['knowledge_grounded']} finding(s) cite a \"\n                       \"ledger entry\")\n        rows.append((\"Knowledge context\", detail))\n    omitted = stats.get(\"context_omitted\") or []\n    if omitted:\n        rows.append((\"Context budget\",\n                     f\"{len(omitted)} file(s) exceeded reviewer context \u2014 \"\n                     \"covered by static analysis only\"))\n    if stats.get(\"adversary\"):\n        rows.append((\"Adversarial validation\", stats[\"adversary\"]))\n    cov = stats.get(\"coverage\") or {}\n    if cov:\n        rows.append((\"Dimension coverage\",\n                     f\"files: {cov.get('files')}; rules: {cov.get('rules')}\"))\n    if stats.get(\"dropped_low_conf\"):\n        rows.append((\"Filtered\", f\"{stats['dropped_low_conf']} low-confidence \"\n                                 \"finding(s) (REVIEW_MIN_CONFIDENCE)\"))\n    if stats.get(\"dropped_over_cap\"):\n        rows.append((\"Truncated\", f\"{stats['dropped_over_cap']} finding(s) \"\n                                  \"over the output cap\"))\n    if stats.get(\"reviewer_errors\"):\n        rows.append((\"Warnings\", f\"{stats['reviewer_errors']} review \"\n                                 \"dimension(s) failed to execute\"))\n    out = [\"### Review Coverage\", \"\", \"| Check | Result |\", \"|---|---|\"]\n    out += [f\"| {k} | {_cell(v)} |\" for k, v in rows]\n    out.append(\"\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _footer(stats: dict) -> str:\n    return (\"\\n---\\n<sub>pipeline v2\"\n            + (f\" \u00b7 rules {stats['rules_sha']}\" if stats.get(\"rules_sha\") else \"\")\n            + \"</sub>\")\n\n\ndef render_markdown(findings: list[Finding], stats: dict) -> str:\n    out: list[str] = [\"## Pull Request Review\"]\n\n    if not stats.get(\"files\"):\n        out.append(\"\\n**No reviewable changes could be extracted from this \"\n                   \"pull request** (empty diff, or all files were skipped). \"\n                   \"This report does **not** constitute approval \u2014 \"\n                   \"investigate the retrieval layer first.\")\n        for n in (stats.get(\"skipped_notes\") or [])[:6]:\n            out.append(f\"- Skipped: {n}\")\n        out.append(\"\")\n        out += _coverage_table(stats)\n        out.append(_footer(stats))\n        return \"\\n\".join(out)\n\n    ordered = sorted(findings, key=sort_key)\n    ids = {id(f): f\"F{i}\" for i, f in enumerate(ordered, 1)}\n\n    if stats.get(\"pr_summary\"):\n        out.append(f\"\\n**Summary of Changes**: {stats['pr_summary']}\")\n    out.append(f\"\\n**Review Outcome**: {_verdict(ordered, stats)}\")\n    if _partial(stats):\n        out.append(\"_Partial coverage: some files exceeded the reviewer \"\n                   \"context budget or were skipped at diff level \u2014 see the \"\n                   \"Coverage Check table. Static analysis covered all files._\")\n    if ordered:\n        out.append(f\"\\n{_counts_line(ordered)}\")\n    out.append(\"\")\n    out += _required_actions(ordered, ids)\n    out += _file_table(stats)\n    out += _graph_section(stats)\n    if ordered:\n        out += _findings_section(ordered, ids)\n    out += _dimension_table(stats, ordered, ids)\n    out += _rule_audit_section(stats, ordered, ids)\n    out += _coverage_table(stats)\n    out.append(_footer(stats))\n    return \"\\n\".join(out)\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/rules.py","perm":"0644","sha":"13e3b75fb29d5a9f5480abd704597abed2ed9ca467d7ee6fb5c600167c824fe3","data":"\"\"\"\u5718\u968a\u898f\u5247\u8f09\u5165\u5668 \u2014\u2014 \u628a rules repo \u7684\u672c\u6a5f clone \u7d44\u9032 review context\u3002\n\n\u5c0d\u76ee\u9304\u7d50\u69cb\u7684\u5047\u8a2d\u53ea\u6709\u5169\u500b\u540d\u5b57\uff08\u90fd\u53ef\u7528\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\u6539\uff0c\u7b49\u65bc\u6c92\u6709\u786c\u4f9d\u8cf4\uff09\uff1a\n\n  <RULES_ROOT>/\n    SKILL.md            \u2190 \u672c loader \u4e0d\u78b0\uff08\u5b83\u662f system prompt \u7684\u4e8b\uff0c\u898b seed_langfuse\uff09\n    rules/              \u2190 RULES_SUBDIR\uff0c\u9810\u8a2d \"rules\"\n      common/           \u2190 RULES_COMMON_DIR\uff0c\u9810\u8a2d \"common\"\uff1b\u6bcf\u6b21 review \u5fc5\u8f09\n      <repo \u540d\u5c0f\u5beb>/     \u2190 \u8207 PR \u6240\u5c6c repo \u540c\u540d\u7684\u76ee\u9304\uff0c\u5b58\u5728\u624d\u8f09\n      \u5176\u4ed6\u76ee\u9304/          \u2190 \u4e00\u5f8b\u5ffd\u7565\uff08\u5225\u7684 repo \u7684\u898f\u5247\u4e0d\u8a72\u6df7\u9032\u4f86\uff09\n\n\u7d00\u5f8b\uff1a\u552f\u8b80\u3001\u4e0d\u78b0\u7db2\u8def\u3001\u5931\u6557\u7d55\u4e0d\u70b8 review \u2014\u2014 RULES_ROOT \u6c92\u8a2d\u6216\u8def\u5f91\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\u6642\n\u56de\u7a7a bundle\uff0c\u884c\u70ba\u8207\u6c92\u6709\u898f\u5247\u529f\u80fd\u7684\u820a\u7248\u5b8c\u5168\u76f8\u540c\u3002\n\n\u8a2d\u5b9a\uff1asettings().rules\uff08RULES_ROOT / RULES_SUBDIR / RULES_COMMON_DIR / RULES_MAX_CHARS\uff09\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport subprocess\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass RulesBundle:\n    \"\"\"\u4e00\u6b21 review \u5be6\u969b\u8f09\u5165\u7684\u898f\u5247\u5feb\u7167\u3002\"\"\"\n\n    text: str = \"\"            # \u7d44\u597d\u7684\u898f\u5247\u5168\u6587\uff08\u542b\u8def\u5f91\u6a19\u982d\uff09\uff1b\u7a7a\u5b57\u4e32 = \u4ec0\u9ebc\u90fd\u6c92\u8f09\u5230\n    sha: str = \"\"             # rules repo \u7684 git commit \u2014\u2014 \u53ef\u91cd\u73fe\u6027\u7684\u9328\u9ede\n    files: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)  # \u5be6\u969b\u8f09\u5165\u7684\u6a94\u6848\uff08\u76f8\u5c0d RULES_ROOT\uff09\n    truncated: bool = False   # \u8d85\u904e RULES_MAX_CHARS \u88ab\u622a\u65b7\n    # \u9010\u6a94\u5167\u5bb9\uff08rel path \u2192 body\uff09\u2014\u2014 planner \u628a\u898f\u5247\u6307\u6d3e\u5230\u9762\u5411\u5f8c\uff0c\n    # reviewer \u53ea\u6536\u5230\u81ea\u5df1\u8a72\u7ba1\u7684\u90a3\u5e7e\u4efd\uff08targeted context\uff09\n    sections: dict[str, str] = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    @property\n    def loaded(self) -> bool:\n        return bool(self.text)\n\n\ndef _root() -> Path | None:\n    return settings().rules.root\n\n\ndef _git_sha(root: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u898f\u5247\u7684\u7248\u672c\u9328\uff1a\u53d6\u300c\u6700\u5f8c\u4e00\u6b21\u52d5\u5230 RULES_ROOT \u5b50\u6a39\u300d\u7684 commit short SHA\u3002\n\n    RULES_ROOT \u53ef\u4ee5\u6307\u5411\u5171\u7528 repo \u88e1\u7684\u5b50\u8cc7\u6599\u593e\uff08git \u6703\u81ea\u5df1\u5f80\u4e0a\u627e .git\uff09\uff1b\n    \u7528\u5b50\u6a39\u7bc4\u570d\u7684 log \u800c\u975e\u6574\u5eab HEAD\uff0c\u540c repo \u5176\u4ed6\u76ee\u9304\u7684 commit \u4e0d\u6703\n    \u6c59\u67d3\u9019\u500b\u9328\u3002\u4e0d\u662f git repo \u6216 git \u4e0d\u5728\u6642\u56de 'no-git'\uff08\u4e0d\u70b8\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    try:\n        r = subprocess.run(\n            [\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%h\", \"--\", \".\"],\n            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10,\n        )\n        return r.stdout.strip() or \"no-git\"\n    except Exception:\n        return \"no-git\"\n\n\ndef _iter_md(dirs: list[Path]):\n    for d in dirs:\n        if not d.is_dir():\n            continue\n        yield from sorted(d.rglob(\"*.md\"))\n\n\ndef load_rules(repo: str | None = None) -> RulesBundle:\n    \"\"\"common \u5fc5\u8f09\uff1brepo \u6709\u7d66\u4e14 rules/<repo\u5c0f\u5beb>/ \u5b58\u5728\u5c31\u758a\u4e0a\u53bb\u3002\n\n    \u8f09\u5165\u9806\u5e8f = common \u5148\u3001repo \u5c08\u5c6c\u5f8c\uff08\u512a\u5148\u5e8f\u8072\u660e\u5728 rules_context \u7684\u6a19\u982d\u88e1\uff09\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    root = _root()\n    if root is None or not root.is_dir():\n        return RulesBundle()\n\n    cfg = settings().rules\n    subdir = root / cfg.subdir\n    dirs = [subdir / cfg.common_dir]\n    if repo:\n        dirs.append(subdir / repo.strip().lower())\n\n    max_chars = cfg.max_chars\n    parts: list[str] = []\n    files: list[str] = []\n    sections: dict[str, str] = {}\n    total = 0\n    truncated = False\n    for f in _iter_md(dirs):\n        try:\n            body = f.read_text(errors=\"replace\").strip()\n        except OSError:\n            continue\n        if not body:\n            continue\n        rel = f.relative_to(root).as_posix()   # \u8de8\u5e73\u53f0\u4e00\u5f8b /\uff08rule_ref \u8207\u5831\u544a\u90fd\u7528\u9019\u500b\uff09\n        block = f\"## {rel}\\n{body}\"\n        if total + len(block) > max_chars:\n            truncated = True\n            break\n        parts.append(block)\n        files.append(rel)\n        sections[rel] = body\n        total += len(block)\n\n    return RulesBundle(\n        text=\"\\n\\n\".join(parts),\n        sha=_git_sha(root),\n        files=files,\n        truncated=truncated,\n        sections=sections,\n    )\n\n\ndef rules_context(bundle: RulesBundle) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\u628a bundle \u5305\u6210\u53ef\u76f4\u63a5 append \u5728 system prompt \u5f8c\u9762\u7684\u5340\u584a\uff1b\u6c92\u8f09\u5230\u5c31\u56de\u7a7a\u5b57\u4e32\u3002\n\n    rule_ref \u7684\u6307\u793a\u653e\u5728\u9019\u88e1\u800c\u4e0d\u662f Langfuse \u4e0a\u7684 prompt \u2014\u2014 \u9019\u6a23\u4e0d\u7ba1\u7dda\u4e0a\u7528\u7684\u662f\n    \u54ea\u4e00\u7248\u53d7\u7248\u63a7 prompt\uff0c\u53ea\u8981\u898f\u5247\u6709\u8f09\u5165\uff0c\u5f15\u7528\u898f\u7bc4\u5c31\u4e00\u5b9a\u8ddf\u8457\u3002\n    \"\"\"\n    if not bundle.loaded:\n        return \"\"\n    head = (\n        f\"\\n\\n# Team Rules (review basis, version {bundle.sha})\\n\"\n        \"The team rule documents follow; each begins with `## <file path>`.\\n\"\n        \"Precedence: repo-specific rules override common rules on conflict.\\n\"\n        \"For any finding based on a rule, set the finding's \\\"rule_ref\\\" \"\n        \"field to the rule file path (e.g. \\\"rules/common/naming.md\\\"); \"\n        \"leave rule_ref empty for general findings.\\n\"\n    )\n    tail = (\"\\n\\n(Note: rule documents exceeded the length limit; only the \"\n            \"leading portion was loaded)\" if bundle.truncated else \"\")\n    return head + \"\\n\" + bundle.text + tail\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/sources.py","perm":"0644","sha":"c9f66eb3c4966d182b13815dc6874a930ef3003be0872fd3bdbd862ba503461e","data":"\"\"\"sources \u2014\u2014 \u9935\u7d66 reviewer \u7684\u4e09\u500b git \u8cc7\u6599\u57df\uff08repos / rules / knowledge\uff09\u7684\u72c0\u614b\u8207\u9810\u89bd\u3002\n\n\u63a7\u5236\u53f0 Sources \u9801\u8981\u56de\u7b54\u7684\u554f\u984c\u53ea\u6709\u4e00\u500b\uff1a\u300creviewer \u7b49\u4e00\u4e0b\u770b\u5230\u7684\u6771\u897f\u65b0\u4e0d\u65b0\u3001\u5c0d\u4e0d\u5c0d\uff1f\u300d\n\u6240\u4ee5\u9019\u88e1\u7684\u6bcf\u500b\u51fd\u5f0f\u90fd\u662f\u8b80\u72c0\u614b\u6216\u6a21\u64ec\u4e00\u6b21\u6ce8\u5165\uff0c\u4e0d\u6539\u4efb\u4f55\u6771\u897f\uff1b\u552f\u4e00\u6703\u5beb\u7684\u662f add_repo\n\uff08git clone \u4e00\u9846\u65b0 clone \u5230 REPOS_ROOT\uff09\uff0c\u800c\u4e14\u5b83\u8dd1\u5b8c\u7acb\u523b\u5c31\u662f repo-sync job \u7684\u7ba1\u8f44\u7bc4\u570d\u3002\n\n\u5168\u90e8\u540c\u6b65\u3001\u6703\u8dd1 git \u5b50\u884c\u7a0b\uff1b\u8def\u7531\u7aef\u7528 asyncio.to_thread\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport time\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\n\ndef _git(path: Path, *args: str, timeout: int = 20) -> tuple[int, str]:\n    try:\n        r = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(path), *args], capture_output=True,\n                           text=True, timeout=timeout)\n        return r.returncode, (r.stdout or r.stderr).strip()\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return 127, f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\"\n\n\ndef _head(path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"{sha, date, subject, branch} \u6216 {error}\u3002\"\"\"\n    rc, out = _git(path, \"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%h%x09%cs%x09%s\")\n    if rc != 0:\n        return {\"error\": out[:200] or \"not a git repo\"}\n    sha, date, subject = (out.split(\"\\t\", 2) + [\"\", \"\"])[:3]\n    _rc, branch = _git(path, \"rev-parse\", \"--abbrev-ref\", \"HEAD\")\n    return {\"sha\": sha, \"date\": date, \"subject\": subject[:80], \"branch\": branch}\n\n\ndef _last_touch(path: Path) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\u4e0a\u6b21 pull / fetch \u7684\u6642\u9593\uff1a.git/FETCH_HEAD \u7684 mtime\uff08\u6c92\u6709\u5c31 HEAD \u7684\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    for name in (\"FETCH_HEAD\", \"HEAD\"):\n        p = path / \".git\" / name\n        if p.exists():\n            return p.stat().st_mtime\n    return None\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass SourceView:\n    kind: str                       # repos | rules | knowledge\n    root: str | None\n    exists: bool\n    head: dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    items: list[dict[str, Any]] = field(default_factory=list)\n    counts: dict[str, int] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    note: str = \"\"\n\n    def as_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return asdict(self)\n\n\n# ---------- repos ----------\n\ndef repos_view() -> SourceView:\n    s = settings()\n    root = s.repos.repos_root\n    if root is None:\n        return SourceView(\"repos\", None, False, note=\"REPOS_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\uff1areview \u7167\u8dd1\uff0c\u4f46\u6c92\u6709 base \u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\")\n    if not root.is_dir():\n        return SourceView(\"repos\", str(root), False, note=\"REPOS_ROOT \u6307\u5411\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\u7684\u76ee\u9304\")\n    items = []\n    for d in sorted(root.iterdir()):\n        if not d.is_dir():\n            continue\n        if not (d / \".git\").exists():\n            items.append({\"name\": d.name, \"git\": False, \"note\": \"\u975e git clone\uff1brepo-sync \u7565\u904e\"})\n            continue\n        h = _head(d)\n        _rc, dirty = _git(d, \"status\", \"--porcelain\", \"--untracked-files=no\")\n        items.append({\"name\": d.name, \"git\": True, **h,\n                      \"dirty\": bool(dirty.strip()) if _rc == 0 else None,\n                      \"last_touch\": _last_touch(d)})\n    return SourceView(\"repos\", str(root), True, items=items,\n                      counts={\"clones\": sum(1 for i in items if i.get(\"git\")),\n                              \"others\": sum(1 for i in items if not i.get(\"git\"))})\n\n\n_URL_OK = re.compile(r\"^https?://[^\\s]+$\")\n_NAME_OK = re.compile(r\"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,63}$\")\n\n\ndef add_repo(name: str, url: str, branch: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"clone \u4e00\u9846\u65b0 repo \u5230 REPOS_ROOT/<name>\u3002PAT \u8d70 RUNBOOK 3.3 \u7684\u65b9\u6848 A\uff08\u9032 URL\uff1b\n    .git/config \u53ea\u6709\u670d\u52d9\u5e33\u865f\u8b80\u5f97\u5230\uff0c\u5167\u7db2\u53ef\u63a5\u53d7\uff09\u3002\u56de\u6bcf\u6b65\u4e00\u884c\u3002\"\"\"\n    s = settings()\n    root = s.repos.repos_root\n    name = name.strip().lower()\n    if root is None:\n        return [\"REPOS_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\uff0c\u7121\u8655\u53ef clone\"]\n    if not _NAME_OK.match(name):\n        return [f\"\u540d\u5b57\u4e0d\u5408\u6cd5\uff1a{name!r}\uff08\u5c0f\u5beb\u3001\u6578\u5b57\u3001. _ -\uff1b\u5fc5\u9808\u7b49\u65bc PR URL \u88e1 _git/<\u9019\u6bb5> \u7684\u5c0f\u5beb\uff09\"]\n    if not _URL_OK.match(url.strip()):\n        return [\"clone URL \u8981\u662f http(s)://\u2026\"]\n    dest = root / name\n    if dest.exists():\n        return [f\"{dest} \u5df2\u5b58\u5728\"]\n    root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    pat = s.ado.pat.get_secret_value()\n    auth_url = url.strip()\n    if pat and \"@\" not in auth_url.split(\"://\", 1)[1].split(\"/\", 1)[0]:\n        scheme, rest = auth_url.split(\"://\", 1)\n        auth_url = f\"{scheme}://anything:{pat}@{rest}\"\n    cmd = [\"git\", \"clone\", \"--quiet\"]\n    if branch.strip():\n        cmd += [\"--branch\", branch.strip()]\n    cmd += [auth_url, str(dest)]\n    try:\n        r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=1800)\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return [f\"clone \u4f8b\u5916\uff1a{type(e).__name__}: {e}\"]\n    if r.returncode != 0:\n        err = (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip().replace(pat, \"***\") if pat else (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()\n        return [f\"clone \u5931\u6557\uff1a{err[:300]}\"]\n    h = _head(dest)\n    return [f\"{name} -> {h.get('sha', '?')}\uff08{h.get('branch', '?')}\uff09\",\n            \"\u4e4b\u5f8c\u7531 repo-sync job \u4fdd\u9bae\uff1bPR URL \u88e1 repo \u540d\u5c0f\u5beb\u8981\u7b49\u65bc\u9019\u500b\u76ee\u9304\u540d\"]\n\n\n# ---------- rules ----------\n\ndef rules_view() -> SourceView:\n    from orchestrator.rules import _git_sha\n    s = settings()\n    root = s.rules.root\n    if root is None:\n        return SourceView(\"rules\", None, False, note=\"RULES_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\uff1a\u898f\u5247\u529f\u80fd\u505c\u7528\")\n    if not root.is_dir():\n        return SourceView(\"rules\", str(root), False, note=\"RULES_ROOT \u6307\u5411\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\u7684\u76ee\u9304\")\n    sub = root / s.rules.subdir\n    items = []\n    for f in sorted(sub.rglob(\"*.md\")) if sub.is_dir() else []:\n        rel = f.relative_to(root).as_posix()\n        scope = rel.split(\"/\")[1] if rel.count(\"/\") >= 2 else \"?\"\n        items.append({\"path\": rel, \"scope\": scope, \"chars\": f.stat().st_size,\n                      \"kind\": \"common\" if scope == s.rules.common_dir else \"repo\"})\n    semgrep = [f.relative_to(root).as_posix() for pat in (\"**/*.semgrep.yml\", \"**/*.semgrep.yaml\")\n               for f in sorted(root.glob(pat))]\n    repos = sorted({i[\"scope\"] for i in items if i[\"kind\"] == \"repo\"})\n    return SourceView(\"rules\", str(root), True, head={\"sha\": _git_sha(root), **_head(root)},\n                      items=items + [{\"path\": p, \"scope\": \"semgrep\", \"chars\": None, \"kind\": \"semgrep\"} for p in semgrep],\n                      counts={\"md\": len(items), \"semgrep\": len(semgrep), \"common\": sum(1 for i in items if i[\"kind\"] == \"common\"),\n                              \"repos\": len(repos)},\n                      note=(\"\u627e\u4e0d\u5230 \" + (sub / s.rules.common_dir).as_posix() + \"\uff08RULES_SUBDIR / RULES_COMMON_DIR \u5c0d\u4e0d\u4e0a\uff09\"\n                            if not (sub / s.rules.common_dir).is_dir() else \"\"))\n\n\ndef rules_preview(repo: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\u6a21\u64ec\u4e00\u6b21 review \u5c0d\u9019\u500b repo \u6703\u8f09\u5165\u54ea\u4e9b\u898f\u5247\uff08\u771f\u7684\u547c\u53eb load_rules\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    from orchestrator.rules import load_rules\n    b = load_rules(repo or None)\n    return {\"repo\": repo, \"loaded\": b.loaded, \"sha\": b.sha, \"files\": b.files,\n            \"chars\": len(b.text), \"truncated\": b.truncated,\n            \"cap\": settings().rules.max_chars,\n            \"sections\": [{\"path\": k, \"chars\": len(v)} for k, v in b.sections.items()]}\n\n\n# ---------- knowledge ----------\n\ndef knowledge_view() -> SourceView:\n    s = settings()\n    root = s.knowledge.root\n    if root is None:\n        return SourceView(\"knowledge\", None, False, note=\"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u672a\u8a2d\uff1aK \u6bb5\u505c\u7528\")\n    if not root.is_dir():\n        return SourceView(\"knowledge\", str(root), False, note=\"KNOWLEDGE_ROOT \u6307\u5411\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\u7684\u76ee\u9304\")\n    items = []\n    for f in sorted(root.rglob(\"*.md\")):\n        rel = f.relative_to(root)\n        if any(part.startswith(\"_\") for part in rel.parts):\n            continue\n        body = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        items.append({\"path\": rel.as_posix(), \"repo\": rel.parts[0] if len(rel.parts) > 1 else \"?\",\n                      \"invariants\": body.count(\"\\n- \") if \"## Invariants\" in body else 0,\n                      \"retired\": body.count(\"\\n- ~~\"), \"chars\": len(body)})\n    pend = root / \"_pending\"\n    pending = sorted(pend.rglob(\"pr-*.json\")) if pend.is_dir() else []\n    cyc = root / \"_cycle\"\n    staged = sorted(cyc.rglob(\"pr-*.json\")) if cyc.is_dir() else []\n    return SourceView(\"knowledge\", str(root), True, head=_head(root), items=items,\n                      counts={\"pages\": len(items), \"pending\": len(pending), \"staged\": len(staged),\n                              \"repos\": len({i[\"repo\"] for i in items})})\n\n\ndef knowledge_preview(repo: str, paths: list[str]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\u6a21\u64ec\u4e00\u6b21 review \u5c0d (repo, \u8b8a\u66f4\u6a94) \u6703\u6ce8\u5165\u54ea\u4e9b\u689d\u76ee\uff08\u771f\u7684\u547c\u53eb load_for\uff09\u3002\"\"\"\n    from orchestrator.knowledge import load_for\n    text, stats = load_for(repo or None, paths)\n    return {\"repo\": repo, \"paths\": paths, \"chars\": len(text), \"stats\": stats, \"text\": text,\n            \"cap\": settings().knowledge.max_chars}\n\n\ndef all_views() -> dict[str, SourceView]:\n    return {\"repos\": repos_view(), \"rules\": rules_view(), \"knowledge\": knowledge_view()}\n\n\ndef now() -> float:\n    return time.time()\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/static_pass.py","perm":"0644","sha":"82a13d0773f0bac8dc4c0a7733cd04088983c1ccbbfa4177d8bffc38eba4199a","data":"\"\"\"static pass\uff08v2 \u7b2c 1 \u6bb5\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u6383\u63cf\uff0c\u96f6 LLM\u3001\u96f6\u5e7b\u89ba\u3001\u884c\u865f\u7cbe\u6e96\u3002\n\n\u505a\u6cd5\uff1a\u5c0d\u6bcf\u500b\u8b8a\u66f4\u6a94\u505a\u300c\u7a00\u758f\u91cd\u5efa\u300d\uff08anatomy.sparse_new_file\uff0c\u884c\u865f\u4fdd\u771f\uff09\u5beb\u9032\n\u66ab\u5b58\u76ee\u9304 \u2192 semgrep / ruff \u6383 \u2192 \u53ea\u4fdd\u7559\u843d\u5728\u300c\u65b0\u589e\u884c\u300d\u4e0a\u7684\u547d\u4e2d\uff08\u4e0d\u5c0d\u672a\u8b8a\u66f4\n\u7684\u7a0b\u5f0f\u8aaa\u6559\uff09\u2192 \u7522\u51fa source=\"static\"\u3001confidence=1.0 \u7684 findings\u3002\n\n\u898f\u5247\u4f86\u6e90\uff1a\n  1) \u5c08\u6848\u5167\u5efa deploy/semgrep/starter.yml\n  2) rules repo \u88e1\u7684 semgrep \u898f\u5247\uff08RULES_ROOT \u5e95\u4e0b **/*.semgrep.yml \u8207\n     semgrep/**/*.yml\uff09\u2014\u2014 \u6a5f\u68b0\u53ef\u67e5\u7684\u5718\u968a\u898f\u5247\u5beb\u6210 semgrep\uff0c\u639b\u5728\u9019\u5c64\uff0c\n     \u547d\u4e2d\u81ea\u52d5\u4ee5\u8a72\u898f\u5247\u6a94\u70ba rule_ref\uff08\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027\u57f7\u6cd5\uff0crule_ref \u4e5f\u662f\u78ba\u5b9a\u7684\uff09\u3002\n\n\u74b0\u5883\u8b8a\u6578\uff1aSTATIC_SEMGREP / STATIC_RUFF\uff08\u9810\u8a2d auto\uff1a\u88dd\u4e86\u5c31\u8dd1\uff0c\u6c92\u88dd\u5c31\u8df3\u904e\u4e26\u8a3b\u8a18\uff09\nproduction \u548c\u96e2\u7dda eval \u5403\u7684\u90fd\u662f\u540c\u4e00\u4efd diff \u2014\u2014 \u9019\u5c64\u5728\u5169\u908a\u884c\u70ba\u4e00\u6a21\u4e00\u6a23\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom orchestrator.anatomy import Anatomy, sparse_new_file\nfrom orchestrator.models import Finding\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\n_PROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nSTARTER = _PROJECT_ROOT / \"deploy\" / \"semgrep\" / \"starter.yml\"\n\n_SEV = {\"ERROR\": \"error\", \"WARNING\": \"warning\", \"INFO\": \"info\"}\n\n\ndef _rules_semgrep_configs() -> list[tuple[Path, str]]:\n    \"\"\"(\u898f\u5247\u6a94\u8def\u5f91, rule_ref) \u2014\u2014 \u4f86\u81ea rules repo \u7684 semgrep \u898f\u5247\u3002\"\"\"\n    r = settings().rules.root\n    if r is None or not r.is_dir():\n        return []\n    seen: dict[Path, str] = {}\n    for pat in (\"**/*.semgrep.yml\", \"**/*.semgrep.yaml\",\n                \"semgrep/**/*.yml\", \"semgrep/**/*.yaml\"):\n        for f in sorted(r.glob(pat)):\n            seen.setdefault(f, str(f.relative_to(r)))\n    return list(seen.items())\n\n\ndef _materialize(ana: Anatomy, tmp: Path) -> dict[Path, str]:\n    \"\"\"\u7a00\u758f\u91cd\u5efa\u5beb\u9032\u66ab\u5b58\u76ee\u9304\u3002\u56de\u50b3 \u66ab\u5b58\u8def\u5f91 \u2192 \u539f\u59cb diff \u8def\u5f91 \u7684\u5c0d\u7167\u3002\"\"\"\n    mapping: dict[Path, str] = {}\n    for fc in ana.files:\n        body = sparse_new_file(fc)\n        if not body.strip():\n            continue\n        rel = fc.path.lstrip(\"/\")\n        dst = (tmp / rel).resolve()\n        if tmp not in dst.parents:            # \u9632\u8def\u5f91\u7a7f\u8d8a\uff08../../ \u4e4b\u985e\uff09\n            continue\n        dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        dst.write_text(body)\n        mapping[dst] = fc.path\n    return mapping\n\n\ndef _timeout() -> int:\n    return settings().static.timeout\n\n\ndef _run(cmd: list[str], env: dict | None = None) -> tuple[int, str, str]:\n    try:\n        p = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True,\n                           timeout=_timeout(), env=env)\n        return p.returncode, p.stdout, p.stderr\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        return -1, \"\", f\"timed out (STATIC_TIMEOUT={_timeout()}s)\"\n    except OSError as e:\n        return -1, \"\", str(e)\n\n\n_RULE_ID = re.compile(r\"^\\s*-\\s*id:\\s*([\\w.\\-]+)\", re.M)\n\n\ndef _id_map(configs: list[tuple[Path, str]]) -> dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"\u898f\u5247 id \u2192 \u4f86\u6e90\u898f\u5247\u6a94\uff08rule_ref \u7528\uff09\u3002id \u649e\u540d\u6642\u5148\u5230\u5148\u8d0f\u3002\"\"\"\n    out: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for cfg, ref in configs:\n        try:\n            text = cfg.read_text(errors=\"replace\")\n        except OSError:\n            continue\n        for rid in _RULE_ID.findall(text):\n            out.setdefault(rid, ref)\n    return out\n\n\ndef _semgrep(tmp: Path, mapping: dict[Path, str], added: dict[str, set[int]],\n             notes: list[str]) -> list[Finding]:\n    configs: list[tuple[Path, str]] = []\n    if STARTER.is_file():\n        configs.append((STARTER, \"\"))\n    configs += _rules_semgrep_configs()\n    if not configs:\n        notes.append(\"semgrep: no rule configs available, skipped\")\n        return [], []\n    checked_refs = sorted({ref for _, ref in configs if ref})\n    ids = _id_map(configs)\n    cmd = [\"semgrep\", \"scan\", \"--json\", \"--quiet\", \"--metrics=off\",\n           \"--timeout\", \"30\", \"--no-git-ignore\"]\n    for cfg, _ in configs:\n        cmd += [\"--config\", str(cfg)]\n    cmd.append(str(tmp))\n    # \u5167\u7db2\u91cd\u9ede\uff1a\u95dc\u6389\u555f\u52d5\u6642\u7684\u7248\u672c\u6aa2\u67e5\uff08\u9023\u4e0d\u4e0a semgrep.dev \u6703\u540a\u5230\u903e\u6642\uff09\n    env = dict(os.environ, SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=\"0\")\n    code, out, err = _run(cmd, env=env)\n    if code < 0 or not out.strip():\n        notes.append(f\"semgrep failed: {err[:120]}\")\n        return [], []\n    try:\n        results = json.loads(out).get(\"results\", [])\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        notes.append(\"semgrep: non-JSON output, skipped\")\n        return [], []\n    finds: list[Finding] = []\n    for r in results:\n        p = Path(r.get(\"path\", \"\")).resolve()\n        orig = mapping.get(p)\n        if not orig:\n            continue\n        line = int((r.get(\"start\") or {}).get(\"line\") or 0)\n        if line not in added.get(orig, set()):\n            continue                       # \u53ea\u8a55\u65b0\u589e\u884c\uff0c\u4e0d\u5c0d\u672a\u8b8a\u66f4\u7a0b\u5f0f\u8aaa\u6559\n        extra = r.get(\"extra\") or {}\n        meta = extra.get(\"metadata\") or {}\n        check = str(r.get(\"check_id\", \"\"))\n        ref = str(meta.get(\"rule_ref\", \"\"))\n        if not ref:                        # check_id \u53ef\u80fd\u5e36\u8def\u5f91\u524d\u7db4\uff0c\u53d6\u5c3e\u6bb5\u5c0d id \u8868\n            ref = ids.get(check) or ids.get(check.rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1], \"\")\n        finds.append(Finding(\n            rule=str(meta.get(\"review_rule\", \"SECURITY\")).upper(),\n            file=orig, line=line,\n            severity=_SEV.get(str(extra.get(\"severity\", \"\")).upper(), \"warning\"),\n            note=(extra.get(\"message\") or check),\n            rule_ref=ref,\n            source=\"static\", confidence=1.0,\n        ))\n    return finds, checked_refs\n\n\ndef _ruff(mapping: dict[Path, str], added: dict[str, set[int]],\n          notes: list[str]) -> list[Finding]:\n    py = [p for p in mapping if p.suffix == \".py\"]\n    if not py:\n        return []\n    cmd = [\"ruff\", \"check\", \"--select\", \"F821,F811,F601,E711,E712\",\n           \"--output-format\", \"json\", \"--no-cache\", \"--isolated\",\n           *map(str, py)]\n    code, out, err = _run(cmd)\n    if not out.strip():\n        if code not in (0, 1):\n            notes.append(f\"ruff failed: {err[:160]}\")\n        return []\n    try:\n        results = json.loads(out)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        notes.append(\"ruff: non-JSON output, skipped\")\n        return []\n    finds: list[Finding] = []\n    for r in results:\n        p = Path(r.get(\"filename\", \"\")).resolve()\n        orig = mapping.get(p)\n        line = int((r.get(\"location\") or {}).get(\"row\") or 0)\n        if not orig or line not in added.get(orig, set()):\n            continue\n        finds.append(Finding(\n            rule=\"BUG\", file=orig, line=line, severity=\"warning\",\n            note=f\"[{r.get('code')}] {r.get('message', '')}\",\n            source=\"static\", confidence=1.0,\n        ))\n    return finds\n\n\n# \u516c\u958b\u540d\uff1aknowledge \u7684\u84b8\u993e\u5207\u7247\u6392\u5e8f\u8207 primary_entity fallback \u5403\u540c\u4e00\u4efd\u5224\u65b7\u2014\u2014\n# \u300c\u54ea\u4e9b\u6a94\u662f\u6e2c\u8a66\u300d\u300c\u54ea\u4e00\u884c\u662f\u65b0\u5ba3\u544a\u300d\u53ea\u80fd\u6709\u4e00\u500b\u5b9a\u7fa9\uff0c\u5426\u5247\u5169\u908a\u6703\u6162\u6162\u6f02\u79fb\u3002\nTEST_PATH_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"(^|/)(tests?)(/|$)|(^|/)(test_[^/]+|[^/]+_test)\\.py$\"\n    r\"|(^|/)[A-Za-z0-9_]*Tests?\\.java$|(^|/)[A-Za-z0-9_]*Spec\\.[a-z]+$\"\n    r\"|\\.(spec|test)\\.[jt]sx?$\", re.I)\n_BEHAVIOR_EXT = {\".java\", \".py\", \".kt\", \".cs\", \".go\", \".ts\", \".js\", \".scala\"}\nDECL_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"^\\s*(def |class |function |func |fun |\"\n    r\"(public|protected|private)\\b[^;=]*\\(|\"\n    r\"(static|final)\\b[^;=]*\\([^)]*\\)\\s*\\{)\")\n\n\ndef _missing_test(ana: Anatomy) -> list[Finding]:\n    \"\"\"\u78ba\u5b9a\u6027 MISSING-TEST\uff1a\u65b0\u589e\u4e86\u53ef\u547c\u53eb\u884c\u70ba\u3001\u540c diff \u537b\u6c92\u78b0\u4efb\u4f55\u6e2c\u8a66\u6a94\u3002\n    \u523b\u610f\u4fdd\u5b88\uff1a\u53ea\u8a8d\u300c\u65b0\u589e\u5ba3\u544a\u300d\u70ba\u884c\u70ba\u8a0a\u865f \u2014\u2014 \u7d14\u91cd\u69cb\uff08\u6539\u5e38\u6578/\u642c\u547c\u53eb\uff09\u4e0d\u89f8\u767c\u3002\n    STATIC_MISSING_TEST=false \u53ef\u6574\u6bb5\u95dc\u9589\u3002\"\"\"\n    if not settings().static.missing_test:\n        return []\n    if any(TEST_PATH_RE.search(fc.path.lstrip(\"/\")) for fc in ana.files):\n        return []                                   # diff \u6709\u5e36\u6e2c\u8a66 \u2192 \u4e0d\u542d\u8072\n    behavior: list[tuple[int, str, int]] = []       # (\u65b0\u589e\u5ba3\u544a\u6578, path, \u9996\u884c)\n    for fc in ana.files:\n        if Path(fc.path).suffix.lower() not in _BEHAVIOR_EXT:\n            continue\n        decls = [ln for ln, text in fc.added if DECL_RE.match(text)]\n        if decls:\n            behavior.append((len(decls), fc.path, decls[0]))\n    if not behavior:\n        return []\n    behavior.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[0], x[1]))\n    _, primary, line = behavior[0]\n    names = \", \".join(b[1] for b in behavior[:3])\n    return [Finding(\n        rule=\"MISSING-TEST\", file=primary, line=line, severity=\"warning\",\n        note=(f\"This diff adds or changes behavior in {len(behavior)} file(s) \"\n              f\"({names}) but touches no test files\"),\n        suggestion=\"Add or update tests covering the new/changed behavior \"\n                   \"in the same pull request.\",\n        source=\"static\", confidence=1.0,\n    )]\n\n\ndef run_static(ana: Anatomy) -> tuple[list[Finding], list[str], list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\u56de\u50b3 (findings, notes, checked_rule_refs)\u3002\n    checked_rule_refs = \u5be6\u969b\u6383\u63cf\u904e\u7684\u300c\u5718\u968a semgrep \u898f\u5247\u6a94\u300d\u2014\u20140 \u547d\u4e2d\u5373\u70ba\n    \u8a72\u898f\u5247\u7684\u6a5f\u68b0\u901a\u904e\u8b49\u64da\u3002\u6383\u63cf\u5668\u7f3a\u5e2d\uff0f\u6545\u969c = \u8a3b\u8a18\u4e26\u8df3\u904e\uff0c\u7d55\u4e0d\u70b8 review\u3002\"\"\"\n    notes: list[str] = []\n    checked: list[str] = []\n    added = {fc.path: fc.added_linenos for fc in ana.files}\n    if not any(added.values()):\n        return [], notes, checked\n    tmp = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"crg-static-\"))\n    try:\n        mapping = _materialize(ana, tmp)\n        finds: list[Finding] = []\n        if settings().static.semgrep_enabled:\n            sg, checked = _semgrep(tmp, mapping, added, notes)\n            finds += sg\n        else:\n            notes.append(\"semgrep: disabled or not installed\")\n        if settings().static.ruff_enabled:\n            finds += _ruff(mapping, added, notes)\n        else:\n            notes.append(\"ruff: disabled or not installed\")\n        finds += _missing_test(ana)\n        return finds, notes, checked\n    finally:\n        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)\n"}
{"path":"orchestrator/store.py","perm":"0644","sha":"8cec8f2a266861a8748904a4ecfecb4fb3955f5c1422845946e22df10d7dfa88","data":"\"\"\"store \u2014\u2014 review \u6b77\u53f2\uff08SQLite\uff0c\u6a19\u6e96\u5eab\uff09\u3002\n\n\u70ba\u4ec0\u9ebc\u8981\u6709\u5b83\uff1a\u4eca\u5929\u300c\u525b\u624d\u90a3\u689d review \u767c\u751f\u4e86\u4ec0\u9ebc\u300d\u53ea\u80fd\u53bb Langfuse \u7ffb trace \u6216\u7ffb\njournal\u3002\u63a7\u5236\u53f0\u7684 Reviews \u9801\u8981\u5728\u672c\u6a5f\u5c31\u80fd\u56de\u7b54\uff1a\u54ea\u689d PR\u3001\u5e7e\u5206\u9418\u524d\u3001v1 \u9084\u662f v2\u3001\n\u5e7e\u689d finding\u3001\u6ce8\u5165\u4e86\u54ea\u4e9b rules / knowledge\u3001\u5831\u544a\u9577\u4ec0\u9ebc\u6a23\u3001trace \u9023\u7d50\u5728\u54ea\u3002\n\n\u4e00\u5f35\u8868\uff0c\u4e00\u500b\u6a94\uff08DATA_DIR/reviews.db\uff09\uff0cWAL \u6a21\u5f0f\uff0c\u6bcf\u6b21\u547c\u53eb\u958b\u95dc\u9023\u7dda\uff08\u884c\u7a0b\u5167\u591a\u57f7\u884c\u7dd2\n\u5b89\u5168\uff09\u3002DATA_DIR \u958b\u4e0d\u51fa\u4f86\uff08\u6b0a\u9650\u3001\u4e0d\u5b58\u5728\u4e14\u5efa\u4e0d\u4e86\uff09= store \u505c\u7528\u3001review \u7167\u8dd1\uff1a\u6b77\u53f2\u662f\n\u52a0\u5206\u9805\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u4f9d\u8cf4\u3002\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport sqlite3\nimport time\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Iterator\n\nfrom shared.settings import settings\n\n_SCHEMA = \"\"\"\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS reviews (\n  id          INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n  pr_url      TEXT NOT NULL,\n  repo        TEXT,\n  pr_id       INTEGER,\n  title       TEXT,\n  user        TEXT,\n  status      TEXT NOT NULL,            -- running | done | error\n  started     REAL NOT NULL,\n  finished    REAL,\n  pipeline    TEXT,\n  n_error     INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n  n_warning   INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n  n_info      INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n  findings    TEXT,                     -- JSON list\n  stats       TEXT,                     -- JSON dict\uff08\u542b rules_files / knowledge_injected \u2026\uff09\n  markdown    TEXT,\n  error       TEXT,\n  trace_id    TEXT\n);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS reviews_started ON reviews(started DESC);\n\"\"\"\n\n_disabled_reason: str = \"\"\n\n\ndef db_path() -> Path:\n    return settings().orchestrator.data_dir / \"reviews.db\"\n\n\ndef enabled() -> bool:\n    return not _disabled_reason\n\n\ndef disabled_reason() -> str:\n    return _disabled_reason\n\n\n@contextmanager\ndef _conn() -> Iterator[sqlite3.Connection]:\n    global _disabled_reason\n    p = db_path()\n    try:\n        p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        c = sqlite3.connect(p, timeout=5.0)\n    except (OSError, sqlite3.Error) as e:\n        _disabled_reason = f\"{p.parent}: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\"\n        raise\n    _disabled_reason = \"\"\n    c.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    try:\n        c.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL\")\n        c.executescript(_SCHEMA)\n        yield c\n        c.commit()\n    finally:\n        c.close()\n\n\ndef _safe(fn, default):\n    \"\"\"store \u662f\u52a0\u5206\u9805\uff1a\u4efb\u4f55\u5931\u6557\u56de default\u3001\u8a18\u4e0b\u539f\u56e0\uff0c\u7d55\u4e0d\u8b93 review \u70b8\u3002\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return fn()\n    except (OSError, sqlite3.Error):\n        return default\n\n\n# ---------- \u5beb ----------\n\ndef start_review(pr_url: str, user: str, meta: dict | None = None) -> int | None:\n    from shared.azdo import parse_pr_url\n    try:\n        ref = parse_pr_url(pr_url)\n        repo, pr_id = ref.repo, ref.pr_id\n    except ValueError:\n        repo, pr_id = None, None\n    meta = meta or {}\n\n    def go():\n        with _conn() as c:\n            cur = c.execute(\n                \"INSERT INTO reviews (pr_url, repo, pr_id, title, user, status, started, pipeline)\"\n                \" VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?)\",\n                (pr_url, repo, pr_id, (meta.get(\"title\") or \"\")[:200], user, \"running\",\n                 time.time(), settings().orchestrator.pipeline))\n            return cur.lastrowid\n    return _safe(go, None)\n\n\ndef set_title(review_id: int | None, title: str) -> None:\n    if review_id is None:\n        return\n    _safe(lambda: _exec(\"UPDATE reviews SET title=? WHERE id=?\", ((title or \"\")[:200], review_id)), None)\n\n\ndef finish_review(review_id: int | None, result, trace_id: str | None = None) -> None:\n    if review_id is None:\n        return\n    findings = list(getattr(result, \"findings\", None) or [])\n    stats = dict(getattr(result, \"stats\", None) or {})\n    sev = {\"error\": 0, \"warning\": 0, \"info\": 0}\n    for f in findings:\n        s = getattr(f, \"severity\", \"info\")\n        sev[s if s in sev else \"info\"] += 1\n    dump = getattr(result, \"findings_summary\", None)\n    summary_list = dump() if callable(dump) else [\n        f.model_dump() if hasattr(f, \"model_dump\") else dict(vars(f)) for f in findings]\n    _safe(lambda: _exec(\n        \"UPDATE reviews SET status='done', finished=?, pipeline=?, n_error=?, n_warning=?, n_info=?,\"\n        \" findings=?, stats=?, markdown=?, trace_id=? WHERE id=?\",\n        (time.time(), stats.get(\"pipeline\"), sev[\"error\"], sev[\"warning\"], sev[\"info\"],\n         json.dumps(summary_list, ensure_ascii=False, default=str),\n         json.dumps(stats, ensure_ascii=False, default=str),\n         getattr(result, \"markdown\", \"\"), trace_id, review_id)), None)\n\n\ndef fail_review(review_id: int | None, error: str) -> None:\n    if review_id is None:\n        return\n    _safe(lambda: _exec(\"UPDATE reviews SET status='error', finished=?, error=? WHERE id=?\",\n                        (time.time(), error[:2000], review_id)), None)\n\n\ndef _exec(sql: str, params: tuple) -> None:\n    with _conn() as c:\n        c.execute(sql, params)\n\n\n# ---------- \u8b80 ----------\n\ndef _row(r: sqlite3.Row, full: bool = False) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    d = dict(r)\n    for k in (\"findings\", \"stats\"):\n        if full and d.get(k):\n            try:\n                d[k] = json.loads(d[k])\n            except ValueError:\n                d[k] = None\n        elif not full:\n            d.pop(k, None)\n    if not full:\n        d.pop(\"markdown\", None)\n    d[\"duration\"] = (d[\"finished\"] - d[\"started\"]) if d.get(\"finished\") else None\n    return d\n\n\ndef list_reviews(limit: int = 50) -> list[dict]:\n    def go():\n        with _conn() as c:\n            rows = c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM reviews ORDER BY started DESC LIMIT ?\", (limit,)).fetchall()\n            return [_row(r) for r in rows]\n    return _safe(go, [])\n\n\ndef get_review(review_id: int) -> dict | None:\n    def go():\n        with _conn() as c:\n            r = c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM reviews WHERE id=?\", (review_id,)).fetchone()\n            return _row(r, full=True) if r else None\n    return _safe(go, None)\n\n\ndef summary(days: int = 7) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Overview \u7528\uff1a\u8fd1 N \u5929\u5e7e\u689d\u3001\u5931\u6557\u5e7e\u689d\u3001\u5e73\u5747\u79d2\u6578\u3001\u5e73\u5747 finding \u6578\u3002\"\"\"\n    since = time.time() - days * 86400\n\n    def go():\n        with _conn() as c:\n            r = c.execute(\n                \"SELECT COUNT(*) n, SUM(status='error') errs, AVG(finished-started) secs,\"\n                \" AVG(n_error+n_warning+n_info) finds FROM reviews WHERE started>=?\", (since,)).fetchone()\n            return {\"days\": days, \"n\": r[\"n\"] or 0, \"errors\": r[\"errs\"] or 0,\n                    \"avg_seconds\": r[\"secs\"], \"avg_findings\": r[\"finds\"]}\n    return _safe(go, {\"days\": days, \"n\": 0, \"errors\": 0, \"avg_seconds\": None, \"avg_findings\": None})\n"}
{"path":"requirements.txt","perm":"0644","sha":"bc00bbcbee13a913d2b0f50bc1bb1a081b3bdf3c40b4e01f5f9d6111482112ca","data":"fastmcp>=2.3\nlangfuse>=4.14,<5\nopenai>=1.40\nfastapi>=0.110\nuvicorn>=0.29\nhttpx>=0.27\npydantic>=2.6\npydantic-settings>=2.3   # shared/settings.py\njinja2>=3.1              # orchestrator/console (server-side templates)\npython-multipart>=0.0.9  # console form posts\n\n# v2 static pass (optional but strongly recommended; skipped with a note when absent)\n# ruff>=0.4\n# semgrep>=1.60\n"}
